    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001) V1 primary visual cortex form constants (Human V1 (Kluver form constants))" ;
        dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/bressloff-v1-form-constants-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/bressloff-v1-form-constants-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/bressloff-v1-form-constants-3> ;
        schema:about "Human V1 (Kluver form constants)" ;
        schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Does not yet claim: Remaining v4 items tracked in the Pass N+1 run record",
            "reconstructed_in_script: Planform bifurcation analysis of V1 activity patterns. Pass N+1 closes 13 open v4 items incl. conjugate-pair harmonic power, bare gamma3/N normalisation, perturbative q in the Kluver CSV, dynamic sqrt(3)k/2k ledger label, correct contoured-even gallery curve in Panel A, and GIF suptitle fixes; exact-operator harmonic switch moved to A_loc~0.22 and is documented. Self-test 41/41 PASS.",
            "reported_in_source: Model and findings as reported in the source publication cited in the flagship script header and datasets/ reference files.",
            "transfer_boundary: Reconstruction is evaluated only within the claim boundary stated in the summary; no transfer beyond the source system is claimed." ;
        pk:hypothesisType "Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking Neural-Field Bifurcation & Log-Polar Retino-Cortical Geometry" ;
        pk:weightOfEvidence 7.84e-01 .

    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Brodland (2002) / Krieg et al. (2008) / Maître et al. (2012) Differential Interfacial Tension Hypothesis (DITH) and zebrafish germ-layer cortical tension sorting, with time-dependent Nodal/TGF-beta coupling (Pass 3) (Danio rerio (zebrafish shield-stage gastrula germ-layer progenitors: ectoderm, mesoderm, endoderm))" ;
        dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-3>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-4>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-5>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-6> ;
        schema:about "Danio rerio (zebrafish shield-stage gastrula germ-layer progenitors: ectoderm, mesoderm, endoderm)" ;
        schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Does not model sub-second single-molecule E-cadherin bond rupture kinetics, whole-embryo epiboly yolk-syncytial-layer microtubule pulling, 2D/3D Nodal-Lefty reaction-diffusion, or quantitative pSmad2 gradient fits.",
            "reconstructed_in_script: 2D deformable DITH cell sorting across all 4 perturbation regimes (wild-type engulfment, caMLCK cortex reversal, Blebbistatin Myosin-II inhibition, and high-HIT mushroom doublet) plus simultaneous 3-germ-layer concentric stratification (r_E = 0.870 > r_M = 0.663 > r_N = 0.446), a 7-point continuous beta_E sweep across the sorting inversion threshold beta_E = beta_M = 95 pN/um, and the Young-Dupré doublet contact curve.",
            "reconstructed_in_script: Computer-vision segmentation of a zebrafish blastoderm transplantation GFP/RFP micrograph (`germ_layer_doublet_specimen.jpg`) across both layered engulfment (Row B, radial profile r = 0.9301, RMSE = 0.1844) and the protruding mushroom doublet (Row C, empirical r_c/R = 0.9717).",
            "reconstructed_in_script: Pass 3: a reduced time-dependent Nodal/TGF-beta coupling — 1D marginal Nodal field C(x,t) with range lambda = 3 tiers and rise time tau_N = 0.6 h from 4.0 hpf, two-threshold Hill dose -> cortical tension target (beta_E/beta_M/beta_N = 50/95/130 pN/um), first-order cortex relaxation tau_beta = 0.5 h, and a continuous-cortex DITH closure gamma_ij = (2/3)|beta_i - beta_j| re-evaluated every MCS inside the lattice sorter; the model reproduces 5 mesendoderm / 2 endoderm tiers at shield stage, establishes the Krieg hierarchy by 4.87 hpf, reaches Delta_r = +0.350 at 7 hpf, and gives Delta_r = 0 with no mesendoderm in the Nodal-null (C0 = 0) control; 5-point C0 dose sweep.",
            "reported_in_source: Brodland (2002) J. Biomech. Eng. Eqs. 1-4: Differential Interfacial Tension Hypothesis (DITH) decomposing cell-cell interfacial tension into actomyosin cortical tension minus cadherin adhesion (gamma_{alpha,beta} = beta_alpha + beta_beta - omega_{alpha,beta}).",
            "reported_in_source: Chen & Schier (2001), Dubrulle et al. (2015), van Boxtel et al. (2015), Hagos & Dougan (2007): Nodal (Squint/Cyclops) acts as a graded marginal morphogen whose signalling domain is set by a temporal window between sphere and shield stage and whose dose specifies mesoderm vs endoderm; Gritsman et al. (1999): MZoep embryos lack all mesendoderm.",
            "reported_in_source: Krieg et al. (2008) Nature Cell Biology Figs. 1-4: AFM cortical tension hierarchy across zebrafish shield-stage germ-layer progenitors (beta_ectoderm ~ 50 < beta_mesoderm ~ 95 < beta_endoderm ~ 130 pN/um) obtained by lefty1 / cyclops / cyclops+casanova mRNA injection, concentric 3-germ-layer sorting, Blebbistatin Myosin-II inhibition arrest, and caMLCK ectodermal cortical stiffening sorting reversal.",
            "reported_in_source: Maître et al. (2012) Science Eq. 1: Young-Dupré cell-doublet contact angle cos(theta) = 1 - gamma_cc/(2*gamma_cm) and normalized contact radius r_c/R = sin(theta).",
            "transfer_boundary: 2D lattice DITH representation of 3D zebrafish germ-layer progenitor reaggregates and blastoderm transplants; the circular 60-cell disc with medium all round is a reaggregate, not an embryo, so 'internalization' is sorting toward the disc centre.",
            "transfer_boundary: The Nodal coupling is 1D in tier distance from the margin, each cell's Nodal exposure is frozen to its tier of origin (specification memory), there is no epiboly / YSL motion and no Lefty feedback; lambda, K_M, K_N, tau_N and tau_beta were chosen to reproduce recalled literature anchors (~5 mesendoderm tiers, endoderm from tiers 1-2), not fitted to a digitised pSmad2 profile.",
            "transfer_boundary: The vendored specimen is a Wikimedia whole-blastoderm / yolk-cell transplant micrograph, not a Krieg et al. (2008) progenitor aggregate or a shield-stage internalization image; it is a proxy for layered GFP/RFP sorting, and no specimen underlies the Nodal row of the figure." ;
        pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1002/aja.1002030302>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0092-8674(00)80720-5>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.devcel.2015.09.014>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/35079121>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/ncb1705>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-017-00146-x>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0704252104>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1115/1.1449491>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1225399>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1186/1471-213X-7-22>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.126.4.827>,
            <https://doi.org/10.7554/eLife.05042> ;
        pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-audit-v3-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-audit-v3-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-10>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-audit-v3-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-11>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-audit-v3-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-12>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-audit-v3-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-13>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-audit-v3-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-audit-v3-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-3>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-audit-v3-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-4>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-audit-v3-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-5>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-audit-v3-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-6>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-audit-v3-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-7>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-audit-v3-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-8>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-audit-v3-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-9> ;
        pk:hypothesisType "Differential Interfacial Tension Hypothesis (DITH) & Young-Dupré Cell-Doublet Mechanics" ;
        pk:weightOfEvidence 8.92e-01 .

    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Cartwright & Checa (2007) & Cartwright et al. (2009) nacre screw-dislocation spirals, Frank-Read target terraces, defect pair annihilation, chitin-membrane perforation bridges and aragonite twin polygonization (Pteria hirundo & Pinctada margaritifera (Bivalvia sheet nacre) / Haliotis rufescens & Gibbula umbilicalis (Gastropoda tower nacre))" ;
        dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-3>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-4>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-5>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-6> ;
        schema:about "Pteria hirundo & Pinctada margaritifera (Bivalvia sheet nacre) / Haliotis rufescens & Gibbula umbilicalis (Gastropoda tower nacre)" ;
        schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: A volumetric 3D phase-field of the chitin membrane, resolution of individual mineral bridges, a derived (not templated) gastropod tower lattice, a time-dependent eikonal or BCF step-flow simulation, literature-digitised species pitch/omega observations, an independently calibrated SEM scale, or validated values of e_6, S_0, beta or the pore statistics",
            "reconstructed_in_script: Closed-form Cabrera-Levine phase fields for single screw, supercritical/subcritical Frank-Read dipoles and same-chirality pairs on a 2D grid with contour winding integrals, an optional direction-dependent step speed A(theta) with single-domain or {110} cyclic-twin averaging, a closed-terrace-ring Fourier polygonization measurement, a stacked-sheet driven Allen-Cahn perforation model whose per-sheet footprint is slaved to the terrace tier and whose bridge site is the early-phi argmax, a sigma / D_tab bridge-localisation sweep, a 12-species BCF pitch/omega regression, a DoG lamellar-seam segmentation of one SEM micrograph, and 7 Lean 4 theorems on the integer/rational skeleton of these laws",
            "reported_in_source: Burton, Cabrera & Frank (1951): Gibbs-Thomson curved-step velocity v(r) = v_inf (1 - r_c / r) and the rotating Archimedean spiral with pitch lambda_0 = (2 pi / omega_0) r_c ~ 19 r_c",
            "reported_in_source: Cartwright & Checa (2007): nacre grows by Burton-Cabrera-Frank screw-dislocation spiral and target terraces on the mineral surface, with a periodic stack of beta-chitin inter-lamellar membranes (h_0 ~ 0.5 um) whose pores admit mineral bridges that nucleate the next tablet (Sec. 4); columnar (gastropod) nacre stacks tablets vertically, sheet (bivalve) nacre staggers them like bricks",
            "reported_in_source: Cartwright et al. (2009): spiral and target patterns in bivalve nacre arise from screw dislocations and Frank-Read-type dislocation pairs; opposite-chirality pairs separated by more than 2 r_c emit closed target terraces",
            "reported_in_source: Checa, Cartwright & Willinger (2011) and Schäffer et al. (1997): mineral bridges (tens of nm) pass through pores of the inter-lamellar membrane and connect vertically stacked tablets",
            "reported_in_source: De Villiers (1971): orthorhombic aragonite lattice constants a = 4.9611, b = 7.9672, c = 5.7407 A",
            "transfer_boundary: The 'eikonal solver' is kinematic: terrace phases are closed-form Cabrera-Levine travel functions divided by A(theta), not a time-stepped front-propagation PDE, and the subcritical vs supercritical dipole regime is selected by an `if` on d <= 2 r_c rather than emerging from the dynamics",
            "transfer_boundary: The 12-species lambda_obs / omega_obs table is within ~1 % of the BCF law for every species and is not traceable to a measured table in the cited papers; r = 0.9999 therefore tests the table's construction, not the biology",
            "transfer_boundary: The SEM um/px calibration (0.019867 um/px) was anchored to h_0 = 0.50 um because the Wikimedia micrograph has no scale bar; only the dimensionless CV and aspect ratio are calibration-independent",
            "transfer_boundary: The membrane model is a stack of 2D sheets (no through-thickness phi(z)) at dx = 0.1875 um, so a perforation patch stands for a cluster of 40-60 nm bridges; the bridge site is the argmax of early phi, not a resolved growth-through-pore process; S_0, beta, eps, pore amplitude/width/density are model parameters tuned so that both regimes perforate on the grid",
            "transfer_boundary: e_6 = 0.15 is a free kinetic anisotropy amplitude; twin averaging is a mean-field superposition of A(theta) with no explicit twin boundaries in the spiral core" ;
        pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jsb.2011.09.011>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1021/cm960429i>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0900867106>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1098/rsif.2006.0188>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1098/rsta.1951.0006>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1098/rsta.2011.0600> ;
        pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-audit-v3-cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-audit-v3-cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-10>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-audit-v3-cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-11>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-audit-v3-cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-12>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-audit-v3-cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-13>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-audit-v3-cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-14>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-audit-v3-cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-15>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-audit-v3-cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-audit-v3-cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-3>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-audit-v3-cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-4>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-audit-v3-cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-5>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-audit-v3-cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-6>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-audit-v3-cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-7>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-audit-v3-cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-8>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-audit-v3-cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-9> ;
        pk:hypothesisType "Burton-Cabrera-Frank (BCF) Screw-Dislocation Eikonal Step-Flow & Chiral Defect Pair Dynamics" ;
        pk:weightOfEvidence 8.52e-01 .

    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Chirat, Moulton & Goriely (2013) & Erlich et al. (2016) mollusc shell marginal buckling, hollow-spine closure and predator damage / mantle repair (Pecten jacobaeus (Mediterranean scallop / Bivalvia, Ammonitida & Brachiopoda); Murex hollow spines (Gastropoda))" ;
        dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-3>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-4>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-5> ;
        schema:about "Pecten jacobaeus (Mediterranean scallop / Bivalvia, Ammonitida & Brachiopoda); Murex hollow spines (Gastropoda)" ;
        schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: A 3D finite-strain morphoelastic shell finite-element solution (Rudraraju et al. 2019), emergent spine base width or wall thickness, measured repair-callus mechanics, free-edge (non-periodic) margin boundary conditions, or an independent empirical closure strain for Murex spines",
            "reconstructed_in_script: Spectral L-BFGS-B minimisation of the fourth-order nonlinear Winkler-beam energy on a periodic margin (Pass 2), now with heterogeneous foundation k(s) and template-memory warm start; pitchfork amplitude law and subcritical control; 3D accretionary valve synthesis across 4 regimes; 12-species quarter-power regression; Pecten specimen costae segmentation; (Pass 3) planar inextensible elastica cross-section of a hollow spine fold with self-contact penalty, continuation in growth excess eps, and stacking into a tube surface; (Pass 3) 14-station damage/repair accretionary trajectory, scar index, healing-length fit, registry error, 5 x 4 chip-size x callus-stiffness outcome phase diagram",
            "reported_in_source: Chirat, Moulton & Goriely (2013): the mantle margin is an elastic beam on the Winkler foundation of the calcified shell edge; compressive growth thrust P above P_c = 2 sqrt(EI k) buckles it at lambda_c = 2 pi (EI/k)^(1/4), and hollow spines form where the buckled fold grows faster than its base",
            "reported_in_source: Erlich et al. (2016): isometric vs rib-intercalating antimarginal ornamentation follows from whether lambda_c scales with the margin length (constant N) or stays fixed (N grows)",
            "reported_in_source: Rudraraju et al. (2019): a 3D finite-strain morphoelastic shell FEM with surface and volume growth reproduces spine formation and closure",
            "reported_in_source: Vermeij (1987): durophagous predators chip shell margins; molluscs repair the break and leave repair scars",
            "transfer_boundary: EI = 1.085 mN mm^2 for Pecten is the value that makes lambda_c = 8.7766 mm give exactly 14 ribs over L = 122.87 mm; the vendored JSON default_parameters.EI_mN_mm2 is 0.18 and the Adult_V ontogenetic stage is 1.79, so the wild-type calibration is self-referential",
            "transfer_boundary: The hollow-spine closure model is a 2D cross-section elastica with prescribed base width W = 6 mm and wall thickness t = 0.35 mm; there is no out-of-plane coupling between cross-sections, no shell stretching energy and no growth tensor, so eps_close = 4.81 is a reduced-model number and its reference value (5.00) is mesh convergence of the same model, not a Murex measurement",
            "transfer_boundary: The repair callus stiffness ratio rho = 1.15 and decay length l_heal = 7 mm are prescribed, not measured; the critical chip arc 1.97 lambda is compared with a half-integer rounding heuristic (1.5 lambda), not a published repair-scar statistic" ;
        pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2012.07.009>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1220443110>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1098/rsif.2016.0592>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1007213> ;
        pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-audit-v3-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-audit-v3-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-10>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-audit-v3-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-11>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-audit-v3-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-12>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-audit-v3-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-13>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-audit-v3-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-14>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-audit-v3-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-15>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-audit-v3-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-16>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-audit-v3-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-audit-v3-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-3>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-audit-v3-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-4>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-audit-v3-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-5>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-audit-v3-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-6>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-audit-v3-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-7>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-audit-v3-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-8>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-audit-v3-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-9> ;
        pk:hypothesisType "Fourth-Order Nonlinear Winkler-Beam Elastic Mantle Buckling & Accretionary Shell Kinematics" ;
        pk:weightOfEvidence 8.7e-01 .

    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-conus-textile-rule30> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Wolfram (1984) Rule 30 & Meinhardt-Klingler Conus textile pigmentation (Conus textile)" ;
        schema:about "Conus textile" ;
        schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Does not yet claim: Autonomous Meinhardt parameterisation without stochastic injection/clipping (structural)",
            "reconstructed_in_script: Rule 30 CA + Meinhardt PDE + Raup shell mapping vs segmented specimen. Pass N+1: percentile (5-95) kymograph normalization fixes the blank cream Meinhardt 3D shell; Raup T scaled by S with default recalibrated to 0.06 (H/W 1.8342 vs specimen 1.8330, IoU 0.835 preserved, T now monotonic for T>~0.19); stochastic activator injection (p=0.18,+0.90) disclosed in the docstring as a stabiliser, not published PDE; Panel F annotates the discriminating 2D ANF carry rates; --no-photos wired.",
            "reported_in_source: Model and findings as reported in the source publication cited in the flagship script header and datasets/ reference files.",
            "transfer_boundary: Reconstruction is evaluated only within the claim boundary stated in the summary; no transfer beyond the source system is claimed." ;
        pk:hypothesisType "Mathematical Morphogenesis Model" ;
        pk:weightOfEvidence 7.29e-01 .

    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Dubrulle & Pourquié (2001, 2004) FGF8 mRNA decay wavefront and determination front positioning in vertebrate somitogenesis, with Goldbeter (2007) RA/FGF8 bistable switch and 2D cell-based PSM strip (Gallus gallus (chick embryo presomitic mesoderm & paraxial somites))" ;
        dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-3>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-4>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-5> ;
        schema:about "Gallus gallus (chick embryo presomitic mesoderm & paraxial somites)" ;
        schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Reproduction of the Goldbeter et al. (2007) parameter table or bifurcation figures; 3D somite epithelialization mechanics; a derivation of the FGF8-bead / SU5402 / electroporation somite-size shifts from the switch dynamics (they remain constants in the lab-frame simulator and the reference JSON)",
            "reconstructed_in_script: 2D cell-based strip with explicit progenitor division and mRNA partitioning: exported level 0.994 vs closed form 1.000, gradient length 370.5 vs 360.7 um, front 698.8 +/- 7.0 um vs lambda_m ln(m_exit/m_crit) = 694.4 um, S_2D = 148.2 um, dilution shift 276-286 um vs closed form 271 um",
            "reconstructed_in_script: Bilateral dorsal somite row DoG peak and inter-somitic cleft segmentation on chick_somite_psm_specimen.jpg (48.47 px mean spacing, symmetry ratio 0.9606)",
            "reconstructed_in_script: Characteristic-upwind 1D advection-decay PDE solver dm/dt + v_g dm/dx = -k_d m (L2 relative error 0.0009 vs analytical exponential)",
            "reconstructed_in_script: Goldbeter-type 3-variable RA/FGF8/Cyp26 switch coupled to the mRNA gradient: saddle-nodes m_SN_lo = 0.184 / m_SN_hi = 0.546, hysteretic cell-trajectory front x_sw = 720.4 um, transition width 198 um vs 792 um, reverse switch at m = 0.675",
            "reconstructed_in_script: Lab-frame FGF8 wavefront-gated somite boundary simulator across wild-type, ectopic FGF8 bead (S_ant = 97.5 um, S_post = 202.5 um), SU5402 (S = 215.0 um) and k_d = 0 ablation control (N = 0 somites) - with the perturbation shifts entered as constants, not derived",
            "reported_in_source: Dubrulle & Pourquie (2004) Nature 427:419-422 cell-autonomous fgf8 mRNA decay gradient m(x) = m_0 exp(-k_d x / v_g) generated by tailbud-restricted transcription and axis elongation",
            "reported_in_source: Dubrulle, McGrew & Pourquie (2001) Cell 106:219-232 determination front threshold positioning x* = (v_g/k_d) ln(m_0/m_crit) and ectopic FGF8 bead / SU5402 somite size perturbations",
            "reported_in_source: Goldbeter, Gonze & Pourquie (2007) Dev. Dyn. 236:1495-1508 bistability of the RA -| FGF -> Cyp26 -| RA double-negative loop defining a sharp determination threshold",
            "transfer_boundary: 1D anteroposterior chick presomitic mesoderm axis mapped to dorsal vertebrate SEM somite rows of a Wikimedia specimen whose species is labelled avian/vertebrate, not confirmed as Gallus gallus",
            "transfer_boundary: 2D strip: PSM cells do not divide, all elongation comes from progenitor division (no Benazeraf 2010 motility gradient), rows are coupled only through FGF8 smoothing (no mechanics)",
            "transfer_boundary: Goldbeter switch functional forms follow the 2007 paper but the dimensionless parameter values (K_A = 0.18, K_I = 0.6, k_C = 2, n = 4, tau_sw = 10 min) are this script's bistable-regime choice; the switch is evaluated along a 1D cell trajectory and is NOT embedded in the 2D strip" ;
        pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1002/dvdy.21193>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0092-8674(01)00437-8>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ydbio.2006.01.018>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature02332>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature09151> ;
        pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-audit-v3-dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-audit-v3-dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-10>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-audit-v3-dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-audit-v3-dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-3>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-audit-v3-dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-4>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-audit-v3-dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-5>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-audit-v3-dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-6>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-audit-v3-dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-7>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-audit-v3-dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-8>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-audit-v3-dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-9> ;
        pk:hypothesisType "Advection-Reaction mRNA Decay Wavefront & Threshold Phase-Gating (Somitogenesis)" ;
        pk:weightOfEvidence 8.62e-01 .

    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Goriely & Tabor (1998) PRL / Gerbode et al. (2012) Science Kirchhoff elastic rod tendril perversion, G-fiber overwinding & Pass 3 thigmotropic contact coiling (Climbing plant tendrils (Cucumis sativus, Passiflora caerulea, Bryonia dioica, Echinocystis lobata))" ;
        dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-3>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-4>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-5> ;
        schema:about "Climbing plant tendrils (Cucumis sativus, Passiflora caerulea, Bryonia dioica, Echinocystis lobata)" ;
        schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Circumnutation or support-search before first touch, a measured tendril-on-wood friction coefficient, compliant or rough or finite-length supports, G-fiber lignification time course, or a validated time-to-wrap (tau_thigmo and v_signal were chosen inside Darwin's 5-60 min window and the model's 4.75 min falls slightly below it)",
            "reconstructed_in_script: Pass 3: 61-node inertia-free discrete rod with contact-gated intrinsic curvature pointing toward the support axis, implicit backward-Euler incremental potential (L-BFGS-B), rigid-cylinder penalty contact, penalty self-contact, lagged-normal Coulomb friction on support and self-contact, quasi-static grip test vs mu*sum(N) and exp(mu Theta); no-support, frictionless, friction-sweep, support-radius-sweep and stacked-turns scenarios",
            "reconstructed_in_script: Timoshenko bilayer kappa_0, exact T_c, 161-node L-BFGS-B Kirchhoff perversion solver with zero-link enforcement and negative controls; 10-point pitchfork sweep; soft vs lignified overwinding; 4-species scaling; DoG segmentation of the SHA-256-locked Passiflora caerulea specimen (Pass 2)",
            "reported_in_source: Darwin (1865) Ch. IV: tendrils curve toward a touched side within tens of seconds, complete a wrap around a thin stick within minutes to about an hour, and grasp thin supports more readily than thick ones (qualitative)",
            "reported_in_source: Gerbode et al. (2012): the cucumber tendril's G-fiber ribbon sets the intrinsic curvature; soft tendrils (Gamma < 1) overwind under axial stretch while lignified ones unwind; coil radius and pitch scale across species",
            "reported_in_source: Goriely & Tabor (1998) / McMillen & Goriely (2002): an intrinsically curved Kirchhoff rod with both ends held undergoes a supercritical pitchfork bifurcation below T_c = B kappa_0^2 / (1 + Gamma) into two opposite-handed helices joined by a perversion, with zero net link",
            "reported_in_source: Jaffe & Galston (1968): thigmotropic coiling is a contact-triggered, propagating growth response; Euler (1762): the capstan law exp(mu Theta) for a flexible line on a cylinder",
            "transfer_boundary: Friction uses normal forces lagged one macro step; F_hold / mu*sum(N) = 0.67 is a consistency check of the scheme, not an experiment; N_wrap counts loose loops that enclose but do not touch the support (contact fraction 33 % of nodes)",
            "transfer_boundary: The contact solver is a separate bending-only rod: it has no material-frame twist, so Gamma = C/B plays no role in contact coiling and the perversion (zero-link) physics of section 3 is not coupled to it",
            "transfer_boundary: mu_support, mu_self, kappa_contact, tau_thigmo, v_signal, the 55 deg approach angle and the initial placement touching the support at 25 % of L are provenance-tagged assumptions; the only empirical anchors for Pass 3 are Darwin's qualitative timings and support-size statements" ;
        pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1007/s00332-002-0493-1>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.80.1564>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1095-8339.1865.tb00011.x>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1223304>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1146/annurev.pp.19.060168.002221>,
            <https://doi.org/10.3732/ajb.0900045> ;
        pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-audit-v3-goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-audit-v3-goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-10>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-audit-v3-goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-11>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-audit-v3-goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-12>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-audit-v3-goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-13>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-audit-v3-goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-14>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-audit-v3-goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-15>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-audit-v3-goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-audit-v3-goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-3>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-audit-v3-goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-4>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-audit-v3-goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-5>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-audit-v3-goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-6>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-audit-v3-goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-7>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-audit-v3-goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-8>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-audit-v3-goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-9> ;
        pk:hypothesisType "Kirchhoff Elastic Rod Hamiltonian Mechanics, Zero-Link Topological Conservation (ΔLk = 0), Pitchfork Bifurcation, G-Fiber Overwinding & Contact-Gated Thigmotropic Coiling with Coulomb Friction" ;
        pk:weightOfEvidence 9.17e-01 .

    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Graner & Glazier (1992) / Glazier & Graner (1993) extended large-Q Cellular Potts Model cell sorting + Ouchi et al. (2003) cortical tension (Hydra attenuata (endoderm/ectoderm reaggregates) & Gallus gallus embryonic cell spheroids)" ;
        dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-3>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-4>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-5>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-6> ;
        schema:about "Hydra attenuata (endoderm/ectoderm reaggregates) & Gallus gallus embryonic cell spheroids" ;
        schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Does not model subcellular cytoskeletal actin-myosin turnover, active chemotactic signaling, cell growth/division, or 3D aggregates; does not reproduce Glazier & Graner (1993) quantitative boundary-length curves at the paper's cell size (V_t ~ 40) or run length (10^4 MCS).",
            "reconstructed_in_script: 2D extended large-Q Cellular Potts Model (60 x 60 lattice, 60 cells of V_t = 16) across all 4 canonical phase regimes plus T=0 pinning and equal-adhesion negative controls, a 7-point continuous J_LD sweep, and a 6-point fluctuation temperature sweep (all at lambda_P = 0).",
            "reconstructed_in_script: Computer-vision segmentation of a confocal fluorescence embryonic cell aggregate (`embryonic_cell_aggregate_specimen.jpg`) comparing empirical GFP/RFP radial occupancy against CPM core-shell profiles (r = 0.961, RMSE = 0.154).",
            "reconstructed_in_script: Ouchi et al. (2003) perimeter / cortical tension term with incremental 8-neighbour bond-count bookkeeping (max drift 0 after 150 MCS), a cortical-tension sorting regime (lambda_P = 2, P_t = 44), a 6-point lambda_P ablation sweep at T = 10 and T = 80, and a 5-point P_t sweep (32-56) with realised-perimeter tracking r = 0.9999.",
            "reported_in_source: Glazier & Graner (1993) PRE Table I & Section III.B: classification of 4 equilibrium phase regimes (complete engulfment, partial sorting lens, checkerboard mixing, and cell dissociation) and fluctuation temperature controls (T=0 lattice pinning arrest vs optimal thermal sorting vs high-T thermal melting).",
            "reported_in_source: Graner & Glazier (1992) PRL Eqs. 1-3 & Fig. 3: extended large-Q Cellular Potts Model Hamiltonian with bond-energy surface tensions gamma_LD = J_LD - (J_LL + J_DD)/2 and gamma_alphaM = J_alphaM - J_alphaalpha/2 driving logarithmic heterotypic boundary decay L_het(t) ~ A - B ln(t).",
            "reported_in_source: Ouchi et al. (2003) Physica A Eq. 2: a perimeter (cortical tension) elasticity term lambda_P (p_sigma - P_t)^2 added to the CPM Hamiltonian suppresses ragged, fragmented cell boundaries; Farhadifar et al. (2007) Eq. 1 is the vertex-model analogue.",
            "transfer_boundary: 2D lattice Cellular Potts representation of 3D multicellular spheroid cross-sections; the specimen is an embryoid-body spheroid, not a Hydra reaggregate, and its core/shell labels are assigned by fluorescence channel, not by cell type.",
            "transfer_boundary: Cells equilibrate at ~76 % of V_t under lambda = 1.2 and a hard v >= 6 floor; the PRL Fig. 3 comparison uses 0-150 MCS checkpoints whose digitisation from the 10^4-MCS figure is not documented.",
            "transfer_boundary: Sorting dynamics include a whole-cell identity-swap move (8 attempts/MCS, Metropolis at 2.5 T) that is not part of the Graner-Glazier single-site copy formalism; the 'partial sorting lens' regime adds an uncited lateral bias field inside that move. Both are disclosed here, not in the script." ;
        pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0378-4371(03)00574-0>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cub.2007.11.049>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/newbio239098a0>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevE.47.2128>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.69.2013>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.141.3579.401>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.122.5.1611> ;
        pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-audit-v3-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-audit-v3-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-10>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-audit-v3-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-11>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-audit-v3-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-12>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-audit-v3-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-13>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-audit-v3-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-14>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-audit-v3-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-15>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-audit-v3-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-audit-v3-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-3>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-audit-v3-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-4>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-audit-v3-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-5>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-audit-v3-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-6>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-audit-v3-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-7>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-audit-v3-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-8>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-audit-v3-graner-cellular-potts-cell-sorting-9> ;
        pk:hypothesisType "Glazier-Graner-Hogeweg Extended Large-Q Cellular Potts Model (CPM)" ;
        pk:weightOfEvidence 8.45e-01 .

    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-kahng-coral-geometry> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Kahng et al. (2024) coral colony geometry & growth (Leptoseris / Agariciid corals)" ;
        schema:about "Leptoseris / Agariciid corals" ;
        schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Does not yet claim: Empirical specimen dataset / CSV export (none vendored at present)",
            "reconstructed_in_script: Surface-area-to-planar (SAP) colony geometry model. Pass N+1: Panel (c) no longer plots a disc at common parameters reaching 26.14 cm/yr on a crushed axis - the Leptoseris disc sits on the main axis (1.67 cm/yr at 30 cm) with an equal-G twin axis and plateau labels corrected; GIF right panel plots S/S0 instead of absolute area reaching 1e12 cm^2; analytic --self-test added (5 checks).",
            "reported_in_source: Model and findings as reported in the source publication cited in the flagship script header and datasets/ reference files.",
            "transfer_boundary: Reconstruction is evaluated only within the claim boundary stated in the summary; no transfer beyond the source system is claimed." ;
        pk:hypothesisType "Mathematical Morphogenesis Model" ;
        pk:weightOfEvidence 6.05e-01 .

    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-kriegman-xenobot-evolutionary-biobots> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Kriegman et al. (2020, 2021) Xenobot evolutionary biomechanics & kinematic self-replication (Xenopus laevis (African clawed frog blastula ectoderm & cardiac progenitor biobots))" ;
        dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/kriegman-xenobot-evolutionary-biobots-1>,
