    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "@drmichaellevin 8-law mathematical synthesis & biological-law-criteria suite (None. This is a cross-law synthesis / aggregator module. No organism, tissue, specimen image, experimental dataset or published figure is loaded or compared; Law 7's data come from the repository's own S_6 sorting simulation)",
            "@drmichaellevin 8-law mathematical synthesis & biological-law-criteria suite faithfully reproduces None. This is a cross-law synthesis / aggregator module. No organism, tissue, specimen image, experimental dataset or published figure is loaded or compared; Law 7's data come from the repository's own S_6 sorting simulation morphology" ;
        dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/levin-youtube-channel-math-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/levin-youtube-channel-math-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/levin-youtube-channel-math-3>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/levin-youtube-channel-math-4>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/levin-youtube-channel-math-5>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/levin-youtube-channel-math-6>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/levin-youtube-channel-math-7>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/levin-youtube-channel-math-8> ;
        dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py, docs/levin_youtube_channel_math_synthesis.png, morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_levin_youtube_channel_math.lean, morphoeval/runs/levin_youtube_channel_math_summary.json implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real None. This is a cross-law synthesis / aggregator module. No organism, tissue, specimen image, experimental dataset or published figure is loaded or compared; Law 7's data come from the repository's own S_6 sorting simulation specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
        dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/docs/levin_youtube_channel_math_synthesis.png>,
            <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py>,
            <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_levin_youtube_channel_math.lean>,
            <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/morphoeval/runs/levin_youtube_channel_math_summary.json> ;
        schema:about "None. This is a cross-law synthesis / aggregator module. No organism, tissue, specimen image, experimental dataset or published figure is loaded or compared; Law 7's data come from the repository's own S_6 sorting simulation" ;
        schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: It does not score the 17 CHANNEL_CONCEPTS_INDEX items, which are correctly excluded from law status",
            "does_not_claim: It does not treat the builder's edits to the KG payload's referee-attributed measurement entries as falsified values (the two numbers written are ones this referee independently reaches); it treats them as a provenance violation",
            "does_not_claim: It does not verify the content of the 63 cited videos (no transcripts offline) and does not recompute the S_6 TPM behind quantifying_emergence_ce2_metrics.json; it re-checks only the arithmetic consistency of the imported numbers",
            "does_not_claim: This audit does not claim any of the 8 source equations is wrong as published, nor that any Lean theorem fails to check (all 8 compile with 0 sorry); it scores whether the suite implements, exercises and validates the laws and whether the O1/O2, T1-T4 and C1-C6 tags are earned by linked artefacts",
            "reconstructed_in_script: 8 Lean theorems (Loop L30-L288, unchanged since Pass 3), each on Nat/Int/Bool reductions of the law; Law 1's theorem formalises the Hill numerator, not the BVP the Python metric is now scored on",
            "reconstructed_in_script: Law 1 (L177-L233): N-cell linear diffusion-leak BVP -G (V_{i-1} - 2V_i + V_{i+1}) + (G_half/N) V_i = delta_{i0}; reach L = sum_i V_i / V_0 at G_gj in {0, 0.5, 1.0} and on a 51-point grid; continuum sqrt(1/k) tanh(N sqrt(k)); Hill form 1 + (N-1) G/(G + G_eff) fitted by curve_fit (G_eff 2.26, RMS 3.05) and reported",
            "reconstructed_in_script: Law 2 (L239-L285, unchanged since Pass 3): 20-cell ODE, cells 0-4 clamped at -10 mV, cubic bistable I_ion with roots -60 / -38 / -10 mV (not Cervera's channel currents), Bell-Boltzmann vs ohmic G_ij, RK45 to t = 80",
            "reconstructed_in_script: Law 3 (L291-L339): 1-D zero-flux BVP with central-difference / Pade(1,1) edge coefficients a_i = G(-1 + dv/2), b_{i+1} = G(1 + dv/2) on a linear voltage profile; grid refinement N_ap = 15..240 and a 5-value G_gj sweep at N_ap = 120",
            "reconstructed_in_script: Law 4 (L345-L412): 24-state CTMC, W(i->j) = r_i^gamma K_ij(alpha) with K(alpha) = (1 - alpha) K_sym + alpha K_trap, K_sym Sinkhorn-symmetrised doubly stochastic, K_trap row-normalised weights linspace(0.1, 2.5)^2.5 (column sums != 1); stationary vector from L^T p = 0; log-log fit of p against the fixed r_exit at alpha = 0, 0.5, 0.9",
            "reconstructed_in_script: Law 6 (L463-L548): 16-gene symmetric J, Hebbian J += eta s s^T for 15 epochs, energy trace, basin fraction over 120 four-flip trials; 3-node ODE dx_CS = -x_CS + I_CS, dx_M = -0.02 x_M + 0.25 sigma(12 (x_CS x_US - 0.5)), dx_US = -x_US + sigma(12 (I_US + 0.9 x_M x_CS - 0.55)) in four phases (CS test, paired training t = 25, washout t = 5, CS test t = 10); the docstring now states this ODE and its results",
            "reconstructed_in_script: Law 8 (L554-L588, unchanged): pi_C(k) = (1 - k^-1/2) b - c and pi_D(k) = b k^-1/2 over k = 1..36; exact m x m directed bond count for m = 1..6",
            "reconstructed_in_script: Laws 5 and 7 (L418-L457): 4-row x 3-gate truth table; S_6 CE2 numbers read from the hash-pinned sorting-morphogenesis JSON",
            "reported_in_source: Cervera, Levin & Mafe (2020): voltage-gated gap-junction coupling G_ij(V_i, V_j) = G_0 / [(1 + e^{(V_i - V_th)/V_0})(1 + e^{(V_j - V_th)/V_0})] with polarising and depolarising channel currents; depolarised domains electrically isolate",
            "reported_in_source: Chvykov et al. (2021): low-rattling principle P_ss ∝ exp(-gamma R) tested on smarticle collectives and simulation; the 'rattling' is a diffusion-tensor quantity, not a scalar exit rate, and the principle is stated for driving whose embedded jump process is unbiased",
            "reported_in_source: Hoel et al. (2013), Hoel (2026): causal emergence via effective information and the determinism/degeneracy decomposition CP = det - deg",
            "reported_in_source: Levin (2019, 2022): TAME cognitive light cone (diagrammatic); Bongard & Levin (2023): polycomputing (conceptual); Shreesha & Levin (2025): agent-based spatial Prisoner's Dilemma with controllable borders",
            "reported_in_source: Pietak & Levin (2016, 2017): Nernst-Planck electrodiffusion in BETSE; at zero flux the charged-morphogen ratio is Boltzmann, exp(-zF dV / RT), independent of gap-junction permeability (with production / decay the steady state is not zero-flux and the ratio does depend on permeability)",
            "reported_in_source: Watson & Szathmary (2016): natural induction / Hebbian deepening of visited attractors; Pigozzi, Goldstein & Levin (2025): associative conditioning in continuous GRN ODE models with measured conditioning success; Biswas et al. (2023): pathway-level memory in transcriptional network models",
            "transfer_boundary: Law 1's BVP reach is a cable-theory space constant (L ≈ sqrt(G/k), measured exponent 0.48 over the sweep); the Hill form fitted to it has its half-saturation (2.26) outside the sweep and a plateau at N the BVP never shows, so the Lean theorem (Hill numerator) and the Python metric (BVP) describe different functions of G_gj",
            "transfer_boundary: Law 3's grid-refinement convergence is a genuine numerical check of the discretisation against the Boltzmann closed form; the G_gj invariance is linear algebra (G_gj scales Q) and holds only in the zero-flux limit the law is restricted to",
            "transfer_boundary: Law 4's breakdown is a genuine property of the model (non-doubly-stochastic routing with fixed exit rates) and its magnitude (+0.1866) is now reported consistently; at alpha = 0 the slope -1 is the elementary CTMC result p ∝ 1/r for a uniform embedded chain",
            "transfer_boundary: Law 6's 3-node ODE is a hand-tuned minimal conditioning circuit, not a model from Pigozzi 2025 or Biswas 2023; it is now documented as what it is",
            "transfer_boundary: Law 8's k >= 17 strict-dominance threshold applies 1 - 1/sqrt(k) to non-square k that no m x m cluster realises; the docs and YAML now also state the first exact square k = 25, the Lean docstring (L274-L275) still says 'k >= 17 in general integer k' against a theorem quantified over the side length",
            "transfer_boundary: The 8 laws are evaluated on synthetic parameter sets chosen by the builder (cubic current coefficients, r_exit table, K_trap weights, J ~ N(0, 0.25), 3-node ODE gains, b = 2, c = 1); no quantity is compared with a value measured in Cervera 2020, Pietak 2016/2017, Chvykov 2021, Pigozzi 2025 or Shreesha 2025" ;
        pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/docs/levin_youtube_channel_math_synthesis.png, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_levin_youtube_channel_math.lean, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/morphoeval/runs/levin_youtube_channel_math_summary.json; output: media/levin_youtube_channel_math_synthesis.png; organism: None. This is a cross-law synthesis / aggregator module. No organism, tissue, specimen image, experimental dataset or published figure is loaded or compared; Law 7's data come from the repository's own S_6 sorting simulation; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, lean 4.35.0; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Cervera, Levin & Mafe (2020): voltage-gated gap-junction coupling G_ij(V_i, V_j) = G_0 / [(1 + e^{(V_i - V_th)/V_0})(1 + e^{(V_j - V_th)/V_0})] with polarising and depolarising channel currents; depolarised domains electrically isolate | Pietak & Levin (2016, 2017): Nernst-Planck electrodiffusion in BETSE; at zero flux the charged-morphogen ratio is Boltzmann, exp(-zF dV / RT), independent of gap-junction permeability (with production / decay the steady state is not zero-flux and the ratio does depend on permeability) | Chvykov et al. (2021): low-rattling principle P_ss ∝ exp(-gamma R) tested on smarticle collectives and simulation; the 'rattling' is a diffusion-tensor quantity, not a scalar exit rate, and the principle is stated for driving whose embedded jump process is unbiased | Watson & Szathmary (2016): natural induction / Hebbian deepening of visited attractors; Pigozzi, Goldstein & Levin (2025): associative conditioning in continuous GRN ODE models with measured conditioning success; Biswas et al. (2023): pathway-level memory in transcriptional network models | Hoel et al. (2013), Hoel (2026): causal emergence via effective information and the determinism/degeneracy decomposition CP = det - deg | Levin (2019, 2022): TAME cognitive light cone (diagrammatic); Bongard & Levin (2023): polycomputing (conceptual); Shreesha & Levin (2025): agent-based spatial Prisoner's Dilemma with controllable borders; reconstructed_in_script: Law 1 (L177-L233): N-cell linear diffusion-leak BVP -G (V_{i-1} - 2V_i + V_{i+1}) + (G_half/N) V_i = delta_{i0}; reach L = sum_i V_i / V_0 at G_gj in {0, 0.5, 1.0} and on a 51-point grid; continuum sqrt(1/k) tanh(N sqrt(k)); Hill form 1 + (N-1) G/(G + G_eff) fitted by curve_fit (G_eff 2.26, RMS 3.05) and reported | Law 2 (L239-L285, unchanged since Pass 3): 20-cell ODE, cells 0-4 clamped at -10 mV, cubic bistable I_ion with roots -60 / -38 / -10 mV (not Cervera's channel currents), Bell-Boltzmann vs ohmic G_ij, RK45 to t = 80 | Law 3 (L291-L339): 1-D zero-flux BVP with central-difference / Pade(1,1) edge coefficients a_i = G(-1 + dv/2), b_{i+1} = G(1 + dv/2) on a linear voltage profile; grid refinement N_ap = 15..240 and a 5-value G_gj sweep at N_ap = 120 | Law 4 (L345-L412): 24-state CTMC, W(i->j) = r_i^gamma K_ij(alpha) with K(alpha) = (1 - alpha) K_sym + alpha K_trap, K_sym Sinkhorn-symmetrised doubly stochastic, K_trap row-normalised weights linspace(0.1, 2.5)^2.5 (column sums != 1); stationary vector from L^T p = 0; log-log fit of p against the fixed r_exit at alpha = 0, 0.5, 0.9 | Laws 5 and 7 (L418-L457): 4-row x 3-gate truth table; S_6 CE2 numbers read from the hash-pinned sorting-morphogenesis JSON | Law 6 (L463-L548): 16-gene symmetric J, Hebbian J += eta s s^T for 15 epochs, energy trace, basin fraction over 120 four-flip trials; 3-node ODE dx_CS = -x_CS + I_CS, dx_M = -0.02 x_M + 0.25 sigma(12 (x_CS x_US - 0.5)), dx_US = -x_US + sigma(12 (I_US + 0.9 x_M x_CS - 0.55)) in four phases (CS test, paired training t = 25, washout t = 5, CS test t = 10); the docstring now states this ODE and its results | Law 8 (L554-L588, unchanged): pi_C(k) = (1 - k^-1/2) b - c and pi_D(k) = b k^-1/2 over k = 1..36; exact m x m directed bond count for m = 1..6 | 8 Lean theorems (Loop L30-L288, unchanged since Pass 3), each on Nat/Int/Bool reductions of the law; Law 1's theorem formalises the Hill numerator, not the BVP the Python metric is now scored on; transfer_boundary: The 8 laws are evaluated on synthetic parameter sets chosen by the builder (cubic current coefficients, r_exit table, K_trap weights, J ~ N(0, 0.25), 3-node ODE gains, b = 2, c = 1); no quantity is compared with a value measured in Cervera 2020, Pietak 2016/2017, Chvykov 2021, Pigozzi 2025 or Shreesha 2025 | Law 1's BVP reach is a cable-theory space constant (L ≈ sqrt(G/k), measured exponent 0.48 over the sweep); the Hill form fitted to it has its half-saturation (2.26) outside the sweep and a plateau at N the BVP never shows, so the Lean theorem (Hill numerator) and the Python metric (BVP) describe different functions of G_gj | Law 4's breakdown is a genuine property of the model (non-doubly-stochastic routing with fixed exit rates) and its magnitude (+0.1866) is now reported consistently; at alpha = 0 the slope -1 is the elementary CTMC result p ∝ 1/r for a uniform embedded chain | Law 3's grid-refinement convergence is a genuine numerical check of the discretisation against the Boltzmann closed form; the G_gj invariance is linear algebra (G_gj scales Q) and holds only in the zero-flux limit the law is restricted to | Law 6's 3-node ODE is a hand-tuned minimal conditioning circuit, not a model from Pigozzi 2025 or Biswas 2023; it is now documented as what it is | Law 8's k >= 17 strict-dominance threshold applies 1 - 1/sqrt(k) to non-square k that no m x m cluster realises; the docs and YAML now also state the first exact square k = 25, the Lean docstring (L274-L275) still says 'k >= 17 in general integer k' against a theorem quantified over the side length; does_not_claim: This audit does not claim any of the 8 source equations is wrong as published, nor that any Lean theorem fails to check (all 8 compile with 0 sorry); it scores whether the suite implements, exercises and validates the laws and whether the O1/O2, T1-T4 and C1-C6 tags are earned by linked artefacts | It does not verify the content of the 63 cited videos (no transcripts offline) and does not recompute the S_6 TPM behind quantifying_emergence_ce2_metrics.json; it re-checks only the arithmetic consistency of the imported numbers | It does not score the 17 CHANNEL_CONCEPTS_INDEX items, which are correctly excluded from law status | It does not treat the builder's edits to the KG payload's referee-attributed measurement entries as falsified values (the two numbers written are ones this referee independently reaches); it treats them as a provenance violation]; other sources: Extended Iterated, Spatialized Prisoner's Dilemma: Game Theory of Multicellularity with Agent-Controlled Borders <https://osf.io/kpzju_v2>, sorting-morphogenesis/figures/quantifying_emergence_ce2_metrics.json - S_n sorting Causal Emergence 2.0 metrics (n = 3..6) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib>, datasets/levin_youtube_channel/levin_youtube_catalog.json - 374-video metadata index of @drmichaellevin <https://www.youtube.com/@drmichaellevin>" ;
        pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.patter.2025.101472>,
