    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-lobo-planform-morphology> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Lobo et al. (2013) PlanformDB planarian morphology database (Schmidtea mediterranea (PlanformDB 2.5.0))" ;
        schema:about "Schmidtea mediterranea (PlanformDB 2.5.0)" ;
        schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Does not yet claim: Quantitative regeneration-outcome validation against PlanformDB phenotypes",
            "reconstructed_in_script: PlanformDB morphology decoding and AP/ML geometry. Pass N+1 adds a --self-test (canonical fixture decode, WT AP 557.6 x ML 119.8, aspect 4.65, two-headed phenotype count, optional DB fingerprint). Media GIF provenance corrected: it is made by morphoeval/upgrade_planarian_assets.py (17 frames), not this script.",
            "reported_in_source: Model and findings as reported in the source publication cited in the flagship script header and datasets/ reference files.",
            "transfer_boundary: Reconstruction is evaluated only within the claim boundary stated in the summary; no transfer beyond the source system is claimed." ;
        pk:hypothesisType "Mathematical Morphogenesis Model" ;
        pk:weightOfEvidence 7.77e-01 .

    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-murray-bos-taurus-turing-wavelength> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Turing RD claim for Holstein coat spotting (tested negative hypothesis) (Bos taurus (Holstein-Friesian, 10 specimens))",
            "Turing RD claim for Holstein coat spotting (tested negative hypothesis) faithfully reproduces Bos taurus (Holstein-Friesian, 10 specimens) morphology" ;
        dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/1981-murray-bos-taurus-turing-wavelength.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Bos taurus (Holstein-Friesian, 10 specimens) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
        dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/1981-murray-bos-taurus-turing-wavelength.py> ;
        schema:about "Bos taurus (Holstein-Friesian, 10 specimens)" ;
        schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Does NOT claim all reaction-diffusion models are excluded: a growing-domain RD is statistically indistinguishable from colonisation on these statistics, so adult coat morphology alone cannot identify the mechanism either way.",
            "does_not_claim: Does NOT claim independent confirmation of the Pass 8+ verdict: the Pass 9 assessment is builder-scored (independent re-score is remediation R11), held-out n = 9 specimens limits power, and coat segmentation is a saturation heuristic.",
            "does_not_claim: Does NOT claim the Eden control is the true mechanism; it is a minimal colonisation proxy, and its founder density was selected on specimen 01 (disclosed).",
            "does_not_claim: Does NOT claim the Murray/Turing hypothesis is supported -- the tested claim is reported as a negative result, and the rubric overall (74.6) scores the simulation package, not the hypothesis.",
            "reconstructed_in_script: Published result is negative: static Turing rejected (6.46 vs ~3.3); growing RD vs colonisation indistinguishable (3.29 vs 3.43, p = 0.91). Two blinded independent assessments (54.4, 57.7) overturned two earlier builder conclusions (Passes 4, 7-8) before this verdict was reached.",
            "reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg-kinetics RD (not Murray's own kinetics) on static and growing domains with gamma heterogeneity, compared with an Eden-process melanoblast-colonisation control, on 10 coat-masked Holstein specimens at matched measurement scale with paired Wilcoxon/bootstrap statistics (Pass 8).",
            "reported_in_source: Established cattle genetics: KIT/MITF regulatory variants cause Holstein white spotting (Jivanji et al. 2019 GWAS; Jivanji et al. 2025 causal variants confirmed in edited mice), and mammalian melanoblast colonisation is stochastic migration plus proliferation (Mort et al. 2016).",
            "reported_in_source: Murray (1981) proposed a reaction-diffusion pre-pattern mechanism for mammalian coat markings; Turing (1952) supplied the instability theory. Neither paper measured Holstein coat patterns against the mechanism.",
            "transfer_boundary: The verdict concerns Holstein-Friesian flank spotting measured by adult patch statistics. It does not transfer to other breeds, other pattern elements (e.g. fine speckling), embryonic pre-pattern stages not observable in adult coat, or other species; Turing mechanisms are experimentally established in other systems (e.g. palate rugae) and nothing here bears on them." ;
        pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/1981-murray-bos-taurus-turing-wavelength.py; output: datasets/bos_taurus_turing_wavelength/bos_taurus_turing_wavelength_comparison.png; organism: Bos taurus (Holstein-Friesian, 10 specimens); environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Murray (1981) proposed a reaction-diffusion pre-pattern mechanism for mammalian coat markings; Turing (1952) supplied the instability theory. Neither paper measured Holstein coat patterns against the mechanism. | Established cattle genetics: KIT/MITF regulatory variants cause Holstein white spotting (Jivanji et al. 2019 GWAS; Jivanji et al. 2025 causal variants confirmed in edited mice), and mammalian melanoblast colonisation is stochastic migration plus proliferation (Mort et al. 2016).; reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg-kinetics RD (not Murray's own kinetics) on static and growing domains with gamma heterogeneity, compared with an Eden-process melanoblast-colonisation control, on 10 coat-masked Holstein specimens at matched measurement scale with paired Wilcoxon/bootstrap statistics (Pass 8). | Published result is negative: static Turing rejected (6.46 vs ~3.3); growing RD vs colonisation indistinguishable (3.29 vs 3.43, p = 0.91). Two blinded independent assessments (54.4, 57.7) overturned two earlier builder conclusions (Passes 4, 7-8) before this verdict was reached.; transfer_boundary: The verdict concerns Holstein-Friesian flank spotting measured by adult patch statistics. It does not transfer to other breeds, other pattern elements (e.g. fine speckling), embryonic pre-pattern stages not observable in adult coat, or other species; Turing mechanisms are experimentally established in other systems (e.g. palate rugae) and nothing here bears on them.; does_not_claim: Does NOT claim the Murray/Turing hypothesis is supported -- the tested claim is reported as a negative result, and the rubric overall (74.6) scores the simulation package, not the hypothesis. | Does NOT claim all reaction-diffusion models are excluded: a growing-domain RD is statistically indistinguishable from colonisation on these statistics, so adult coat morphology alone cannot identify the mechanism either way. | Does NOT claim the Eden control is the true mechanism; it is a minimal colonisation proxy, and its founder density was selected on specimen 01 (disclosed). | Does NOT claim independent confirmation of the Pass 8+ verdict: the Pass 9 assessment is builder-scored (independent re-score is remediation R11), held-out n = 9 specimens limits power, and coat segmentation is a saturation heuristic.]; phenomenon_size: 50 cm (0.5 m, log10=-0.301 m, tier=8_colonial_m); species_scale_ladder (2 runs from 9.5 mm to 50 cm): 9.5 mm:airway-mucosal-creasing, 50 cm:bos-taurus-turing-wavelength" ;
        pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1007/s13258-016-0493-4>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(79)90042-0>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(81)90334-9>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/ncomms10288>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1952.0012>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1126/sciadv.adt5913>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1186/s12711-019-0506-2> ;
        pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-murray-bos-taurus-turing-wavelength-code-traceability>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-murray-bos-taurus-turing-wavelength-model-fidelity>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-murray-bos-taurus-turing-wavelength-morphometric-validation>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-murray-bos-taurus-turing-wavelength-overall>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-murray-bos-taurus-turing-wavelength-parameter-expressivity>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-murray-bos-taurus-turing-wavelength-repro-package>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-murray-bos-taurus-turing-wavelength-source-traceability>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-murray-bos-taurus-turing-wavelength-specimen-match> ;
        pk:hypothesisType "Mathematical Morphogenesis Model" ;
        pk:weightOfEvidence 7.46e-01 .

    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-odell-apical-constriction-invagination> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Odell, Oster, Alberch & Burnside (1981) / Martin, Kaschube & Wieschaus (2009) stretch-activated apical purse-string constriction and ventral furrow invagination (Drosophila melanogaster (gastrulating embryo ventral furrow epithelium))" ;
        dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/odell-apical-constriction-invagination-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/odell-apical-constriction-invagination-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/odell-apical-constriction-invagination-3> ;
        schema:about "Drosophila melanogaster (gastrulating embryo ventral furrow epithelium)" ;
        schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Full 3D anteroposterior cephalic furrow / germband extension viscous shell hydrodynamics or explicit subcellular Rho1-Rok-Myosin II reaction-diffusion kinetics",
            "reconstructed_in_script: 5-regime genetic & mechanical perturbation simulator (Wild-Type D_inv=38.0 um, L_ap=2.10 um; No-Stretch D_inv=21.0 um; cta mutant D_inv=15.5 um; snail unratcheted D_inv=5.12 um, L_ap=6.76 um; twist;snail null D_inv=0.0 um, L_ap=8.20 um; Pearson r=0.9996, RMSE=0.42 um)",
            "reconstructed_in_script: 64-cell viscoelastic epithelial ring solver with exact incompressible cytoplasmic area conservation (A_i = A_0 = 262.4 um^2, error < 1e-9) and midpoint RK2 rest-length ODE verification (L2 error 9.8e-7)",
            "reconstructed_in_script: Automated 4-stage confocal specimen segmentation on drosophila_ventral_furrow_specimen.jpg (DV/ML aspect 1.050 -> 1.029 -> 0.962 -> 0.922, trajectory r=0.9942)",
            "reported_in_source: Martin, Kaschube & Wieschaus (2009) Nature 457:495-499 pulsed actomyosin coalescence driven by Twist and ratcheted rest-length stabilization driven by Snail across wild-type, snail, and twist;snail embryos",
            "reported_in_source: Odell, Oster, Alberch & Burnside (1981) Dev. Biol. 85:446-462 stretch-activated viscoelastic apical purse-string rest-length bistability (L_1 vs L_2 < L_1) and incompressible trapezoidal cell ring invagination",
            "transfer_boundary: 2D transverse cross-sectional viscoelastic ring of 64 trapezoidal cells mapped to confocal transverse sections of Drosophila ventral furrow formation" ;
        pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/0012-1606(81)90434-6>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.bpj.2014.07.013>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jmbbm.2007.10.002>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature07522> ;
        pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-apical-constriction-invagination-audit-v2-odell-apical-constriction-invagination-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-apical-constriction-invagination-audit-v2-odell-apical-constriction-invagination-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-apical-constriction-invagination-audit-v2-odell-apical-constriction-invagination-3>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-apical-constriction-invagination-audit-v2-odell-apical-constriction-invagination-4>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-apical-constriction-invagination-audit-v2-odell-apical-constriction-invagination-5>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-apical-constriction-invagination-audit-v2-odell-apical-constriction-invagination-6>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-apical-constriction-invagination-audit-v2-odell-apical-constriction-invagination-7> ;
        pk:hypothesisType "Viscoelastic Stretch-Activated Apical Purse-String Constriction & Incompressible Wedge Invagination Mechanics" ;
        pk:weightOfEvidence 9.17e-01 .

    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-pezzulo-bioelectric-target-morphology-memory> a pk:Claim ;
