    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling> a ns1:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Campas et al. (2010) PNAS affine scaling-and-shear transformation + Abzhanov et al. (2004, 2006) Bmp4/Calmodulin beak morphogenesis + Soons et al. (2010-2015) reduced FEM fracture risk faithfully reproduces Darwin's finches (Geospiza magnirostris, Geospiza fortis, Geospiza scandens, Camarhynchus parvulus, Certhidea olivacea) morphology" ;
        dct:description "The simulation script(s) 2021-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Darwin's finches (Geospiza magnirostris, Geospiza fortis, Geospiza scandens, Camarhynchus parvulus, Certhidea olivacea) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 87.6/100, audit 2026-10-19-avian-beak-darwin-scaling-audit-v3) and the assessments." ;
        dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8a7928d7/2021-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling.py> ;
        ns1:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8a7928d7/2021-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling.py; output: docs/media/avian_beak_darwin_scaling_comparison.png; organism: Darwin's finches (Geospiza magnirostris, Geospiza fortis, Geospiza scandens, Camarhynchus parvulus, Certhidea olivacea); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/8a7928d7; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0; spec_fingerprint: 69389d287a403dfef90b7be15dfd80b39613de2e2fd62676231e5453b6f3f2f1; artifact_sha256: 4f214f0596736b346a6af38f147815d628f8ab44dd8430463f6115382d10b90b; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/avian_beak_darwin_scaling/avian_beak_darwin_scaling_reference.json=cf6430de0c52d725..., datasets/avian_beak_darwin_scaling/beak_fem_fracture_reference.json=bff86f96d0fcc2fd..., datasets/avian_beak_darwin_scaling/darwin_finches_specimen.jpg=5ea7ada14a01ba77..., datasets/avian_beak_darwin_scaling/paper_citations.bib=f0b9fb929ffd2d09..., datasets/avian_beak_darwin_scaling/pass3_citations.bib=37c2a856e17b123b..., datasets/avian_beak_darwin_scaling/scout_manifest.json=4b321120fd7b2736...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-avian-beak-darwin-scaling-audit-v2; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Campas et al. (2010): upper-beak profiles of the 14 Darwin's finch species collapse onto one master curve under a 3-parameter affine scaling-and-shear group M(s_L, s_D, gamma); Geospiza (Group A) collapse under pure scaling, Camarhynchus/Platyspiza/Cactospiza (Group B) and Certhidea/Pinaroloxias (Group C) need the shear | Abzhanov et al. (2004, 2006): Bmp4 scales beak depth/width and calmodulin scales length; RCAS::Bmp4, RCAS::Noggin and RCAS::CaM in chick change beak proportions accordingly | Soons et al. (2010, 2012, 2015): micro-CT finite-element models of Geospiza upper beaks show peak von Mises stress under in vivo bite force far less variable than bite force itself, a stress-reducing role for the keratin rhamphotheca, and lower stresses for base biting than tip biting | Herrel et al. (2005): in vivo bite forces of Darwin's finches scale with head width; reconstructed_in_script: Affine matrix and analytic inverse, canonical culmen curve, 2D/3D conical-parabolic beak surface, 14-species collapse with a pure-scaling negative control, 2D Bmp4/CaM Gaussian mesenchymal field, cantilever bending index W D^3/(12 L), four RCAS conditions, connected-component culmen contour extraction on the Gould (1845) plate, and (Pass 3) a two-material plane-stress Q4 FEM of the sagittal upper-beak section with Gibson-Ashby trabecular core, keratin shell, tip/base/oblique seed loads, beam-theory verification, mesh convergence, 14-species fracture-risk indices, keratin-modulus and BV/TV ablations; transfer_boundary: The 14-species 'empirical' profiles are generated by the script's own forward transform plus Gaussian noise (sigma = 0.24 % of s_D), so the collapse RMS 0.0021 / r = 0.9999 and the 45x negative-control ratio validate the inverse of the same transform, not digitised Campas Fig. 2/3 profiles | The FEM is a 2D sagittal plane-stress idealisation (out-of-plane thickness = W_mm everywhere) of a Law-1 sheared culmen profile with a 0.7 mm solid-keratin tip clamp, not a voxel-resolved micro-CT mesh; all moduli, strengths, thicknesses and the three Soons predictions were transcribed offline from memory and are order-of-magnitude anchors | The 'observed' RCAS D/L values and several reference values equal Law-2 formula outputs or the script's own earlier output, so those comparisons are self-referential; does_not_claim: Reproduction of any digitised Campas, Abzhanov or Soons figure value; a 3D micro-CT finite-element model; crack initiation or propagation; keratin-bone interface failure; mediolateral load asymmetry; per-species provenance of the species table (s_L, s_D, s_W, gamma, bite force)]" ;
        ns1:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.actamat.2005.04.048>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9781139878326>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature04843>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0911575107>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1098/rsif.2011.0910>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1098/rsif.2014.0284>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.2009.0280>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1420-9101.2004.00857.x>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1098095>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0129479> ;
        ns1:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling-code-traceability>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling-model-fidelity>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling-morphometric-validation>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling-overall>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling-parameter-expressivity>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling-repro-package>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling-source-traceability>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling-specimen-match> ;
        ns1:weightOfEvidence 8.76e-01 .

