            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-bailleul-allometric-cranial-sutures-specimen-match> ;
        ns1:weightOfEvidence 8.65e-01 .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-baker-fgf-wnt-bistable-wavefront> a ns1:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Goldbeter, Gonze & Pourquié (2007) / Baker, Schnell & Maini (2006) RA–FGF8/Wnt mutual cross-inhibition bistable determination wavefront in vertebrate somitogenesis, gated by a Lewis (2003) delayed Her1/Hes7 clock lattice on 2D bilateral paraxial mesoderm strips faithfully reproduces Gallus gallus (chick embryo presomitic mesoderm & bilateral paraxial somites) morphology" ;
        dct:description "The simulation script(s) 2012-baker-fgf-wnt-bistable-wavefront.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Gallus gallus (chick embryo presomitic mesoderm & bilateral paraxial somites) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 92.0/100, audit 2026-10-19-fgf-wnt-bistable-wavefront-audit-v3) and the assessments." ;
        dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2012-baker-fgf-wnt-bistable-wavefront.py> ;
        ns1:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2012-baker-fgf-wnt-bistable-wavefront.py; output: docs/media/fgf_wnt_bistable_wavefront_comparison.png; organism: Gallus gallus (chick embryo presomitic mesoderm & bilateral paraxial somites); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/d58a084; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0, lean 4.35.0; spec_fingerprint: 8dd375129916874341f9ce3cd615881707510415d2e6ec1d5f2914264a78a000; artifact_sha256: ce04ae4bd568fab038e1731acc826d8aade9d36fef83013221614779e63441e8; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/fgf_wnt_bistable_wavefront/chick_ra_fgf_somites_specimen.jpg=8b80971796cb29e2..., datasets/fgf_wnt_bistable_wavefront/fgf_wnt_bistable_wavefront_reference.json=42c6196ddd32cee9..., datasets/fgf_wnt_bistable_wavefront/fgf_wnt_clock_lr_reference.json=16deab8565d154cb..., datasets/fgf_wnt_bistable_wavefront/scout_manifest.json=783faa9ee6b3db0c...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-fgf-wnt-bistable-wavefront-audit-v2; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Goldbeter, Gonze & Pourquie (2007) Dev. Cell / Dev. Dyn. 236:1495-1508 mutual cross-inhibition + CYP26A1 RA-degradation PDEs producing an S-shaped hysteresis curve [M_1, M_2], an all-or-none determination front switch, and (Fig. 10) a bistability window that must span at least one segment so the clock can time the arrest | Baker, Schnell & Maini (2006) J. Theor. Biol. 239:413-429 & Diez del Corral et al. (2003) Neuron 40:65-79 opposing Vitamin A Deficiency (VAD) anterior front shift vs exogenous RA / SU5402 posterior front shift | Lewis (2003) Curr. Biol. 13:1398-1408 delayed autoinhibition her1/her7 oscillator (Eqs. 1-3, period ~ 2(T_m + T_p + 1/b + 1/c)), Notch-Delta synchronisation of adjacent cells and anti-phase locking at half-period coupling delay (Fig. 4); Palmeirim et al. (1997) Cell 91:639-648 90-min chick c-hairy1 period | Vermot & Pourquie (2005) Nature 435:215-220 and Vermot et al. (2005) Science 308:563-566: RA buffers a lateralizing bias so WT somites form bilaterally in synchrony, whereas VAD / disulfiram chick (left delayed) and Raldh2-/- mouse (right delayed) show a one-somite left-right desynchronisation that reverses under situs inversus; reconstructed_in_script: Analytical inverse hysteresis S-curve M(F) solver extracting lower saddle-node M_1 = 1.0254 nM and upper saddle-node M_2 = 3.3038 nM (Delta_M = 2.2784 nM) | 1D coupled RA-FGF8/Wnt reaction-diffusion PDE solver along the 1000 um chick PSM demonstrating 22.2x sharpening of the determination front (Delta_x_front = 16.22 um vs lambda_M = 360.67 um) at x_front = 571.46 um | 150-cell delayed Her1/Hes7 DDE lattice with delayed saturating Notch-Delta input, advected at v_g through the competence window [149.4, 571.4] um; cells arrest only at a Her protein peak -> saltatory cohort arrest (T_osc = 92.0 min, S = v_g*T_osc = 153.3 um, nearest-neighbour coherence 0.84 vs 0.03 Notch-ablated, saltatory index 0.87 vs 0.42) | 2D (x, y) RA-FGF8/Wnt reaction-diffusion solve on left strip + neural tube + right strip (1500 x 500 um) with RA-buffered lateralizing bias; WT Delta_x_LR = 6.3 um (0.04 somite), VAD 149.8 um (1.00 somite, left delayed), situs inversus and Raldh2-/- mouse right delayed; v_sc buffering sweep monotone | 5-regime somite perturbation evaluator (Pearson r = 0.9999, RMSE = 0.81 um) plus bilateral dorsal somite row segmentation on chick_ra_fgf_somites_specimen.jpg (48.47 px mean spacing); transfer_boundary: 1D anteroposterior chick presomitic mesoderm axis mapped to dorsal vertebrate SEM somite rows; the 2D bilateral strip geometry (strip half-width 250 um, neural tube half-width 80 um) is derived from the specimen's two somite-row pixel offsets | Lewis (2003) zebrafish her1 rate constants (a, b, c, k, p_0) reused with chick-scale transcription delay T_m = 31.5 min to reach the 90-min chick period; does_not_claim: Full 3D mesenchymal-to-epithelial somite rosette mechanics | Explicit deltaC mRNA/protein kinetics: Notch-Delta coupling is a delayed saturating readout of neighbour her1 transcript with K_D = k/(2c) (Lewis publishes no numeric value) | A molecular origin for the lateralizing bias b_LR = 0.727: it is a calibrated free parameter fitted to the one-somite VAD lag, buffered by anterior RA through a Hill law]" ;
        ns1:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1002/dvdy.21193>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0092-8674(00)80451-1>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0092-8674(01)00437-8>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0896-6273(03)00565-8>,
