    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-bi-vertex-glass-jamming> a ns1:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Bi et al. (2015), Park et al. (2015) & Bi et al. (2016) zero-temperature shape-index unjamming, asthmatic bronchial epithelial rigidity transition and self-propelled Voronoi motility-driven glass transition faithfully reproduces Human (Homo sapiens) bronchial epithelial monolayer & Drosophila epithelial sheet morphology" ;
        dct:description "The simulation script(s) 2015-bi-vertex-glass-jamming.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Human (Homo sapiens) bronchial epithelial monolayer & Drosophila epithelial sheet specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 90.1/100, audit 2026-10-19-vertex-glass-jamming-audit-v3) and the assessments." ;
        dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/7e4f207/2015-bi-vertex-glass-jamming.py> ;
        ns1:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/7e4f207/2015-bi-vertex-glass-jamming.py; output: docs/media/vertex_glass_jamming_comparison.png; organism: Human (Homo sapiens) bronchial epithelial monolayer & Drosophila epithelial sheet; checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/7e4f207; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0; spec_fingerprint: 52abc2dcaa2857a7c9b54a7d8ac8d7ebb1e0481dc0dc957ca72fa6bc9190d466; artifact_sha256: 6a5f0e91d8d909aeb16fa43c8d4fdc90f3abcf274beabe497959c412b909893b; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-vertex-glass-jamming-audit-v2; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Bi, Lopez, Schwarz & Manning (2015) Nature Physics Eqs. 1-2 & Figs. 1-4: dimensionless vertex energy e = (1/2) sum [(a_i - 1)^2 + r(p_i - p_0)^2] exhibits a density-independent rigidity transition at critical target shape index p_0^* approx 3.813 (> p_5 approx 3.8119 > p_hex approx 3.7224), where T1 energy barrier Delta e_T1(p_0) and static shear modulus G(p_0) vanish identically for p_0 >= p_0^*. | Park et al. (2015) Nature Materials Figs. 1-4 & Atia et al. (2018) Nature Physics Figs. 1-2: primary human bronchial epithelial cells (HBECs) from non-asthmatic donors jam into a solid monolayer by Day 14 (q = 3.792 < 3.813), whereas asthmatic donor HBECs (q = 3.955 > 3.813) and mechanically compressed HBECs (30 cm H2O, q = 3.945 > 3.813) remain unjammed, with standardized cell shapes obeying a universal k-Gamma distribution. | Bi, Yang, Marchetti & Manning (2016) Physical Review X Eqs. 1-3 & Figs. 1, 3-4: in the Self-Propelled Voronoi model dr_i/dt = mu F_i + v_0 n_i with rotational diffusion D_r, the glass transition line p_0^c(v_0, D_r) meets p_0 = 3.81 at v_0 -> 0, is lowered by motility v_0, rises toward 3.81 as persistence shortens (larger D_r), and the observed shape index at the boundary is q_c approx 3.81 for all (v_0, D_r); solids have D_eff = D_s/D_0 < 1e-3 at long times.; reconstructed_in_script: 2D periodic confluent monolayer phenomenological vertex-Voronoi relaxation across 4 regimes (Non-Asthmatic Solid p_0=3.70, Critical Point p_0^*=3.813, Asthmatic Fluid p_0=3.955, and Zero-Perimeter-Modulus Ablation r=0.0), 8-point p_0 phase sweep in [3.55, 4.00], and Park et al. (2015) Days 3-18 bronchial maturation trajectories (curve fits to the vendored Park values). | Junction-guided Voronoi segmentation of the human in situ monolayer micrograph (`human_epithelial_monolayer_specimen.jpg`, N=101 interior cells, <q>=3.7961, k-Gamma correlation r = 0.9334). | Pass 3: Bi et al. (2016) SPV model with exact analytic Voronoi forces (circumcenter Jacobians, FD-verified), FIRE inherent-structure quench, overdamped active-Brownian integration (dt = min(0.1, 0.2/D_r)), time-origin-averaged MSD -> D_s and D_eff = D_s/D_0, per-cell T1 rate; a 6x4 (p_0, v_0) glass map at D_r = 1 (boundary p_0^c(v_0) = 3.828, 3.755, 3.678, 3.594 for v_0 = 0.05, 0.15, 0.30, 0.45; linear intercept p_0^c(0) = 3.850, slope alpha = 0.575; q_c = 3.818 +/- 0.013), a D_r sweep at v_0 = 0.30 (p_0^c = 3.677, 3.678, 3.748 for D_r = 0.25, 1, 4; D_s at p_0 = 3.70 decreasing in D_r), and an energy-minimised v_0 = 0 <q>(p_0) sweep (Pearson r = 0.9966 vs the Bi 2015 reference, solid-branch <q> = 3.829).; transfer_boundary: 2D apical polygonal projection of pseudostratified bronchial and simple monolayer epithelia; the vendored specimen is a human corneal endothelium micrograph used as a generic human polygonal monolayer, not an HBEC culture. | The SPV glass boundary is a finite-time (T = 150 in units of 1/(mu K_A A_0)), finite-size (N = 100), single-seed estimate classified by a script-defined per-free-path T1 criterion (Gamma_T1 / v_0 > 0.02); Bi (2016)'s long-time D_eff < 1e-3 criterion is not resolvable in this window (solid floor ~5e-3) and D_eff is reported alongside only.; does_not_claim: Does not model 3D mucociliary beating hydrodynamics or sub-epithelial airway smooth muscle contraction. | Does not compute the T1 energy barrier or shear modulus from the energy landscape (Panel B1 uses the hard-coded linear law Delta e_T1 = 0.40 r (p_0^* - p_0), G = 1.00 r (p_0^* - p_0)); does not reproduce the full curved Bi (2016) Fig. 1(a) boundary or a (v_0, D_r) surface beyond two orthogonal slices; does not include cell division, apoptosis or alignment interactions.]" ;
        ns1:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1038/nmat4357>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/nphys3471>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41567-018-0089-9>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.97.170201>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevX.6.021011>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1140/epje/i2010-10677-0> ;
        ns1:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-bi-vertex-glass-jamming-code-traceability>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-bi-vertex-glass-jamming-model-fidelity>,
