        dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/317bc3c/2008-burak-grid-cell-hexagonal-attractor.py> ;
        ns1:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/317bc3c/2008-burak-grid-cell-hexagonal-attractor.py; output: docs/media/grid_cell_hexagonal_attractor_comparison.png; organism: Rattus norvegicus medial entorhinal cortex (MEC Layer II) & hippocampal-entorhinal circuit; checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/317bc3c; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1; spec_fingerprint: d708b4028fb6bc24d11a5b20d2c0b94776416b67d14792a0ba60270e21d2be62; artifact_sha256: 9e15f015a1a8af316481cb068cc21589a23e8c95c9287f102d59cfa9d52e96bb; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/grid_cell_hexagonal_attractor/grid_cell_hexagonal_attractor_reference.json=951b00ff56331c34..., datasets/grid_cell_hexagonal_attractor/paper_citations.bib=e1074e8d98b9dc00..., datasets/grid_cell_hexagonal_attractor/rat_entorhinal_hippocampal_specimen.jpg=63b3a392f8d0b25f..., datasets/grid_cell_hexagonal_attractor/scout_manifest.json=77ac05875318888d...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-grid-cell-hexagonal-attractor-audit; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Hafting et al. (2005) Nature 436:801-806 discovery of 60 deg hexagonal firing lattices in Rattus norvegicus dorsomedial entorhinal cortex Layer II with rotational autocorrelogram peaks at 60 deg and 120 deg | Burak & Fiete (2009) PLoS Comput. Biol. 5:e1000291 2D continuous attractor network model with 4 head-direction-conjunctive subpopulations (N, S, E, W), outgoing kernel shift l*e_hat(theta), and velocity modulation alpha*v(t).e_hat(theta) | Stensola et al. (2012) Nature 492:72-78 discretized dorso-ventral grid modules M1..M4 scaling by geometric ratio lambda_{m+1}/lambda_m approx sqrt(2) approx 1.42 ({38, 54, 76, 108} cm); reconstructed_in_script: 2D FFT Burak-Fiete 4-subpopulation (E, N, W, S) continuous attractor neural network solver on a 36x36 toroidal sheet coupled to a 120-step 2D foraging trajectory across all 4 Stensola modules, 90 deg square non-resonant control, and Brandon et al. (2011) medial-septum inactivation (l=0, alpha=0) pinned-bump control | Automated CV segmentation of the Rattus norvegicus hippocampal-entorhinal immunofluorescence micrograph (N=902 NeuN+ neuronal somata, 50-bin dorso-ventral laminar density profile r=0.9822, and MBP+ perforant-path fiber fraction); transfer_boundary: Normalized 2D periodic neural sheet S(x,t) on [0, 2*pi)^2 mapped onto the 270x270 cm open-field foraging arena via velocity-integrated phase Phi(t); does_not_claim: Biophysical HCN1 h-current single-channel gating kinetics or border-cell environmental wall shearing]" ;
        ns1:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature03721>,
