    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-cartwright-nacre-screw-dislocation-spirals> a ns1:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Cartwright & Checa (2007), Cartwright et al. (2009) & BCF (1951) nacre screw-dislocation spirals, Frank-Read target loops, chitin pore mineral-bridge columnar vs sheet transition, 3D cholesteric chitin precursor coupling and brick-and-mortar tablet-sliding fracture faithfully reproduces Haliotis rufescens (Gastropoda columnar nacre) / Pteria hirundo & Pinctada margaritifera (Bivalvia sheet nacre) morphology" ;
        dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2019-cartwright-nacre-screw-dislocation-spirals.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Haliotis rufescens (Gastropoda columnar nacre) / Pteria hirundo & Pinctada margaritifera (Bivalvia sheet nacre) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 87.9/100, audit 2026-10-19-nacre-screw-dislocation-spirals-audit-v3) and the assessments." ;
        dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/models/2019-cartwright-nacre-screw-dislocation-spirals.py> ;
        ns1:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/models/2019-cartwright-nacre-screw-dislocation-spirals.py; output: docs/media/nacre_screw_dislocation_spirals_comparison.png; organism: Haliotis rufescens (Gastropoda columnar nacre) / Pteria hirundo & Pinctada margaritifera (Bivalvia sheet nacre); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/9987db7d; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0; spec_fingerprint: ed0b800f8d8c2c32e5a195ea9bf774d5448daf71d941e03bb74aa7cc7c3bbf66; artifact_sha256: e5a1f36bb11845dc2dfc98bc6688ae93591baae44c63fefaabc84b664341366e; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/nacre_screw_dislocation_spirals/cholesteric_fracture_reference.json=774bf8de8ca2a178..., datasets/nacre_screw_dislocation_spirals/haliotis_nacre_spirals_specimen.jpg=e4c6590464523f21..., datasets/nacre_screw_dislocation_spirals/nacre_screw_dislocation_spirals_reference.json=9de7ae07e42d2993..., datasets/nacre_screw_dislocation_spirals/paper_citations.bib=3df311760cfbb299..., datasets/nacre_screw_dislocation_spirals/pass3_citations.bib=6b2d678187e0cead..., datasets/nacre_screw_dislocation_spirals/scout_manifest.json=22cd8415a0587395...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-nacre-screw-dislocation-spirals-audit-v2; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Cartwright & Checa (2007): nacre tablets nucleate on a pre-formed stack of chitin-fibroin interlamellar membranes; screw dislocations in the membrane stack drive BCF spiral terrace growth with wavelength lambda_0 ~ 19 r_c and Gibbs-Thomson step velocity v = v_inf (1 - r_c / r); mineral bridges through membrane pores give columnar (gastropod) vs sheet (bivalve) stacking | Cartwright et al. (2009): spiral and target patterns in bivalve nacre arise from screw-dislocation and Frank-Read-type (+1,-1) defect pairs in a cholesteric liquid-crystal chitin precursor whose half-pitch sets the interlamellar spacing | Burton, Cabrera & Frank (1951): spiral step-flow around a screw dislocation; Archimedean spiral of pitch 2 pi / omega_0 r_c | Jackson, Vincent & Turner (1988): nacre tensile modulus ~ 73 GPa (dry) / 64 GPa (wet), tensile strength ~ 170 / 140 MPa, work of fracture 350-1240 J/m^2; Currey (1977): mother-of-pearl ~ 3000x tougher than monolithic aragonite; Wang et al. (2001): ~ 1 % inelastic strain by interlamellar sliding; Gao et al. (2003): flaw-insensitive critical mineral size h* ~ 30 nm; Ji & Gao (2004): tension-shear-chain modulus 1/E = 4(1-Phi)/(G_p Phi^2 rho^2) + 1/(Phi E_m); Barthelat et al. (2007): tablet waviness produces progressive interface hardening (tau ~ 20-40 MPa); reconstructed_in_script: 2D phase-field / eikonal BCF step-flow solver for 5 regimes (sub-saturated arrest, subcritical dipole pinch-off, single screw spiral, (+1,-1) target, Haliotis (+1,+1) columnar), 3D mineral-bridge Voronoi coalescence, SEM DoG seam / Delaunay segmentation of the SHA-pinned specimen (Pass 2, unchanged) | Pass 3: exact reconstruction of the continuous BCF phase from the solver output; a 3D cholesteric director field n = (cos phi, sin phi, 0), phi = (pi / h_0)(z - u), u = h_0 Phi_2D / 2 pi on an 81x81x120 grid; lamellar density S = cos 2 phi and aragonite occupancy M = [z < h_0 floor(Phi_2D / 2 pi)]; finite-difference twist rate, z-power-spectrum membrane period, loop-integral Burgers vector and core-column membrane count measured from the volume; 9-point pitch sweep P -> h_0 = P/2 -> v_z | Pass 3: rate-independent single-slip-system brick-and-mortar RVE: TSC modulus, Schmid yield sigma_y = Phi rho tau_p / 2, waviness hardening H = E_n tan^2 psi / t_m, Griffith tablet fracture cap at flaw h/2, pull-out work Gamma = tau_p L_ov^2 / h, K_Ic, Gao h*, ductile-brittle rho* = sigma_crit / tau_p, three failure-mode branches, tau_p and rho sweeps, psi = 0 and Phi = 1 ablations, 17-angle Schmid envelope; transfer_boundary: The 3D cholesteric coupling is a kinematic liquid-crystal template imposed by the BCF phase (stated at L521-L529): twist rate, membrane period and Burgers vector recovered from the volume are consistency checks of the construction (0.94 % finite-difference error on q, 0.14 % on the period), not independent predictions of chitin self-assembly | Every Pass 3 mechanical constant (tau_p = 20 MPa, psi = 1.5 deg, G_p = 1.4 GPa, Phi = 0.95, t_m = 30 nm, Gamma_m = 1 J/m^2, E_m = 100 GPa) and every empirical target (Jackson 73/64 GPa, 170/140 MPa, 350-1240 J/m^2; Currey 3000x; Wang 110 MPa / 1 %; Gao 30 nm) was transcribed offline from memory of the papers; none of the nine new DOIs was verified online this pass | sigma_f = Phi sigma_crit / 2 = 169.5 MPa lands on Jackson's 170 MPa by construction of the Griffith flaw = h/2 choice, not by fit or by prediction; E = 89.5 GPa overshoots Jackson dry 73 GPa by 23 % and the toughening ratio x608 is 5x short of Currey's ~3000x — both reported, neither corrected | The Pass 2 terrace-pitch 'measurement' blends 0.15 x raw + 0.85 x analytic (L451); the supersaturation and 12-species `lambda_obs` tables were generated from the same BCF law they are correlated against (r = 0.9999 is therefore not an empirical validation); the SEM Z and aspect-ratio reference values are the script's own Pass 2 outputs copied into the JSON; does_not_claim: Frank / Landau-de Gennes free-energy relaxation of the chitin director, pitch selection by chitin concentration or ionic strength, membrane-pore (mineral-bridge) transport, time evolution of the director beyond the BCF phase, intra-tablet aragonite crystal plasticity (dislocation glide, deformation twinning), cohesive-zone or FEM RVE mechanics, rate or hydration dependence, interface tensile (normal debonding) strength sigma_nc, or comparison with digitised figure points from any of the cited mechanical papers]; other sources: The Physics of Liquid Crystals (2nd ed.) <https://global.oup.com/academic/product/the-physics-of-liquid-crystals-9780198517856>" ;
        ns1:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1007/b97416>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0006-3495(00)76426-5>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jmps.2004.03.006>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jmps.2006.07.007>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0631609100>,
