        ns1:weightOfEvidence 8.52e-01 .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling> a ns1:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Chirat, Moulton & Goriely (2013) & Erlich et al. (2016) mollusc shell marginal buckling, hollow-spine closure and predator damage / mantle repair faithfully reproduces Pecten jacobaeus (Mediterranean scallop / Bivalvia, Ammonitida & Brachiopoda); Murex hollow spines (Gastropoda) morphology" ;
        dct:description "The simulation script(s) 2013-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Pecten jacobaeus (Mediterranean scallop / Bivalvia, Ammonitida & Brachiopoda); Murex hollow spines (Gastropoda) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 87.0/100, audit 2026-10-19-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-audit-v3) and the assessments." ;
        dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e651a8b8/2013-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling.py> ;
        ns1:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e651a8b8/2013-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling.py; output: docs/media/mollusc_shell_marginal_buckling_comparison.png; organism: Pecten jacobaeus (Mediterranean scallop / Bivalvia, Ammonitida & Brachiopoda); Murex hollow spines (Gastropoda); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/e651a8b8; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1; spec_fingerprint: 5ce4d2a0cdd2530a2bb4e03307b8a1565e305db6cf6b377ff8cb6db26ef82d9e; artifact_sha256: 9a3f32d98065e16f7fa63f39ab8a2b61e070b482616d8e3ef280efaef20643a0; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/mollusc_shell_marginal_buckling/mollusc_shell_marginal_buckling_reference.json=dec7d148f176932a..., datasets/mollusc_shell_marginal_buckling/pass3_spine_closure_damage_repair_reference.json=dcc719fadd231691..., datasets/mollusc_shell_marginal_buckling/ribbed_bivalve_shell_specimen.jpg=a0ac69e8a9be3928..., datasets/mollusc_shell_marginal_buckling/scout_manifest.json=2fb38cc60b112598...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-audit-v2; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Chirat, Moulton & Goriely (2013): the mantle margin is an elastic beam on the Winkler foundation of the calcified shell edge; compressive growth thrust P above P_c = 2 sqrt(EI k) buckles it at lambda_c = 2 pi (EI/k)^(1/4), and hollow spines form where the buckled fold grows faster than its base | Erlich et al. (2016): isometric vs rib-intercalating antimarginal ornamentation follows from whether lambda_c scales with the margin length (constant N) or stays fixed (N grows) | Rudraraju et al. (2019): a 3D finite-strain morphoelastic shell FEM with surface and volume growth reproduces spine formation and closure | Vermeij (1987): durophagous predators chip shell margins; molluscs repair the break and leave repair scars; reconstructed_in_script: Spectral L-BFGS-B minimisation of the fourth-order nonlinear Winkler-beam energy on a periodic margin (Pass 2), now with heterogeneous foundation k(s) and template-memory warm start; pitchfork amplitude law and subcritical control; 3D accretionary valve synthesis across 4 regimes; 12-species quarter-power regression; Pecten specimen costae segmentation; (Pass 3) planar inextensible elastica cross-section of a hollow spine fold with self-contact penalty, continuation in growth excess eps, and stacking into a tube surface; (Pass 3) 14-station damage/repair accretionary trajectory, scar index, healing-length fit, registry error, 5 x 4 chip-size x callus-stiffness outcome phase diagram; transfer_boundary: The hollow-spine closure model is a 2D cross-section elastica with prescribed base width W = 6 mm and wall thickness t = 0.35 mm; there is no out-of-plane coupling between cross-sections, no shell stretching energy and no growth tensor, so eps_close = 4.81 is a reduced-model number and its reference value (5.00) is mesh convergence of the same model, not a Murex measurement | The repair callus stiffness ratio rho = 1.15 and decay length l_heal = 7 mm are prescribed, not measured; the critical chip arc 1.97 lambda is compared with a half-integer rounding heuristic (1.5 lambda), not a published repair-scar statistic | EI = 1.085 mN mm^2 for Pecten is the value that makes lambda_c = 8.7766 mm give exactly 14 ribs over L = 122.87 mm; the vendored JSON default_parameters.EI_mN_mm2 is 0.18 and the Adult_V ontogenetic stage is 1.79, so the wild-type calibration is self-referential; does_not_claim: A 3D finite-strain morphoelastic shell finite-element solution (Rudraraju et al. 2019), emergent spine base width or wall thickness, measured repair-callus mechanics, free-edge (non-periodic) margin boundary conditions, or an independent empirical closure strain for Murex spines]; other sources: Evolution and Escalation: An Ecological History of Life <https://press.princeton.edu/books/paperback/9780691000800/evolution-and-escalation>" ;
        ns1:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2012.07.009>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1220443110>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1098/rsif.2016.0592>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1007213> ;
        ns1:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-code-traceability>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-model-fidelity>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-morphometric-validation>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-overall>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-parameter-expressivity>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-repro-package>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-source-traceability>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-specimen-match> ;
        ns1:weightOfEvidence 8.7e-01 .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette> a ns1:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Young et al. (1992) & Jaya et al. (2016) Emiliania huxleyi V/R calcite crystal coccolith rosette shield & interlocking spherical coccosphere mechanics faithfully reproduces Emiliania huxleyi (Morphotypes A, B, B/C, C, R, O) & Gephyrocapsa / Calcidiscus / Coccolithus (Haptophyta) morphology" ;
        dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2022-coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Emiliania huxleyi (Morphotypes A, B, B/C, C, R, O) & Gephyrocapsa / Calcidiscus / Coccolithus (Haptophyta) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 79.3/100, audit 2026-10-19-emiliania-calcite-rosette-audit-v3) and the assessments." ;
        dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/models/2022-coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette.py> ;
        ns1:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/models/2022-coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette.py; output: docs/media/emiliania_calcite_rosette_comparison.png; organism: Emiliania huxleyi (Morphotypes A, B, B/C, C, R, O) & Gephyrocapsa / Calcidiscus / Coccolithus (Haptophyta); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/9987db7d; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0; spec_fingerprint: 965ae13d1916a73bad9dca346e9176f4f9220e85b7c520cf8b7bb71057d4f791; artifact_sha256: a51c56828e0a56922fc52ef5383b841b1037b1b7d4aa33b14f593bf88059e97d; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/emiliania_calcite_rosette/emiliania_calcite_rosette_reference.json=6e0133f11f7fd993..., datasets/emiliania_calcite_rosette/emiliania_huxleyi_coccolith_specimen.jpg=94d4b431c4912727..., datasets/emiliania_calcite_rosette/scout_manifest.json=d838aa9cca83725c...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-emiliania-calcite-rosette-audit-v2; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Young et al. (1992): coccolith shield elements nucleate as alternating V- and R-units with mutually orthogonal calcite c-axis orientations on an organic baseplate ring; morphology follows from crystallographic control of {10-14} growth | Didymus et al. (1993): stage-specific E. huxleyi coccolith growth from proto-coccolith ring to T-shaped hammer elements of the distal shield | Jaya et al. (2016): E. huxleyi coccospheres confer mechanical protection; under nanoindentation individual coccoliths slide relative to each other and cracks are arrested at coccolith boundaries | Walker et al. (2018): the requirement for calcification differs between coccolithophore species; reduced calcification under acidification / CAP perturbation | Reissner (1946): point-load stiffness of a thin shallow spherical shell k = 4 E h^2 / (R sqrt(3 (1 - nu^2))); reconstructed_in_script: 3D V/R c-axis ring with exact orthogonality, T-shaped hammer-element rosette across morphotypes A/B/C/R and an acidification / CAP ablation control, 12-taxon L_d(N_seg) scaling table, spherical coccosphere Voronoi / Euler packing with a prescribed 2.36x buckling amplification, elliptical polar DoG spoke segmentation of the vendored SEM micrograph | Pass 3: spherical-Voronoi suture network, reduced lumped-plate FE flat-punch nanoindentation with Coulomb + organic-interlock slide thresholds, plate bending fracture and cascade arrest tests, sigma_lock x overlap regime map; anisotropic vesicle rim tension law b/a = (2 + lambda)/(1 + 2 lambda) with an area-conserving contour relaxation and lambda* inferred from the SEM aspect ratio; transfer_boundary: The contact model is a lumped network (one radial DOF per coccolith), not a continuum 3D FEM with Hertzian punch contact; E_cell, p_turgor, mu, sigma_lock, sigma_f, alpha_p, phi_res are order-of-magnitude `model_assumption` constants and no number is quoted from Jaya et al. (2016); the v2 2.36x amplification is not reproduced (model protection ratio ~1e4, measuring shedding rather than buckling) | lambda* = 1.656 is a calibration to the hand-annotated SEM ellipse (92 x 78 px), not an independent measurement of vesicle rim tension anisotropy; only the normal Laplace balance is imposed | The 12-taxon 'observed' L_d column equals the formula prediction to the rounding digit, so r = 1.0000 is a self-consistency check, not a validation against measured taxa; does_not_claim: Continuum fracture mechanics of calcite plates, measured interlock shear strength, independent vesicle rim tension data, detection of the SEM ellipse from pixels (centre, semi-axes and tilt are annotations), or verification of the Jaya 2016 / Walker 2018 venue-DOI pairs and the Reissner 1946 DOI (offline round)]" ;
        ns1:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1002/sapm194625180>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/356516a0>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/ncomms11904>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-018-04168-9>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1098/rspb.1993.0073> ;
        ns1:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette-code-traceability>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-coccolith-emiliania-calcite-rosette-model-fidelity>,
