    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock> a ns1:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Diaz-Cuadros et al. (2020, 2023) & Matsuda et al. (2020) human pluripotent stem-cell segmentation clock and metabolic tempo scaling model faithfully reproduces Homo sapiens vs Mus musculus (hPSC-derived presomitic mesoderm / axioloid somite organoid) morphology" ;
        dct:description "The simulation script(s) 2019-diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Homo sapiens vs Mus musculus (hPSC-derived presomitic mesoderm / axioloid somite organoid) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 80.0/100, audit 2026-10-19-human-somite-organoid-clock-audit-v3) and the assessments." ;
        dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2019-diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock.py> ;
        ns1:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2019-diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock.py; output: docs/media/human_somite_organoid_clock_comparison.png; organism: Homo sapiens vs Mus musculus (hPSC-derived presomitic mesoderm / axioloid somite organoid); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/d58a084; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0; spec_fingerprint: dc5fc9fc0d0a3efa51f3e2df8dff0c42308ff7921502f484af6294b4b564fb24; artifact_sha256: 9f51f92b46d6a341eea40af3bf94cfb9d643809033460182d5d2873b9bd4c2d2; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/human_somite_organoid_clock/human_somite_organoid_clock_reference.json=b045a3f334ced9d4..., datasets/human_somite_organoid_clock/human_somite_organoid_specimen.jpg=8b80971796cb29e2..., datasets/human_somite_organoid_clock/scout_manifest.json=a3af01b1b2956954...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-human-somite-organoid-clock-audit-v2; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Diaz-Cuadros et al. (2020) Nature 580:113-118: ~5.0 h (300 +/- 18 min) HES7-Achilles oscillations in human pluripotent stem-cell-derived presomitic mesoderm vs ~2.0 h (122 min) in mouse PSM | Matsuda et al. (2020) Science 369:1450-1455: species-specific HES7 intron splicing delay and protein/mRNA half-lives, not the hHES7 locus sequence, govern the ~2.5x human slowdown; intronless Hes7 abolishes oscillations | Diaz-Cuadros et al. (2023) Nature 613:550-557: mitochondrial ETC activity and cytosolic NAD+/NADH modulate translation rate and clock period (LbNOX acceleration ~228 min, azide/rotenone slowdown ~402 min) | Matsuda et al. (2020) Nature 580:124-129: a DAPT pulse followed by washout synchronises HES7 oscillations across hPSC-derived PSM cultures; Riedel-Kruse et al. (2007) Science: Notch inhibition desynchronises segmentation clock cells; Herrgen et al. (2010) Curr. Biol.: delayed intercellular coupling sets the collective period | Yamanaka et al. (2023) Nature 614:509-520 and Sanaki-Matsumiya et al. (2022) Nat. Commun. 13:2325: epithelial somite rosettes form only in Matrigel-embedded human axioloids / somitoids (qualitative); reconstructed_in_script: Delayed autoinhibitory HES7 TTFL RK2 DDE solver (mouse WT 122.00 min; rescaled 'human' cell 300.01 min), exact tempo-rescaling collapse across lambda in [1, 3] (max std 2.32e-13 nM), intronless-Hes7 subcritical collapse, and a 6-regime series whose per-regime tempo factors are hard-coded from the observed periods (Pearson r = 0.9999 is a calibration, not a prediction) | 6-species vertebrate clock allometry (r = 0.9970) from a vendored species table of delays/half-lives, a kinematic (not DDE-derived) axioloid phase-wave kymograph, and bilateral DoG somite segmentation on a chick embryo SEM (47.14 px mean spacing, CV 0.2010) | Pass 3: DLL1-Notch delay-coupled HES7 lattice (12 x 12 hex, eps = 0.25, tau_c = 0.8 T, 5 % tempo CV) through the DAPT pulse-washout protocol: R_0 = 0.19 -> R_pre = 0.40 after 5 coupled cycles; DAPT amplitude ratio 0.17; washout reset R = 0.9995; R retained after 6 cycles = 0.85 (coupled) vs 0.21 (coupling-ablated, lost at 3.0 cycles); T_coll = 298.2 min; in-phase stable for tau_c/T in [0.625, 0.95]; T_coll(tau_c) spans 235-417 min; R_end(eps) 0.26 -> 0.96 (eps 0 -> 0.25), 0.88 at 0.35 | Pass 3: reduced 2D cell-centre Matrigel rosette model: P_rad = -0.08 (0 %) -> 0.99 (10 %), epithelial fraction 0 -> 0.67, aggregate radius 85 -> 28 um, Matrigel sweep Spearman rho = 0.94; transfer_boundary: Single-cell / lattice HES7 DDE kinetics are compared with a chick (Gallus gallus) dorsal SEM, not with a human axioloid image; the 47.14 px 'reference' spacing is the script's own measurement recorded in the dataset JSON | tau_c = 0.8 T (240 min) is an assumption from delayed-coupling-theory stability, not a human measurement; the DAPT basal promoter fraction b = 0.1 and the competitive-promoter gate (synthesis and threshold both scaled by (1 - eps) + 2 eps S) are modelling reductions | Matrigel stiffness kappa = 0.01 min^-1 per % and the polarisation / constriction rate constants are phenomenological; the rosette reference values (P_rad = 1, contrast = 1) are geometric ideals, not measured organoid morphometrics; does_not_claim: Prediction of the LbNOX / azide / hHES7-swap periods from independently measured kinetics (they are encoded); 3D actomyosin apical-constriction FEM; Matrigel rheology; measured human Notch coupling delay; Floquet/stability analysis of the coupled DDE beyond the numerical lattice scan]" ;
        ns1:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0960-9822(03)00534-7>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cub.2010.06.034>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-022-29967-1>,
