            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-diaza-human-somite-organoid-clock-specimen-match> ;
        ns1:weightOfEvidence 8e-01 .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-douady-magnetic-drop-phyllotaxis> a ns1:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Douady & Couder (1992, 1996) self-organized magnetic-drop phyllotaxis & imperfect pitchfork cascade faithfully reproduces Pinus sp. conifer seed cone & botanical shoot apical meristem (SAM) morphology" ;
        dct:description "The simulation script(s) 1992-douady-magnetic-drop-phyllotaxis.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Pinus sp. conifer seed cone & botanical shoot apical meristem (SAM) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 90.2/100, audit 2026-10-19-magnetic-drop-phyllotaxis-audit-v3) and the assessments." ;
        dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/1992-douady-magnetic-drop-phyllotaxis.py> ;
        ns1:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/1992-douady-magnetic-drop-phyllotaxis.py; output: docs/media/magnetic_drop_phyllotaxis_comparison.png; organism: Pinus sp. conifer seed cone & botanical shoot apical meristem (SAM); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/d58a084; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0; spec_fingerprint: 045b0921b1b4726ce33d0ec3190a3812d349153acf150593c5bf6c01da8f1e43; artifact_sha256: 09cbec33b6c20133934e29b9b7d5f3a8061d3f6cb4e1ddb93832f9db58f2db6d; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/magnetic_drop_phyllotaxis/conifer_cone_specimen.jpg=7bcb68e856d4db53..., datasets/magnetic_drop_phyllotaxis/magnetic_drop_phyllotaxis_reference.json=9ae33106a0fea23f..., datasets/magnetic_drop_phyllotaxis/paper_citations.bib=2c3aa1ec0e4c53de...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-magnetic-drop-phyllotaxis-audit-v2; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Douady & Couder (1992) Phys. Rev. Lett. 68:2098-2101 iterative magnetic-dipole repulsion energy E(phi) = sum_{k>=1} d_k(phi, phi_{n-k})^{-3} on a circular rim r = R_0 with linear dish advection r_k = R_0(1 + kG) controlled by the plastochron ratio G = V T / R_0; Figs. 1-2 dish regimes (1,1), (2,3), (3,5), (5,8), (8,13) and a metastable Lucas (4,7) | Douady & Couder (1992) Fig. 3 & (1996) J. Theor. Biol. 178:255-274 Secs. 3-4: supercritical (1,1)->(1,2) pitchfork of the iterated map, imperfect pitchfork cascade along the Fibonacci branch -> 137.508 deg, disconnected Lucas branch -> 99.502 deg, and nearest-neighbour contact parastichies on the van Iterson lattice; reconstructed_in_script: Exact static Hessian fold (G_fold = 0.773484 exp / 2.514560 lin) AND dynamical pitchfork (G_c1 = 0.859019 exp full chain / 3.631432 lin 2-drop) roots, the EMERGENT threshold of the unclamped iterated map (G_c1^emp = 0.8595 by bisection), the regular-spiral zero-force locus F(G, dphi) = 0, and adiabatic continuation along both Fibonacci (r = 0.99999, RMSE = 0.065 deg, contact pairs 9/10 table rows) and Lucas (RMSE = 0.141 deg) branches | Nearest-neighbour contact parastichy pairs on the true radii r_k = exp(kG) (Delaunay census kept as a secondary, biased extractor), memory-depth sweep N_mem in {1,2,3,5,8,13,21,45}, gamma in {1,3,5} universality, and simulated divergence / pair at the six tabulated dish regimes (RMSE 0.141 deg, 6/6 pairs) | Reciprocal-lattice inversion m*alpha + omega_m*G = 2*pi*j_m of the sub-bin (5, 8) log-polar FFT peaks of `conifer_cone_specimen.jpg` giving alpha_emp = 138.03 deg and G_emp = 0.0308, validated on a synthetic log-polar image of the simulated G = 0.06 lattice (0.014 deg / 0.06 % recovery error); transfer_boundary: Exponential meristem advection r_k = R_0 exp(kG) is displayed in the log-radial projection rho = 1 + ln(r/R_0) = 1 + kG, which coincides with the PRL 1992 silicone-oil dish geometry; the mature cone's apparent radial law fits the linear dish law better (R^2 0.977) than the exponential law (R^2 0.899), and its lattice is not perfectly log-periodic (closure residual 2.2 bins), so G_emp = 0.031 is an effective, not a developmental, plastochron ratio | The 'observed' per-regime divergence means in the reference table are regime-level readings of Douady & Couder (1992) Figs. 1-2 and text, not digitised data with uncertainties; the dish-regime RMSE of 0.141 deg should be read against that provenance; does_not_claim: Subcellular PIN1 polar auxin efflux carrier trafficking or continuous reaction-diffusion PDE dynamics on the meristem (Slot 033 Jönsson et al. 2006 / Smith et al. 2006); 3D photogrammetric or micro-CT cone reconstruction (the specimen analysis is a single 2D apical photograph of a 3D cone); a scale-level segmentation of the cone (the DoG detections over-count by ~2x and are not used at lattice level)]; other sources: Mathematische und mikroskopisch-anatomische Studien über Blattstellungen, nebst Betrachtungen über den Schalenbau der Miliolinen <https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/bibliography/9466>" ;
        ns1:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1006/jtbi.1996.0024>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1006/jtbi.1996.0025>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.68.2098>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1209/0295-5075/14/6/006> ;
        ns1:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-douady-magnetic-drop-phyllotaxis-code-traceability>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-douady-magnetic-drop-phyllotaxis-model-fidelity>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-douady-magnetic-drop-phyllotaxis-morphometric-validation>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-douady-magnetic-drop-phyllotaxis-overall>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-douady-magnetic-drop-phyllotaxis-parameter-expressivity>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-douady-magnetic-drop-phyllotaxis-repro-package>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-douady-magnetic-drop-phyllotaxis-source-traceability>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-douady-magnetic-drop-phyllotaxis-specimen-match> ;
        ns1:weightOfEvidence 9.02e-01 .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis> a ns1:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Dubrulle & Pourquié (2001, 2004) FGF8 mRNA decay wavefront and determination front positioning in vertebrate somitogenesis, with Goldbeter (2007) RA/FGF8 bistable switch and 2D cell-based PSM strip faithfully reproduces Gallus gallus (chick embryo presomitic mesoderm & paraxial somites) morphology" ;
        dct:description "The simulation script(s) 2003-dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Gallus gallus (chick embryo presomitic mesoderm & paraxial somites) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 86.2/100, audit 2026-10-19-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-audit-v3) and the assessments." ;
        dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2003-dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis.py> ;
        ns1:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2003-dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis.py; output: docs/media/fgf8_wavefront_somitogenesis_comparison.png; organism: Gallus gallus (chick embryo presomitic mesoderm & paraxial somites); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/d58a084; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0; spec_fingerprint: c932f4a1dd2d2a7154d419f019c4a647891c78e7cc462bb8f1d3ef6cb210100e; artifact_sha256: 61b31ffd1e1b1344790d330a58240354a24d2ec245281da77adea61593631ff4; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/fgf8_wavefront_somitogenesis/chick_somite_psm_specimen.jpg=8b80971796cb29e2..., datasets/fgf8_wavefront_somitogenesis/fgf8_wavefront_somitogenesis_reference.json=0a4d2aabb27a874d..., datasets/fgf8_wavefront_somitogenesis/scout_manifest.json=a38a686592f1ffd0...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-audit-v2; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Dubrulle & Pourquie (2004) Nature 427:419-422 cell-autonomous fgf8 mRNA decay gradient m(x) = m_0 exp(-k_d x / v_g) generated by tailbud-restricted transcription and axis elongation | Dubrulle, McGrew & Pourquie (2001) Cell 106:219-232 determination front threshold positioning x* = (v_g/k_d) ln(m_0/m_crit) and ectopic FGF8 bead / SU5402 somite size perturbations | Goldbeter, Gonze & Pourquie (2007) Dev. Dyn. 236:1495-1508 bistability of the RA -| FGF -> Cyp26 -| RA double-negative loop defining a sharp determination threshold; reconstructed_in_script: Characteristic-upwind 1D advection-decay PDE solver dm/dt + v_g dm/dx = -k_d m (L2 relative error 0.0009 vs analytical exponential) | Lab-frame FGF8 wavefront-gated somite boundary simulator across wild-type, ectopic FGF8 bead (S_ant = 97.5 um, S_post = 202.5 um), SU5402 (S = 215.0 um) and k_d = 0 ablation control (N = 0 somites) - with the perturbation shifts entered as constants, not derived | Goldbeter-type 3-variable RA/FGF8/Cyp26 switch coupled to the mRNA gradient: saddle-nodes m_SN_lo = 0.184 / m_SN_hi = 0.546, hysteretic cell-trajectory front x_sw = 720.4 um, transition width 198 um vs 792 um, reverse switch at m = 0.675 | 2D cell-based strip with explicit progenitor division and mRNA partitioning: exported level 0.994 vs closed form 1.000, gradient length 370.5 vs 360.7 um, front 698.8 +/- 7.0 um vs lambda_m ln(m_exit/m_crit) = 694.4 um, S_2D = 148.2 um, dilution shift 276-286 um vs closed form 271 um | Bilateral dorsal somite row DoG peak and inter-somitic cleft segmentation on chick_somite_psm_specimen.jpg (48.47 px mean spacing, symmetry ratio 0.9606); transfer_boundary: 1D anteroposterior chick presomitic mesoderm axis mapped to dorsal vertebrate SEM somite rows of a Wikimedia specimen whose species is labelled avian/vertebrate, not confirmed as Gallus gallus | Goldbeter switch functional forms follow the 2007 paper but the dimensionless parameter values (K_A = 0.18, K_I = 0.6, k_C = 2, n = 4, tau_sw = 10 min) are this script's bistable-regime choice; the switch is evaluated along a 1D cell trajectory and is NOT embedded in the 2D strip | 2D strip: PSM cells do not divide, all elongation comes from progenitor division (no Benazeraf 2010 motility gradient), rows are coupled only through FGF8 smoothing (no mechanics); does_not_claim: Reproduction of the Goldbeter et al. (2007) parameter table or bifurcation figures; 3D somite epithelialization mechanics; a derivation of the FGF8-bead / SU5402 / electroporation somite-size shifts from the switch dynamics (they remain constants in the lab-frame simulator and the reference JSON)]" ;
        ns1:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1002/dvdy.21193>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0092-8674(01)00437-8>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ydbio.2006.01.018>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature02332>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature09151> ;
        ns1:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-code-traceability>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-model-fidelity>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-morphometric-validation>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-overall>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-parameter-expressivity>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-repro-package>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-source-traceability>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-dubrulle-fgf8-wavefront-somitogenesis-specimen-match> ;
        ns1:weightOfEvidence 8.62e-01 .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-economou-palate-ruguga-turing> a ns1:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Economou et al. (2012) FGF10/FGF7-SHH activator-inhibitor Turing stripe mechanism at mammalian palatal growth zones, coupled to quasi-static epithelial plate ridge elevation faithfully reproduces Mammalian secondary hard palate (Mus musculus E12.0-E15.5 & Equus caballus Rugae palatinae) morphology" ;
        dct:description "The simulation script(s) 2012-economou-palate-ruguga-turing.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Mammalian secondary hard palate (Mus musculus E12.0-E15.5 & Equus caballus Rugae palatinae) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 91.2/100, audit 2026-10-19-palate-ruguga-turing-audit-v3) and the assessments." ;
        dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2012-economou-palate-ruguga-turing.py> ;
        ns1:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2012-economou-palate-ruguga-turing.py; output: docs/media/palate_ruguga_turing_comparison.png; organism: Mammalian secondary hard palate (Mus musculus E12.0-E15.5 & Equus caballus Rugae palatinae); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/d58a084; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0; spec_fingerprint: 14f358af9d03b3980dc4c8f810f623b9c4299743ce9b93b063da6d1923819d25; artifact_sha256: 716777da0d6ff0938c1e277351c739fbfbed969691b961cf0e467f02ef0dce32; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/palate_ruguga_turing/palate_ridge_mechanics_reference.json=2e673658c9722aeb..., datasets/palate_ruguga_turing/palate_rugae_specimen.jpg=a38f6c053ffe9048..., datasets/palate_ruguga_turing/palate_ruguga_turing_reference.json=e76e670dd50c86fe..., datasets/palate_ruguga_turing/paper_citations.bib=fd020997fb3c2db0..., datasets/palate_ruguga_turing/scout_manifest.json=f0a345a5c9039e78...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-palate-ruguga-turing-audit-v2; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Economou et al. (2012): mesenchymal FGF10/FGF7 (activator) and epithelial SHH (inhibitor) form a Turing reaction-diffusion system at the rugae growth zone anterior to ruga 8; rugae are added sequentially 8 -> 1..7b as the palate elongates; a coronal explant cut across the growth zone yields bifurcations / spots whereas a sagittal cut preserves stripes; cyclopamine broadens and FGF10 beads / Spry2-/-;Spry4+/- compact the pattern; Shh expression marks each morphological ruga (Fig. 1) | Pantalacci et al. (2008), Welsh & O'Brien (2009): staging of sequential ruga addition in the RGZ anterior to ruga 8 | Turing (1952): diffusion-driven instability of a two-component activator-inhibitor system | Landau & Lifshitz (1986): equilibrium equation of a thin elastic plate and its bending stiffness; reconstructed_in_script: 2x2 Jacobian and dispersion relation with lambda_c = 3.2221; 1D and 2D RD solvers with growth-zone envelope; 9-stage L/lambda_c intercalation count; 6-condition perturbation suite; DoG segmentation of the specimen shelves (15 / 16 rugae); Pass 3: quasi-static Kirchhoff plate on a Winkler foundation driven by beta max(A, 0), solved exactly by DCT-II, optional chi_m feedback, ridge count / phase-offset / duty-cycle morphometrics, kappa / k_f / chi_m sweeps, 2 Lean 4 theorems on the transfer stiffness; transfer_boundary: The plate constants kappa = 0.05, T = 0.2, k_f = 1, beta = 1 are dimensionless modelling assumptions (no offline-verifiable measurement of embryonic palatal epithelial stiffness); only the sign-preservation, wavelength-transfer and monotone-attenuation predictions are scored, not ridge heights in micrometres | The specimen is an adult horse palate photograph; its duty cycle (0.49 / 0.44) is compared qualitatively with the simulated mouse-embryo ridges (0.42) after the same peak_widths estimator; DoG smoothing broadens the specimen crests | The 2D RD solver integrates on a rescaled x spacing dx_eff = dx (q / 1.24), so the realised grid wavelength (3.37) differs from the dispersion lambda_c (3.22) that Panels B / D use; the plate solver uses the physical dx; does_not_claim: A 3D finite-element simulation of epithelial invagination with large deflections or nonlinear growth; calibrated ridge heights; emergence of the coronal-cut / bead / cyclopamine phenotypes from identical initial conditions (they are seeded by condition-specific initial patterns at L606-633); mechanics-dependent phenotypes compared with a published mechanical perturbation]; other sources: Theory of Elasticity (Course of Theoretical Physics, Vol. 7), 3rd edition — Secs. 11-14, equilibrium of thin plates <https://www.sciencedirect.com/book/9780080570693/theory-of-elasticity>" ;
