        ns1:weightOfEvidence 8.04e-01 .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-gierer-hydra-activator-inhibitor> a ns1:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Gierer & Meinhardt (1972) & Meinhardt (1993, 2012) Hydra vulgaris activator-inhibitor morphogenesis, head regeneration, tentacle ring & coupled three-system 3D shell faithfully reproduces Freshwater cnidarian polyp (Hydra vulgaris): apical hypostome polarity, surgical head regeneration, sub-hypostomal tentacle ring and basal foot on a specimen-shaped body shell morphology" ;
        dct:description "The simulation script(s) 1972-gierer-hydra-activator-inhibitor.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Freshwater cnidarian polyp (Hydra vulgaris): apical hypostome polarity, surgical head regeneration, sub-hypostomal tentacle ring and basal foot on a specimen-shaped body shell specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 89.5/100, audit 2026-10-19-hydra-activator-inhibitor-audit-v3) and the assessments." ;
        dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/4d5512d/1972-gierer-hydra-activator-inhibitor.py> ;
        ns1:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/4d5512d/1972-gierer-hydra-activator-inhibitor.py; output: docs/media/hydra_activator_inhibitor_comparison.png; organism: Freshwater cnidarian polyp (Hydra vulgaris): apical hypostome polarity, surgical head regeneration, sub-hypostomal tentacle ring and basal foot on a specimen-shaped body shell; checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/4d5512d; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0; spec_fingerprint: 49a5051749b0c67e34c6eeaa4fb8201bc071879dc58596403d8aa74086bc42c4; artifact_sha256: e0c4e97130d2627ad31b6cf098d20e0b26bcc7658a7b2fcd94ffe4d9c9d8bc3d; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/hydra_activator_inhibitor/hydra_activator_inhibitor_reference.json=21cb10a1cf38b4c9..., datasets/hydra_activator_inhibitor/hydra_vulgaris_specimen.jpg=007d127bcfa8501d..., datasets/hydra_activator_inhibitor/paper_citations.bib=49b5c0a5531a00fe..., datasets/hydra_activator_inhibitor/scout_manifest.json=b57d0d923283daaf...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-hydra-activator-inhibitor-audit-v2; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Gierer & Meinhardt (1972) Eqs. (15a)-(15b): short-range autocatalytic activator a^2/h with long-range inhibitor; a shallow source gradient yields a single apical peak (Fig. 2); removing the apical half lets the basal fragment regenerate a peak at its cut end (Fig. 3) | Meinhardt (1993): hypostome, tentacles and foot are generated by separate activator-inhibitor systems coupled through a slowly adapting source density; tentacle activation requires a high source density and is locally suppressed by the head activator (so tentacles form at the border of the hypostome); the foot forms where the source density is lowest; fragments regenerate a hypostome and a new tentacle ring | Meinhardt (2012): review of the same three-system scheme including size-dependent and regeneration behaviour; reconstructed_in_script: Exact homogeneous steady state, Jacobian, d_c = (sqrt(2)+1)^2 and dispersion relation; 1D polar column (N = 40) with apical dominance; surgical bisection with 87.4 % head recovery; periodic 64-cell tentacle ring (6 peaks) with equal-diffusion control, diffusivity-ratio and domain-length sweeps; computer-vision segmentation of the vendored specimen (6 tentacles) | Pass 3: the specimen's body-column radius profile, tentacle-attachment ring and inter-tentacle spacing; a finite-difference Laplace-Beltrami shell (90 x 64) on that surface of revolution; reduced head / tentacle / foot Gierer-Meinhardt loops with basal inhibitor production (analytic firing threshold w_c = 0.1633) and a head-raised source density; kappa_a sweep with kappa_a = 0 ablation, body-length sweep, amputation at L/2 with head/ring regeneration timeline; 14 quantitative measurements; transfer_boundary: The three-system couplings (Hill gating sigma^8/(0.6^8 + sigma^8), suppression 1/(1 + kappa_a a), foot drive 1/(1 + (sigma/0.03)^2), sigma dynamics c_sigma a - mu_sigma (sigma - sigma_0)) and all coefficients are this script's reduced choices calibrated to reproduce the qualitative Meinhardt (1993) layout; they are not digitised from the paper's appendix equations | The shell body length L = 90 cells is a declared scale calibration (model tentacle spacing ~8.1 cells vs specimen spacing 0.084 of body length), so the tentacle COUNT (7 vs specimen 6) is a geometric consequence, not an independent prediction; the ring axial offset (0.111 vs 0.070 +- 0.081), uniform hypostome cap, basal foot and head-before-ring regeneration order are uncalibrated predictions | The 1D ring (N_ring = 64, lambda ~10.7 cells, 6 peaks) and the shell ring (lambda ~8.1 cells) use the same D_b, D_c but select different wavelengths; the 1D '6 tentacles' therefore also rests on an (undeclared in v2) circumference calibration | Specimen references are measured on a 2D projection of a tilted, contracted polyp and used as bands, not exact targets; there is one specimen and one seed; does_not_claim: A finite-element mesh, wound closure or tissue remodelling (the regenerated head on the wide cut surface is a localised spot, CV_theta = 0.95, not a cap), Meinhardt's tentacle-before-hypostome regeneration order (the model gives t_head < t_ring), the foot -> source-density negative feedback, budding, or a quantitative size series for tentacle number]" ;
        ns1:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1006/dbio.1993.1138>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1007/BF00289234>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1242/jcs.15.2.321>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1387/ijdb.113483hm> ;
        ns1:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-gierer-hydra-activator-inhibitor-code-traceability>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-gierer-hydra-activator-inhibitor-model-fidelity>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-gierer-hydra-activator-inhibitor-morphometric-validation>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-gierer-hydra-activator-inhibitor-overall>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-gierer-hydra-activator-inhibitor-parameter-expressivity>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-gierer-hydra-activator-inhibitor-repro-package>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-gierer-hydra-activator-inhibitor-source-traceability>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-gierer-hydra-activator-inhibitor-specimen-match> ;
        ns1:weightOfEvidence 8.95e-01 .

