    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation> a ns1:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Hannezo et al. (2017) Cell & Scheele et al. (2017) Nature unifying theory of branching morphogenesis via branching and annihilating random walks (BARW) faithfully reproduces Mus musculus (mouse pubertal mammary gland, embryonic metanephric kidney, embryonic pancreas, and salivary gland ductal networks) morphology" ;
        dct:description "The simulation script(s) 2017-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Mus musculus (mouse pubertal mammary gland, embryonic metanephric kidney, embryonic pancreas, and salivary gland ductal networks) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 88.9/100, audit 2026-10-19-branching-random-walk-annihilation-audit-v3) and the assessments." ;
        dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/74d06a5c/2017-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation.py> ;
        ns1:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/74d06a5c/2017-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation.py; output: docs/media/branching_random_walk_annihilation_comparison.png; organism: Mus musculus (mouse pubertal mammary gland, embryonic metanephric kidney, embryonic pancreas, and salivary gland ductal networks); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/74d06a5c; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0; spec_fingerprint: 0705016d88b40abfd432a650c7382c2c601d9cfa65577d8735df8bfc6facc377; artifact_sha256: 50078c445a1f7e01ce6cc208f501bd1f251962f63f7798c0eec4e4bb723f1dfe; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/branching_random_walk_annihilation/barw_3d_ecm_clonal_reference.json=c716e3a9cce08d6f..., datasets/branching_random_walk_annihilation/branching_random_walk_annihilation_reference.json=d85ad5c91bd80050..., datasets/branching_random_walk_annihilation/mouse_branched_ductal_network_specimen.jpg=d8946f47dcc4d313..., datasets/branching_random_walk_annihilation/paper_citations.bib=d777ef20e9e92830..., datasets/branching_random_walk_annihilation/scout_manifest.json=8b04ea70e9991ba0...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-branching-random-walk-annihilation-audit-v2; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Hannezo et al. (2017): ductal trees of mammary gland, kidney and pancreas are self-organised by a branching-and-annihilating random walk of active tips (A -> 2A at rate k_b, A -> A + I trail deposition, A + I -> I annihilation within R_a), giving N_term = N_branch + 1, q_branch -> 1/2, a critical Galton-Watson subtree law P(S) ~ S^(-3/2), a universal generational q(g) relaxation and a travelling-wave mean-field with homeostatic duct density i_inf = k_b/k_a | Scheele et al. (2017): mammary TEB stem cells follow neutral drift (equipotent, Moran-type) so clone fates are set by TEB bifurcation/termination; clone-size distributions inherit the tree statistics | Bordeu et al. (2023): salivary-gland BARW in an inflating 3D domain; domain growth and local geometry, not tip-intrinsic rules, set branch density | Moran (1958), Klein & Simons (2011): neutral birth-death drift is a martingale in the labelled fraction with variance 2k(N-k)/N^2 per step; reconstructed_in_script: 2D off-lattice BARW tree, 1D Fisher-KPP mean-field wave, exact Catalan critical GW pmf, 3-organ universality collapse, R_a perturbation/ablation suite, specimen bud/junction segmentation (all Pass 2) | Pass 3: 3D off-lattice BARW in a cylindrical fat pad and a spherical (optionally inflating) capsule with a nematic ECM alignment torque, a length-weighted nematic order parameter S, a paired-seed lambda sweep with a true-isotropic control, an inflation sweep, a birth-vertex annihilation-exemption rule, a Moran neutral-drift clonal model inside TEBs with hypergeometric splits at bifurcations and label inheritance by ducts, 64 mosaic replicates and 600 single-cell clones, 6 additional measurements with reference values, 2 new self-test suites and 3 new Lean theorems; transfer_boundary: The 3D fat pad is a cylinder, not Bordeu's flattened slab; only the spherical capsule inflates and already-deposited ducts are NOT advected with the domain; no Bordeu figure or table value is reproduced numerically — only the qualitative monotonic S(lambda) and inflation ordering of L_total; S reference values are the theoretical 0 / 1 extremes | N_TEB = 64 and the Moran rate rho = 1 per unit duct length are free parameters (real TEBs have O(10^2) cells); no Scheele clone-size histogram is reproduced numerically — only the exact martingale f_bar = f_0 and the S^(-3/2) tail inherited from the tree | The 1D PDE carries uncited calibration constants (1.82 k_a, 0.55 v_0, v_drift = 0.35 v_0) tuned so the wake plateau matches k_b/k_a; the i_inf agreement is therefore a self-calibration, not an independent test | The SHA-pinned specimen is a Wikimedia whole-mount of an embryonic branched gland, not a pubertal mammary TEB network; its reference values (N_term = 34, r/R_max = 0.783) are the segmentation's own outputs; does_not_claim: Quantitative reproduction of any Hannezo/Scheele/Bordeu figure or table beyond the reference JSON tables; advected-duct inflation; a slab fat-pad geometry; multi-seed statistics for the 3D lambda sweep; Scheele clone-size histograms; a mammary-specific specimen]" ;
        ns1:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2017.08.026>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1017/S0305004100033193>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature21060>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-023-39124-x>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.060103>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.147645> ;
        ns1:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation-code-traceability>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation-model-fidelity>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation-morphometric-validation>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation-overall>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation-parameter-expressivity>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation-repro-package>,
