    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-he-drosophila-ventral-furrow> a ns1:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Conte et al. (2012), Martin et al. (2009) & He et al. (2014) Drosophila ventral furrow invagination biomechanics faithfully reproduces Drosophila melanogaster (gastrulating cellular blastoderm embryo) morphology" ;
        dct:description "The simulation script(s) 2012-he-drosophila-ventral-furrow.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Drosophila melanogaster (gastrulating cellular blastoderm embryo) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 89.9/100, audit 2026-10-19-drosophila-ventral-furrow-audit-v3) and the assessments." ;
        dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/7e4f207/2012-he-drosophila-ventral-furrow.py> ;
        ns1:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/7e4f207/2012-he-drosophila-ventral-furrow.py; output: docs/media/drosophila_ventral_furrow_comparison.png; organism: Drosophila melanogaster (gastrulating cellular blastoderm embryo); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/7e4f207; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0; spec_fingerprint: 231d3bda8cca542298a1fb5749dc44c894794b8e0ed35252a225b4a9fa7bd0aa; artifact_sha256: 1fc501631ab9c6ab13eaf2ac9a771c53029337b6fdb3ddd5880ed8f4211d9a76; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/drosophila_ventral_furrow/ap_shell_stokes_reference.json=8f196893e04e6457..., datasets/drosophila_ventral_furrow/drosophila_ventral_furrow_reference.json=5c6f1960cef1be19..., datasets/drosophila_ventral_furrow/drosophila_ventral_furrow_specimen.jpg=f426366f7ede436d..., datasets/drosophila_ventral_furrow/scout_manifest.json=0c6354ab1d934ba3...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-drosophila-ventral-furrow-audit-v2; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Conte, Munoz, Baum & Miodownik (2012) PLoS ONE 7(11):e49973 incompressible finite-element cross-sectional decomposition showing apical constriction alone produces only a shallow groove (16.5 um) with over-elongated cells (48.1 um), whereas synergy with basal relaxation, lateral shortening, and ectodermal pushing drives full invagination (41.0 um) | Martin, Kaschube & Wieschaus (2009) Nature 457:495-499 Twist-stabilized ratcheted Myosin-II pulses (T_pulse = 82 s) vs unratcheted relaxation recoil; He et al. (2014) Nature 508:392-396 apically driven hydrodynamic cytoplasmic flow that carries nuclei basally as passive tracers during cell lengthening | Sweeton et al. (1991) / Leptin & Grunewald (1990): the ventral furrow spans roughly the mesoderm primordium (~0.15-0.80 EL) and germband extension begins as the furrow closes (approximate, not digitised here); reconstructed_in_script: 64-cell 2D incompressible trapezoidal blastoderm ring enclosed by the vitelline membrane (R_vit = 83.2 um, A_0 = 262.4 um^2), RK2 integration of the ratcheted Myosin-II apical-width pulse ODE, 6-regime benchmark and 15x15 (r_twist x sigma_synergy) morphospace; NOTE: regime depth and cell height are target-pinned interpolants, not emergent mechanics | [Pass 3] Reduced 3D AP shell: Donnell/Winkler elastic line ell_B^4 D'''' - ell_N^2 D'' + k_rel(z) D = D_2D(t) chi_meso(z) on the prolate ellipsoid (exact kappa_z, kappa_theta; k_pole/k_eq = 13x), driven by the ring depth at each snapshot with a germband-extension tension ramp, swept into a 65x81 theta x z shell mesh; sweeps over ell_N (0-150 um, ablation ratio 0.53, monotone) and a/b (1.5-4.0) | [Pass 3] Variable-viscosity Stokes flow (stream-function form, 35x192 grid, 6,110 unknowns) inside the Phase-I lengthening mesoderm cell with incompressible-trapezoid boundary kinematics, a 50x-viscosity nucleus (v_nuc/v_cyto = 0.983, rigid-body CV 0.004), exact affine verification (L2 8.1e-13) and a Phase-I nuclear trajectory (4.5 um basal displacement over 16.2 um lengthening) | Automated 4-stage confocal cross-section segmentation and ventral apical Myosin-II red enrichment analysis on drosophila_ventral_furrow_specimen.jpg (DV/ML = 1.0496 -> 0.9217, MyoII enrichment = 1.63x, trajectory r = 0.9993); transfer_boundary: The AP coupling is a 1D elastic line with a curvature-weighted Winkler foundation and a kinematic circumferential sweep; ell_B = 22 um and the WT ell_N ramp to 30 um are model assumptions not measured in any cited paper, and N_GB is not calibrated to Lye et al. (2015) ablation recoil | The Stokes solve is 2D on a fixed rectangle frozen at t = 1.8 min with velocity (not stress) boundary data; nucleus size/position are order-of-magnitude values; the He et al. (2014) comparison is the qualitative passive-tracer ratio ~1, not a digitised velocity field | The 2D ring depth that drives both new layers is pinned to the Conte (2012) / Martin (2009) reference values at the last step, so the 6-regime r = 1.0000 is a consistency check of the calibration, not an independent prediction; does_not_claim: A 3D finite-element shell with coupled membrane/bending stresses, a moving-boundary (ALE) or 3D Stokes solve with cortical actomyosin stress boundary conditions, emergent (un-pinned) invagination depth from the viscous-vertex mechanics, or subcellular Rho1/Rok reaction-diffusion signaling]" ;
        ns1:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.bpj.2014.07.013>,
