        dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/58b898c/2004-hentschel-tgfb-fibronectin-limb.py> ;
        ns1:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/58b898c/2004-hentschel-tgfb-fibronectin-limb.py; output: docs/media/tgfb_fibronectin_limb_comparison.png; organism: Gallus gallus domesticus embryonic wing bud & high-density mesenchymal micromass (HH20 stylopod humerus -> HH24 zeugopod radius+ulna -> HH27 autopod digits II-IV); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/58b898c; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0; spec_fingerprint: 25a54774cc76963703511eae8cb9dc8b8fea2169f1c58b48380f2c9d1c3fe31f; artifact_sha256: f0533eb3a15144051abc88f164c957218c60b35cd76f3088949b7fd3d12be3e2; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/tgfb_fibronectin_limb/chick_limb_chondrogenesis_specimen.jpg=771e26f9fe8c813d..., datasets/tgfb_fibronectin_limb/kiskowski_ggh_cpm_reference.json=a7d13368e41d762a..., datasets/tgfb_fibronectin_limb/scout_manifest.json=c810bd77e66557c8..., datasets/tgfb_fibronectin_limb/tgfb_fibronectin_limb_reference.json=33d554e44b712e2b...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-tgfb-fibronectin-limb-audit-v2; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Hentschel et al. (2004): a 4-field TGF-beta activator / FGF-dependent inhibitor / fibronectin / mesenchymal-cell-density reaction-diffusion-haptotaxis system whose AER-FGF-modulated unstable wavenumber increases proximodistally, giving 1 -> 2 -> 3 skeletal elements | Kiskowski et al. (2004): discrete cells on a lattice with a continuous activator/inhibitor prepattern, activated cells deposit fibronectin and bind to it, producing autonomous condensations; Chaturvedi et al. (2005): the same scheme realised in a GGH cellular Potts framework (CompuCell) | Graner & Glazier (1992) / Glazier & Graner (1993): differential adhesion with J_dd < J_ld < J_ll < J_cM at T = 10 sorts cells; heterotypic boundary length decreases | Miura & Shiota (2000): exogenous TGF-beta2 fuses micromass condensations into bar-like patterns; anti-fibronectin treatment blocks condensation; reconstructed_in_script: Linear dispersion of the activator/inhibitor subsystem, 1D and 2D (x, z) pseudo-spectral IMEX integration of the 4-field system with zero-flux boundaries, 2D periodic micromass morphospace with volume-filling haptotaxis, dual negative controls, a GGH cellular Potts lattice coupled through the PDE's Hill switch and a two-way fibronectin field, four GGH regimes plus a wing-bud GGH run, specimen segmentation of a Gallus wing, 14 measurements, 5 Lean 4 theorems; transfer_boundary: Kiskowski et al. (2004) is a lattice-cell / biased-random-walk model, not a cellular Potts model; the GGH realisation follows Chaturvedi et al. (2005), as the Pass 2 remediation item requested, and the dataset JSON says so | The 1D stage and 2D wing continuum solutions are chemotactically collapsed (clip_fraction_R = 1.00 at fa = 11, 18; 0.52 at fa = 6; 0.193 in 2D): condensation counts are reproduced but amplitudes, std(R) and F-R correlations are clip-determined | GGH references are internal (continuum ratio, ablation value, adopted thresholds) because the cited discrete-model papers do not report the metrics used here; does_not_claim: A hexagonal nodular-spot micromass regime (both resolved continuum regimes are labyrinthine), a discrete stylopod condensation (GGH gives [0, 2, 3]), quantitative agreement with Kiskowski et al. (2004) condensation sizes, a sequential (exact-volume) cellular Potts update, 3D geometry, limb outgrowth, or cell division]" ;
        ns1:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1006/aama.2001.0721>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1006/jtbi.1996.0237>,
