    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-honda-dichotomous-tree-branching> a ns1:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Honda (1971) J. Theor. Biol. & Honda & Fisher (1978) Science 3D recursive dichotomous tree branching, effective leaf area optimization, Leonardo da Vinci pipe-model area conservation, and solar-elevation ray tracing of tiered crowns vs latitude faithfully reproduces Cornus controversa (Pagoda dogwood / wedding cake tree) & Terminalia catappa (Tropical almond pagoda tree) morphology" ;
        dct:description "The simulation script(s) 1976-honda-dichotomous-tree-branching.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Cornus controversa (Pagoda dogwood / wedding cake tree) & Terminalia catappa (Tropical almond pagoda tree) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 91.2/100, audit 2026-10-19-dichotomous-tree-branching-audit-v3) and the assessments." ;
        dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/1976-honda-dichotomous-tree-branching.py> ;
        ns1:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/1976-honda-dichotomous-tree-branching.py; output: docs/media/dichotomous_tree_branching_comparison.png; organism: Cornus controversa (Pagoda dogwood / wedding cake tree) & Terminalia catappa (Tropical almond pagoda tree); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/028758bc; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0; spec_fingerprint: 7cfa8b501a15c214e965ecf451b63af5fa8b3bb7f3a5e144483628cccc87fe3b; artifact_sha256: 581f4f616734e5fca1c57a025888323716a41e79137972f0611843524777aceb; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/dichotomous_tree_branching/cornus_controversa_tiered_crown_specimen.jpg=47cbd7225997789e..., datasets/dichotomous_tree_branching/dichotomous_tree_branching_reference.json=9b8cd89b9fa19fbf..., datasets/dichotomous_tree_branching/solar_tier_spacing_reference.json=640596fc8c3df302...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-dichotomous-tree-branching-audit-v2; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Honda (1971) J. Theor. Biol. 31(2):331-338 3D recursive vector-rotation tree architecture parameterized by daughter divergence angles (theta_1, theta_2), length contraction ratios (r_1, r_2), and vertical phyllotactic roll angle alpha = 137.5 deg in the local horizontal plane spanned by v and v x z_hat | Honda & Fisher (1978) Science 199(4331):888-890 & Fisher & Honda (1979) Am. J. Bot. 66:633-644 demonstration that empirical branching angles (theta_1 approx 24-32 deg, theta_2 approx 52-62 deg) and contraction ratios (r_1 = 0.90, r_2 = 0.70) in Terminalia catappa and Cornus controversa maximize non-overlapping effective leaf area A_eff / A_total across 5-branch horizontal whorls | Shinozaki et al. (1964) Jpn. J. Ecol. 14:97-105 pipe-model theory and Eloy (2011) Phys. Rev. Lett. 107:258101 wind-stress derivation of Leonardo da Vinci's cross-sectional area conservation d_parent^Delta = d_1^Delta + d_2^Delta (Delta = 2.0) | Campbell & Norman (1998) Ch. 11 solar geometry sin h = sin(phi) sin(delta) + cos(phi) cos(delta) cos(H) with Cooper (1969) declination delta = 23.45 sin(2 pi (284 + n)/365) and the Monsi & Saeki (1953) Beer-Lambert canopy extinction tau = exp(-LAI); reconstructed_in_script: Full Honda (1971) 3D rotation-matrix tree builder (`grow_honda_1971_3d_tree`) across 4 botanical crown archetypes (excurrent conifer, pagoda tiered Cornus, decurrent deliquescent Quercus, weeping pendulous Salix) over k = 6 orders (127 internodes, 64 terminal leaf clusters) | Honda & Fisher (1978) 5-whorl horizontal tier disk-union integration (`compute_effective_leaf_area_ratio`) and 2D (theta_1, theta_2) optimization surface (`evaluate_honda_fisher_optimization_surface`), Pearson r = 0.99782 against the vendored 8-regime benchmark curve, Terminalia (0.7739) and Cornus (0.7591) vs the collinear theta_1 = theta_2 = 0 ablation control (0.2001, 74.14% self-shading penalty) | Exact Leonardo da Vinci / Shinozaki pipe-model sapwood area conservation (sum d_{k,i}^2 / d_0^2 = 1.0000 across all 6 orders and 63 bifurcations) contrasted against Murray's cube law (Delta = 3.0) and untapered cylinder controls | Pass 3: diurnal/seasonal direct-beam sun paths at 6 latitudes (0, 15, 30, 45, 50.93 Meise, 60 deg N), a 7-tier stacked Honda & Fisher crown ray-traced tier-to-tier with Beer-Lambert tau_c^n attenuation (tau_c = exp(-2) = 0.135), annual beam light capture E(s/R) over 14 tier spacings, parameter-free 90% saturation spacing s_90/R = 1.832 (0 deg), 0.969 (45 deg), 0.850 (Meise), 0.710 (60 deg), ratio s_90(0)/s_90(45) = 1.89, and the specimen's projected tier spacing s/R = 0.376 +- 0.134 giving E = 0.747 at Meise vs 0.621 if transplanted to the equator | Computer-vision segmentation of the Pagoda Dogwood (Cornus controversa 'Variegata') specimen (`cornus_controversa_tiered_crown_specimen.jpg`, Botanic Garden Meise, 960x1280 px) detecting 7 horizontal pagoda foliage tiers, 25 Y-bifurcations with theta_1 = 22.40 +- 8.18 deg, theta_2 = 50.93 +- 14.23 deg, Leonardo area ratio 0.9533 +- 0.1705, and 6 inter-tier spacing pairs; transfer_boundary: 3D recursive vector-rotation internode skeletons and 2D horizontal whorl leaf-cluster disk unions mapped to optical crown stratigraphy and woody bifurcation geometry of Cornus controversa | The ray-traced 'tiered crown' is a stack of planar Honda & Fisher 5-whorl disk-union tiers with a uniform per-tier transmittance, not the 3D Honda (1971) internode skeleton of `grow_honda_1971_3d_tree`; light capture is direct beam only (no diffuse sky radiance, no leaf scattering, no penumbra), and the latitude prediction is validated against the null ratio 1.0 and self-consistency, not against measured tier spacings across latitudes | The Honda & Fisher benchmark curve, the specimen theta_1/theta_2/beta/tier references and the specimen s/R reference in the vendored JSON files are values previously produced by this script (regression anchors), not digitised figure values or independent measurements; does_not_claim: Cambial auxin-cytokinin molecular transport kinetics, turbulent eddy-resolvable wind-tunnel aeroelasticity at individual leaf blades, diffuse-sky or scattered-light radiative transfer, photosynthetic light-response curves, or a literature-anchored optimal tier spacing vs latitude]" ;
