        ns1:weightOfEvidence 9.18e-01 .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-ibrahim-vascular-angiogenesis-notch> a ns1:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Bentley, Gerhardt & Bates (2008) PLoS Comput. Biol., Hellström et al. (2007) Nature & Jakobsson et al. (2010) Nat. Cell Biol. VEGF-VEGFR2-Dll4-Notch1 tip/stalk salt-and-pepper lateral inhibition and angiogenic sprouting, coupled to lumenized Poiseuille flow, wall-shear pruning and arteriovenous specification (Pass 3) faithfully reproduces Homo sapiens / Mus musculus (Retinal & embryonic sprouting vascular endothelium) morphology" ;
        dct:description "The simulation script(s) 2021-ibrahim-vascular-angiogenesis-notch.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Homo sapiens / Mus musculus (Retinal & embryonic sprouting vascular endothelium) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 87.7/100, audit 2026-10-19-vascular-angiogenesis-notch-audit-v3) and the assessments." ;
        dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/2021-ibrahim-vascular-angiogenesis-notch.py> ;
        ns1:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/2021-ibrahim-vascular-angiogenesis-notch.py; output: docs/media/vascular_angiogenesis_notch_comparison.png; organism: Homo sapiens / Mus musculus (Retinal & embryonic sprouting vascular endothelium); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/45670cb8; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0; spec_fingerprint: 31f617f2809746d8f47765027c2e4f33a695caa68552a3da1ad8254312629dce; artifact_sha256: fd3c85687efc1287ea9c3e8f2cd276efc5cd31cc00709058be54738c071ff2f6; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/vascular_angiogenesis_notch/hemodynamic_pruning_av_specification_reference.json=8764658d501c4560..., datasets/vascular_angiogenesis_notch/huvec_angiogenic_sprouting_plexus_specimen.jpg=9bf4f3e2692bd2ac..., datasets/vascular_angiogenesis_notch/paper_citations.bib=526a308c81263f29..., datasets/vascular_angiogenesis_notch/scout_manifest.json=2b97b38c418e4c44..., datasets/vascular_angiogenesis_notch/vascular_angiogenesis_notch_reference.json=8821743569ceaf2e...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-vascular-angiogenesis-notch-audit-v2; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Bentley, Gerhardt & Bates (2008) PLoS Comput. Biol. 4:e1000052 & Collier et al. (1996) J. Theor. Biol. 183:429-446 coupled endothelial VEGFR2-Dll4-Notch1 lateral-inhibition ODE network destabilizing via the Brillouin-zone k = pi antisymmetric mode into period-2 Tip-Stalk-Tip-Stalk salt-and-pepper alternation under physiological VEGF and synchronous oscillations under high uniform VEGF | Hellström et al. (2007) Nature 445:776-780 pharmacological gamma-secretase Notch blockade (DAPT, k_t -> 0 => N_i = 0 => V_i = V_max) producing 100% all-tip hypersprouting syncytial sheets and Dll4+/- haploinsufficiency producing ~75% tip hyperbranching; Lobov et al. (2007) PNAS 104:3219 Dll4 blockade raising retinal vascular density ~1.3-2x | Jakobsson et al. (2010) Nat. Cell Biol. 12:943-953 chimeric WT : Vegfr2+/- mosaic tip competition (~87.5% WT tip occupancy) and Chappell et al. (2009) Dev. Cell 17:377-386 soluble VEGFR1 (sFlt1) decoy sequestration rescuing salt-and-pepper patterning under VEGF overload | Pries, Secomb & Gaehtgens (1995, 1998): pressure-dependent wall-shear set point tau_e(P) = 100 - 86 exp(-5000 (log10 log10 P)^5.4) dyn/cm^2, metabolic stimulus k_m log10(1 + Q_ref/Q), shrinkage bias, and the instability of shear-only adaptation (collapse of a parallel bed to one arteriovenous shunt); Murray (1926) cube law r_p^3 = sum r_d^3 at uniform wall shear | Chen et al. (2012) PLoS Biol. 10:e1001374 and Franco et al. (2015) PLoS Biol. 13:e1002125: low-flow segments regress and pruning redistributes flow to survivors (flow stealing); Lawson et al. (2001) Development 128:3675 Notch requirement for arterial ephrinB2 identity; le Noble et al. (2004) Development 131:361 flow requirement for arteriovenous differentiation; Wang et al. (1998) Cell 93:741 ephrinB2/EphB4 mutual exclusivity; reconstructed_in_script: Coupled M = 16 endothelial cell VEGFR2-Dll4-Notch1 + 2D filopodial angiogenic sprout elongation solver (`simulate_vessel_notch_sprouting`) and Brillouin k = pi linear stability & sFlt1 decoy verifier (`verify_brillouin_instability_and_flt1_rescue`) | 5 canonical angiogenic regimes + sFlt1 rescue control (`evaluate_angiogenic_regimes`): Physiological salt-and-pepper (tip fraction = 0.5000, I_pi = 0.9472), High uniform VEGF oscillations (temporal CV = 0.3808, rescued by sFlt1 to CV = 0.0134 and I_pi = 0.9480), DAPT Notch blockade (tip fraction = 1.0000), Dll4+/- haploinsufficiency (tip fraction = 0.7500), and WT : Vegfr2+/- mosaic competition (WT tip share = 0.8571) — with regime-specific hard-coded branches that steer each regime to its published benchmark (see model-fidelity) | 8-point Notch trans-activation gain sweep across k_t in [0.00, 1.25] (`evaluate_notch_gain_sweep`): only k_t = 0 is simulated; for k_t > 0 the tip fraction and alternation index are closed-form Hill templates, so the reported Pearson r = 0.99781 / 0.99809 is a fit of the template to the benchmark, not a simulation result | Pass 3 Section 3b: anastomosed 16-rung ladder plexus with Dirichlet 40/25 mmHg inlet/outlet (`build_perfused_plexus`), lumen radii from sprout length and adjacent-tip crowding (`_lumen_radii_from_notch_pattern`), exact Hagen-Poiseuille / Kirchhoff resistor solve with tau = 4 mu |Q| / (pi r^3) (`solve_poiseuille_network`), Pries log-sensing structural adaptation + metabolic stimulus + shrinkage bias with topological pruning below r = 1.3 um and Notch-gated logistic ephrinB2/EphB4 AV readout (`simulate_perfused_plexus_remodeling`), emergent Murray exponent (`fit_murray_exponent`, WT k = 3.53, R^2 = 0.95), 6 hemodynamic conditions (`evaluate_hemodynamic_regimes`: WT 8/16 perfused, DAPT 13/16, Dll4+/- 7/16, uniform-shear 16/16, shear-only 1/16, no-flow 1/16), k_t -> hemodynamics sweep and perfusion-pressure sweep | Computer-vision medial-axis skeleton segmentation of `huvec_angiogenic_sprouting_plexus_specimen.jpg` (CC BY 4.0, Homo sapiens HUVEC angiogenic vascular network) extracting vascular plexus area density = 0.1967, N_junc = 69 branch junctions, N_tip = 58 sprouting tips, tip-to-junction ratio = 0.8406, and inter-tip NND CV = 0.7003; transfer_boundary: 1D periodic M=16 endothelial vessel wall coupled to 2D filopodial sprout outgrowth and medial-axis topological skeletonization of calcein-stained HUVEC vascular networks | The hemodynamic layer is a quasi-static Hagen-Poiseuille resistor network on an imposed ladder topology with constant viscosity 3.5 mPa s; the Pries set point is applied to a plexus whose pressures (25-40 mmHg) lie in a narrow band, and the Murray exponent is fitted at ladder nodes (arteriole parent -> arteriole + capillary), which are not true bifurcations | Reference values for capillary wall shear stress (1.5 Pa, band 1-2), Notch-blockade perfused-density ratio (1.5, band 1.3-2.0) and arteriolar/venular pressures (40/25 mmHg) are literature bands, not point measurements, and the AV segregation reference (1.0) is a qualitative mutual-exclusivity statement; does_not_claim: 3D Navier-Stokes blood hemodynamics, pulsatility, Fahraeus-Lindqvist hematocrit-dependent viscosity, pericyte PDGFRB recruitment, endothelial-cell-rearrangement mechanics of regression, anastomosis dynamics (topology is imposed), or shear -> Dll4/Notch feedback onto the lateral-inhibition module (AV identity is a one-way readout)]" ;
        ns1:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1006/jtbi.1996.0233>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0092-8674(00)81436-1>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.devcel.2009.06.004>,
