        ns1:weightOfEvidence 8.99e-01 .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-lewis-her1-her7-delayed-oscillator> a ns1:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Lewis (2003) zebrafish her1/her7 autoinhibitory delay differential oscillator, DeltaC-Notch synchronization, and (Pass 3) 2D her1/her7/deltaC DDE lattice with NICD kinetics on a Schroter (2012) Hes6 dimer-truth-table gradient faithfully reproduces Danio rerio (zebrafish presomitic mesoderm & paraxial somites); vendored SEM specimen is a chick-embryo cross-species proxy morphology" ;
        dct:description "The simulation script(s) 2003-lewis-her1-her7-delayed-oscillator.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Danio rerio (zebrafish presomitic mesoderm & paraxial somites); vendored SEM specimen is a chick-embryo cross-species proxy specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 87.2/100, audit 2026-10-19-her1-her7-delayed-oscillator-audit-v3) and the assessments." ;
        dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2003-lewis-her1-her7-delayed-oscillator.py> ;
        ns1:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2003-lewis-her1-her7-delayed-oscillator.py; output: docs/media/her1_her7_delayed_oscillator_comparison.png; organism: Danio rerio (zebrafish presomitic mesoderm & paraxial somites); vendored SEM specimen is a chick-embryo cross-species proxy; checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/d58a084; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0; spec_fingerprint: 3359489370da632246e18833410da2ca588eb4932d80863d4bcc1a6360ecd4fb; artifact_sha256: f5ee9226fc709b1bd5be49ec6f0075bba0ce2e7066d65a0036c4cf97bd3ef858; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/her1_her7_delayed_oscillator/her1_her7_delayed_oscillator_reference.json=7e974cd678ea5489..., datasets/her1_her7_delayed_oscillator/scout_manifest.json=ebe3f2cee38772dd..., datasets/her1_her7_delayed_oscillator/zebrafish_somites_specimen.jpg=8b80971796cb29e2...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-her1-her7-delayed-oscillator-audit-v2; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Lewis (2003) Current Biology 13:1398-1408 single-cell her1/her7 delay differential equations dp/dt = a m(t - T_p) - b p(t) and dm/dt = k / (1 + (p(t - T_m)/p_0)^n) - c m(t), Box 1 period law T_osc ~ 2(T_m + T_p + tau_p + tau_m) ~ 30 min at 28 C, coupled-cell DeltaC-Notch DDEs (Figs. 5-6) and bea/des/aei desynchronization after 5-7 anterior somites | Herrgen et al. (2010): the intercellular coupling delay sets the collective segmentation clock period | Schroter et al. (2012): Her1 homodimers and Her7:Hes6 heterodimers are the DNA-binding repressors of the core circuit; Her1:Her7, Her1:Hes6, Her7:Her7 and Hes6:Hes6 do not bind; hes6 is expressed in a non-oscillating posterior-high PSM gradient; reconstructed_in_script: RK4 method-of-steps single-cell DDE (total-delay invariance, computed Hopf threshold T_crit = 7.54 min, subcritical intron-deletion damping, cycloheximide arrest m* = k/c) and a (T_tot, b) Hopf/period morphospace | 5-regime period table reported three ways: JSON-tabulated (r = 0.9999, Pass 2 headline, NOT computed), Box 1 law gated by the computed T_crit (r = 0.790) and RK4 DDE per regime (r = 0.791, RMSE = 11.8 min); the her7 fast regime (T_tot = 6.3 min) is Hopf-subcritical in the implemented model | 1D 32-cell stochastic Kuramoto-Notch phase chain (WT late R = 0.984 vs mutant 6 intact somites, late R = 0.232) | (Pass 3) 8 x 24 two-dimensional DDE lattice with 7 delayed variables per cell: her1 (9.5 + 2.8 min), her7 (4.6 + 1.7 min), deltaC (16.0 + 20.5 min) mRNA/protein and NICD (Michaelis-Menten occupancy of 4-neighbour DeltaC after T_N = 2 min, decay b_N = 0.35/min), Notch-gated transcription G_N with eps_N = 0.9 (0 in mutants), Langevin mRNA noise and 7% delay heterogeneity; WT late column R = 0.669 with every cycle above 0.5, eps_N = 0 keeps 7 (5-7 across seeds) anterior cycles coherent then drops to R = 0.33; collective period increases monotonically with T_N (39.6 / 42.2 / 44.6 min at T_N = 2 / 10 / 20) | (Pass 3) Schroter (2012) truth table as a mass-action repression functional Rep = [Her1:Her1]/K_11 + [Her7:Hes6]/K_76 on a posterior-high Hes6 gradient (4 -> 40): single-cell period 41.2 -> 36.4 min for Hes6 0 -> 90 (monotone), lattice AP gradient 40.8 (anterior) -> 38.6 (posterior) min, hes6-null lattice uniform 41.4 min = her1-only DDE 42.9 +/- 2.5 min, kinematic wave count 0.14 across the sheet | Bilateral somite-row DoG segmentation of the vendored SEM (48.47 px mean spacing, symmetry 0.9605); transfer_boundary: The vendored `zebrafish_somites_specimen.jpg` is a chick (Gallus gallus) embryo SEM per its Commons source title and is used only as a cross-species proxy for vertebrate somite metamerism; no zebrafish her1 in situ or PSM image is compared | The lattice runs on gene-specific her1/her7 delays and therefore cycles at 38.6-41.2 min, not the 30 min zebrafish clock; deltaC delays (16.0 / 20.5 min), NICD kinetics (k_N, b_N, K_D, N_0, h), dimer constants (K_11 = 400, K_76 = 150), Hes6 levels and the noise/heterogeneity calibration are this repository's reduced parameters, not values tabulated by Lewis or Schroter | Hes6 >~ 80 quenches the oscillation in the truth-table model because the her7 branch alone is Hopf-subcritical, whereas real posterior PSM oscillates robustly; the Hes6 period span (4.9 min single-cell, 2.2 min lattice) is reported against a model-internal reference | References for the lattice synchrony (0.965), the T_N lengthening (2.5 min) and the Hes6 span are model- or table-derived magnitudes with literature direction only; does_not_claim: Tailbud growth, axis elongation or Doppler wave-shortening (Soroldoni et al. 2014), explicit Her1:Hes6 titration depletion or Hes6 dimerization stoichiometry, measured dissociation constants, quantitative agreement with Schroter (2012) hes6 / her7 mutant period shifts, reproduction of the 30 min WT period by the two-gene lattice, or any comparison with zebrafish in situ images]" ;
        ns1:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0960-9822(03)00534-7>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cub.2010.06.034>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pbio.0050150>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pbio.1001364> ;
        ns1:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-lewis-her1-her7-delayed-oscillator-code-traceability>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-lewis-her1-her7-delayed-oscillator-model-fidelity>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-lewis-her1-her7-delayed-oscillator-morphometric-validation>,
