        ns1:weightOfEvidence 8.72e-01 .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-liang-chiral-seed-pod-opening> a ns1:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Armon et al. (2011) Science / Efrati et al. (2009) JMPS Incompatible Shell Elasticity & Chiral Seed Pod Opening faithfully reproduces Bauhinia variegata (Orchid tree chiral seed pod valves) & Erythrina corallodendron morphology" ;
        dct:description "The simulation script(s) 2007-liang-chiral-seed-pod-opening.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Bauhinia variegata (Orchid tree chiral seed pod valves) & Erythrina corallodendron specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 87.1/100, audit 2026-10-19-chiral-seed-pod-opening-audit-v3) and the assessments." ;
        dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/2007-liang-chiral-seed-pod-opening.py> ;
        ns1:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/2007-liang-chiral-seed-pod-opening.py; output: docs/media/chiral_seed_pod_opening_comparison.png; organism: Bauhinia variegata (Orchid tree chiral seed pod valves) & Erythrina corallodendron; checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/45670cb8; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0; spec_fingerprint: 988d946ef567ff70b70ecbbb7abf3522d31bdbaab73fbfe18f6b573345ff5c32; artifact_sha256: 172e958f57c4f16dd8b2e082fc2efb5442a52bdf87f09ac52a5d36928b1c4960; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/chiral_seed_pod_opening/bauhinia_chiral_seed_pod_specimen.jpg=047f357961bc58c5..., datasets/chiral_seed_pod_opening/chiral_seed_pod_opening_reference.json=4b1fa5df06327c65..., datasets/chiral_seed_pod_opening/paper_citations.bib=41f9ca2ead3c8d74..., datasets/chiral_seed_pod_opening/scout_manifest.json=05711e5e7df6cb17..., datasets/chiral_seed_pod_opening/suture_fracture_ballistic_reference.json=fc8fab08281dd6e0...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-chiral-seed-pod-opening-audit-v2; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Armon et al. (2011): orthogonal +-45 deg sclerenchyma layers prescribe a saddle target curvature b_0 = diag(kappa_0, -kappa_0) with det(b_0) < 0; narrow strips (w_tilde below a critical FvK width) adopt pure-twist helicoids, wide strips cylindrical helical ribbons; cutting angle controls chirality and pitch | Efrati et al. (2009): incompatible non-Euclidean plate energy E = E_stretch + E_bend with bending content proportional to Y h^3 [nu Tr(M)^2 + (1 - nu) Tr(M^2)], M = b - b_0 | Freund (1990): mode-I dynamic energy release rate G_dyn(v) ~ (1 - v/c_R) G, so a crack runs at v = c_R (1 - Gamma_c/G) and arrests when Gamma_c >= G | Hofhuis et al. (2016) / Swaine & Beer (1977) / Vogel (2005): explosive seed launch speeds of order 10 m/s (Cardamine) and 70 m/s (Hura), elastic-catapult energy budgets and drag-limited ranges of small projectiles; reconstructed_in_script: Reduced L-BFGS-B non-Euclidean energy functional U(H, D, phi; w_tilde) over the dimensionless width, pitchfork sweep, cutting-angle sweep, 4-system table, 3-D ribbon mesh and specimen segmentation (Pass 2); Pass 3 adds B_eff Delta_e -> suture G, a 1-D Freund crack equation of motion over a seeded heterogeneous toughness field, drying-coupled Griffith initiation and stick-slip propagation, an elastic-catapult launch-speed estimate and an RK4 quadratic-drag trajectory, and a 7-point Gamma_c/G ablation sweep; transfer_boundary: The `*_obs` columns of the width and cutting-angle sweep tables in chiral_seed_pod_opening_reference.json are analytical values of the same reduced model (H_obs = (1 - nu)/2 sqrt(1 - (w_tilde_c/w_tilde)^4), tau_obs = D sin 2theta), not digitised Armon 2011 figure points; the r = 1.0000 correlations are self-consistency, not validation | The launch-speed benchmark (10 m/s) is Cardamine hirsuta and the upper bound (70 m/s) is Hura crepitans; no Bauhinia variegata launch-speed, suture-toughness or dispersal datum was verifiable offline, and the predicted 2.8-3.8 m/s is ~3.6x below the Cardamine value | All 12 fracture/ballistic constants (rho, Gamma_c, CV_Gamma, a_0, tau_dry, n_seeds, m_seed, r_seed, C_d, eta, launch angle, launch height) are `provenance: model` in suture_fracture_ballistic_reference.json; does_not_claim: 3-D elastodynamic shell or FEM simulation of valve coiling (inertia enters only via eta and a first-mode cantilever coil time), plate-wave corrections to c_R, a measured Bauhinia fracture toughness or seed mass, or digitised comparison against Armon 2011 Figs. 3-4]" ;
        ns1:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1007/BF02703696>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2016.05.002>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jmps.2008.12.004>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9780511546761>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature03185>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1039/c3sm52313f>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1469-8137.1977.tb02174.x>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1203874> ;
        ns1:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-liang-chiral-seed-pod-opening-code-traceability>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-liang-chiral-seed-pod-opening-model-fidelity>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-liang-chiral-seed-pod-opening-morphometric-validation>,
