        ns1:weightOfEvidence 8.71e-01 .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-manukyan-ocellated-lizard-ca> a ns1:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Manukyan et al. (2017) Nature hexagonal skin-scale border thickness reduction & outer-totalistic cellular automaton — 3D skin-volume reaction-diffusion (Pass 3) faithfully reproduces Ocellated / jeweled lizard (Timon lepidus) dorsal skin scale labyrinth morphology" ;
        dct:description "The simulation script(s) 2015-manukyan-ocellated-lizard-ca.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Ocellated / jeweled lizard (Timon lepidus) dorsal skin scale labyrinth specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 83.6/100, audit 2026-10-19-ocellated-lizard-ca-audit-v3) and the assessments." ;
        dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/bd54e11/2015-manukyan-ocellated-lizard-ca.py> ;
        ns1:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/bd54e11/2015-manukyan-ocellated-lizard-ca.py; output: docs/media/ocellated_lizard_ca_comparison.png; organism: Ocellated / jeweled lizard (Timon lepidus) dorsal skin scale labyrinth; checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/bd54e11; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0; spec_fingerprint: 46cc2c30ccba89108a6a17ed5177834284431b172cd845c2faca9279833944dd; artifact_sha256: f3a39c7c6dedb783fd81cb698c652481d6057844e19017873d6e0f82d7c76b4e; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/ocellated_lizard_ca/ocellated_lizard_ca_reference.json=53832b76e25303a6..., datasets/ocellated_lizard_ca/scout_manifest.json=e5bca2d8766b49e7..., datasets/ocellated_lizard_ca/skin_volume_reference.json=dc8da9f0b72dad3a..., datasets/ocellated_lizard_ca/timon_lepidus_specimen.jpg=bc8e149849e6729d...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-ocellated-lizard-ca-audit-v2; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Manukyan et al. (2017): skin thickness at inter-scale borders is reduced to P = h_border/h_interior ~ 0.17; a Kondo-Asai reaction-diffusion system on this geometry homogenises within scales and reduces to a hexagonal outer-totalistic cellular automaton whose adult neighbour histogram peaks at n_g = 3 (Figs. 2-4) | Fofonjka & Milinkovitch (2021): reaction-diffusion in a growing 3D skin-scale domain with thin inter-scale borders generates the discrete cellular automaton | Turing (1952): diffusion-driven instability requires tr J < 0, det J > 0, d f_u + g_v > 2 sqrt(d det J); reconstructed_in_script: A genuine 3D finite-volume voxel reaction-diffusion solver on a stepped-thickness skin volume (12 interior voxels, dz = 0.2 px, h_border = round(P*12)) with zero-flux surfaces and an implicit vertical solve; its depth-averaged thin-film 2D reduction (1/h) div(h D grad u) with min(h_i, h_j) D face conductances; a leak-proof hexagonal scale geometry; Turing linear stability (d_c, k_c, lambda_c, unstable band) for the script kinetics and for the vendored canonical set; a 5-regime P sweep in 3D and 2D; insulated / equal-diffusion / continuum controls; the stochastic hexagonal outer-totalistic CA; chromatic segmentation of 182 dorsal scales on a SHA-256-pinned Timon lepidus photograph; 16 measurements and 14 self-test checks; transfer_boundary: The 3D domain is a stepped voxel skin on a 5 px scale pitch (border area fraction 0.36, no domain growth), not the micro-CT-derived finite-element geometry of Fofonjka & Milinkovitch (2021); the reaction kinetics (f_u = 0.50, f_v = -0.75, g_u = 0.82, g_v = -0.65, cubic 1.25) are a phenomenological Kondo-Asai-type set, not the Methods parameters of Manukyan et al. (2017) | The CA transition probabilities and adult histogram targets in ocellated_lizard_ca_reference.json carry no digitisation provenance to a specific figure/table; the 'canonical' clipped-linear parameter set in the same file is not Turing-unstable at its stated d = 20 (d_c = 23.57) and is not used by the solvers | The specimen comparison samples a fixed 13 x 14 hexagonal lattice over the dorsal ROI rather than detecting scale centres, so neighbour statistics inherit lattice-registration error; does_not_claim: Reproduction of the paper's exact PDE parameters, a micro-CT skin mesh, domain growth, derivation of the CA flip probabilities from the PDE time series, or a neighbour-histogram match to Manukyan Fig. 3 beyond the vendored target vectors]" ;
        ns1:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1038/376765a0>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature22031>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-021-22525-1>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1952.0012>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevX.13.041011> ;
        ns1:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-manukyan-ocellated-lizard-ca-code-traceability>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-manukyan-ocellated-lizard-ca-model-fidelity>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-manukyan-ocellated-lizard-ca-morphometric-validation>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-manukyan-ocellated-lizard-ca-overall>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-manukyan-ocellated-lizard-ca-parameter-expressivity>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-manukyan-ocellated-lizard-ca-repro-package>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-manukyan-ocellated-lizard-ca-source-traceability>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-manukyan-ocellated-lizard-ca-specimen-match> ;
        ns1:weightOfEvidence 8.36e-01 .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-meinhardt-echinoderm-pentaradial-symmetry> a ns1:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Morris (2012), Mooi & David (1998/2008), Lovén (1874), Duboc et al. (2005), Luo & Su (2012) & Meinhardt (2008) echinoderm bilateral-to-pentaradial hydrocoel ring symmetry breaking with Ocular Plate Rule test growth faithfully reproduces Strongylocentrotus purpuratus & Tripneustes gratilla (Echinoidea crown-group echinoderms) morphology" ;
        dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2005-meinhardt-echinoderm-pentaradial-symmetry.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Strongylocentrotus purpuratus & Tripneustes gratilla (Echinoidea crown-group echinoderms) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 89.2/100, audit 2026-10-19-echinoderm-pentaradial-symmetry-audit-v3) and the assessments." ;
        dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a69596cc/models/2005-meinhardt-echinoderm-pentaradial-symmetry.py> ;
        ns1:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a69596cc/models/2005-meinhardt-echinoderm-pentaradial-symmetry.py; output: docs/media/echinoderm_pentaradial_symmetry_comparison.png; organism: Strongylocentrotus purpuratus & Tripneustes gratilla (Echinoidea crown-group echinoderms); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/a69596cc; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0; spec_fingerprint: cd13db70aa61071108eb599c5b5e2da1617f948ac60e0ad765eabfe5fa619518; artifact_sha256: df03cccaab05e99639f38fa2c234607621bb59d89aae097f3d56431244b5d9c6; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/echinoderm_pentaradial_symmetry/echinoderm_pentaradial_symmetry_reference.json=c516e298727883cf..., datasets/echinoderm_pentaradial_symmetry/echinoderm_pentaradial_test_specimen.jpg=953b2f7e38029627..., datasets/echinoderm_pentaradial_symmetry/opr_plate_addition_nodal_dose_reference.json=f93ea0ba8cc2fe82..., datasets/echinoderm_pentaradial_symmetry/scout_manifest.json=0b333ebe2a2ed524...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-echinoderm-pentaradial-symmetry-audit-v2; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Morris (2012): the pentaradial adult body plan arises from the left hydrocoel crescent closing into a ring, with the five primary podia initiated in the sequence II, IV, I, III, V (Carpenter C, A, D, B, E) | Lovén (1874): in each ambulacrum one of the two primary peristomial plates is enlarged, in the asymmetric pattern Ib, IIb, IIIa, IVa, Va, and ambulacral/interambulacral plates form alternating biserial columns | Mooi & David (1998, 2008): the Ocular Plate Rule — every new coronal plate is added at the ocular (apical) end of its column, so plate age increases toward the peristome and plate count increases with test size | Duboc et al. (2005): right-sided Nodal signalling represses the right hydrocoel; Nodal morpholino gives bilateral twin rudiments (2 x 5 podia) and bilateral Nodal overexpression gives none | Luo & Su (2012): BMP2/4 signalling on the left is required for rudiment formation and opposes Nodal | Raup (1968), Zachos (2009): echinoid test growth can be modelled as plate addition plus plate growth on a domed surface | Meinhardt (2008): activator-inhibitor dynamics on a closed domain select a wavenumber set by domain circumference / critical wavelength; reconstructed_in_script: A circular-ring mode-selection solver with a prescribed dispersion curve, crescent-to-ring closure gates at the Lovén ray angles, an m in {3..7} circumference staircase and an equal-diffusion negative control; a 2D rudiment field with a binary Nodal switch; a reduced Ocular Plate Rule plate-addition solver on a spherical-cap test seeded from the ring lobes, with logistic plate accretion, ocular-end nucleation, Lovén-enlarged primordials and an aboral projection measured with the specimen's polar Fourier pipeline; a 1D steady-state screened-Poisson Nodal/BMP2-4 gradient model with Hill competence, a dose sweep and a 2D dose map; automated specimen segmentation of a Tripneustes gratilla test; 16 reference-anchored measurements; 5 Lean 4 theorems; transfer_boundary: The Section 2 ring solver is NOT an integrated Gierer-Meinhardt PDE: the growth rate sigma(m) = 0.0480 (1 - 5.2 det^2) is hard-coded (L218, L283), the target mode is seeded in the initial condition (L289), the inhibitor is algebraic h = 1 + 0.65 (a - 1) (L318) and the Lovén initiation order is prescribed through delay_frac gates (L264-270). m* = 5, the staircase r = 1.0000 and the Lovén order r = 1.0000 therefore hold by construction; the DEFAULT_DA/DH/RHO constants (L120-123) do not enter the dynamics | The OPR solver is 1D meridional plate heights in rectangular azimuth bands on a sphere: no plate-plate mechanics, Voronoi packing, FEM or ambitus flattening; growth factor 40, colatitudes 22/150 deg and h_nuc/h_max are labelled assumptions in the reference JSON; the Amb/IA plate ratio target 3.0 is approximate and the emergent value 2.06 misses it | The Nodal/BMP2-4 gradient parameters were tuned only so that WT / MO / GOF give 5 / 10 / 0 podia; EC50 = 0.175 x WT is a model prediction with no empirical anchor; no Lefty/Pitx2 and no explicit Nodal-BMP antagonism term | The specimen is Tripneustes gratilla while the header organism is S. purpuratus; specimen references (C_5 = 0.9255, ray angles) are the script's own segmentation outputs, not independent measurements; does_not_claim: Quantitative reproduction of Duboc (2005) penetrance percentages or in-situ intensity profiles, mechanical plate packing, measured plate counts for any named species, or an integrated activator-inhibitor PDE in Section 2]; other sources: Theoretical morphology of echinoid growth <https://www.jstor.org/stable/1302410>" ;
        ns1:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0070-2153(07)81001-5>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.devcel.2005.05.008>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2009.04.007>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1093/icb/38.6.965>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1525-142X.2012.00552.x>,
