    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing> a ns1:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Menshykau & Iber (2013), Zubkov et al. (2015) & Watanabe & Costantini (2004) kidney ureteric bud GDNF-RET-Wnt11 Turing branching morphogenesis with stromal BMP4/7-Gremlin1-FGF7 feedback and reduced-3D ampulla necking faithfully reproduces Mus musculus (embryonic E11.5-E13.5 mouse metanephric kidney ureteric bud tree, cap and stromal mesenchyme) morphology" ;
        dct:description "The simulation script(s) 2012-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Mus musculus (embryonic E11.5-E13.5 mouse metanephric kidney ureteric bud tree, cap and stromal mesenchyme) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 83.8/100, audit 2026-10-19-kidney-ureteric-bud-gdnf-ret-audit-v3) and the assessments." ;
        dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/2012-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing.py> ;
        ns1:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/2012-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing.py; output: docs/media/kidney_ureteric_bud_gdnf_ret_comparison.png; organism: Mus musculus (embryonic E11.5-E13.5 mouse metanephric kidney ureteric bud tree, cap and stromal mesenchyme); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/028758bc; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0; spec_fingerprint: f29be7f1600499fda53bd2dbabe454bd253465ad82fc249a5ca7afb434d430b0; artifact_sha256: 818d1b74f25bf359339b3bb4f553b254ee38435cc9e836d37f4e53acd0367e10; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/kidney_ureteric_bud_gdnf_ret/kidney_ureteric_bud_gdnf_ret_reference.json=a15b7c6b44319cfd..., datasets/kidney_ureteric_bud_gdnf_ret/kidney_ureteric_tree_specimen.jpg=3264f509ba3a6686..., datasets/kidney_ureteric_bud_gdnf_ret/paper_citations.bib=698d3f067b082cc3..., datasets/kidney_ureteric_bud_gdnf_ret/scout_manifest.json=c55304eda64bfba4...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-kidney-ureteric-bud-gdnf-ret-audit-v2; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Menshykau & Iber (2013): a Schnakenberg-type GDNF-RET receptor-ligand reaction-diffusion system on the ureteric epithelium has a homogeneous steady state R* = a + b, G* = b/(a + b)^2 and a Turing instability whose fastest mode on the ampulla selects elongation, bifurcation or trifurcation as the tip radius grows | Watanabe & Costantini (2004): time-lapse of cultured E11.5 kidneys shows predominantly dichotomous (with some trichotomous) ampulla splitting and generation-dependent tip counts and branch angles | Basson et al. (2005): Spry1-/- kidneys hyper-branch with supernumerary buds; exogenous GDNF beads induce ectopic budding | Michos et al. (2004), Qiao et al. (1999), Miyazaki et al. (2000): Grem1-/- fails ureteric outgrowth, Fgf7-/- reduces ureteric growth and nephron number, Bmp4+/- shows ectopic budding (qualitative) | Menshykau et al. (2012), Metzger et al. (2008): branch-mode selection depends on the local geometry of the growing tip; successive lung bifurcation planes rotate ~90 deg (orthogonal bifurcation); reconstructed_in_script: Steady state, dispersion relation, lambda_c and (a, b) phase space; 1D Neumann ampulla-cap IMEX solver with band-seeded and noise-seeded initial conditions; 1D Lagrangian moving-boundary necking of the dome; linear two-lobe axis selection on an anisotropic dome and a dihedral cascade; 2D self-avoiding ureteric tree coupled to GDNF sink, BMP, Gremlin1 and FGF7 Gaussian fields with per-tip stromal gain feeding R_tip -> rho_tip -> splitting multiplicity; 7 genetic/bead conditions plus no-sink, equal-diffusion and stromal-ablation controls; GFP specimen segmentation and tip counting; transfer_boundary: The 3D phase-field/ALE item is closed only as a 1D moving boundary on the dome plus a linear axis-selection argument; no surface tension, curvature, re-meshing or E13.5-E16.5 calyx stage; the 90 deg dihedral follows from an explicit daughter-orientation assumption (daughter_long_axis_parallel=True), not from the dynamics | Stromal constants k_B = 3.0, k_G = 4.0, k_F7 = 0.8, BMP baseline 0.5 and the Gaussian field amplitudes/widths are model-scale calibrations, not measured rate constants; BMP4 and BMP7 share a single field; ligand fields are quasi-static per generation | The band-seeded mode staircase [1, 2, 3, 4] is conditioned on its own cosine initial condition; the noise-seeded honesty control gives [2, 3, 5, 5]; does_not_claim: Quantitative reproduction of Grem1-/-, Fgf7-/- or Bmp4+/- tip counts (the reference ratios 0.08/0.70/1.20 are qualitative encodings); 3D ampulla shape; derivation of bifurcation angles from the PDE (half-angles are prescribed per generation); a kidney-specific dihedral distribution; verification offline of the 5 new DOIs]" ;
        ns1:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1007/s11538-015-0073-9>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.devcel.2004.12.004>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.devcel.2014.02.017>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ydbio.2004.03.025>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature07005>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1088/1478-3975/10/4/046003>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1172/JCI8256>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.01251>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.086207>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.126.3.547> ;
        ns1:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing-code-traceability>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing-model-fidelity>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing-morphometric-validation>,
