        ns1:weightOfEvidence 8.81e-01 .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching> a ns1:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Metzger et al. (2008) & Menshykau et al. (2012, 2014) mouse lung stereotyped branching modes (Domain D, Planar P, Orthogonal O), FGF10-SHH-Ptch1 Turing mode selection, pleura-confined diffuse-domain FGF10 cavity and stochastic postnatal septation faithfully reproduces Mus musculus (embryonic E11-E15 mouse bronchial tree; postnatal P4-P36 alveolarisation) morphology" ;
        dct:description "The simulation script(s) 2008-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Mus musculus (embryonic E11-E15 mouse bronchial tree; postnatal P4-P36 alveolarisation) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 88.5/100, audit 2026-10-19-lung-stereotyped-branching-modes-audit-v3) and the assessments." ;
        dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/2008-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching.py> ;
        ns1:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/2008-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching.py; output: docs/media/lung_stereotyped_branching_modes_comparison.png; organism: Mus musculus (embryonic E11-E15 mouse bronchial tree; postnatal P4-P36 alveolarisation); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/028758bc; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0; spec_fingerprint: d02b0c3844bcaa108ea9ec4bb8fce374a8da22fe6801db1a8256bba00a9e901f; artifact_sha256: 39a638e50c464718f55cb5a04c00c6dbe57169032a3a3896d1e76a6400bec3d4; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/lung_stereotyped_branching_modes/bronchial_tree_specimen.jpg=3247bc8c35eddcad..., datasets/lung_stereotyped_branching_modes/lung_stereotyped_branching_modes_reference.json=860ab1e53046d2e7...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-lung-stereotyped-branching-modes-audit-v2; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Metzger et al. (2008): the E11-E15 mouse bronchial tree is built from three stereotyped subroutines — Domain Branching, Planar Bifurcation (confined to lobe edges/margins) and Orthogonal Bifurcation (lobe interiors) — composed in a genetically encoded sequence | Menshykau et al. (2012, 2014): an FGF10 / SHH-Ptch1 receptor-ligand Turing system on a growing epithelial domain selects between apical (bifurcation) and lateral (domain) budding, and mesenchymal geometry biases the direction of outgrowth | Mund, Stampanoni & Schittny (2008): mouse alveolarisation proceeds in a bulk phase P4-P21 and a continued phase P14-P36; Knust et al. (2009): the adult C57BL/6 mouse lung holds ~2.3e6 alveoli; reconstructed_in_script: 3D Bishop-frame D/P/O grammar with the 4m + 1 tip law and a 181-point dihedral sweep; the Menshykau dispersion relation and a 1D spectral PDE mode switch; a quasi-2D diffuse-domain FGF10 cavity bounded by a dilating lens-shaped pleura with the tip as Ptch1 sink, whose supply anisotropy chooses P (0 deg) vs O (90 deg) at each bifurcation; an exact-increment Yule septation ensemble seeded by the grammar's extrapolated E16.5 terminal-unit count; chromatic segmentation and skeletonisation of a bronchial-tree image; transfer_boundary: The pleura model is a transverse cross-section (z-invariant) with a prescribed, tree-independent dilation; tips choose P/O from the field but are not advected by grad F, and the pleura does not deform in response to the tree — the v2 item asked for a 3D moving-boundary phase-field/BEM, which this is not | lambda_bulk is fitted to the adult alveolar count, so the P36 total is a calibration, not a prediction; the 632 terminal units at E16.5 are a log-linear extrapolation of the vendored E11-E14.5 timecourse table; lambda_cont / lambda_bulk = 0.12 and birth at E19.5 are assumptions | The 'specimen' is a Wikimedia medical illustration of human bronchioles/alveoli, not a mouse E11-E15 lung; its junction angles are compared with the model's reference angles but cannot validate the mouse grammar; does_not_claim: A 3D moving-boundary mesenchyme, tip chemotaxis, per-age alveolar counts from Mund (2008), digitised Metzger (2008) lineage coordinates, or an independent prediction of the adult alveolar number]" ;
        ns1:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1002/ar.20747>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1002/dvdy.21633>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature07005>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.081679>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1003421>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0041643>,
            <https://doi.org/10.4310/CMS.2009.v7.n1.a4> ;
        ns1:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-code-traceability>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-model-fidelity>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-morphometric-validation>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-overall>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-parameter-expressivity>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-repro-package>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-source-traceability>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-specimen-match> ;
        ns1:weightOfEvidence 8.85e-01 .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-miller-ocular-dominance-stripes> a ns1:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Miller, Keller & Stryker (1989) & Hubel, Wiesel & LeVay (1977) ocular dominance column development & plasticity faithfully reproduces Macaca mulatta / Felis catus primary visual cortex (V1 Layer IVC) morphology" ;
        dct:description "The simulation script(s) 1989-miller-ocular-dominance-stripes.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Macaca mulatta / Felis catus primary visual cortex (V1 Layer IVC) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 92.8/100, audit 2026-10-19-ocular-dominance-stripes-audit-v2) and the assessments." ;
        dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/317bc3c/1989-miller-ocular-dominance-stripes.py> ;
        ns1:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/317bc3c/1989-miller-ocular-dominance-stripes.py; output: docs/media/ocular_dominance_stripes_comparison.png; organism: Macaca mulatta / Felis catus primary visual cortex (V1 Layer IVC); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/317bc3c; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1; spec_fingerprint: 819128bbec5b994d73c8b186f4a86b2d2df6149663f61bdaf866cb36447d290f; artifact_sha256: d9836de9bccac0673460f380c616ad3321ffc7b4d515cc99a0a2314c303799eb; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/ocular_dominance_stripes/macaque_striate_cortex_specimen.jpg=fe74eb6f9db7dea1..., datasets/ocular_dominance_stripes/ocular_dominance_stripes_reference.json=7041693bc0b54b31..., datasets/ocular_dominance_stripes/odc_tangential_pattern_specimen.png=fac59bb151b4eb1d..., datasets/ocular_dominance_stripes/paper_citations.bib=29c3ea74bae42954..., datasets/ocular_dominance_stripes/scout_manifest.json=2f54657c6b0c2050...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-ocular-dominance-stripes-audit; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Miller, Keller & Stryker (1989) Science 245:605-615 correlation-based Hebbian synaptic competition model showing that subtractive homeostatic normalization conserves S_Sigma = S^L + S^R while S_Delta = S^L - S^R amplifies at the Mexican-hat band-pass peak k_c | Hubel, Wiesel & LeVay (1977) Phil. Trans. R. Soc. B 278:377-409 tangential autoradiographs of Macaca mulatta V1 Layer IVC showing ~400 um single-eye column width (~800 um full wavelength), monocular deprivation shrinkage of deprived-eye stripes into narrow islands, and critical-period reverse suture rescue | Stryker & Harris (1986) J. Neurosci. 6:2117-2133 showing that bilateral intraocular TTX retinal impulse blockade (C_Delta = 0) completely prevents ocular dominance column segregation; reconstructed_in_script: 2D spectral Miller-Keller-Stryker / Swindale solver on a 96x96 periodic tangential V1 Layer IVC sheet (6400x6400 um) across all 5 canonical regimes plus a 6-point intracortical inhibition range sigma_I wavelength sweep (170-290 um, Pearson r = 0.9970) | Automated CV segmentation of stripe territories (f_L = 0.5000), 2D Hanning FFT spectral peak (16 cycles, 800 um scaled wavelength), and N = 71 Y-branchpoints on `odc_tangential_pattern_specimen.png` plus Layer IVC laminar Nissl optical density profiling (s* = 0.35) on `macaque_striate_cortex_specimen.jpg`; transfer_boundary: 2D tangential Layer IVC cortical sheet x in [0, 6.4 mm]^2 with isotropic Difference-of-Gaussians lateral interaction I(r) and coupled S^L, S^R synaptic densities; does_not_claim: Subcellular NMDA receptor channel kinetics, cytochrome oxidase blob co-alignment with orientation pinwheels in Layers 2/3, or curved calcarine sulcus 3D cortical folding geometry]" ;
        ns1:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1098/rspb.1980.0051>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1977.0050>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.2762813>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1523/JNEUROSCI.06-08-02117.1986> ;
        ns1:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-miller-ocular-dominance-stripes-code-traceability>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-miller-ocular-dominance-stripes-model-fidelity>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-miller-ocular-dominance-stripes-morphometric-validation>,
