            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-onuff-joint-interzone-clefting-source-traceability>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-onuff-joint-interzone-clefting-specimen-match> ;
        ns1:weightOfEvidence 8.94e-01 .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis> a ns1:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Oster, Murray & Harris (1983) / Oster, Murray & Maini (1985) mechanochemical limb chondrogenesis faithfully reproduces Ambystoma mexicanum & Oedipina ecuatoriana urodele salamander limb cartilage morphology" ;
        dct:description "The simulation script(s) 1983-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Ambystoma mexicanum & Oedipina ecuatoriana urodele salamander limb cartilage specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 87.1/100, audit 2026-10-19-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-audit-v3) and the assessments." ;
        dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/1983-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis.py> ;
        ns1:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/1983-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis.py; output: docs/media/mechanochemical_chondrogenesis_comparison.png; organism: Ambystoma mexicanum & Oedipina ecuatoriana urodele salamander limb cartilage; checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/d58a084; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0; spec_fingerprint: 176fd41f0d953b7b1e5e1437961112bdacb6e1e1e0faf2536dab887008a3d35d; artifact_sha256: 6d4816d74352461ad321163dc15069950d6724ef0b09f62e43ad1f1d533ee5ff; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/mechanochemical_chondrogenesis/mechanochemical_chondrogenesis_reference.json=f2c0be56cbef12c2..., datasets/mechanochemical_chondrogenesis/salamander_limb_cartilage_specimen.jpg=8030c8291c3a6d5b..., datasets/mechanochemical_chondrogenesis/scout_manifest.json=cb9d73c33c4113e4...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-audit-v2; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Oster, Murray & Harris (1983) J. Embryol. Exp. Morph. 78:83-125 and Oster, Murray & Maini (1985) J. Embryol. Exp. Morph. 89:93-112 coupled mesenchymal cell-density and viscoelastic ECM traction PDE system; the AER maintains a distal recruitment/progress zone and condensations are laid down proximo-distally | Critical cell traction bifurcation threshold tau_c driving focal condensation (stylopod), dichotomous Y-bifurcation (zeugopod) and digital branching (autopod: 4 forelimb / 5 hindlimb digits in urodele salamanders) | Saunders (1948): removing the chick-wing AER at progressively later stages leaves progressively more distal skeletal parts (proximo-distal sequence of origin) | Raspopovic et al. (2014): a Bmp-Sox9-Wnt Turing network with Sox9 out of phase with Bmp and Wnt patterns the digits; reconstructed_in_script: Exact marginal stability curve tau_eff(k^2) with analytic tau_c = 1.2776 at k_c = 0.9597 (lambda_c = 6.5472) and the 1D spectral-pseudospectral cell-ECM solver reproducing modes [0, 1, 2, 4, 5] on periodic domains W = m lambda_c with seeded m-cosine perturbations | A 2D coupled cell-ECM PDE on a limb paddle with a moving free-boundary AER front (progress-zone traction suppression and proliferation, AER regression, anisotropic PD cell diffusion a_y = 3, ectoderm-balanced prestress) producing the forelimb [1, 2, 4] and hindlimb [1, 2, 5] hierarchies from a seeded proximal nucleus plus noise, with proximo-distal onset order and the Saunders (1948) ablation series [1, 1, 2, 3] | A 4x4 hybrid Jacobian and 1D hybrid PDE coupling the mechanics to Raspopovic (2014) BSW kinetics (tau(1 + alpha_S S), +kappa_S (n - N_0)), with wavelength-matched ligand diffusivities, showing tau_c lowering 1.44 -> 0.35 and a 2x2 factorial [0, 0, 0, 4] at tau = 0.85 | Morphological segmentation of the vendored Oedipina ecuatoriana specimen giving [1, 2, 4] / [1, 2, 5] hierarchies, autopod spacings 39.0 / 41.25 px and the zeugopod/autopod spacing ratio compared with the 2D PDE (1.235 vs 1.373); transfer_boundary: The 2D domain is a Fourier-periodic box with a diffuse (tanh) competence field, not a sharp Neumann boundary; the ECM force balance is reduced to a component-wise Helmholtz operator (no shear/Poisson coupling, no ECM density equation) and the viscous relaxation rate 1/(mu + 0.15) is ad hoc | The solvers' drift kernel includes mu k^2 in the quasi-static stiffness, so their effective tau_c (1.4397) is 12.7% above the analytic 1.2776 shown in Panels A/D; all supercritical regimes used exceed both | Only the proximal humeral/femoral nucleus is seeded in the 2D solver; the stylopod width W = 1.4 lambda_c is a tuned choice (W = 1.0 is marginal), and the autopod count is partly inherited by 2 -> 4 bifurcation rather than set by W / lambda_c | The BSW parameters are copied from the Slot 016 reference JSON, rescaled in diffusivity to match lambda_c; the Saunders (1948) comparison is a qualitative stage-to-segment mapping, not digitised data; lengths are in lambda_c units with no micron calibration against the specimen; does_not_claim: A 3D finite-element limb, explicit ECM density/advection, joint/phalangeal segmentation of the rods, Hoxd13 gene-dosage polydactyly scaling (Slot 017), or quantitative reproduction of the full Raspopovic (2014) 2D autopod (Slot 016)]" ;
        ns1:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1002/(SICI)1521-1878(200002)22:2%3C138::AID-BIES5%3E3.0.CO;2-4>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1002/jez.1401080304>,
