            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-przemyslaw-allometric-compound-leaf-specimen-match> ;
        ns1:weightOfEvidence 6.82e-01 .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-raspopovic-bmp-sox9-wnt-digits> a ns1:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Raspopovic et al. (2014) 3-node Bmp-Sox9-Wnt Turing digit patterning network modulated by distal FGF on a moving-boundary FEM limb-bud outgrowth mesh faithfully reproduces Embryonic mouse autopod (Mus musculus, E11.5-E13.5) morphology" ;
        dct:description "The simulation script(s) 2014-raspopovic-bmp-sox9-wnt-digits.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Embryonic mouse autopod (Mus musculus, E11.5-E13.5) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 84.0/100, audit 2026-10-19-bmp-sox9-wnt-digits-audit-v3) and the assessments." ;
        dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2014-raspopovic-bmp-sox9-wnt-digits.py> ;
        ns1:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2014-raspopovic-bmp-sox9-wnt-digits.py; output: docs/media/bmp_sox9_wnt_digits_comparison.png; organism: Embryonic mouse autopod (Mus musculus, E11.5-E13.5); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/d58a084; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0; spec_fingerprint: fcc019aeaf38ae13b447dccbc8f276f80745d761e03ea95627ecad0617dd1321; artifact_sha256: 22b27c34b46a015ca80913991f77bbaec823119454402539c53eb86847740d91; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/bmp_sox9_wnt_digits/bmp_sox9_wnt_digits_reference.json=c0444b665610be2e..., datasets/bmp_sox9_wnt_digits/limb_bud_outgrowth_fem_reference.json=3db7c9493f12c2b3..., datasets/bmp_sox9_wnt_digits/paper_citations.bib=88ff32a60b567060..., datasets/bmp_sox9_wnt_digits/paper_citations_pass3.bib=eab1e111424c9ac1..., datasets/bmp_sox9_wnt_digits/scout_manifest.json=f990b473b6a93cfa..., datasets/bmp_sox9_wnt_digits/sox9_limb_digits_specimen.jpg=533f621904d6f2ce...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-bmp-sox9-wnt-digits-audit-v2; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Raspopovic et al. (2014): a 3-node network of cell-autonomous Sox9 with diffusing Bmp and Wnt (Sox9 represses both ligands, Bmp activates and Wnt represses Sox9) is Turing-unstable without ligand self-activation; Sox9 digit stripes are out of phase with Bmp and Wnt; on the growing autopod a distal FGF / Hoxd gradient that lengthens the wavelength keeps the stripes unbranched, and the growing-domain simulations were run on a realistic limb-bud growth map (Marcon et al. 2011) | Sheth et al. (2012): digit number scales with autopod width / Hox dosage through the Turing wavelength | Crampin, Gaffney & Maini (1999): on a growing domain every species acquires the dilution term -(div u) c and modes are inserted sequentially as the domain lengthens | Boehm et al. (2010): finite-element limb-bud growth; a proliferation gradient alone does not explain the bud shape | Farin et al. (2013): E12.5 Sox9 / E13.5 Col2a1 WISH of wild-type (5) and Tbx2-/- (6) digit condensations (the vendored specimen) | Shubin & Alberch (1986): the digital arch forms posterior to anterior with the marginal digit I last; reconstructed_in_script: 3-node and reduced 2-diffuser Jacobians, dispersion relation and D = 0 control (Laws 1-3); 1D distal-arc explicit solver; 2D polar-fan finite-difference solver carried from v2; 7-regime FGF/Hox table; 6-condition perturbation suite; DoG + chromogen segmentation of the WISH specimen (5 WT vs 6 Tbx2-/- rays) | Pass 3: P1 finite-element solver on a Lagrangian / ALE polar-fan mesh with a moving AER boundary, implicit diffusion, conservative lumped-mass dilution, re-assembled stiffness, AER-anchored wavelength modulation with three modes, FEM verification against the analytic dispersion relation, growth-dilution sweep, final-arc sweep, 3 x 3 modulation ablation, 9 new reference-anchored measurements and 3 new Lean theorems (Laws 4-6); transfer_boundary: The mesh is a prescribed polar fan (r_prox = 4.2, R: 5.0 -> 8.4, theta_max = 0.38 pi) with a uniform radial Lagrangian stretch and an exponential-then-capped outgrowth law; there is no proliferation field, no realistic bud outline, no dorsoventral axis and no measured growth kinetics | The FGF / Hoxd modulation enters as D ∝ (r / R(t))^2 (lambda ∝ r / R(t)); this is the unique modulation that keeps sigma_max fixed while scaling lambda with the arc, not an equation of Raspopovic et al. (2014), whose supplementary modulation functions were not retrieved | All new reference values are analytic consequences of the baseline parameters (dispersion relation, Lean Laws 4-6) or qualitative statements from the papers; no digitised stripe count, growth curve or width-vs-digit-number data are vendored | The v2 7-regime FGF/Hox collapse depends on a fitted exponent (3.12) in a diffusion scaling that the network itself does not produce; the v2 LDN / CHIR digit counts are capped by hand; the v2 2D polar-fan result is mode-seeded and cosmetically masked (all three are disclosed here and carried as Pass 4 items); does_not_claim: A reproduction of the Raspopovic et al. (2014) supplementary growing-domain simulations, measured outgrowth kinetics of the mouse limb bud, the posterior-to-anterior order of digit condensation (the model inserts new rays in the interior), chondrogenic condensation mechanics, 3D geometry, or digit identity]" ;
        ns1:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1006/bulm.1999.0131>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1007/978-1-4615-6983-1_6>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1226804>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1252960>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pbio.1000420>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1001071>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pgen.1003467>,
            <https://doi.org/10.7554/eLife.14022> ;
        ns1:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-raspopovic-bmp-sox9-wnt-digits-code-traceability>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-raspopovic-bmp-sox9-wnt-digits-model-fidelity>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-raspopovic-bmp-sox9-wnt-digits-morphometric-validation>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-raspopovic-bmp-sox9-wnt-digits-overall>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-raspopovic-bmp-sox9-wnt-digits-parameter-expressivity>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-raspopovic-bmp-sox9-wnt-digits-repro-package>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-raspopovic-bmp-sox9-wnt-digits-source-traceability>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-raspopovic-bmp-sox9-wnt-digits-specimen-match> ;
        ns1:weightOfEvidence 8.4e-01 .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling> a ns1:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Richman et al. (1975) & Tallinen et al. (2014, 2016) neo-Hookean constrained cortical expansion and sulcal creasing instability, with a Pass 3 3D hemispheric Swift-Hohenberg surface surrogate faithfully reproduces Mammalian cerebral cortex & subcortical white matter (Homo sapiens, Pan troglodytes, Macaca mulatta, Tursiops truncatus, Felis catus, Mus musculus) morphology" ;
        dct:description "The simulation script(s) 1975-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Mammalian cerebral cortex & subcortical white matter (Homo sapiens, Pan troglodytes, Macaca mulatta, Tursiops truncatus, Felis catus, Mus musculus) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 80.2/100, audit 2026-10-19-cortical-gyrification-folding-audit-v3) and the assessments." ;
        dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/1975-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling.py> ;
        ns1:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/1975-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling.py; output: docs/media/cortical_gyrification_folding_comparison.png; organism: Mammalian cerebral cortex & subcortical white matter (Homo sapiens, Pan troglodytes, Macaca mulatta, Tursiops truncatus, Felis catus, Mus musculus); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/45670cb8; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0, scikit-image 0.26.0, lean 4.35.0; spec_fingerprint: 13499943306506233e29ef0e44d9eb95a08cb36c62618ec286f2346b2d38f941; artifact_sha256: ca86dd76e3d0c81460ea4a15d6e3c54f90b997c4272caa3b12ede091364d7413; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/cortical_gyrification_folding/cerebral_cortex_gyri_specimen.jpg=ff9a25e993fd5aad..., datasets/cortical_gyrification_folding/cortical_gyrification_folding_reference.json=94947373ac49d97d..., datasets/cortical_gyrification_folding/paper_citations.bib=c330565c1bac7790..., datasets/cortical_gyrification_folding/scout_manifest.json=7f5410ff8ad2c1ee..., datasets/cortical_gyrification_folding/surface_sh_3d_reference.json=5421bbea0b8fa9e5...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-cortical-gyrification-folding-audit-v2; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Richman et al. (1975): a stiff cortical plate growing on a softer subcortical foundation buckles with wavelength lambda = 2 pi h (mu_c / 3 mu_s)^(1/3), predicting fine folds for thin (microgyric) cortex and broad folds for thick cortex | Tallinen et al. (2014, 2016): multiplicative tangential growth F = F_e G of a neo-Hookean cortex above a critical excess g_c produces cusped sulci; a 3D gel-brain and a tetrahedral FEM on a GW22 MRI template reproduce fetal gyrification GW22-GW34 with GI rising to about 2.5 | Mota & Herculano-Houzel (2015): cortical folding scales universally with surface area and thickness across mammals | Zilles et al. (1988): human whole-hemisphere coronal gyrification index 2.56 +/- 0.08 | Stoop et al. (2015): a stiff film on a soft curved substrate follows a generalized Swift-Hohenberg equation whose curvature-induced quadratic term selects hexagonal dimples at low overstress and labyrinths at high overstress | Fischl & Dale (2000): regional human cortical thickness varies from about 1 mm to 4.5 mm (mean about 2.5 mm) across the hemisphere; reconstructed_in_script: Laws 1-3 (growth excess, cube-root wavelength, GI = 1 + 2 N d / P_hull) as closed-form functions; a 2D coronal shell relaxation (L-BFGS-B) toward a prescribed cusp profile with sulcus count and GI target set from the formula; 11-species and 4-condition sweeps; segmentation of one coronal specimen image | Pass 3: generalized Swift-Hohenberg relaxation on an ellipsoidal hemisphere surface (cotangent Laplace-Beltrami, semi-implicit Euler, Lyapunov energy), regional k_c(x) from a linear thickness gradient, raster skeleton Y-junction counting, marching-triangles iso-contour fundus length, 3D crease-wall GI with depth imported from the 2D solver, 4-point thickness-gradient sweep; transfer_boundary: The 11-species lambda_obs values in the reference JSON are generated from the Richman formula (4.3633 h), so cross-species wavelength agreement (r = 1.0000, alpha = 0.9993, lambda/h = 4.3642) is formula-vs-formula, not model-vs-measurement | The 2D coronal solver's sulcus count, GI target and cusp profile are prescribed before minimisation; L-BFGS-B removes injected noise rather than selecting a buckling mode, so GI_sim, lambda_sim and sulcus counts equal their targets by construction | The 3D surrogate's preferred wavenumber k_c(x) is imposed by the GSH operator; lambda_3D = 11.41 vs 11.33 and the gradient slope 1.006 are consistency checks of the nonlinear planform, and eps_scale = 0.5 / g2_curvature_coeff = 0.35 are tuning constants chosen to place GW26 in the dimple phase and GW38 in the labyrinth phase | The ellipsoid (1.30 R, 0.70 R, 0.95 R) is not an MRI template; Y-junction density has only the honeycomb upper bound 2.31 per lambda^2 as reference; the percolation ratio has only a > 1 lower bound; does_not_claim: A volumetric tetrahedral neo-Hookean FEM, emergent sulcal depth or GI amplitude in 3D, gyral-crown vs fundus thickness differentiation, MRI-template geometry, a Floquet/linear-stability derivation of g_c, or validation of Y-junction density against measured fetal sulcal graphs]" ;
