    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-riedel-delta-notch-phase-synchrony> a ns1:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Riedel-Kruse et al. (2007) & Morelli et al. (2009) zebrafish Delta-Notch delayed Kuramoto phase synchrony on an advected FGF8/Wnt-graded PSM lattice: kinematic waves, Mib1-gated coupling, emergent DAPT ALD/PRP faithfully reproduces Danio rerio (zebrafish presomitic mesoderm & paraxial somites); vendored SEM specimen is a chick (Gallus gallus) embryo used as a vertebrate somite-metamere stand-in morphology" ;
        dct:description "The simulation script(s) 2006-riedel-delta-notch-phase-synchrony.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Danio rerio (zebrafish presomitic mesoderm & paraxial somites); vendored SEM specimen is a chick (Gallus gallus) embryo used as a vertebrate somite-metamere stand-in specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 86.5/100, audit 2026-10-19-delta-notch-phase-synchrony-audit-v3) and the assessments." ;
        dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2006-riedel-delta-notch-phase-synchrony.py> ;
        ns1:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2006-riedel-delta-notch-phase-synchrony.py; output: docs/media/delta_notch_phase_synchrony_comparison.png; organism: Danio rerio (zebrafish presomitic mesoderm & paraxial somites); vendored SEM specimen is a chick (Gallus gallus) embryo used as a vertebrate somite-metamere stand-in; checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/d58a084; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0; spec_fingerprint: 09e5aac12df2ce2cf18eea96b6a21a56461679db4c6b4516072331c47fa27633; artifact_sha256: 24bdb2e7c7c300913001ecb821a0c2953e925858f4f6af09969f9ddf45047588; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/delta_notch_phase_synchrony/delta_notch_phase_synchrony_reference.json=209a056625b68a89..., datasets/delta_notch_phase_synchrony/scout_manifest.json=e3250a43b4bc0c22..., datasets/delta_notch_phase_synchrony/zebrafish_psm_synchrony_specimen.jpg=8b80971796cb29e2...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-delta-notch-phase-synchrony-audit-v2; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Riedel-Kruse et al. (2007) Science 317:1911-1915 & Morelli et al. (2009) HFSP J. 3:55-66 delayed Kuramoto phase-oscillator model dtheta_i/dt = omega_i + (kappa/z)*sum_j sin(theta_j(t - tau_c) - theta_i(t)) + xi_i(t), collective frequency shift Omega = omega_0 - kappa*sin(Omega*tau_c), linear stability stiffness kappa_eff = kappa*cos(Omega*tau_c) > 0 | Riedel-Kruse et al. (2007): DAPT pulse-chase Anterior Limit of Defects ALD(s_in) = s_in + ~5.5 somites (obs 5.4 +/- 0.8, 9.6 +/- 0.9, 14.4 +/- 0.9 for s_in = 0, 4, 9) and Posterior Rescue Point PRP = 14.7 +/- 1.1 after washout at s_out = 9; mib/aei/des/bea mutants desynchronise like early DAPT | Morelli et al. (2009) frequency profile omega(x) and kinematic phase waves k = (Omega - omega(x))/v travelling posterior -> anterior; Soroldoni et al. (2014) order 1-2 waves across the zebrafish PSM, waves slowing anteriorly; Herrgen et al. (2010) DAPT lengthens the segmentation period | Itoh et al. (2003): Mind bomb E3 ubiquitin ligase ubiquitinates Delta, required for Delta endocytosis and trans-activation of Notch; mib^ta52b abolishes Delta-Notch signalling; reconstructed_in_script: Transcendental collective frequency solver and 2D (tau_c, kappa) linear stability tongue (T_sync = 22.18 min, kappa_eff = 0.0623 min^-1 at tau_c = 20.5 min vs -0.0353 min^-1 at tau_c = 11.0 min) | Advected 24 x 12 AP x lateral nearest-neighbour delayed Kuramoto PSM lattice (open AP, periodic lateral, per-column period-scaled delay) under a tailbud-anchored exponential FGF8/Wnt frequency profile (f_A = 0.5): N_w = 1.58 kinematic waves (analytic 1.61), anterior wavelength 2.21 S (analytic 2.00 S), N_w monotone in f_A (2.52 -> -0.03 for f_A 0.3 -> 1.0) | Mib1-gated coupling kappa(t) = kappa_max u(t) g(t) with ubiquitination ODE (k_ub = 0.08, k_endo = 0.02 min^-1, u_ss^WT = 0.8) and gamma-secretase gate with 8-min DAPT clearance; mib1-null late R = 0.28 (ALD 5.8), Mib1 restoration at s = 9 rescues to R = 0.77 (PRP 15.3); dose sweep monotone | Emergent ALD/PRP from R_crit = 0.5 crossings of the half-period-smoothed front lateral order parameter + Delta_n_det = 2.5: 5-seed means ALD = 5.41 / 9.21 / 14.24 (obs 5.4 / 9.6 / 14.4), PRP = 14.86 (obs 14.7), RMSE 0.22 somites, Pearson r = 0.9998 (0.9986 over the 4 perturbed regimes); somite stage clock-counted at Omega(kappa(t)) so continuous DAPT lengthens the period from 22.18 to 25.00 min | Bilateral dorsal somite row DoG peak segmentation on the vendored SEM (48.47 px mean spacing, symmetry ratio 0.9606, fitted-sinusoid r = 0.563); transfer_boundary: The frequency profile is a single exponential with f_A = 0.5 and L = 6 S chosen to land in the 1-2-wave range reported for zebrafish; it is not digitised from Morelli (2009) Fig. 3 or Soroldoni (2014) kymographs, and the N_w measurement's reference value is the model's own analytic law | tau_c(x) omega(x) = const (coupling delay scales with the local period) is this script's assumption; the Eulerian-delay alternative was not simulated | k_ub, k_endo, tau_wash, DAPT dose/IC50 and Hill n are the script's reduced rate constants; D_phi = 0.003 rad^2/min, sigma_omega = 0.014 rad/min and tau_wash = 8 min were calibrated so the emergent ALD/PRP lags match the Riedel-Kruse (2007) data (as the paper fitted its desynchronisation rate) | The SEM specimen is a chick embryo (Wikimedia 'Aves Neural tube and somites in chick embryo'), used as a vertebrate somite-metamere stand-in; no zebrafish her1/deltaC in-situ wave pattern is vendored; does_not_claim: PSM shortening and the Soroldoni (2014) Doppler contribution to the segmentation period, cell division/ingression in the tailbud, 3D cell sorting, explicit Mib1 E3-ligase stoichiometry or measured Delta endocytosis rates, or a boundary profile derived from the phase pattern (chi(s) is a coherence-gated synthetic rendering)]" ;
        ns1:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0092-8674(01)00437-8>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/S1534-5807(02)00409-4>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cub.2010.06.034>,
