    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-runions-leaf-venation> a ns1:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Runions et al. (2005) Leaf Venation Space-Colonization & Murray's Law faithfully reproduces Ginkgo biloba (open dichotomous venation) & angiosperm dicot lamina (reticulate venation) morphology" ;
        dct:description "The simulation script(s) 2005-runions-leaf-venation.py, docs/media/runions_leaf_venation_growth.gif, runions_leaf_venation_metrics.csv implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Ginkgo biloba (open dichotomous venation) & angiosperm dicot lamina (reticulate venation) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 91.3/100, audit 2026-10-18-venation-audit-v2) and the assessments." ;
        dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/c89d18d/2005-runions-leaf-venation.py>,
            <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/c89d18d/docs/media/runions_leaf_venation_growth.gif>,
            <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/c89d18d/runions_leaf_venation_metrics.csv> ;
        ns1:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/c89d18d/2005-runions-leaf-venation.py, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/c89d18d/docs/media/runions_leaf_venation_growth.gif, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/c89d18d/runions_leaf_venation_metrics.csv; output: runions_leaf_venation_comparison.png; organism: Ginkgo biloba (open dichotomous venation) & angiosperm dicot lamina (reticulate venation); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/c89d18d; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1; spec_fingerprint: 9c51f0ee1bb18dac15303bbc28f21b848e721403f4cfc6f6459cd6e7325c2ab9; artifact_sha256: d7f0922fe27597dd1757a5525cd01c5a03356d817ba67aec405a918bfb794e34; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/venation/ginkgo_open_venation_specimen.jpg=5a620943881fe698..., datasets/venation/reticulate_vein_skeleton_specimen.jpg=6d06d3e545bd585b..., datasets/venation/venation_reference.json=c22c5f4e26f3e2c6...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-18-venation-audit; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Runions et al. (2005) define open auxin space-colonization (Eq. 1) via Voronoi nearest-vein neighborhoods and closed reticulate venation (Eq. 2-3) via Toussaint Relative Neighborhood Graph (RNG) neighborhoods with persistent tagged-source anastomosis | Murray (1926) derives minimum-work pipe scaling r_parent^3 = sum r_child^3, while Price et al. (2013) measure 349 cleared leaves (1,514,771 junctions) showing a transition from Murray's law in minor veins (gamma ~ 3, area ratio ~ 1.25) to area-preserving branching in major veins (gamma ~ 2, area ratio ~ 1.01) | Katifori & Magnasco (2012) and Ronellenfitsch et al. (2015) quantify hierarchical areole loop nesting via recursive minimum-width vein removal on the planar dual graph; reconstructed_in_script: Open Ginkgo biloba (Table 1 Fig. 10) and closed dicot (Table 1 Fig. 15) space-colonization simulators with persistent V(s) source tagging and planar segment-intersection checks, multiscale Horton-Strahler vascular tree measurement, and planar dual areole loop nesting on both simulated networks and segmented specimen photographs; transfer_boundary: Direct comparison of simulated planar dual areole nesting and Strahler bifurcation scaling against segmented leaf skeleton specimens and Price et al. (2013) / Ronellenfitsch et al. (2015) empirical benchmarks; does_not_claim: 2D planar lamina space-colonization and pipe-model radius propagation do not model 3D mesophyll thickness or stomatal transpiration dynamics]" ;
        ns1:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.12.3.207>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1145/1073204.1073251>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1004680>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0037994>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0085420> ;
