    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth> a ns1:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Savin et al. (2011) discrete gut rod coupled to a finite-element (CST, St.Venant-Kirchhoff) dorsal-mesentery membrane with an apicobasal Pitx2 stiffness gradient faithfully reproduces Vertebrate midgut & dorsal mesentery (Gallus gallus, Coturnix japonica, Taeniopygia guttata, Mus musculus) morphology" ;
        dct:description "The simulation script(s) 2011-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Vertebrate midgut & dorsal mesentery (Gallus gallus, Coturnix japonica, Taeniopygia guttata, Mus musculus) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 80.0/100, audit 2026-10-19-gut-looping-differential-growth-audit-v3) and the assessments." ;
        dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/327729c8/2011-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth.py> ;
        ns1:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/327729c8/2011-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth.py; output: docs/media/gut_looping_differential_growth_comparison.png; organism: Vertebrate midgut & dorsal mesentery (Gallus gallus, Coturnix japonica, Taeniopygia guttata, Mus musculus); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/327729c8; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0; spec_fingerprint: 6fb7e55e6158cd10ddf94728c17f791e81e999f808f135655cb2a64003d9cc1b; artifact_sha256: ecc65dee03e0c3a533d95c7271c0e853a30687d6ea5ba5c237d41f3e7f9c41e4; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/gut_looping_differential_growth/fe_mesentery_mesh_reference.json=8025ecf7fd54a0ef..., datasets/gut_looping_differential_growth/gut_looping_differential_growth_reference.json=f73121bb4140187f..., datasets/gut_looping_differential_growth/intestine_mesentery_specimen.jpg=e12fee9ac1fb5f3d..., datasets/gut_looping_differential_growth/paper_citations.bib=201f4db588717f47..., datasets/gut_looping_differential_growth/scout_manifest.json=0723b42b4d825087...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-gut-looping-differential-growth-audit-v2; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Savin et al. (2011): the midgut loops because the tube grows faster than the dorsal mesentery it is attached to (strain epsilon = (L_t - L_m)/L_m); loop wavelength and radius scale as lambda = 4.55 ell_*, R = 1.68 ell_* with ell_* = (E_t I_t / (E_m h_m))^(1/3); surgically freed tubes uncoil; the collapse holds across chick ontogeny (E8-E16) and across zebra finch, quail, chick and mouse (Fig. 4e-f) | Nerurkar, Mahadevan & Tabin (2017): BMP2 over-expression increases and Noggin decreases the differential strain and the number of loops at E12 | Kurpios et al. (2008), Davis et al. (2008): Pitx2-dependent left-right asymmetric condensation and architecture of the dorsal mesentery set the handedness of looping; reconstructed_in_script: Analytical strain, annular inertia and cube-law predictions; a 96-node discrete rod (axial + second-difference bending energy) sharing its nodes with the gut edge of a 96 x 5 CST St.Venant-Kirchhoff plane-stress membrane mesh of a trapezoidal fan (root fixed, rod ends pinned) with a mean-preserving apicobasal Pitx2 stiffness field; L-BFGS-B relaxation with emergent turning-number loop count, R = 1/<kappa>, contour length per loop and tortuosity for E8-E16, BMP2/WT/Noggin/ablation at E12, a Pitx2-gradient sweep and a mesh-refinement check; the 14-point analytical collapse; chromaticity + DoG segmentation of a vendored mesentery photograph; transfer_boundary: The FE model is a pure membrane (no sheet bending, no left-right rest curvature): looping handedness is NOT selected and the script makes no chirality claim; W_m/L_m = 0.18, root fraction 0.7, nu_m = 0.45 and a_Pitx2 = 0.4 are modelling assumptions flagged in fe_mesentery_mesh_reference.json, not measurements | The emergent morphometrics are unfitted: E12 N = 9.81 vs 8.5, R = 0.952 vs 1.15 mm; E8-E16 MAPE 18.7 % (N) and 21.4 % (R); the ontogenetic log-log slope of R_sim vs ell_* is 0.61 (cube law 1.0); N changes by 7.7 % on 96x5 -> 128x6 refinement | The 14-point cross-species table in gut_looping_differential_growth_reference.json reproduces lambda = 4.55 ell_* and R = 1.68 ell_* to ~1 % with identical log-log slopes for lambda and R, so the r = 0.9999 collapse is a consistency check of the table against the law, not an independent validation against digitised Fig. 4e-f data; does_not_claim: A Kirchhoff rod with twist, a Kirchhoff-Love shell, chirality / handedness selection, mesh-converged loop numbers, measured Pitx2 stiffness gradients, moduli for the BMP2/Noggin conditions traceable to Nerurkar 2017, or an embryonic-chick specimen image (the vendored photograph is an adult mammalian mesentery)]" ;
        ns1:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.devcel.2008.05.001>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature10277>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0803578105>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1618677114>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1238842> ;
        ns1:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth-code-traceability>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth-model-fidelity>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth-morphometric-validation>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth-overall>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth-parameter-expressivity>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth-repro-package>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth-source-traceability>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-savin-gut-looping-differential-growth-specimen-match> ;
        ns1:weightOfEvidence 8e-01 .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing> a ns1:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Schnakenberg (1979) tri-molecular limit-cycle & Turing reaction-diffusion morphogenesis faithfully reproduces Dictyostelium discoideum (cellular slime mold cAMP oscillations & fruiting body aggregation) morphology" ;
        dct:description "The simulation script(s) 1979-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Dictyostelium discoideum (cellular slime mold cAMP oscillations & fruiting body aggregation) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 89.8/100, audit 2026-10-19-limit-cycle-turing-audit-v3) and the assessments." ;
        dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/3aaa03d/1979-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing.py> ;
        ns1:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/3aaa03d/1979-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing.py; output: docs/media/limit_cycle_turing_comparison.png; organism: Dictyostelium discoideum (cellular slime mold cAMP oscillations & fruiting body aggregation); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/3aaa03d; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0; spec_fingerprint: 2171bdf8211cc376e4fec882bcd645f848050c6a4e0c6d15ce22984bb3384713; artifact_sha256: a323c621aa63149ccc29db5fba8d855d51e45cdd34cffd63205b81f1dff7e9e7; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/limit_cycle_turing/dictyostelium_specimen.jpg=e2d2b739211bda97..., datasets/limit_cycle_turing/limit_cycle_turing_reference.json=cc22252b314c8bb8..., datasets/limit_cycle_turing/scout_manifest.json=e71deffb9f317a88...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-limit-cycle-turing-audit-v2; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Schnakenberg (1979): the tri-molecular cubic autocatalytic scheme has a unique positive steady state (a+b, b/(a+b)^2), a Hopf curve b - a = (a+b)^3 and, beyond it, a Poincaré–Bendixson limit cycle | Turing (1952): differential diffusion destabilizes a stable reaction equilibrium in a finite wavenumber band; on a sphere the unstable modes are spherical harmonics | Martiel & Goldbeter (1987): a 3-variable receptor-desensitization model (rho_T, beta, gamma) with extracellular PDE rate k_e produces autonomous cAMP oscillations and relay | Gerisch & Hess (1974): suspended D. discoideum cells show spontaneous cAMP-controlled oscillations with a period of several minutes (~5-10 min) | Crampin, Gaffney & Maini (1999): on uniformly growing domains reaction-diffusion patterns undergo frequency-doubling with a dilution term -(L'/L) u; reconstructed_in_script: Exact equilibrium, Jacobian, Hopf curve, d_c(a,b), planar dispersion sigma(k^2) and its Turing band (q_-, q_+); RK4 limit-cycle ODE; 2D pseudo-spectral RD solver with 5 regimes and a 7-point d sweep; SHA-256-locked specimen segmentation (Pass 2) | Hemispherical-mound RD solver with exact Laplace–Beltrami propagators, spherical-harmonic (Legendre) power spectrum, mound-radius sweep against l*(R) and hexagonal packing, critical mound radius R_min; elongating-stalk solver with ring-count kymograph (Pass 3 R1) | First-order and Michaelis–Menten PDE sinks with closed-form equilibria, analytical + numerical Hopf thresholds, Martiel–Goldbeter relay integration and k_e sweep, dimensionless pulse-shape comparison (Pass 3 R2) | Five Lean 4 theorems (Laws 1-5) mirrored by integer checks in --self-test; transfer_boundary: Mound radius R, stalk radius 0.08 and lengths 1->4 are in the dimensionless planar domain units (L = 6); they are NOT calibrated to the specimen's 32.9 px sorus diameter or stalk length, so the curved-geometry results are predictions of the model's own scaling, not specimen measurements | The Martiel–Goldbeter parameter set is the widely used Table I set; with it this implementation gives a 10.68 min period at k_e = 5.4 min^-1, above the ~7 min (5-10 min) Gerisch & Hess anchor; the discrepancy is reported, not tuned away | Schnakenberg u is identified with extracellular cAMP for the PDE sink; the 2-species model has no receptor variable, so the pulse-shape comparison with Martiel–Goldbeter is dimensionless (duty cycle, fold change, waveform r = 0.78), not a time-scale match; does_not_claim: A volumetric 3D solver of the culminant, tip-growth (non-uniform) stalk elongation, chemotactic cell movement, or that Turing rings on a stalk are an observed Dictyostelium phenotype; a digitized comparison with Martiel & Goldbeter's own time-series figures; spatial (Turing) analysis of the PDE-extended model]" ;
        ns1:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1006/bulm.1999.0131>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(79)90042-0>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0006-3495(87)83275-7>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/253540a0>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.71.5.2118>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1952.0012>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1004367> ;
        ns1:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing-code-traceability>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing-model-fidelity>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing-morphometric-validation>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing-overall>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing-parameter-expressivity>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing-repro-package>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing-source-traceability>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-schnakenberg-limit-cycle-turing-specimen-match> ;
        ns1:weightOfEvidence 8.98e-01 .

