        ns1:weightOfEvidence 9.21e-01 .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly> a ns1:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Sheth et al. (2012) Science distal Hoxa13/Hoxd11-13 + Gli3 dose modulation of Turing digit wavelength on a fan-shaped embryonic autopod, with Pass 3 AER-FGF8 mitogenic outgrowth on a deforming Lagrangian mesh faithfully reproduces Vertebrate embryonic autopod (Mus musculus distal Hox/Gli3 allelic series & postaxial hexadactylous autopod radiograph) morphology" ;
        dct:description "The simulation script(s) 2012-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Vertebrate embryonic autopod (Mus musculus distal Hox/Gli3 allelic series & postaxial hexadactylous autopod radiograph) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 91.3/100, audit 2026-10-19-hox-turing-polydactyly-audit-v3) and the assessments." ;
        dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/58b898c/2012-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly.py> ;
        ns1:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/58b898c/2012-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly.py; output: docs/media/hox_turing_polydactyly_comparison.png; organism: Vertebrate embryonic autopod (Mus musculus distal Hox/Gli3 allelic series & postaxial hexadactylous autopod radiograph); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/58b898c; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0; spec_fingerprint: df2380b6b9d39cc7343d21970d756072ccaee92ea4d1cd0e08f469c328909c2c; artifact_sha256: 4f0e23e35e7cb8c99037a2861ab479bf20313159bb3b61db076535db0ba71572; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/hox_turing_polydactyly/hox_turing_polydactyly_reference.json=06c60968ccdce3a7..., datasets/hox_turing_polydactyly/pass3_aer_growth_reference.json=311a1e81311eabab..., datasets/hox_turing_polydactyly/scout_manifest.json=c0608869f6d213a4..., datasets/hox_turing_polydactyly/vertebrate_autopod_digits_specimen.jpg=995e43a2a0cf7815...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-hox-turing-polydactyly-audit-v2; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Sheth et al. (2012): progressive loss of distal Hox (Hoxa13, Hoxd11-13) in a Gli3-null background shrinks the digit period (wavelength) of a Turing-type mechanism, raising digit number from 5 to ~14 at roughly constant autopod width (Figs. 1-3) | Crampin, Gaffney & Maini (1999): on a growing domain the reaction-diffusion equations acquire an advection term and a dilution term -(div v) u; patterns lag the fixed-domain wavelength and transition by peak insertion / frequency doubling | Boehm et al. (2010): limb bud proliferation is distally biased but a proliferation gradient alone is insufficient to explain bud shape | Summerbell (1974): AER excision arrests distal outgrowth; the earlier the excision the more proximal the truncation; reconstructed_in_script: Sheth et al. (2012) linear dispersion, k_c(H) and the cubic-saturated two-component PDE on a 1D Neumann arc and a 2D fixed-width polar fan (Pass 2), plus the Pass 3 AER-FGF8 kinematic growing fan in ALE form with dilution, mesh-relative advection, physical-metric angular modes, backward-Euler radial diffusion, Lagrangian tracers, AER regression and ablation, a g_max sweep and the quasi-static digit-number/width law; 6-genotype allelic series; dual negative controls; radiograph digit-ray segmentation; 5 Lean 4 theorems; transfer_boundary: Growth is kinematic: g(r,t) is prescribed by the mitogen field and div v = g; no elastic/viscous constitutive law, stress balance or oriented cell behaviour is solved (Boehm et al. 2010 show these matter for shape) | Digit-ray (stripe) orientation is imposed by PD/AP diffusion anisotropy D_r = 0.05 D rather than derived from the Fgf/Wnt proximodistal modulation of Raspopovic et al. (2014) | k_c(H) = 14 - 9H and g_u(H) = 200 f_u + 25 k_c^4 - 4.5|tr J_kc| are closure ansaetze that interpolate the allelic series and pin sigma_max ~ 4.5; they are not fitted to Sheth et al.'s supplementary parameter values | The 1D arc and fixed-width fan solvers seed the target cosine mode (-0.08 cos(n_target s)); only the Pass 3 growing fan evolves from seeded noise alone, and it shows a growth-induced wavelength lag (N_grow = 3.5 WT, 13.0 null vs law 5 / 14); does_not_claim: 3D limb bud geometry, cell-level mechanics, Sox9/Bmp/Wnt three-node kinetics, quantitative reproduction of Sheth et al.'s Fig. 2G digit-period measurements (not vendored), or hour-calibrated developmental time]" ;
        ns1:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1006/bulm.1999.0131>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2005.10.016>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1179047>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1226804>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1252960>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.462174>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.32.3.651>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pbio.1000420> ;
        ns1:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly-code-traceability>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly-model-fidelity>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly-morphometric-validation>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly-overall>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly-parameter-expressivity>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly-repro-package>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly-source-traceability>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly-specimen-match> ;
        ns1:weightOfEvidence 9.13e-01 .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-shyer-intestinal-villi-buckling> a ns1:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Hannezo et al. (2011) PRL & Shyer et al. (2013) Science sequential smooth-muscle mucosal buckling into ridges, zigzags, and hexagonal villi faithfully reproduces Vertebrate embryonic gut mucosa (Gallus gallus, Coturnix japonica, Mus musculus) morphology" ;
        dct:description "The simulation script(s) 2013-shyer-intestinal-villi-buckling.py, docs/media/epithelial_buckling_crypt_villus_growth.gif, docs/media/epithelial_buckling_crypt_villus_tubular_shh_bmp.png, datasets/epithelial_buckling_crypt_villus/tubular_shh_bmp_reference.json, datasets/epithelial_buckling_crypt_villus/pass3_citations.bib implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Vertebrate embryonic gut mucosa (Gallus gallus, Coturnix japonica, Mus musculus) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 87.8/100, audit 2026-10-19-epithelial-buckling-crypt-villus-audit-v3) and the assessments." ;
        dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/2013-shyer-intestinal-villi-buckling.py>,
            <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/datasets/epithelial_buckling_crypt_villus/pass3_citations.bib>,
            <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/datasets/epithelial_buckling_crypt_villus/tubular_shh_bmp_reference.json>,
            <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/docs/media/epithelial_buckling_crypt_villus_growth.gif>,
            <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/docs/media/epithelial_buckling_crypt_villus_tubular_shh_bmp.png> ;
        ns1:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/2013-shyer-intestinal-villi-buckling.py, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/docs/media/epithelial_buckling_crypt_villus_growth.gif, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/docs/media/epithelial_buckling_crypt_villus_tubular_shh_bmp.png, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/datasets/epithelial_buckling_crypt_villus/tubular_shh_bmp_reference.json, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/datasets/epithelial_buckling_crypt_villus/pass3_citations.bib; output: docs/media/epithelial_buckling_crypt_villus_comparison.png; organism: Vertebrate embryonic gut mucosa (Gallus gallus, Coturnix japonica, Mus musculus); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/45670cb8; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0; spec_fingerprint: da01f54f3142bab9fe39c5f26bd338e06f8c4d88ac4dfcc5ab72c0d0def8016a; artifact_sha256: a1cc184d192301cde6a1045c99e0774008edf896123bc90cac8a1251cb7ea1a5; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/epithelial_buckling_crypt_villus/epithelial_buckling_crypt_villus_reference.json=1887bf2160034e33..., datasets/epithelial_buckling_crypt_villus/intestinal_villi_crypts_specimen.jpg=30afcb789bbdc60c..., datasets/epithelial_buckling_crypt_villus/paper_citations.bib=a8bc0251af8be542..., datasets/epithelial_buckling_crypt_villus/pass3_citations.bib=38af06185530b95f..., datasets/epithelial_buckling_crypt_villus/scout_manifest.json=1e6e1bbc98fb4873..., datasets/epithelial_buckling_crypt_villus/tubular_shh_bmp_reference.json=c3f1b76b4c31b3a1...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-epithelial-buckling-crypt-villus-audit-v2; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Shyer et al. (2013): sequential differentiation of circumferential, longitudinal and second circumferential smooth-muscle layers compresses the chick gut mucosa into longitudinal ridges (E8-E10), herringbone zigzags (E13-E14) and a hexagonal array of villi (E16); FK506 muscle inhibition and surgical slitting arrest the cascade at the preceding regime; the wavelength scales as a quartic length (B_e/K_s)^(1/4) across chick, quail and mouse | Hannezo, Prost & Joanny (2011): buckling of a monolayered epithelium on an elastic stroma with wavenumber q_* = (K_s/B_e)^(1/4) and an apicobasal cubic term that selects finger-like protrusions over invaginations | Walton et al. (2012, 2016) and Shyer et al. (2015): Hh-responsive mesenchymal clusters localise under the epithelium at the tips of emerging villi (mouse) and at the high-curvature elbows of zigzags (chick), with BMP signalling from the clusters | Timoshenko & Goodier (1970) §28 and Donnell (1933): the Lamé thick-walled cylinder displacement u = A r + B/r and the shell curvature parameter that controls when a flat-plate (FvK) reduction of a thin cylindrical shell is valid; reconstructed_in_script: Mucosal bending rigidity B_e, Winkler foundation K_s, quartic length ell_* and a 4-regime classifier; a 64^2 pseudo-spectral FvK free energy minimised by L-BFGS-B (65 iterations) then blended with a prescribed cosine; a 48-element axisymmetric plane-strain ring FEM of the mesenchymal annulus with rigid outer (smooth-muscle) wall giving K_tube, slab limit, curvature factor and optional neo-Hookean prestrain tangent; integer mode quantisation n = round(2 pi R / lambda) and the Donnell ratio per stage; an OLS-through-origin tube prefactor c_tube = 0.5513; a curvature-driven Shh field, percentile-thresholded cluster indicator, localized cubic gain and a linear spectral Newton response with a 30% trust region; a 12-point 3-species wavelength collapse; 5 FK506/surgical controls; DoG + Delaunay segmentation of the vendored specimen; 17 reference-anchored measurements; transfer_boundary: The tubular coupling is a 1D-radial axisymmetric FEM feeding a scalar K_eff into the 2D flat FvK sheet, not a 3D non-axisymmetric tubular neo-Hookean solid; the Donnell ratio itself says the flat reduction is only well justified from E13 on (gamma 0.65 at E8) | Stage amplitudes, zigzag angles and |Psi_6| are prescribed from the observed values (or literals) rather than emerging from the minimiser, so the amplitude, theta and |Psi_6| 'measurements' are templated; the reported lambda_sim is 0.85 lambda_* + 0.15 lambda_fft | The stage-resolved E_e, E_s, H_s, epsilon_x, epsilon_y, alpha_3 in epithelial_buckling_crypt_villus_reference.json were fitted so that the flat model with C_LAMBDA_PREFACTOR = 0.5690 reproduces lambda_obs; the r = 0.9996 collapse inherits that fit | The Shh field is curvature-driven (no Ptch1/Gli reaction-diffusion); elbow curvature is proxied by crest-contour turning curvature because the prescribed developable surface has no preferential elbow dome curvature; cluster-enrichment references are qualitative (null = 1.0) | The SHA-pinned specimen is a CC0 terminal-ileum H&E cross-section of unknown species and age, compared with chick E16 hexagonal order without a pixel scale; does_not_claim: A full 3D tubular neo-Hookean finite-element solution, emergent (unprescribed) stage amplitudes or zigzag angles, a reaction-diffusion Shh/BMP/Ptch1 network, finite smooth-muscle sheath stiffness, species-matched specimen histology, or empirically measured stage-resolved mesenchymal moduli]; other sources: Stability of thin-walled tubes under torsion <https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/19930091553>, Theory of Elasticity (3rd ed.), §28 thick-walled cylinder (Lamé problem) <https://archive.org/details/theoryofelastici0000timo>" ;
        ns1:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2015.03.041>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1205669109>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.107.078104>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.110.024302>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1238842>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.130112> ;
        ns1:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-shyer-intestinal-villi-buckling-code-traceability>,
