        ns1:weightOfEvidence 8.59e-01 .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting> a ns1:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Steinberg (1963, 1970) & Graner-Glazier (1992) differential adhesion cell sorting faithfully reproduces Chick embryo (Gallus gallus) dissociated tissue aggregates & multicellular embryoid body spheroids morphology" ;
        dct:description "The simulation script(s) 1964-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Chick embryo (Gallus gallus) dissociated tissue aggregates & multicellular embryoid body spheroids specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 89.9/100, audit 2026-10-19-differential-adhesion-sorting-audit-v3) and the assessments." ;
        dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/654cd6fc/1964-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting.py> ;
        ns1:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/654cd6fc/1964-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting.py; output: docs/media/differential_adhesion_sorting_comparison.png; organism: Chick embryo (Gallus gallus) dissociated tissue aggregates & multicellular embryoid body spheroids; checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/654cd6fc; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0; spec_fingerprint: 439c3a9015bc8fdc9014e2aa3a89cd71cffc876fcd81d0cb0b2f88bbf798d5a9; artifact_sha256: 6046cb66ae62af9e47d3b593c06f690c6b389ec313e42183a47ccced8c8cf39f; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-differential-adhesion-sorting-audit-v2; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Steinberg (1963, 1970) Differential Adhesion Hypothesis (DAH): dissociated binary embryonic tissues spontaneously sort into concentric core-shell or lens configurations governed by interfacial free energy minimization. | Graner & Glazier (1992) PRL Eqs. 1-3: extended Cellular Potts Hamiltonian with interfacial tensions gamma_AB = J_AB - (J_AA + J_BB)/2 and gamma_tauM = J_tauM - J_tautau/2 partitioning parameter space into checkerboard (gamma_AB < 0), complete engulfment (0 < gamma_AB < gamma_BM - gamma_AM), partial engulfment (gamma_AB > gamma_BM - gamma_AM > 0), and dissociation (gamma_AM < 0); Fig. 3 reports logarithmically slow decay of the heterotypic boundary length. | Foty, Pfleger, Forgacs & Steinberg (1996) Development Table 1: empirical Gallus gallus tissue surface tensions (20.1 > 12.6 > 8.5 > 4.6 > 1.6 dyn/cm) strictly predict transitive mutual envelopment.; reconstructed_in_script: 2D extended Cellular Potts Model (60^2, 68 cells) across all 5 thermodynamic regimes plus a 7-point continuous J_AB sweep, with a cell-level type-swap accelerator and, in the partial-engulfment regime only, an ad hoc symmetry-breaking field. | Pass 3: 3D extended Cellular Potts spheroid on a 64^3 lattice (840 cells, 26-neighbour adhesion, volume constraint, 8-colour sublattice-parallel Metropolis) with its 2D equatorial z-section, a Kawasaki-swap ablation and a 3D equal-adhesion control; logarithmic vs power-law fits of L_AB(t)/L(t) with exponents compared to the LSW alpha = 1/3 bound. | Computer-vision segmentation of a confocal fluorescence embryoid body spheroid (`cell_sorting_specimen.jpg`) comparing empirical GFP/RFP radial occupancy against the 2D Potts core-shell profile (r = 0.925) and the 3D equatorial-section profile (r = 0.758).; transfer_boundary: 64^3 x 200 MCS is far from the asymptotic coarsening regime; exponents are fitted over ~2.3 decades of MCS including the initial transient, and the power-law vs logarithmic R^2 (0.9965 vs 0.9845 in 3D; 0.737 vs 0.769 in 2D) do not discriminate the two laws. | The LSW alpha = 1/3 reference is a conserved-order-parameter coarsening bound, not an exponent measured for the Cellular Potts model; the Nakajima & Ishihara (2011) exponent is deliberately left null in the reference JSON because the paper could not be consulted offline. | The vendored specimen is a Wikimedia Commons embryoid body, not a chick-tissue aggregate from Steinberg or Foty; the radial-profile comparison is a morphological analogy, not a reproduction of a paper figure.; does_not_claim: Does not model active chemotaxis, subcellular cadherin trafficking kinetics, or the fluctuation-dependence of sorting studied by Mombach et al. (1995). | Does not claim the cell-level type-swap accelerator or the partial-engulfment bias field are part of the Graner & Glazier (1992) Hamiltonian.]" ;
        ns1:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1002/jez.1401730406>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cpc.2007.03.007>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1088/1367-2630/13/3/033035>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevE.47.2128>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.69.2013>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.75.2244>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.141.3579.401>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.122.5.1611> ;
        ns1:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting-code-traceability>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting-model-fidelity>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting-morphometric-validation>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting-overall>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting-parameter-expressivity>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting-repro-package>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting-source-traceability>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting-specimen-match> ;
        ns1:weightOfEvidence 8.99e-01 .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-streichan-global-morphogenetic-flow> a ns1:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Streichan et al. (2018), Mayer et al. (2010), Lefebvre et al. (2023) & Brauns et al. (2024) Drosophila global morphogenetic flow, curved-surface active nematic myosin mechanics & cell intercalation faithfully reproduces Drosophila melanogaster (whole-embryo cellular blastoderm & germband extension stages 6-8) morphology" ;
        dct:description "The simulation script(s) 2018-streichan-global-morphogenetic-flow.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Drosophila melanogaster (whole-embryo cellular blastoderm & germband extension stages 6-8) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 91.0/100, audit 2026-10-19-global-morphogenetic-flow-audit-v3) and the assessments." ;
        dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/f18e3533/2018-streichan-global-morphogenetic-flow.py> ;
        ns1:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/f18e3533/2018-streichan-global-morphogenetic-flow.py; output: docs/media/global_morphogenetic_flow_comparison.png; organism: Drosophila melanogaster (whole-embryo cellular blastoderm & germband extension stages 6-8); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/f18e3533; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0; spec_fingerprint: c6f91e927b85c9e6c96461d53e4ae9c082d9c0ad9d74ed650b6b2f21fb08b782; artifact_sha256: c2b12d9cc11f49cbc76202021e27a120ea25ff2713abd4ee312c77cb90e82127; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/global_morphogenetic_flow/drosophila_germband_extension_specimen.jpg=2d7fad8f57edcadf..., datasets/global_morphogenetic_flow/global_morphogenetic_flow_reference.json=160ead86ff9c447b..., datasets/global_morphogenetic_flow/scout_manifest.json=990f3ea83019f3d1...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-global-morphogenetic-flow-audit-v2; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Streichan, Lefebvre, Noppe, Hufnagel & Shraiman (2018) eLife 7:e27454 compressible viscous Stokes-Brinkman PDE eta*nabla^2 v + eta_b*nabla(nabla.v) - (eta/ell_H^2)*v = -nabla.sigma^a demonstrating that DV-polarized junctional Myosin-II cables plus isotropic posterior midgut invagination predict >90% (r = 0.924) of global embryonic tissue velocity | Mayer et al. (2010) Nature 467:617-621 hydrodynamic screening length ell_H = sqrt(eta/xi); Lefebvre et al. (2023) eLife 12:e78787 geometric/mechanical control of Myosin-II orientation and recruitment on the ellipsoidal embryo; Brauns et al. (2024) eLife 13:RP95521 tension-isogonal decomposition of convergent extension into cell rearrangement (T1/rosette) and cell-shape parts; Bertet et al. (2004) / Blankenship et al. (2006) junction shrinkage and 5-11-cell rosettes; reconstructed_in_script: 64x48 2D spectral Helmholtz compressible Stokes-Brinkman solver on the 500x420 um cartographic domain (Green's function L2 error 3.6e-16), 6-regime wild-type/mutant benchmark and 30 min Lagrangian marker advection (unchanged from Pass 2) | Pass 3: 56x48 (s, phi) finite-difference solver of the same force balance ON the prolate spheroid a = 250, b = 105 um using the exact embedded covariant strain, metric and Gaussian curvature K = a^2/g_ss^2 (sphere-limit analytic residual 5.8e-3, order 2.04; curved-vs-cartographic WT vector correlation r = 0.833; 31% of nodes carry intrinsic pole-return flow), strain-rate positive-feedback myosin recruitment to its fixed point (g = 0.358, m*/m_0 = 1.70), and a 240-junction T1/rosette ledger with tension-isogonal split (125 collapses, 24 rosettes up to 10 cells, median shrink 7.75 min, intercalation share 0.64) | Automated computer-vision contour, pair-rule stripe, DV cable gradient anisotropy, and posterior midgut invagination fold segmentation on drosophila_germband_extension_specimen.jpg (IDR0151, AP/DV = 2.3853 vs 2.3810 biological, 8 stripes, spacing = 75.86 px, solidity = 0.9383); transfer_boundary: Reduced curved-surface continuum: finite differences (not FEM) on a truncated (s, phi) grid with 20 um pole caps held at v = 0, single velocity-scale calibration to the 6.40 um/min WT peak, one-way myosin -> flow -> junction coupling; ledger rate constants calibrated to the Bertet (5-10 min) and Brauns (0.5-0.8) windows; does_not_claim: A predictive (uncalibrated) flow-correlation against measured PIV fields, two-way vertex-continuum coupling, 3D yolk/vitelline fluid-structure interaction, or digitised values for the Bertet/Blankenship/Brauns anchors (verified_offline = false)]" ;
        ns1:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.devcel.2006.09.007>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature02590>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature09376>,
            <https://doi.org/10.7554/eLife.27454>,
            <https://doi.org/10.7554/eLife.78787>,
            <https://doi.org/10.7554/eLife.95521> ;
        ns1:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-streichan-global-morphogenetic-flow-code-traceability>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-streichan-global-morphogenetic-flow-model-fidelity>,
