    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep> a ns1:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Sumper (2002) & Lenoci-Camp (2008) hierarchical Cahn-Hilliard diatom biosilica phase separation (Pass 3: centrifugal precipitation front + 3-stage single-domain quench) faithfully reproduces Coscinodiscus wailesii (Centric marine diatom frustule valve pores: foramen, cribrum, cribrella; radial costae) morphology" ;
        dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2002-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Coscinodiscus wailesii (Centric marine diatom frustule valve pores: foramen, cribrum, cribrella; radial costae) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 89.0/100, audit 2026-10-19-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-audit-v3) and the assessments." ;
        dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a69596cc/models/2002-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep.py> ;
        ns1:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a69596cc/models/2002-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep.py; output: docs/media/diatom_frustule_phase_sep_comparison.png; organism: Coscinodiscus wailesii (Centric marine diatom frustule valve pores: foramen, cribrum, cribrella; radial costae); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/a69596cc; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1; spec_fingerprint: a0656c1e84af378ca65d37247e04ce369aa44a7a1166c9de2688cf2ac0451d64; artifact_sha256: a9c947d7cead9aa4a0732db15d97ed3496cfd5451433cba2f7314b23cf1a6e47; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/diatom_frustule_phase_sep/coscinodiscus_diatom_specimen.jpg=47aca39b720b67b1..., datasets/diatom_frustule_phase_sep/diatom_frustule_phase_sep_reference.json=b6ffc32e8bdecb23..., datasets/diatom_frustule_phase_sep/scout_manifest.json=0eea5a04552420e8...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-audit-v2; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Sumper (2002): LCPA/silica liquid-liquid phase separation inside the SDV yields three self-similar hexagonal pore tiers (foramen d_1 = 1250 nm / a_1 = 1850 nm; cribrum d_2 = 220 / a_2 = 380 nm; cribrella d_3 = 42 / a_3 = 75 nm) | Lenoci & Camp (2008): a two-stage quenched Cahn-Hilliard model with solidified silica walls reproduces nested foramen/cribrum pore hierarchies; linear spinodal dispersion sigma(k) = M k^2 (1 - 3 phi0^2 - eps^2 k^2) | Furukawa (1992): a quench front moving at speed v through a binary mixture produces lamellae perpendicular to the front at slow speeds and parallel to the front at fast speeds, with an isotropic limit as v -> infinity | Schmid & Volcani (1983): C. wailesii valve morphogenesis proceeds centrifugally from the pattern centre with radial costae branching toward the margin; reconstructed_in_script: Semi-implicit spectral Cahn-Hilliard solver with exact zero-mode mass conservation, extended with a spatially varying bulk term phi^3 - a(x) phi and a zero-mobility frozen mask with total-mass re-projection (L178-L243) | Radial quench front a(r,t) = tanh((R0 + v t - r)/w) with lagging solidification front R_s = R - lag lambda_c on a disc, conserved thermal noise, margin gradient-tensor anisotropy A, front Peclet number v/(lambda_c sigma_max), 5-speed ablation and 3-seed isotropic null (L346-L580) | Three-stage single-domain 512^2 quench with per-tier eps from lambda_c inversion at 12.5 nm/px, eroded parent-pore chambers with frozen walls, per-tier counts, nested multiplicities, nearest-neighbour pitches and equivalent diameters (L587-L724) | Pass 2 two-stage hierarchy, dispersion relation, eps sweep, SEM segmentation of 139 foramina / 74 cribrum pores, hexatic |psi_6| and 3-tier log-linear scaling (L124-L171, L244-L331, L730-L975); transfer_boundary: The costae model is validated against its own isotropic null and the sign of A, not against a specimen: the vendored SEM shows the valve face at three magnifications and no margin, so no empirical A or rib spacing exists in the package | Front speed, solidification lag (1.0 lambda_c), noise amplitude (0.005), front width (2.0) and R0 (8) were selected from ~24 exploratory runs to reach the radial regime; the stage durations (290, 160, 100 steps) and erosions (0, 3, 1 px) of the 3-stage model were tuned from 4 trial runs for nested-count visibility. None of these values is from the cited papers | Frozen-silica conservation is global (leaked spectral flux spread uniformly over all mobile pixels), not local; the 3-stage cribrella sit at the grid floor (d_3 = 3.4 px target, 3.7 px measured), so their pitch/diameter are resolution-biased upward | Costae (phi0 = 0 rib layer) and areolae (phi0 = -0.30 droplet layer) are separate simulations; the model does not produce both in one domain; does_not_claim: Quantitative agreement with measured C. wailesii costae spacing or bifurcation count, the exact Furukawa crossover speed, cribrum-per-foramen multiplicities of 7-19 (model gives 4.8 at 512^2), SDV chemistry, or online verification of the Furukawa (1992) and Schmid & Volcani (1983) DOIs]" ;
        ns1:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/0378-4371(92)90111-2>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1021/la7022784>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1063/1.1744102>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1111/j.0022-3646.1983.00387.x>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1070026>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1166/jnn.2006.174> ;
        ns1:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-code-traceability>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-model-fidelity>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-morphometric-validation>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-overall>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-parameter-expressivity>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-repro-package>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-source-traceability>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-specimen-match> ;
        ns1:weightOfEvidence 8.9e-01 .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-tailbud-neuromesodermal-jamming> a ns1:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Mongera et al. (2018) & Kim et al. (2021) zebrafish tailbud active fluid-to-solid jamming transition & yield-stress axis elongation faithfully reproduces Danio rerio (zebrafish tailbud mesodermal progenitor zone MPZ & presomitic mesoderm PSM) morphology" ;
        dct:description "The simulation script(s) 2022-tailbud-neuromesodermal-jamming.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Danio rerio (zebrafish tailbud mesodermal progenitor zone MPZ & presomitic mesoderm PSM) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 90.0/100, audit 2026-10-19-neuromesodermal-jamming-audit-v3) and the assessments." ;
        dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2022-tailbud-neuromesodermal-jamming.py> ;
        ns1:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2022-tailbud-neuromesodermal-jamming.py; output: docs/media/neuromesodermal_jamming_comparison.png; organism: Danio rerio (zebrafish tailbud mesodermal progenitor zone MPZ & presomitic mesoderm PSM); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/d58a084; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0; spec_fingerprint: 5225f2c29acda8d1ee81d082219556f85a1159006d552c629f56ce7d8a842027; artifact_sha256: 57d7a446903c3cc022726dc33c7904454b93ad9f642da0182f250a8fb9e200a3; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-neuromesodermal-jamming-audit-v2; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Mongera et al. (2018) Nature 561:401-405 Figs. 1-4: along the posterior-to-anterior axis of the zebrafish tailbud, extracellular space fraction phi_ECS(x) decreases from ~14.5% in the posterior Mesodermal Progenitor Zone (MPZ) to ~4.9% in the Anterior Presomitic Mesoderm (A-PSM), driving cell packing phi_pack = 1 - phi_ECS across the rigidity-percolation threshold phi_c approx 0.860 and elevating ferrofluid-measured yield stress sigma_y(x) from ~11 Pa to ~118 Pa while active Myosin-II tension fluctuations sigma_A(x) decline from ~50 Pa to ~13 Pa. | Kim et al. (2021) Nature Physics 17:859-866 & Mongera et al. (2018) Fig. 4: active tension fluctuations fluidize the MPZ (sigma_A > sigma_y) via frequent T1 neighbor exchanges, whereas the jammed solid A-PSM (sigma_y >> sigma_A) serves as an internal mechanical backstop that rectifies MPZ progenitor addition into unidirectional posterior elongation and preserves left-right symmetry; N-cadherin (cdh2) knockdown expands phi_ECS > 14%, unjamming the PSM, slowing elongation, and inducing bilateral body-axis asymmetry. | Dray et al. (2013) Current Biology 23:1335-1341 Figs. 1-4: a fibronectin matrix wraps the tailbud and PSM; fn1a;fn1b double morphants and itga5 morphants lose this boundary, elongate the trunk more slowly and show altered posterior tissue shape and mechanics (the script vendors these as APPROXIMATE ratios, v/v_WT ~0.70 / ~0.82, width ~1.20 / ~1.08, +/-25%). | Herrgen et al. (2010) / Soroldoni et al. (2014): the zebrafish her1/her7 clock period is ~23.5 min at 28 C and clock waves slow and compress toward the anterior PSM before arresting into somite stripes (Cooke-Zeeman S = v_front T).; reconstructed_in_script: Continuous posterior-to-anterior active-foam & Bingham viscoplastic solver across x in [0, 300] um (`solve_ap_jamming_profile`, r_sigma_y = 0.9989, r_kT1 = 0.9922, jamming crossover x* = 81.0 um) and 2D U-shaped tailbud cellular flow simulator across 5 experimental regimes (WT Control, cdh2 Morphant, Blebbistatin, SU5402, Zero-Backstop Ablation; v_elong r = 0.9748, L-R asymmetry r = 0.9851). | (Pass 3) Quasi-3D fibronectin sheath: f_FN(x) profile, hoop equilibrium eps_r = max(0, sigma_A - sigma_y)/(K_FN f_FN + K_t), equilibrium radius R_eq(x), influx-weighted channeling chi (0.951 WT, 0.907 itga5 MO, 0.736 fn1a;fn1b MO) multiplying the elongation speed, tailbud width ratio (1.04 / 1.08 / 1.24), 12-point fn_scale sweep (monotonic), and a diagnostic wall-friction force F_drag. | (Pass 3) Her1/Her7 clock phase advection in the tip frame with a mechanical arrest gate sigma_y/sigma_A >= 4 (x_arrest = 161.1 um > x_jam = 81.0 um), Cooke-Zeeman somite length S = (v_elong + 0.45) * 23.5 min = 46.2 um, frozen her1 stripe wavelength 46.2 um measured on the kymograph, per-regime arrest fronts (cdh2 and ablation: none), and somite-border fibronectin feedback into the sheath profile. | Nuclear-seeded Voronoi tessellation and regional interstitial space segmentation of the Danio rerio posterior tailbud lightsheet micrograph (`zebrafish_tailbud_psm_specimen.jpg`, IDR0051, N = 391 nuclei, <z> = 5.88, AP compaction r = 0.9915).; transfer_boundary: 2D dorsal-ventral optical-plane projection of the 3D U-shaped zebrafish posterior tailbud and paraxial presomitic mesoderm; the fibronectin sheath is a thin-rod axisymmetric reduction (one radius per AP position), not a 3D boundary mesh. | The sheath channeling argument (influx stored in radial dilation is lost to elongation) is a transient-window argument, not a steady-state Stokes balance; K_FN and K_t are calibrated to the approximate Dray et al. (2013) ratios; the dynamic ECM friction F_drag does not feed back on v_elong. | The clock is a phase oscillator with a prescribed frequency profile and a mechanical arrest gate (Lambda_arrest = 4, a modelling choice standing in for the FGF/Wnt determination front and Yap mechanosensitivity), not the Lewis (2003) her1/her7 delay-differential oscillator; v_PSM-shortening = 0.45 um/min and the ~47 um somite length are approximate anchors.; does_not_claim: Does not model 3D notochord vacuolation turgor mechanics, anterior somite epithelialization clefting, an FGF8/Wnt morphogen determination front, Delta-Notch phase coupling, or a full axisymmetric/3D Stokes-Bingham solve with fibronectin traction boundary conditions.]" ;
        ns1:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0960-9822(03)00534-7>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2017.08.043>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cub.2010.06.034>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cub.2013.05.052>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/nmeth.4101>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41567-021-01215-1>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-018-0479-2>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1253089>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.090381> ;
        ns1:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-tailbud-neuromesodermal-jamming-code-traceability>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-tailbud-neuromesodermal-jamming-model-fidelity>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-tailbud-neuromesodermal-jamming-morphometric-validation>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-tailbud-neuromesodermal-jamming-overall>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-tailbud-neuromesodermal-jamming-parameter-expressivity>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-tailbud-neuromesodermal-jamming-repro-package>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-tailbud-neuromesodermal-jamming-source-traceability>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-tailbud-neuromesodermal-jamming-specimen-match> ;
        ns1:weightOfEvidence 9e-01 .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-tero-physarum-transport-network> a ns1:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Tero et al. (2010) Science & Tero, Kobayashi & Nakagaki (2007) J. Theor. Biol. adaptive Physarum tube conductivity network, shortest-path phase transition, Murray's cube law, Tokyo rail Pareto trade-off, and (Pass 3) peristaltic shuttle-streaming coupling faithfully reproduces Physarum polycephalum (acellular plasmodial slime mold) morphology" ;
        dct:description "The simulation script(s) 2010-tero-physarum-transport-network.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Physarum polycephalum (acellular plasmodial slime mold) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 80.4/100, audit 2026-10-19-physarum-transport-network-audit-v3) and the assessments." ;
        dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/171769b9/2010-tero-physarum-transport-network.py> ;
        ns1:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/171769b9/2010-tero-physarum-transport-network.py; output: docs/media/physarum_transport_network_comparison.png; organism: Physarum polycephalum (acellular plasmodial slime mold); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/171769b9; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0; spec_fingerprint: 9d2ad477cfb2fd69b34482f7554563764e14b823bf3616cc6b81b255bf0d40eb; artifact_sha256: 62ea6f63e161d275493b770aecf64e1191174f3c35bd7a93b7884d4d1a900657; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/physarum_transport_network/paper_citations.bib=b5e0e4eccbb78c29..., datasets/physarum_transport_network/peristaltic_shuttle_streaming_reference.json=299541a0501eb573..., datasets/physarum_transport_network/physarum_polycephalum_specimen.jpg=86a37f7c73c8527b..., datasets/physarum_transport_network/physarum_transport_network_reference.json=4a54186a148929f7..., datasets/physarum_transport_network/scout_manifest.json=edb27b0addb825b3...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-physarum-transport-network-audit-v2; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Tero et al. (2010) Science 327:439-442 & Tero, Kobayashi & Nakagaki (2007) J. Theor. Biol. 244:553-564 Hagen-Poiseuille Kirchhoff flow sum_j (D_ij/L_ij)*(p_i - p_j) = S_i coupled to nonlinear shear-stress tube adaptation dD_ij/dt = f(|Q_ij|) - mu*D_ij | Two-path parallel competition (L_1 < L_2) exhibiting parallel loop coexistence for gamma < 1, critical shortest-path selection at gamma_c = 1, and winner-takes-all Steiner minimum tree convergence for gamma > 1 | Multi-source Kanto / Tokyo rail Pareto trade-off across gamma optimizing normalized Total Length (TL_MST ~ 1.75), Transport Efficiency (MD_MST ~ 0.85), and Fault Tolerance (FT ~ 0.84) at gamma = 1.8, plus Murray's cube law (r_0^3 = r_1^3 + r_2^3) at gamma = 4/3 | Alim et al. (2013) PNAS 110:13306-13311: actomyosin peristaltic contraction waves with period ~100 s and wavelength of order the organism size drive shuttle streaming (flow reversing twice per cycle) and a second-order net transport; Kamiya (1981): sinusoidal shuttle streaming reverses twice per contraction period; reconstructed_in_script: Full graph Laplacian Kirchhoff pressure solver (`solve_kirchhoff_potentials`, with a zero-sum `extra_sources` vector) across N_f = 36 food sources on a jittered 8x8 lattice; nodal conservation error < 1e-11 and flux antisymmetry < 1e-14 | 8-point gamma sweep in [0.8, 2.4] with TL_MST / MD_MST / FT / Betti-1 computed from the pruned graph (`compute_network_morphometrics`, fixed threshold D >= 0.10 max D) against the vendored reference table: TL r = 0.987 (RMSE 1.61), FT r = 0.848 (RMSE 0.178); gamma = 1.8: TL_MST 1.703, FT 0.745, MD_MST 0.796, Betti-1 8 | Reduced two-timescale peristalsis: imposed plane wave rho_e(t) = 1 - eps cos(omega t - 2 pi x_e.n / lambda), instantaneous conductivity D_e rho_e^4, mean-corrected nodal volume source, Kirchhoff re-solved at 48 phases with D frozen; 1.70 reversals/cycle over active tubes (85.1 % reverse; eps = 0 ablation 0 / 0 %), osc/steady flux rms 0.697; pure-peristalsis wavelength sweep argmax lambda*/L = 1.5 (shallow, non-unique); eps sweep of the coupled pruning Betti-1 = [4, 5, 8, 27, 34, 71], Spearman rho = 1.0 | Two-path competition sweep (gamma = 0.6: Q1/I0 = 0.7322; gamma = 1.0, 1.8: 1.0000; gamma = 0 ablation 0.6667) and Murray's cube law (r_1^3 + r_2^3)/r_0^3 = 1.0000 at gamma = 4/3 | Computer-vision segmentation of `physarum_polycephalum_specimen.jpg` (Betti-1 = 33 loops, 3-tier vein-width hierarchy, Y-junction Murray cubic ratio 0.8926 +- 0.2774, N = 17); transfer_boundary: 2D planar multi-source Kirchhoff Poiseuille network on a jittered 8x8 lattice (not Kanto geography) and EDT medial-axis skeletonization mapped to macroscopic Physarum polycephalum plasmodial veins | The contraction wave is imposed (prescribed sinusoid along a fixed 20 deg direction, single wavelength), not generated by cortex mechanics or hydrodynamic feedback; T_c = 100 s is an input and 1/mu = 1800 s is an unsourced model-scale anchor, so only the 2-per-cycle phase locking, the second-order net transport and the eps-pruning coupling are model results | eps = 0.0025 is a disclosed calibration chosen so that the gamma = 1.8 network lands in the Physarum TL_MST band; with eps = 0 the same model gives TL_MST = 1.149; does_not_claim: 3D actomyosin cortex viscoelastic mechanics, calcium oscillator or Alim et al. (2013) hydrodynamic-feedback generation of the contraction wave, random-network-peristalsis phase statistics, or a compliance model for volume closure]" ;
