    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "@drmichaellevin 8-law mathematical synthesis & biological-law-criteria suite — MorphoEval overall 63.5/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-24"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 3.2 referee score of the committed 8-law `@drmichaellevin` synthesis suite at 9987ff10: 63.5/100 (57.4 on the uncommitted Pass 3.1 tree; 44.8 on Pass 3; v2 26.4 on the 25-law version; v1 self-score 93.8), verdict band 'mostly faithful' by 3.5 points. Five of the seven Pass 3.1 remediation items are closed on the evidence: the written record now matches the code everywhere it is generated or hand-aligned (criteria doc, YAML, KG verified_laws, script header and Law 6 docstring); Law 1 fits the Hill form to the BVP curve with curve_fit (G_eff 2.26, RMS 3.05, reproduced); the Ross DOI resolves at the third attempt (10.1017/9781009300940, 2025); froese2024 and hoel2026ce2 carry the Crossref titles and author lists and all 17 bib DOIs resolve; the package is committed and the audited files are unchanged through HEAD. One is partial (`--delta-v-mv 0` passes and the summary JSON records the script hash, but `--law` still runs every solver). One is not closed and regressed: docs/bioelectricity/levin_youtube_kg.json has no generator, its eight code_locus values are the pre-commit line numbers (Laws 2-8 no longer start at their `def`), its domain_summary keeps the Stoica / Morozov names, and two entries of the referee's Pass 3 sidecar embedded in it (m4, m5) were rewritten by the builder under the referee's meas_ids - the values match this referee's own findings, but builder-authored numbers under referee identifiers is the pattern C6 exists to prevent. Substantively the eight laws are unchanged: Laws 3 and 4 are correct textbook statements (zero-flux Boltzmann ratio; p ∝ 1/r for a uniform embedded chain) with genuine numerical checks; Law 2 is a real two-regime ODE on an invented current; Law 1 is a cable-theory space constant relabelled as a cognitive light cone, with a Lean theorem about a different (Hill) function; Laws 5 and 7 are elementary identities (a symmetric Boolean function factors through a + b; a telescoping sum) dressed as T1 theorems; Law 6 is a Hebbian identity plus a hand-built conditioning circuit; Law 8 is a closed form evaluated at k values no square cluster realises. No law is compared with any published measurement, which keeps specimen-match and morphometric-validation where they were. Overall 63.5/100 (faithfulness 53.5, reproducibility 86.7); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 9987ff10; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, lean 4.35.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 78, Morphological realism / specimen match 24, Parameter expressivity 82, Morphometric validation 51, Source and data traceability 88, Code-to-model traceability 80, Reproducibility package 90. Output judged: media/levin_youtube_channel_math_synthesis.png: rendered output of models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py, not present when the audit was snapshotted (unfingerprinted). Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 01d7a346279b91d7e7f753c7b63c7f94a397b3bba9949666ed7ce868b8196e34; artifact_sha256: 93541cfba66e436d973f1aee7c8c6a6cd1cbac78d2693f37e3d4cc61c100417f; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/levin_youtube_channel/levin_youtube_catalog.json=216a474f76c137c3..., datasets/levin_youtube_channel/paper_citations.bib=1491f6f1107bea0d..., sorting-morphogenesis/figures/quantifying_emergence_ce2_metrics.json=b54103b87a1f5d77...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-24-levin-youtube-channel-math-audit-v2. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Cervera, Levin & Mafe (2020): voltage-gated gap-junction coupling G_ij(V_i, V_j) = G_0 / [(1 + e^{(V_i - V_th)/V_0})(1 + e^{(V_j - V_th)/V_0})] with polarising and depolarising channel currents; depolarised domains electrically isolate | Pietak & Levin (2016, 2017): Nernst-Planck electrodiffusion in BETSE; at zero flux the charged-morphogen ratio is Boltzmann, exp(-zF dV / RT), independent of gap-junction permeability (with production / decay the steady state is not zero-flux and the ratio does depend on permeability) | Chvykov et al. (2021): low-rattling principle P_ss ∝ exp(-gamma R) tested on smarticle collectives and simulation; the 'rattling' is a diffusion-tensor quantity, not a scalar exit rate, and the principle is stated for driving whose embedded jump process is unbiased | Watson & Szathmary (2016): natural induction / Hebbian deepening of visited attractors; Pigozzi, Goldstein & Levin (2025): associative conditioning in continuous GRN ODE models with measured conditioning success; Biswas et al. (2023): pathway-level memory in transcriptional network models | Hoel et al. (2013), Hoel (2026): causal emergence via effective information and the determinism/degeneracy decomposition CP = det - deg | Levin (2019, 2022): TAME cognitive light cone (diagrammatic); Bongard & Levin (2023): polycomputing (conceptual); Shreesha & Levin (2025): agent-based spatial Prisoner's Dilemma with controllable borders; reconstructed_in_script: Law 1 (L177-L233): N-cell linear diffusion-leak BVP -G (V_{i-1} - 2V_i + V_{i+1}) + (G_half/N) V_i = delta_{i0}; reach L = sum_i V_i / V_0 at G_gj in {0, 0.5, 1.0} and on a 51-point grid; continuum sqrt(1/k) tanh(N sqrt(k)); Hill form 1 + (N-1) G/(G + G_eff) fitted by curve_fit (G_eff 2.26, RMS 3.05) and reported | Law 2 (L239-L285, unchanged since Pass 3): 20-cell ODE, cells 0-4 clamped at -10 mV, cubic bistable I_ion with roots -60 / -38 / -10 mV (not Cervera's channel currents), Bell-Boltzmann vs ohmic G_ij, RK45 to t = 80 | Law 3 (L291-L339): 1-D zero-flux BVP with central-difference / Pade(1,1) edge coefficients a_i = G(-1 + dv/2), b_{i+1} = G(1 + dv/2) on a linear voltage profile; grid refinement N_ap = 15..240 and a 5-value G_gj sweep at N_ap = 120 | Law 4 (L345-L412): 24-state CTMC, W(i->j) = r_i^gamma K_ij(alpha) with K(alpha) = (1 - alpha) K_sym + alpha K_trap, K_sym Sinkhorn-symmetrised doubly stochastic, K_trap row-normalised weights linspace(0.1, 2.5)^2.5 (column sums != 1); stationary vector from L^T p = 0; log-log fit of p against the fixed r_exit at alpha = 0, 0.5, 0.9 | Laws 5 and 7 (L418-L457): 4-row x 3-gate truth table; S_6 CE2 numbers read from the hash-pinned sorting-morphogenesis JSON | Law 6 (L463-L548): 16-gene symmetric J, Hebbian J += eta s s^T for 15 epochs, energy trace, basin fraction over 120 four-flip trials; 3-node ODE dx_CS = -x_CS + I_CS, dx_M = -0.02 x_M + 0.25 sigma(12 (x_CS x_US - 0.5)), dx_US = -x_US + sigma(12 (I_US + 0.9 x_M x_CS - 0.55)) in four phases (CS test, paired training t = 25, washout t = 5, CS test t = 10); the docstring now states this ODE and its results | Law 8 (L554-L588, unchanged): pi_C(k) = (1 - k^-1/2) b - c and pi_D(k) = b k^-1/2 over k = 1..36; exact m x m directed bond count for m = 1..6 | 8 Lean theorems (Loop L30-L288, unchanged since Pass 3), each on Nat/Int/Bool reductions of the law; Law 1's theorem formalises the Hill numerator, not the BVP the Python metric is now scored on; transfer_boundary: The 8 laws are evaluated on synthetic parameter sets chosen by the builder (cubic current coefficients, r_exit table, K_trap weights, J ~ N(0, 0.25), 3-node ODE gains, b = 2, c = 1); no quantity is compared with a value measured in Cervera 2020, Pietak 2016/2017, Chvykov 2021, Pigozzi 2025 or Shreesha 2025 | Law 1's BVP reach is a cable-theory space constant (L ≈ sqrt(G/k), measured exponent 0.48 over the sweep); the Hill form fitted to it has its half-saturation (2.26) outside the sweep and a plateau at N the BVP never shows, so the Lean theorem (Hill numerator) and the Python metric (BVP) describe different functions of G_gj | Law 4's breakdown is a genuine property of the model (non-doubly-stochastic routing with fixed exit rates) and its magnitude (+0.1866) is now reported consistently; at alpha = 0 the slope -1 is the elementary CTMC result p ∝ 1/r for a uniform embedded chain | Law 3's grid-refinement convergence is a genuine numerical check of the discretisation against the Boltzmann closed form; the G_gj invariance is linear algebra (G_gj scales Q) and holds only in the zero-flux limit the law is restricted to | Law 6's 3-node ODE is a hand-tuned minimal conditioning circuit, not a model from Pigozzi 2025 or Biswas 2023; it is now documented as what it is | Law 8's k >= 17 strict-dominance threshold applies 1 - 1/sqrt(k) to non-square k that no m x m cluster realises; the docs and YAML now also state the first exact square k = 25, the Lean docstring (L274-L275) still says 'k >= 17 in general integer k' against a theorem quantified over the side length; does_not_claim: This audit does not claim any of the 8 source equations is wrong as published, nor that any Lean theorem fails to check (all 8 compile with 0 sorry); it scores whether the suite implements, exercises and validates the laws and whether the O1/O2, T1-T4 and C1-C6 tags are earned by linked artefacts | It does not verify the content of the 63 cited videos (no transcripts offline) and does not recompute the S_6 TPM behind quantifying_emergence_ce2_metrics.json; it re-checks only the arithmetic consistency of the imported numbers | It does not score the 17 CHANNEL_CONCEPTS_INDEX items, which are correctly excluded from law status | It does not treat the builder's edits to the KG payload's referee-attributed measurement entries as falsified values (the two numbers written are ones this referee independently reaches); it treats them as a provenance violation." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Finish the attribution sweep: Loop .lean L229 ('Albantakis (2024)' -> Albantakis 2023 or remove), L255 and the theorem name L276 (Morozov), script comments L552 / L683, KG L1068 / L1139 / L129 (Sweet); README L4 (remove 'MathOfBiology.lean (§17)') and KG L627. Either cite a causal-emergence paper by Albantakis or state that the IIT 4.0 DOI is for the speaker, not for Law 7's equation.",
