    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-badin-hydractinia-stolon-vascular-net> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Buss, Anderson & Perry (2015) Biol. Bull., Dudgeon et al. (1999) Am. Nat. & Blackstone (1999) Syst. Biol. colonial hydroid pulsatile gastrovascular stolon network, anastomosis loop closure, and runner-to-sheet morphospace (Hydractinia symbiolongicarpus / Podocoryna carnea (Colonial marine hydroids))" ;
        dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/badin-hydractinia-stolon-vascular-net-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/badin-hydractinia-stolon-vascular-net-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/badin-hydractinia-stolon-vascular-net-3> ;
        schema:about "Hydractinia symbiolongicarpus / Podocoryna carnea (Colonial marine hydroids)" ;
        schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Subcellular chitin synthase secretion kinetics or allorecognition histocompatibility (alr1/alr2) fusion/rejection signaling between genetically distinct colonies",
            "reconstructed_in_script: 5 canonical morphospace regimes: Podocoryna runner (eta = 0.55, alpha = 0.1064, b_1 = 5), 2,4-DNP redox-uncoupled shift (eta = 0.90, alpha = 0.3404, b_1 = 16, delta = +0.2340), Hydractinia intermediate web (eta = 1.25, alpha = 0.5745, b_1 = 27), Hydractinia mature stolonal sheet (eta = 1.65, alpha = 0.7872, b_1 = 37), and polyp-excision / MgCl2 contraction arrest regression control (eta = 0.0, surviving stolon fraction = 0.0, b_1 = 0)",
            "reconstructed_in_script: 8-point polyp pumping gain sweep across eta in [0.35, 1.65] reproducing the runner-to-sheet planar meshedness continuum alpha (Pearson r = 0.99886, RMSE = 0.0130, p = 3.74e-9) and coenosarc mat area coverage (Pearson r = 0.99768, RMSE = 0.0213, p = 3.12e-8)",
            "reconstructed_in_script: Computer-vision segmentation of Yale Peabody Museum `hydractinia_symbiolongicarpus_specimen.jpg` (`YPM IZ 080458`, CC0) extracting coenosarc mat coverage 0.8918, V = 332 gastrovascular polyp cavities, E = 845 stolon links, b_1 = 514 closed anastomosed loops, planar meshedness alpha = 0.7800, and inter-polyp NND CV = 0.3022 (18.64 +- 5.63 px)",
            "reconstructed_in_script: Full weighted graph Laplacian Kirchhoff gastrovascular solver (`solve_gastrovascular_kirchhoff`) across V = 26 stolon/polyp nodes and E = 62 stolon segments verifying nodal volume conservation (error 1.42e-12 < 1e-11), flux antisymmetry (< 1e-14), and cubic-radius wall shear identity (< 1e-12)",
            "reported_in_source: Blackstone (1999) Syst. Biol. 48:75-85 & Buss (2001) Evol. Dev. 3:311-322 heterochronic runner-to-sheet colonial hydroid morphospace continuum: low polyp pumping produces sparse Podocoryna runner trees (low planar meshedness alpha), 2,4-DNP redox uncoupling shifts runner colonies toward reticulate webs, and high Hydractinia pumping produces confluent anastomosed stolonal mats/sheets (alpha ~ 0.78)",
            "reported_in_source: Buss, Anderson & Perry (2015) Biol. Bull. 228:146-158 & Dudgeon et al. (1999) Am. Nat. 153:292-309 pulsatile polyp contraction oscillators V_p(t) = V_0 + Delta_V sin(omega_p t + phi_p) driving Hagen-Poiseuille gastrovascular lumen flow Q_ij = (pi r_ij^4 / (8 mu L_ij))(p_i - p_j) and endodermal wall shear stress tau_w = 4 mu |Q_ij| / (pi r_ij^3)",
            "reported_in_source: Polyp excision or MgCl2 muscular contraction arrest (Delta_V_p = 0) eliminates gastrovascular flow and wall shear stress below tau_reg, triggering stolon lumen collapse and regression into empty chitinous perisarc tubes",
            "transfer_boundary: 2D planar pulsatile Kirchhoff pipe network with shear-stress-gated lumen adaptation and Delaunay-coenosarc vascular graph extraction mapped to colonial hydroid stolonal mats" ;
        pk:anatomicalStructure "Collective swarm / biofilm / colonial array in Hydractinia symbiolongicarpus" ;
        pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "10. Stigmergy & Active Swarms" ;
        pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "II. Anaima (Invertebrata)" ;
        pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Biofilm Wrinkles & Hex Combs" ;
        pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Chemotactic / Stigmergic Pe" ;
        pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Zoophyta & Vermes (Cnidaria/Platyhelminthes)" ;
        pk:biologicalGenus "Hydractinia" ;
        pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1023/A:1018310324258>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1046/j.1525-142x.2001.01039.x>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1080/106351599260454>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1086/303167>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1086/BBLv228n2p146> ;
        pk:geologicalAgeMa 0e+00 ;
        pk:geologicalPeriod "Holocene (Extant)" ;
        pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-hydractinia-stolon-vascular-net-audit-v2-badin-hydractinia-stolon-vascular-net-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-hydractinia-stolon-vascular-net-audit-v2-badin-hydractinia-stolon-vascular-net-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-hydractinia-stolon-vascular-net-audit-v2-badin-hydractinia-stolon-vascular-net-3>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-hydractinia-stolon-vascular-net-audit-v2-badin-hydractinia-stolon-vascular-net-4>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-hydractinia-stolon-vascular-net-audit-v2-badin-hydractinia-stolon-vascular-net-5>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-hydractinia-stolon-vascular-net-audit-v2-badin-hydractinia-stolon-vascular-net-6>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-hydractinia-stolon-vascular-net-audit-v2-badin-hydractinia-stolon-vascular-net-7>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-hydractinia-stolon-vascular-net-audit-v2-badin-hydractinia-stolon-vascular-net-8>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-hydractinia-stolon-vascular-net-audit-v2-badin-hydractinia-stolon-vascular-net-9> ;
        pk:hypothesisType "Pulsatile Peristaltic Kirchhoff Gastrovascular Flow Coupled to Shear-Stress-Gated Stolon Tip Outgrowth, Anastomosis Loop Closure, and Regression Across the Runner-to-Sheet Colony Morphospace" ;
        pk:phenomenonScaleTier "7_organism_cm" ;
