    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-boehm-limb-bud-elongation-pushing> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Boehm et al. (2010) & Gros et al. (2010) vertebrate limb bud oriented cell division & Wnt5a/FGF8 pushing vs proliferation-gradient hypothesis (Mus musculus & Gallus gallus embryonic hindlimb and forelimb buds)" ;
        dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/boehm-limb-bud-elongation-pushing-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/boehm-limb-bud-elongation-pushing-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/boehm-limb-bud-elongation-pushing-3>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/boehm-limb-bud-elongation-pushing-4>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/boehm-limb-bud-elongation-pushing-5> ;
        schema:about "Mus musculus & Gallus gallus embryonic hindlimb and forelimb buds" ;
        schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Reproduction of the paper's inverse-optimisation (Hooke-Jeeves) in 3D, chick-embryo (Gros) geometry, cell-level oriented-division statistics, a Navier-Stokes (inertial) solver, or that the active-stress Model II as implemented reproduces the AP/DV changes of the specimen (it does not: AP -10.9 %, DV -14.5 %)",
            "reconstructed_in_script: Pass 2 Sections 2-3 (retained, now labelled): analytic strain-rate laws, IddU/BrdU vs Hooke-Jeeves inverse-opt profiles, a 2D Poisson pressure field used for visualisation, and a 2D boundary-advection model whose per-axis coefficients were calibrated to the 5-regime table; Pass 2 specimen segmentation of 5 sub-panels",
            "reconstructed_in_script: Pass 3 Section 5: visual-hull reconstruction of the St0/St1 3D surfaces from the vendored specimen's two orthogonal iso-surface silhouettes; conforming prism-split P1 tetrahedral mesh; P1-P1 Brezzi-Pitkaranta-stabilised 3D Stokes growth solver with IddU/BrdU source, extensile oriented-division stress, AER-FGF8 body force, traction-free ectoderm and flank Dirichlet/ALE inflow plane; two closed-form oracles to 8.2e-14; Lagrangian RK2 growth with volume budget closed to 0.5 %; 2-gain calibration (k_chi, k_zeta) with Wnt5a-/-, Model I and uniform control out of sample; flank-influx sweep; mesh-convergence; silhouette IoU against the specimen St1 hull",
            "reported_in_source: Boehm et al. (2010): OPT-measured mouse limb bud growth E11.0 (St0, L_PD 1020 um) -> E11.25 (St1, L_PD 1450 um, +42.2 % PD, +12 % AP, +1 % DV; volume 0.551 -> 0.914 mm^3); dual-label IddU/BrdU cell-cycle atlas (T_c 11-25 h); a 3D Navier-Stokes growth model on a tetrahedral FEM mesh of the OPT iso-surface in which the measured proliferation (Model I) yields only 3.4-11.8 % PD elongation while inverse optimisation demands s_opt > 8 s_emp with negative DV growth; anisotropic/directional growth (Model II) therefore required",
            "reported_in_source: Dillon & Othmer (1999): viscous incompressible continuum with distributed sources as the mechanical model of limb-bud outgrowth; Reynolds number irrelevant in the creeping-flow limit",
            "reported_in_source: Gros et al. (2010): Wnt5a/JNK-controlled oriented cell division and FGF8/MAPK-controlled directional motility drive PD elongation; Wnt5a-/- and FGF-inhibited buds are shorter and more bulbous (E11.5 aspect ratios 2.1 WT, ~1.3 Wnt5a-/-)",
            "transfer_boundary: Panels C-J of the main figure and 8 of the 20 measurements still come from the calibrated 2D reduced model",
            "transfer_boundary: The 3D geometry is a visual hull of two projections (elliptical cross-sections), not the OPT voxel iso-surface, and the mesh is structured, not unstructured Delaunay; the specimen's own St1/St0 PD ratio (1.364) and DV thickness (926 um) disagree with the reference table (1.422; 580 um)",
            "transfer_boundary: The 5-regime FEM Pearson r = 0.9944 counts 2 calibrated regimes; the fully out-of-sample set is Model I (+5.2 % vs 10.1 %), Wnt5a-/- (+12.0 % vs 18.5 %) and the uniform control, RMSE 5.3 pp",
            "transfer_boundary: The Stokes FEM is Reynolds-number independent by construction; the 5-decade Re sweep remains in the 2D reduced model where Re enters only through a phenomenological `re_factor`" ;
        pk:anatomicalStructure "Morphogen gradient & pre-cartilage condensation zone in Mus musculus" ;
        pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "2. Morphogen + Condensations" ;
        pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "I. Enaima (Vertebrata)" ;
        pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Skeletal Rays & Joints" ;
        pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "French-Flag / PSHM Thresholds" ;
