    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Farhadifar et al. (2007) Drosophila wing disc apical vertex model, Lewis's law packing & PCP (Fz/Stbm) hinge-contraction vertex dynamics (Fruit fly (Drosophila melanogaster) 3rd-instar larval wing imaginal disc & pupal wing epithelium (vendored specimen micrograph is a Mus musculus epithelium — see transfer_boundary))" ;
        dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model-3>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model-4>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model-5> ;
        schema:about "Fruit fly (Drosophila melanogaster) 3rd-instar larval wing imaginal disc & pupal wing epithelium (vendored specimen micrograph is a Mus musculus epithelium — see transfer_boundary)" ;
        schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Does not claim to reproduce the Classen et al. (2005) PCP-mutant loss of hexagonal order: in this model the PCP coupling lowers the final hexagon fraction (sign mismatch disclosed in measurement `pcp_wt_minus_mutant_hexagonal_fraction_delta`).",
            "does_not_claim: Does not model basal extracellular matrix curvature, 3D apico-basal scutoid transitions, Fat/Dachsous polarity, the pre-15 hAPF margin-directed PCP pattern, cell divisions or extrusions during pupal morphogenesis, the hinge as a separate mechanical compartment, or periodic boundary conditions for the explicit vertex model (the patch is clamped at its margin).",
            "reconstructed_in_script: 2D periodic Voronoi-seed (Lloyd-type) packing and mitotic cleavage simulation across 4 regimes (Proliferating Wing Disc, Post-Mitotic Pupal Wing, High-Contractility Case I, Soft Case II), 2D (Lambda_bar, Gamma_bar) phase diagram, UV laser junction ablation recoil curves, and 7-point continuous Lambda_bar sweep (Section 2, panels A1-A4, B1-B5).",
            "reconstructed_in_script: Junction-guided Voronoi-watershed segmentation of the vendored apical junction-stained polygonal epithelial micrograph (N=37 interior cells, P(6)=0.4865, P(n) correlation r = 0.9913 against the Farhadifar wing-disc distribution).",
            "reconstructed_in_script: Pass 3: explicit tri-cellular vertex model (analytic forces of Eq. 1, T1 exchanges) on a 100-cell patch with a per-bond Frizzled/Strabismus asymmetry tensor Q_ab modulating line tension Lambda_ab = Lambda_bar (1 + eps_pcp n.Q_ab.n), Fz-Stbm feedback + flow-alignment polarity dynamics, an area-preserving hinge-contraction boundary strain diag(lambda, 1/lambda) with ln lambda = 0.35, shear decomposition into cell-elongation and rearrangement parts, a PCP loss-of-function (eps_pcp = 0) control and a 6-point eps_pcp sweep (Section 2b, panels C1-C5, GIF panel 4).",
            "reported_in_source: Aigouy et al. (2010) Cell & Etournay et al. (2015) eLife: hinge contraction from ~15 hAPF stretches the blade along the proximal-distal axis, cells elongate along PD and then relax through oriented cell rearrangements while the Fz/Stbm PCP axis reorients to PD; tissue shear decomposes into cell-elongation change plus rearrangement, division and correlation contributions.",
            "reported_in_source: Farhadifar et al. (2007) Fig. 3-4, Gibson et al. (2006) Nature & Classen et al. (2005) Dev. Cell: proliferating 3rd-instar Drosophila wing disc exhibits P(6) approx 0.455 and obeys Lewis's Law <A_n>/<A> = (n-2)/4, whereas post-mitotic pupal wing annealing increases P(6) to ~0.78, and PCP (fz, stbm) mutants fail to reach wild-type hexagonal order.",
            "reported_in_source: Farhadifar, Röper, Aigouy, Eaton & Jülicher (2007) Current Biology Eqs. 1-2 & Fig. 2A: apical epithelial vertex energy functional E({r_i}) = sum (K/2)(A_alpha - A^(0))^2 + sum Lambda_{ij} l_{ij} + sum (Gamma/2) L_alpha^2 parameterized by (Lambda_bar, Gamma_bar), partitioning ground states into Case I (rigid hexagonal, canonical wing disc Lambda_bar=0.12, Gamma_bar=0.04), Case II (soft network), and Case III (cell collapse).",
            "transfer_boundary: 2D apical junctional projection of 3D pseudostratified/columnar wing imaginal disc epithelial cells.",
            "transfer_boundary: The PCP coupling sign (PCP-complex-bearing AP junctions stiffened for eps_pcp > 0), the polarity-dynamics gains (k_fb = 0.6, k_flow = 0.4), the initial polarity spread (0.6 rad) and the hinge log-strain (0.35) are modelling choices, not fitted to data; Pass 3 reference values from Etournay (2015) and Classen (2005) are approximate figure reads recorded offline.",
            "transfer_boundary: The Section 2 regimes are Voronoi-seed relaxations with a post-hoc Lewis's-law area reweighting and a hexagonal-lattice pull in the pupal regime; only Section 2b integrates the Farhadifar energy on vertex degrees of freedom.",
            "transfer_boundary: The vendored specimen `drosophila_wing_epithelium_specimen.jpg` is a Wikimedia Commons epithelial monolayer whose scout manifest records organism Mus musculus; its polygon statistics are compared with Drosophila literature values as a cross-species epithelial-packing transfer, not as a Drosophila specimen." ;
        pk:anatomicalStructure "Apical epithelial cell vertex polygon in Drosophila melanogaster" ;
        pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "5. Vertex / Potts / Nematics" ;
        pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "II. Anaima (Invertebrata)" ;
        pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Polygonal Packing & Furrows" ;
        pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Shape Index p_0* = 3.813" ;
        pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Entoma (Arthropoda)" ;
        pk:biologicalGenus "Drosophila" ;
        pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1002/ar.1090380305>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2010.07.042>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cub.2007.11.049>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.devcel.2005.10.016>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature05014>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1080/13642810108205772>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.094060>,
            <https://doi.org/10.7554/eLife.07090> ;
        pk:geologicalAgeMa 0e+00 ;
