    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Hannezo, Prost & Joanny (2014) PNAS & Krajnc & Ziherl (2015) PRE 3D epithelial sheet morphology (squamous-to-cuboidal-to-columnar scaling, apico-basal buckling & Gómez-Gálvez scutoid tube packing) (Mus musculus / Drosophila melanogaster epithelial monolayers)" ;
        dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d-3>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d-4>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d-5> ;
        schema:about "Mus musculus / Drosophila melanogaster epithelial monolayers" ;
        schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: A relaxed 3D vertex/scutoid energy (apical, basal and lateral tensions minimised with free vertices), T1 or apico-basal intercalation dynamics, quantitative agreement with the Gómez-Gálvez scutoid counts in salivary gland / egg chamber tubes, measured per-tissue surface tensions, or more than one histological specimen",
            "reconstructed_in_script: Analytic + L-BFGS-B single-cell equilibrium (L205-271), quartic buckling wavelength (L274-287), a 5-regime threshold phase classifier (L289-317), a 2D pseudo-spectral Swift-Hohenberg-type relaxation F[w] with cubic (spontaneous-curvature) and quartic terms (L323-490), a 12-tissue table and 5 perturbations driven from epithelial_buckling_3d_reference.json (L863-1017), CV segmentation of one CC0 histology micrograph (L1023-1120), and (Pass 3) a doubly periodic Voronoi tube mesh with scutoid detection, surface-ratio sweep and fold-crest curvature coupling (L497-857)",
            "reported_in_source: Gómez-Gálvez et al. (2018): on curved tubes the basal/apical surface ratio makes Voronoi tessellations of the two surfaces differ; cells with apico-basal neighbour intercalations (scutoids) appear and their number increases with the surface ratio",
            "reported_in_source: Hannezo, Prost & Joanny (2014): single-cell energy E_cell(A) = (Gamma_a + Gamma_b) A + c Gamma_l V_0 / (2 sqrt A) gives h_0/d_0 = c Gamma_l / [4 (Gamma_a + Gamma_b)] spanning squamous/cuboidal/columnar; an elastic foundation selects lambda_c = 2 pi (kappa_eff / K_sub)^(1/4); apico-basal tension asymmetry sets a spontaneous curvature whose sign follows Gamma_a - Gamma_b",
            "reported_in_source: Krajnc & Ziherl (2015): convexity of the cell energy at equilibrium and the continuum elastic limit of the 3D vertex monolayer",
            "transfer_boundary: The 12-tissue Gamma_a/Gamma_b/Gamma_l/K_sub 'norm' values are not measured tensions; they reproduce aspect_ratio_obs through the Law-1 formula to <0.5 % per row and carry no per-row source, so the r = 1.0000 collapse is a parity check of the JSON with itself, not a test against the papers",
            "transfer_boundary: The scutoid mesh is a Voronoi projection (seeds fixed, lateral faces evaluated geometrically); it is not a relaxed 3D vertex model and no Gómez-Gálvez figure value is digitised - the scutoid reference values are geometric identities (f_s(1) = 0, mean neighbours 6, Spearman 1) plus a crest ratio derived from the already-pinned WT fold geometry",
            "transfer_boundary: lambda_sim = 0.85 lambda_c + 0.15 lambda_FFT (L467) and the WT amplitude is rescaled to fold_amplitude_ref_um (L454-455, L999), so the wavelength r = 0.9993 and the WT amplitude 'match' are dominated by construction" ;
        pk:anatomicalStructure "Apical epithelial cell vertex polygon in Mus musculus" ;
        pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "5. Vertex / Potts / Nematics" ;
        pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "I. Enaima (Vertebrata)" ;
        pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Polygonal Packing & Furrows" ;
        pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Shape Index p_0* = 3.813" ;
        pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Mammalia (Zootoka)" ;
        pk:biologicalGenus "Mus" ;
        pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.bpj.2015.11.024>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-018-05376-1>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-018-06497-3>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1321766111>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevE.92.052713> ;
        pk:geologicalAgeMa 0e+00 ;
        pk:geologicalPeriod "Holocene (Extant)" ;
        pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-epithelial-buckling-3d-audit-v3-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-epithelial-buckling-3d-audit-v3-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d-10>,
