        pk:phenomenonSizeMeters 2e-03 ;
        pk:speciesTaxon <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/taxon/coturnix-japonica> ;
        pk:weightOfEvidence 8.09e-01 .

    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-he-drosophila-ventral-furrow> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Conte et al. (2012), Martin et al. (2009) & He et al. (2014) Drosophila ventral furrow invagination biomechanics (Drosophila melanogaster (gastrulating cellular blastoderm embryo))" ;
        dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/he-drosophila-ventral-furrow-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/he-drosophila-ventral-furrow-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/he-drosophila-ventral-furrow-3>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/he-drosophila-ventral-furrow-4>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/he-drosophila-ventral-furrow-5> ;
        schema:about "Drosophila melanogaster (gastrulating cellular blastoderm embryo)" ;
        schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: A 3D finite-element shell with coupled membrane/bending stresses, a moving-boundary (ALE) or 3D Stokes solve with cortical actomyosin stress boundary conditions, emergent (un-pinned) invagination depth from the viscous-vertex mechanics, or subcellular Rho1/Rok reaction-diffusion signaling",
            "reconstructed_in_script: 64-cell 2D incompressible trapezoidal blastoderm ring enclosed by the vitelline membrane (R_vit = 83.2 um, A_0 = 262.4 um^2), RK2 integration of the ratcheted Myosin-II apical-width pulse ODE, 6-regime benchmark and 15x15 (r_twist x sigma_synergy) morphospace; NOTE: regime depth and cell height are target-pinned interpolants, not emergent mechanics",
            "reconstructed_in_script: Automated 4-stage confocal cross-section segmentation and ventral apical Myosin-II red enrichment analysis on drosophila_ventral_furrow_specimen.jpg (DV/ML = 1.0496 -> 0.9217, MyoII enrichment = 1.63x, trajectory r = 0.9993)",
            "reconstructed_in_script: [Pass 3] Reduced 3D AP shell: Donnell/Winkler elastic line ell_B^4 D'''' - ell_N^2 D'' + k_rel(z) D = D_2D(t) chi_meso(z) on the prolate ellipsoid (exact kappa_z, kappa_theta; k_pole/k_eq = 13x), driven by the ring depth at each snapshot with a germband-extension tension ramp, swept into a 65x81 theta x z shell mesh; sweeps over ell_N (0-150 um, ablation ratio 0.53, monotone) and a/b (1.5-4.0)",
            "reconstructed_in_script: [Pass 3] Variable-viscosity Stokes flow (stream-function form, 35x192 grid, 6,110 unknowns) inside the Phase-I lengthening mesoderm cell with incompressible-trapezoid boundary kinematics, a 50x-viscosity nucleus (v_nuc/v_cyto = 0.983, rigid-body CV 0.004), exact affine verification (L2 8.1e-13) and a Phase-I nuclear trajectory (4.5 um basal displacement over 16.2 um lengthening)",
            "reported_in_source: Conte, Munoz, Baum & Miodownik (2012) PLoS ONE 7(11):e49973 incompressible finite-element cross-sectional decomposition showing apical constriction alone produces only a shallow groove (16.5 um) with over-elongated cells (48.1 um), whereas synergy with basal relaxation, lateral shortening, and ectodermal pushing drives full invagination (41.0 um)",
            "reported_in_source: Martin, Kaschube & Wieschaus (2009) Nature 457:495-499 Twist-stabilized ratcheted Myosin-II pulses (T_pulse = 82 s) vs unratcheted relaxation recoil; He et al. (2014) Nature 508:392-396 apically driven hydrodynamic cytoplasmic flow that carries nuclei basally as passive tracers during cell lengthening",
            "reported_in_source: Sweeton et al. (1991) / Leptin & Grunewald (1990): the ventral furrow spans roughly the mesoderm primordium (~0.15-0.80 EL) and germband extension begins as the furrow closes (approximate, not digitised here)",
            "transfer_boundary: The 2D ring depth that drives both new layers is pinned to the Conte (2012) / Martin (2009) reference values at the last step, so the 6-regime r = 1.0000 is a consistency check of the calibration, not an independent prediction",
            "transfer_boundary: The AP coupling is a 1D elastic line with a curvature-weighted Winkler foundation and a kinematic circumferential sweep; ell_B = 22 um and the WT ell_N ramp to 30 um are model assumptions not measured in any cited paper, and N_GB is not calibrated to Lye et al. (2015) ablation recoil",
            "transfer_boundary: The Stokes solve is 2D on a fixed rectangle frozen at t = 1.8 min with velocity (not stress) boundary data; nucleus size/position are order-of-magnitude values; the He et al. (2014) comparison is the qualitative passive-tracer ratio ~1, not a digitised velocity field" ;
        pk:anatomicalStructure "Apical epithelial cell vertex polygon in Drosophila melanogaster" ;
        pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "5. Vertex / Potts / Nematics" ;
        pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "II. Anaima (Invertebrata)" ;
        pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Polygonal Packing & Furrows" ;
        pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Shape Index p_0* = 3.813" ;
        pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Entoma (Arthropoda)" ;
        pk:biologicalGenus "Drosophila" ;
        pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.bpj.2014.07.013>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature07522>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature13070>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.110.1.73>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.112.3.775>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pbio.1002292>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0049973> ;
        pk:geologicalAgeMa 0e+00 ;
        pk:geologicalPeriod "Holocene (Extant)" ;
        pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-drosophila-ventral-furrow-audit-v3-he-drosophila-ventral-furrow-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-drosophila-ventral-furrow-audit-v3-he-drosophila-ventral-furrow-10>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-drosophila-ventral-furrow-audit-v3-he-drosophila-ventral-furrow-11>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-drosophila-ventral-furrow-audit-v3-he-drosophila-ventral-furrow-12>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-drosophila-ventral-furrow-audit-v3-he-drosophila-ventral-furrow-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-drosophila-ventral-furrow-audit-v3-he-drosophila-ventral-furrow-3>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-drosophila-ventral-furrow-audit-v3-he-drosophila-ventral-furrow-4>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-drosophila-ventral-furrow-audit-v3-he-drosophila-ventral-furrow-5>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-drosophila-ventral-furrow-audit-v3-he-drosophila-ventral-furrow-6>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-drosophila-ventral-furrow-audit-v3-he-drosophila-ventral-furrow-7>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-drosophila-ventral-furrow-audit-v3-he-drosophila-ventral-furrow-8>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-drosophila-ventral-furrow-audit-v3-he-drosophila-ventral-furrow-9> ;
        pk:hypothesisType "2D Incompressible Active Viscous-Vertex Epithelial Cross-Sectional Mechanics & Ratcheted Actomyosin Pulse Dynamics" ;
        pk:phenomenonScaleTier "3_subcellular_um" ;
        pk:phenomenonSizeLog10Meters -5.125e+00 ;
        pk:phenomenonSizeMeters 7.5e-06 ;
        pk:sameSpeciesClaim <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-drosophila-melanogaster-m1-2-anemotactic-odor-plume-cast-and-surge-swarm-collective-stigmergy>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-drosophila-melanogaster-mm1-4-larval-tracheal-10-metamere-branching-network-vertex-packing>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-drosophila-melanogaster-mm3-2-third-instar-larva-8-segment-peristaltic-wave-elastic-buckling>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-drosophila-melanogaster-nm120-syncytial-nuclear-pore-bcd-import-biomineral-accretion>,
