    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-hentschel-tgfb-fibronectin-limb> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Hentschel, Glimm, Glazier & Newman (2004) Proc. R. Soc. B / Kiskowski et al. (2004) Dev. Biol. multiscale TGF-beta / FGF-inhibitor reaction-diffusion and fibronectin haptotaxis PDE in developing Gallus gallus limb bud, coupled to a Glazier-Graner-Hogeweg cellular Potts cell lattice (Gallus gallus domesticus embryonic wing bud & high-density mesenchymal micromass (HH20 stylopod humerus -> HH24 zeugopod radius+ulna -> HH27 autopod digits II-IV))" ;
        dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/hentschel-tgfb-fibronectin-limb-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/hentschel-tgfb-fibronectin-limb-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/hentschel-tgfb-fibronectin-limb-3>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/hentschel-tgfb-fibronectin-limb-4>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/hentschel-tgfb-fibronectin-limb-5> ;
        schema:about "Gallus gallus domesticus embryonic wing bud & high-density mesenchymal micromass (HH20 stylopod humerus -> HH24 zeugopod radius+ulna -> HH27 autopod digits II-IV)" ;
        schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: A hexagonal nodular-spot micromass regime (both resolved continuum regimes are labyrinthine), a discrete stylopod condensation (GGH gives [0, 2, 3]), quantitative agreement with Kiskowski et al. (2004) condensation sizes, a sequential (exact-volume) cellular Potts update, 3D geometry, limb outgrowth, or cell division",
            "reconstructed_in_script: Linear dispersion of the activator/inhibitor subsystem, 1D and 2D (x, z) pseudo-spectral IMEX integration of the 4-field system with zero-flux boundaries, 2D periodic micromass morphospace with volume-filling haptotaxis, dual negative controls, a GGH cellular Potts lattice coupled through the PDE's Hill switch and a two-way fibronectin field, four GGH regimes plus a wing-bud GGH run, specimen segmentation of a Gallus wing, 14 measurements, 5 Lean 4 theorems",
            "reported_in_source: Graner & Glazier (1992) / Glazier & Graner (1993): differential adhesion with J_dd < J_ld < J_ll < J_cM at T = 10 sorts cells; heterotypic boundary length decreases",
            "reported_in_source: Hentschel et al. (2004): a 4-field TGF-beta activator / FGF-dependent inhibitor / fibronectin / mesenchymal-cell-density reaction-diffusion-haptotaxis system whose AER-FGF-modulated unstable wavenumber increases proximodistally, giving 1 -> 2 -> 3 skeletal elements",
            "reported_in_source: Kiskowski et al. (2004): discrete cells on a lattice with a continuous activator/inhibitor prepattern, activated cells deposit fibronectin and bind to it, producing autonomous condensations; Chaturvedi et al. (2005): the same scheme realised in a GGH cellular Potts framework (CompuCell)",
            "reported_in_source: Miura & Shiota (2000): exogenous TGF-beta2 fuses micromass condensations into bar-like patterns; anti-fibronectin treatment blocks condensation",
            "transfer_boundary: GGH references are internal (continuum ratio, ablation value, adopted thresholds) because the cited discrete-model papers do not report the metrics used here",
            "transfer_boundary: Kiskowski et al. (2004) is a lattice-cell / biased-random-walk model, not a cellular Potts model; the GGH realisation follows Chaturvedi et al. (2005), as the Pass 2 remediation item requested, and the dataset JSON says so",
            "transfer_boundary: The 1D stage and 2D wing continuum solutions are chemotactically collapsed (clip_fraction_R = 1.00 at fa = 11, 18; 0.52 at fa = 6; 0.193 in 2D): condensation counts are reproduced but amplitudes, std(R) and F-R correlations are clip-determined" ;
        pk:anatomicalStructure "Morphogen gradient & pre-cartilage condensation zone in Gallus gallus" ;
        pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "2. Morphogen + Condensations" ;
        pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "I. Enaima (Vertebrata)" ;
