    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Kondo & Asai (1995) Pomacanthus reaction-diffusion stripe insertion & Y-branch unzipping (Pomacanthus semicirculatus & Pomacanthus imperator (marine angelfish))" ;
        dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion-3>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion-4>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion-5> ;
        schema:about "Pomacanthus semicirculatus & Pomacanthus imperator (marine angelfish)" ;
        schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: 2D agent-field coupling on the curved domain, pigment-cell migration or Delta-Notch-type contact signalling, a conformal map of the real body outline, or 3D body-fin boundary mechanics",
            "reconstructed_in_script: 1D and 2D IMEX spectral solvers for the Kondo-Asai piecewise-linear saturating PDE across stationary domain doubling scales s in {1, 2, 4, 8} (body length 2, 4, 8, 16 cm -> 3, 6, 12, 24 stripes), subcritical inhibitor-diffusion control D_I = 0.050 < d_c D_A (0 stripes), continuous growing-domain kymograph (3 -> 6 -> 12 stripes), and 2D Y-branch horizontal unzipping (3 -> 4 stripes, +0.663 domain fraction displacement)",
            "reconstructed_in_script: Computer-vision segmentation of juvenile Pomacanthus semicirculatus specimen (`pomacanthus_semicirculatus_specimen.jpg`, CC BY-SA 4.0): 115 row-wise inter-stripe spacings (3.80 mm at 40 mm body span, CV = 0.34), primary/secondary prominence ratio 2.65x, bimodal Kondo-Asai waveform r = 0.858, and (Pass 3) structure-tensor concentric-arc fit (centre (262, 217) px, 8 arc radii, curvature-corrected radial spacing 2.62 mm, CV 0.28)",
            "reconstructed_in_script: Pass 3: curvilinear C-shaped polar-sector solver (rho in [0.25, 1], theta in [-100, 100] deg, 48 x 96, sparse-LU IMEX) with growing outer radius; 3 -> 6 concentric arcs at s* = 2.18 with mid-trough inhibitor trace I_mid(s) against the zero-activator threshold c_3/|c_2| = 0.625; 1D hybrid field + 128-cell iridophore/melanophore agent lattice with contact rules and bounded feedback kappa on c_3/c_5, ablated over kappa in {0, 0.005, 0.01, 0.02}",
            "reported_in_source: Gierer & Meinhardt (1972) Kybernetik 12:30-39 short-range autocatalytic activation and long-range lateral inhibition",
            "reported_in_source: Kondo & Asai (1995) Nature 376(6543):765-768 piecewise-linear saturating Gierer-Meinhardt reaction-diffusion PDE on an expanding skin domain L(t) = L_0 exp(gamma t), mid-trough secondary stripe insertion cascade (3 -> 6 -> 12 -> 24 stripes) in Pomacanthus semicirculatus, and 2D horizontal Y-junction branch point unzipping in Pomacanthus imperator",
            "reported_in_source: Nakamasu et al. (2009) PNAS 106:8429-8434 pigment-cell interaction network (short-range mutual exclusion, long-range support) and Bullara & De Decker (2015) lattice chromatophore model",
            "transfer_boundary: The agent layer is 1D on a periodic L = 6 lambda_c domain, so the wavelength is quantised to L/6 and only stripe contrast responds to the feedback; the rule probabilities (0.9 / 0.1 / update rate 0.35 / softness 0.3) are modelling choices, not values from Nakamasu et al. (2009)",
            "transfer_boundary: The curvilinear domain is an idealised polar sector (fixed rho_in = 0.25, theta_half = 100 deg), not the specimen's body silhouette; its centre and radial extent are not fitted to the specimen's concentric centre, so arc angular spans are not compared",
            "transfer_boundary: The mid-trough threshold c_3/|c_2| = 0.625 is the A = 0 sufficient condition; the simulated insertion fires at I_mid = 0.742 because flanking arcs supply activator diffusively" ;
        pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Pomacanthus imperator" ;
        pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
        pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "I. Enaima (Vertebrata)" ;
        pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
        pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
        pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Pisces (Ichthyes)" ;
        pk:biologicalGenus "Pomacanthus" ;
        pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1006/bulm.1999.0131>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1007/BF00289234>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/376765a0>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/ncomms7971>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0808622106>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1387/ijdb.072502sk> ;
        pk:geologicalAgeMa 0e+00 ;
        pk:geologicalPeriod "Holocene (Extant)" ;
        pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion-audit-v3-kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion-audit-v3-kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion-audit-v3-kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion-3>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion-audit-v3-kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion-4>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion-audit-v3-kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion-5>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion-audit-v3-kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion-6>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion-audit-v3-kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion-7>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion-audit-v3-kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion-8>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion-audit-v3-kondo-pomacanthus-stripe-insertion-9> ;
        pk:hypothesisType "Growing-Domain Reaction-Diffusion" ;
        pk:phenomenonScaleTier "6_organ_mm" ;
        pk:phenomenonSizeLog10Meters -2.616e+00 ;
        pk:phenomenonSizeMeters 2.42e-03 ;
        pk:sameSpeciesClaim <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-turing-gray-scott> ;
        pk:speciesTaxon <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/taxon/pomacanthus-imperator> ;
        pk:weightOfEvidence 9.31e-01 .

    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Lauschke, Tsiairis, François & Aulehla (2013) scale-invariant phase-gradient encoding in ex vivo monolayer presomitic mesoderm (mPSM) (Mus musculus (mouse E10.5 tailbud LuVeLu Lfng-Venus monolayer presomitic mesoderm))" ;
        dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM-3>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM-4>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM-5>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM-6> ;
        schema:about "Mus musculus (mouse E10.5 tailbud LuVeLu Lfng-Venus monolayer presomitic mesoderm)" ;
        schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Subcellular Lfng/Hes7 transcriptional-translational delay ODEs, explicit Notch-ligand delay-differential coupling, time-integrated morphogen transport on the moving boundary, 3D fibronectin traction mechanics, or cell movement/rearrangement within the reaggregate",
            "reconstructed_in_script: Bilateral dorsal somite row DoG peak and inter-somitic cleft segmentation on the vendored SEM (47.14 px mean spacing, CV = 0.2010; Panels E-F)",
            "reconstructed_in_script: Disordered reaggregate lattice of 1577 Kuramoto-Sakaguchi cells (K = 0.5 rad/min, eta = 0.25, a = 0.6 rad, correlation length 40 um): median 4 de novo pacemakers in cycles 1-3 consolidating to 1 in cycles 12-14 located 17.7 um from the local frequency maximum, local coherence 0.945; K = 0 -> coherence 0.004 and 0 sources, eta = 0 -> coherence 1.000 and 0 sources; K and eta sweeps (Panels H-I, reaggregate GIF)",
            "reconstructed_in_script: Quasi-static FGF/Wnt source-sink gradient (half-length exponent 1.000) vs fixed-length exponential gradient (exponent 0.000) driving dynamic wavelength relaxation d lambda/dt = -(lambda - c l_half)/tau_lambda with fixed-window segment gating: emergent alpha_8 = 0.1103 and mean Phi = 6.125 rad (2.5% from 2*pi) at tau_lambda = 35 min; alpha_8 = 0.5601 with tau_lambda = inf; constant 39.48 um segments (CV 0.032) with the fixed gradient (Panel G)",
            "reconstructed_in_script: Universal normalized phase-gradient collapse phi(r/R(t)) across R_0 in {150, 250, 350, 450} um (collapse std 9.93e-16 rad) vs non-scaling constant-gradient divergence; 2D circular mPSM LuVeLu target-wave kymograph; geometric radius progression with constant-velocity and DAPT (0 segments) controls (Panels A-D)",
            "reported_in_source: Aulehla et al. (2008) and Dubrulle & Pourquie (2004): graded posterior Wnt/beta-catenin and fgf8 signalling across the PSM, the latter set by mRNA decay (fixed length) rather than tissue size",
            "reported_in_source: Kuramoto (1984): a pacemaker with frequency excess beta k^2 in the nonlinear phase-diffusion equation emits a target wave of wavenumber k and the fastest pacemaker entrains the medium",
            "reported_in_source: Lauschke, Tsiairis, Francois & Aulehla (2013) Nature 493:101-105 scale-invariant phase-gradient encoding in ex vivo E10.5 mouse tailbud LuVeLu (Lfng-Venus) monolayer presomitic mesoderm (mPSM) with invariant ~2*pi phase span across the shrinking radius R(t), linear segment scaling S_n = alpha R(t_n) (alpha ~ 0.11) and wave velocity ~ R(t)/T_osc; Fig. 4 links the gradient steepening to a shrinking Wnt/FGF signalling domain",
            "reported_in_source: Tsiairis & Aulehla (2016) Cell 164:656-667: dissociated, randomised PSM cells re-synchronise LuVeLu oscillations in culture and self-organise multiple de novo target-wave foci",
            "transfer_boundary: Reaggregate pacemaker counts are compared with the paper's qualitative report of several foci (lower bound >= 2) and the Kuramoto single-dominant-pacemaker end state, not with digitised counts; the Sakaguchi lag a = 0.6 rad and kappa_init = 1 (partially synchronous initial phases) are modelling choices",
            "transfer_boundary: The FGF/Wnt gradient is quasi-static (analytic sinh / exponential profiles re-evaluated at each step), the sink-dominated limit is imposed through l_k = 1e6 um rather than derived from measured diffusion/decay constants, and c_lambda and delta_phi_seg are calibrated so that the adapted state reproduces Phi_0 = 2*pi and alpha = 0.11",
            "transfer_boundary: The vendored SEM specimen is a chick embryo (Wikimedia 'Aves Neural tube and somites in chick embryo', CC BY 4.0) used as a structural reference for somite periodicity; it is not mouse mPSM and no mPSM explant or reaggregate micrograph is compared" ;
        pk:anatomicalStructure "Segmentation clock somite / metamere unit in Mus musculus" ;
        pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "3. Phase/Delay Oscillators" ;
        pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "I. Enaima (Vertebrata)" ;
        pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Periodic Somites & Segments" ;
        pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Somite Length S = u·T_clock" ;
        pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Mammalia (Zootoka)" ;
        pk:biologicalGenus "Mus" ;
        pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-69689-3>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2016.01.028>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature02216>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature11804>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/ncb1679>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1088/1478-3975/13/3/036009> ;
        pk:geologicalAgeMa 0e+00 ;
        pk:geologicalPeriod "Holocene (Extant)" ;
        pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM-audit-v3-lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM-audit-v3-lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM-10>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM-audit-v3-lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM-2>,
