    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Metzger et al. (2008) & Menshykau et al. (2012, 2014) mouse lung stereotyped branching modes (Domain D, Planar P, Orthogonal O), FGF10-SHH-Ptch1 Turing mode selection, pleura-confined diffuse-domain FGF10 cavity and stochastic postnatal septation (Mus musculus (embryonic E11-E15 mouse bronchial tree; postnatal P4-P36 alveolarisation))" ;
        dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-3>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-4>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-5> ;
        schema:about "Mus musculus (embryonic E11-E15 mouse bronchial tree; postnatal P4-P36 alveolarisation)" ;
        schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: A 3D moving-boundary mesenchyme, tip chemotaxis, per-age alveolar counts from Mund (2008), digitised Metzger (2008) lineage coordinates, or an independent prediction of the adult alveolar number",
            "reconstructed_in_script: 3D Bishop-frame D/P/O grammar with the 4m + 1 tip law and a 181-point dihedral sweep; the Menshykau dispersion relation and a 1D spectral PDE mode switch; a quasi-2D diffuse-domain FGF10 cavity bounded by a dilating lens-shaped pleura with the tip as Ptch1 sink, whose supply anisotropy chooses P (0 deg) vs O (90 deg) at each bifurcation; an exact-increment Yule septation ensemble seeded by the grammar's extrapolated E16.5 terminal-unit count; chromatic segmentation and skeletonisation of a bronchial-tree image",
            "reported_in_source: Menshykau et al. (2012, 2014): an FGF10 / SHH-Ptch1 receptor-ligand Turing system on a growing epithelial domain selects between apical (bifurcation) and lateral (domain) budding, and mesenchymal geometry biases the direction of outgrowth",
            "reported_in_source: Metzger et al. (2008): the E11-E15 mouse bronchial tree is built from three stereotyped subroutines — Domain Branching, Planar Bifurcation (confined to lobe edges/margins) and Orthogonal Bifurcation (lobe interiors) — composed in a genetically encoded sequence",
            "reported_in_source: Mund, Stampanoni & Schittny (2008): mouse alveolarisation proceeds in a bulk phase P4-P21 and a continued phase P14-P36; Knust et al. (2009): the adult C57BL/6 mouse lung holds ~2.3e6 alveoli",
            "transfer_boundary: The 'specimen' is a Wikimedia medical illustration of human bronchioles/alveoli, not a mouse E11-E15 lung; its junction angles are compared with the model's reference angles but cannot validate the mouse grammar",
            "transfer_boundary: The pleura model is a transverse cross-section (z-invariant) with a prescribed, tree-independent dilation; tips choose P/O from the field but are not advected by grad F, and the pleura does not deform in response to the tree — the v2 item asked for a 3D moving-boundary phase-field/BEM, which this is not",
            "transfer_boundary: lambda_bulk is fitted to the adult alveolar count, so the P36 total is a calibration, not a prediction; the 632 terminal units at E16.5 are a log-linear extrapolation of the vendored E11-E14.5 timecourse table; lambda_cont / lambda_bulk = 0.12 and birth at E19.5 are assumptions" ;
        pk:anatomicalStructure "Bifurcating vascular / bronchial / hyphal branch in Mus musculus" ;
        pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "6. Tip-Splitting & Flow Trees" ;
        pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "I. Enaima (Vertebrata)" ;
        pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Bifurcating Vascular/Lung Trees" ;
        pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Murray Law r_0^3 = r_1^3 + r_2^3" ;
        pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Mammalia (Zootoka)" ;
        pk:biologicalGenus "Mus" ;
        pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1002/ar.20747>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1002/dvdy.21633>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature07005>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.081679>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1003421>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0041643>,
            <https://doi.org/10.4310/CMS.2009.v7.n1.a4> ;
        pk:geologicalAgeMa 0e+00 ;
        pk:geologicalPeriod "Holocene (Extant)" ;
        pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-lung-stereotyped-branching-modes-audit-v3-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-1>,
