    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Moulton, Goriely & Chirat (2015) & Chirat et al. (2013) hierarchical mollusc aperture spine folding and fractal frond serration (Murex pecten (Venus comb murex) & Chicoreus ramosus (ramose murex / Muricidae))" ;
        dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-3>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-4>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-5> ;
        schema:about "Murex pecten (Venus comb murex) & Chicoreus ramosus (ramose murex / Muricidae)" ;
        schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: A finite-strain shell FE solution, a numerically integrated Kirchhoff-Clebsch elastica, emergent fractal frond serrations, emergent varix periodicity, measured mantle thickness data for any species, or sourced empirical k_2/k_1 and spine counts for the 10 muricid species",
            "reconstructed_in_script: Hierarchical wavenumber law k_i^* = (3 K_s / (E h_i^3))^(1/4); 1-D unilateral fourth-order comb energy minimised by L-BFGS-B at the rounded mode q_mode = 2 pi round(L/lambda_1)/L; parametric omega-loop spine profile with a linear neck-gap law; prescribed 3-stage frond cosines; prescribed 120 deg varix bursts; 10-species cross-taxa table; DoG specimen segmentation (Pass 2)",
            "reconstructed_in_script: Pass 3: reduced linearised Koiter/FvK surface w(s,t) on a 192x96 bi-periodic torus (L_s = 67.2 mm, L_t = 24 mm, D = 1, K_0 = (k_1^*)^4) with varix growth window P(t), additive cord ridge forcing, semi-implicit gradient flow + L-BFGS-B relaxation from noise, emergent spine count / cord-intersection registration / ridge tilt; locking-tongue and obliquity sweeps; inverse-WKB h(u) from the specimen spacing profile; graded-rigidity 1-D comb with uniform control; allometric instar series with Brent root beta*",
            "reported_in_source: Chirat, Moulton & Goriely (2013): the mantle edge is an elastic strip growing against the calcified shell margin; excess growth gamma > gamma_c buckles it with wavelength lambda_1 ~ (E h_1^3 / 3 K_s)^(1/4) set by the mantle thickness and the foundation stiffness, giving comb spines along the siphonal canal of Murex pecten and varix spines in muricids",
            "reported_in_source: Koiter (1966) and Manor, Hagberg & Meron (2008): the thin-shell energy used for the reduced surface model, and wave-number locking of a pattern-forming system to a spatially periodic forcing (Arnold tongues)",
            "reported_in_source: Moulton, Goriely & Chirat (2015): further growth folds each spine into a Kirchhoff elastica loop that self-contacts into a hollow tube, and thinner secondary/tertiary mantle generations produce the fractal frond cascade k_{i+1}/k_i = (h_i/h_{i+1})^(3/4) of Chicoreus ramosus",
            "reported_in_source: Rudraraju et al. (2019): the full problem is a finite-strain morphoelastic shell with surface and volume growth, solved by finite elements",
            "transfer_boundary: The 1-D comb spine count 16, the 120 deg varix spacing, the Chicoreus k_2/k_1 = 3.80, the neck-gap delta -3.1059 mm, the specimen CV 0.2092 reference, beta* = 4/3 and the rigid-spine 22.8 deg are prescribed or self-referential and must not be read as validations",
            "transfer_boundary: The Koiter surface is linearised (no finite membrane strain, flat reference torus, nondimensional D = 1 with outputs labelled mm) and the planar elastica cross-section is not coupled to it; both are separate modules, so the Pass 2 item 1 (3D finite-strain Koiter FE coupling) is addressed only in reduced form",
            "transfer_boundary: h(s) is inferred from a Murex pecten photograph via inverse WKB (R^2 = 0.29, floor 0.35), not measured by micro-CT, and the species is not the Chicoreus ramosus the Pass 2 item asked for; no Chicoreus specimen is vendored" ;
        pk:anatomicalStructure "Biomineralized shell whorl / spicule / test in Murex pecten" ;
        pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "8. Crystal Accretion & TPMS" ;
        pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "II. Anaima (Invertebrata)" ;
        pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Coiled Shells, Spicules & Gyroids" ;
        pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Raup (W,D,S) / Gyroid Mean H=0" ;
        pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Ostrakoderma (Mollusca & Echinodermata)" ;
        pk:biologicalGenus "Murex" ;
        pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2012.07.009>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2014.09.021>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1220443110>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1209/0295-5075/83/10005>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1007213> ;
        pk:geologicalAgeMa 0e+00 ;
        pk:geologicalPeriod "Holocene (Extant)" ;
        pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-audit-v3-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-audit-v3-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-10>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-audit-v3-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-11>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-audit-v3-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-12>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-audit-v3-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-13>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-audit-v3-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-14>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-audit-v3-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-15>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-audit-v3-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-16>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-audit-v3-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-17>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-audit-v3-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-audit-v3-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-3>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-audit-v3-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-4>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-audit-v3-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-5>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-audit-v3-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-6>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-audit-v3-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-7>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-audit-v3-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-8>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-audit-v3-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-9> ;
        pk:hypothesisType "Kirchhoff-Clebsch Elastica on Unilateral Foundation & Hierarchical Multi-Stage Mantle Spine Buckling" ;
        pk:phenomenonScaleTier "7_organism_cm" ;
        pk:phenomenonSizeLog10Meters -1.626e+00 ;
        pk:phenomenonSizeMeters 2.365e-02 ;
        pk:speciesTaxon <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/taxon/murex-pecten> ;
        pk:weightOfEvidence 8.75e-01 .

    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-murray-mammalian-coat-markings> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Murray (1981) Thomas substrate-inhibition reaction-diffusion pre-pattern, conical tail spot-to-ring transition & P1 surface-FEM felid body (African leopard (Panthera pardus) coat rosettes and tapered tail markings)" ;
        dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/murray-mammalian-coat-markings-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/murray-mammalian-coat-markings-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/murray-mammalian-coat-markings-3>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/murray-mammalian-coat-markings-4>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/murray-mammalian-coat-markings-5> ;
        schema:about "African leopard (Panthera pardus) coat rosettes and tapered tail markings" ;
        schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: That Murray (1981) or Liu et al. (2006) reported any of the FEM, annularity, growth-sweep or marking-density numbers; all are v3 reconstructions",
            "does_not_claim: That the Thomas kinetics are the biological mechanism of felid pigmentation",
            "reconstructed_in_script: Exact steady state, Jacobian, d_c, dispersion curve and Turing band; Neumann cylinder eigenmode counting including n = 0; r_crit (fastest-mode) and r_excl = 1/k_+ (full-exclusion) radii; fully implicit conical-tail PDE; planar DCT-II IMEX PDE run to saturation with a genuine two-stage protocol and growth-factor sweep; P1 surface FEM (stiffness/mass assembly, spectrum verification, two-stage run on the felid body) with annularity and spot-spacing diagnostics; DoG segmentation of the Kruger specimen",
            "reported_in_source: Dziuk (1988), Pinkall & Polthier (1993), Dziuk & Elliott (2013): P1 surface finite elements with cotangent weights converge to the Laplace-Beltrami operator on a triangulated surface",
            "reported_in_source: Liu, Liaw & Maini (2006): leopard rosettes arise from a two-stage process in which a juvenile spot pre-pattern is re-run under changed parameters on the grown adult skin",
            "reported_in_source: Murray (1981): Thomas substrate-inhibition kinetics at a = 92, b = 64, alpha = 1.5, rho = 18.5, K = 0.1 are diffusively unstable for d > d_c; the domain scale factor gamma selects between no pattern, stripes, spots and crowding; on a tapered cylinder spot modes (m >= 1) are excluded below a critical radius so a spotted animal can have a ringed tail but not vice versa",
            "transfer_boundary: The 3D body is a parametric surface of revolution with hand-set knots (felid_body_profile.json), not a photogrammetric scan; its head-body length of 22 cub wavelengths and the growth factor G = 2 are ASSUMED, not fitted, which is why the FEM marking density (5.1 per torso depth) is 3.7x below the specimen estimate (18.9)",
            "transfer_boundary: The specimen is a 3/4-view photograph: the flank ROI is foreshortened and the v2 tail ROI covers hindquarters/background, so the Delaunay CV and polygonality are flank-only statistics",
            "transfer_boundary: The tail ring onset comparison (0.82 measured vs 0.86 predicted) is on the surrogate taper, whose tip radius (0.004 HBL) was chosen to lie below r_excl; it is a consistency check of solver against linear theory, not a measurement on a real tail" ;
