    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Oster, Murray & Harris (1983) / Oster, Murray & Maini (1985) mechanochemical limb chondrogenesis (Ambystoma mexicanum & Oedipina ecuatoriana urodele salamander limb cartilage)" ;
        dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-3>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-4>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-5> ;
        schema:about "Ambystoma mexicanum & Oedipina ecuatoriana urodele salamander limb cartilage" ;
        schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: A 3D finite-element limb, explicit ECM density/advection, joint/phalangeal segmentation of the rods, Hoxd13 gene-dosage polydactyly scaling (Slot 017), or quantitative reproduction of the full Raspopovic (2014) 2D autopod (Slot 016)",
            "reconstructed_in_script: A 2D coupled cell-ECM PDE on a limb paddle with a moving free-boundary AER front (progress-zone traction suppression and proliferation, AER regression, anisotropic PD cell diffusion a_y = 3, ectoderm-balanced prestress) producing the forelimb [1, 2, 4] and hindlimb [1, 2, 5] hierarchies from a seeded proximal nucleus plus noise, with proximo-distal onset order and the Saunders (1948) ablation series [1, 1, 2, 3]",
            "reconstructed_in_script: A 4x4 hybrid Jacobian and 1D hybrid PDE coupling the mechanics to Raspopovic (2014) BSW kinetics (tau(1 + alpha_S S), +kappa_S (n - N_0)), with wavelength-matched ligand diffusivities, showing tau_c lowering 1.44 -> 0.35 and a 2x2 factorial [0, 0, 0, 4] at tau = 0.85",
            "reconstructed_in_script: Exact marginal stability curve tau_eff(k^2) with analytic tau_c = 1.2776 at k_c = 0.9597 (lambda_c = 6.5472) and the 1D spectral-pseudospectral cell-ECM solver reproducing modes [0, 1, 2, 4, 5] on periodic domains W = m lambda_c with seeded m-cosine perturbations",
            "reconstructed_in_script: Morphological segmentation of the vendored Oedipina ecuatoriana specimen giving [1, 2, 4] / [1, 2, 5] hierarchies, autopod spacings 39.0 / 41.25 px and the zeugopod/autopod spacing ratio compared with the 2D PDE (1.235 vs 1.373)",
            "reported_in_source: Critical cell traction bifurcation threshold tau_c driving focal condensation (stylopod), dichotomous Y-bifurcation (zeugopod) and digital branching (autopod: 4 forelimb / 5 hindlimb digits in urodele salamanders)",
            "reported_in_source: Oster, Murray & Harris (1983) J. Embryol. Exp. Morph. 78:83-125 and Oster, Murray & Maini (1985) J. Embryol. Exp. Morph. 89:93-112 coupled mesenchymal cell-density and viscoelastic ECM traction PDE system; the AER maintains a distal recruitment/progress zone and condensations are laid down proximo-distally",
            "reported_in_source: Raspopovic et al. (2014): a Bmp-Sox9-Wnt Turing network with Sox9 out of phase with Bmp and Wnt patterns the digits",
            "reported_in_source: Saunders (1948): removing the chick-wing AER at progressively later stages leaves progressively more distal skeletal parts (proximo-distal sequence of origin)",
            "transfer_boundary: Only the proximal humeral/femoral nucleus is seeded in the 2D solver; the stylopod width W = 1.4 lambda_c is a tuned choice (W = 1.0 is marginal), and the autopod count is partly inherited by 2 -> 4 bifurcation rather than set by W / lambda_c",
            "transfer_boundary: The 2D domain is a Fourier-periodic box with a diffuse (tanh) competence field, not a sharp Neumann boundary; the ECM force balance is reduced to a component-wise Helmholtz operator (no shear/Poisson coupling, no ECM density equation) and the viscous relaxation rate 1/(mu + 0.15) is ad hoc",
            "transfer_boundary: The BSW parameters are copied from the Slot 016 reference JSON, rescaled in diffusivity to match lambda_c; the Saunders (1948) comparison is a qualitative stage-to-segment mapping, not digitised data; lengths are in lambda_c units with no micron calibration against the specimen",
            "transfer_boundary: The solvers' drift kernel includes mu k^2 in the quasi-static stiffness, so their effective tau_c (1.4397) is 12.7% above the analytic 1.2776 shown in Panels A/D; all supercritical regimes used exceed both" ;
        pk:anatomicalStructure "Morphogen gradient & pre-cartilage condensation zone in Ambystoma mexicanum" ;
        pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "2. Morphogen + Condensations" ;
        pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "I. Enaima (Vertebrata)" ;
        pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Skeletal Rays & Joints" ;
        pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "French-Flag / PSHM Thresholds" ;
        pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Amphibia & Reptilia (Ootoka)" ;
        pk:biologicalGenus "Ambystoma" ;
        pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1002/(SICI)1521-1878(200002)22:2%3C138::AID-BIES5%3E3.0.CO;2-4>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1002/jez.1401080304>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1007/978-1-4615-6983-1_6>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1093/imammb/1.1.51>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1252960>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.023176>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.78.1.83>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.89.1.93> ;
        pk:geologicalAgeMa 0e+00 ;
        pk:geologicalPeriod "Holocene (Extant)" ;
        pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-audit-v3-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-audit-v3-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-10>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-audit-v3-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-11>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-audit-v3-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-12>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-audit-v3-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-13>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-audit-v3-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-14>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-audit-v3-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-audit-v3-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-3>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-audit-v3-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-4>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-audit-v3-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-5>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-audit-v3-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-6>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-audit-v3-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-7>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-audit-v3-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-8>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-audit-v3-oster-mechanochemical-chondrogenesis-9> ;
        pk:hypothesisType "Mechanochemical Cell-Traction & Viscoelastic ECM Chondrogenesis PDE (Oster-Murray-Harris 1983 / Oster-Murray-Maini 1985)" ;
        pk:phenomenonScaleTier "7_organism_cm" ;
        pk:phenomenonSizeLog10Meters -1.407e+00 ;
        pk:phenomenonSizeMeters 3.92e-02 ;
        pk:sameSpeciesClaim <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-lobo-limbform-morphology> ;
        pk:speciesTaxon <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/taxon/ambystoma-mexicanum> ;
        pk:weightOfEvidence 8.71e-01 .

    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-painter-chemotactic-stripe-splitting> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Painter, Maini & Othmer (1999) Pomacanthus Turing-chemotaxis stripe doubling on a growing curved flank & Keller-Segel rippling with slime-trail tensor (Pomacanthus semicirculatus juvenile pigment stripes (model target) & Myxococcus xanthus rippling cell populations (specimen))" ;
        dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/painter-chemotactic-stripe-splitting-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/painter-chemotactic-stripe-splitting-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/painter-chemotactic-stripe-splitting-3>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/painter-chemotactic-stripe-splitting-4>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/painter-chemotactic-stripe-splitting-5>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/painter-chemotactic-stripe-splitting-6> ;
        schema:about "Pomacanthus semicirculatus juvenile pigment stripes (model target) & Myxococcus xanthus rippling cell populations (specimen)" ;
        schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Individual-cell C-signal contact-reversal mechanics or 3D fruiting-body stalk elevation",
            "does_not_claim: Reproduction of PNAS 1999 Fig. 4-5 anisotropic 2D growth (1.8e-4 / 2.2e-4) or Fig. 8 Lengyel-Epstein adult stripe-to-spot transition",
            "reconstructed_in_script: Computer-vision segmentation of the Myxococcus xanthus specimen (`chemotactic_pattern_specimen.jpg`, CC BY-SA 4.0): 4 fruiting-body spot aggregates and 362 rippling stripe spacings (74.10 um mean wavelength via the 500 um = 125 px scale bar)",
            "reconstructed_in_script: Generic Keller-Segel chemotaxis-logistic 1D/2D IMEX pseudospectral solvers (stationary s in {1, 2, 4, 8}, subcritical control chi = 3.0, growing-domain kymograph 1 -> 2 -> 4, 2D cubic stripes vs quadratic spots) and a slime-trail nematic tensor Q with mobility M = I + aQ tested by a chi-drop hysteresis protocol (grow at 6.2, hold at 4.0 / 4.4)",
            "reconstructed_in_script: PNAS 1999 Fig. 3 system integrated on a uniformly growing surface of revolution (1D line, cylinder K = 0, spindle K lambda_c^2 = 0.69) with a Laplace-Beltrami eigenbasis solver, fully implicit diffusion + Jacobian + 2r dilution, explicit clipped kinetics and chemotactic flux; stripe counts 3 -> 6 -> 12 on flat flanks (doubling scale ratio 2.03), 3 -> 6 -> 8 on the spindle; chi_0 sweep over two orders of magnitude",
            "reported_in_source: Balagam & Igoshin (2015) trail-following alignment of gliding M. xanthus cells",
            "reported_in_source: Keller & Segel (1970) J. Theor. Biol. 26:399-415 chemotactic flux cross-diffusion -div(n chi(c) grad(c)) and its linear instability; Crampin, Gaffney & Maini (1999) growing-domain dilution and mode doubling; Ermentrout (1991) stripe-vs-spot selection",
            "reported_in_source: Painter, Maini & Othmer (1999) PNAS 96(10):5549-5554 Eqs. (1)-(3): Kondo-Asai piecewise-linear Turing morphogens u, v with chemotactic iridophores n, chi(u) = chi_0/(k+u)^2, chi_0 < 0, on an exponentially growing domain L(t) = 11 exp(1e-4 t) (Fig. 3: 3-peak juvenile pattern; Fig. 1 / Kondo & Asai 1995: 3 -> 6 -> 12 stripes at 2, 6, 12 months)",
            "transfer_boundary: The Keller-Segel rippling model and slime-trail tensor are mapped to M. xanthus rippling ridges; the tensor is a continuum closure, not an agent-based trail model",
            "transfer_boundary: The PNAS 1999 iridophore model is compared against Kondo & Asai's stripe COUNTS (3, 6, 12) only; no Pomacanthus photograph is vendored, so curvature-dependent stripe geometry is not validated against a fish specimen" ;
        pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Myxococcus xanthus" ;
        pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
        pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "IV. Protista & Monera" ;
        pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
        pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
        pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Slime Molds & Bacteria" ;
        pk:biologicalGenus "Myxococcus" ;
        pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1006/bulm.1999.0131>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1007/BF02458621>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(70)90092-5>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.physd.2010.09.011>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/376765a0>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.96.10.5549>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1098/rspa.1991.0100>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1004474> ;
        pk:geologicalAgeMa 0e+00 ;
        pk:geologicalPeriod "Holocene (Extant)" ;
        pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-chemotactic-stripe-splitting-audit-v3-painter-chemotactic-stripe-splitting-1>,
