    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-runions-leaf-venation> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Runions et al. (2005) Leaf Venation Space-Colonization & Murray's Law (Ginkgo biloba (open dichotomous venation) & angiosperm dicot lamina (reticulate venation))" ;
        dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/runions-leaf-venation-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/runions-leaf-venation-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/runions-leaf-venation-3> ;
        schema:about "Ginkgo biloba (open dichotomous venation) & angiosperm dicot lamina (reticulate venation)" ;
        schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: 2D planar lamina space-colonization and pipe-model radius propagation do not model 3D mesophyll thickness or stomatal transpiration dynamics",
            "reconstructed_in_script: Open Ginkgo biloba (Table 1 Fig. 10) and closed dicot (Table 1 Fig. 15) space-colonization simulators with persistent V(s) source tagging and planar segment-intersection checks, multiscale Horton-Strahler vascular tree measurement, and planar dual areole loop nesting on both simulated networks and segmented specimen photographs",
            "reported_in_source: Katifori & Magnasco (2012) and Ronellenfitsch et al. (2015) quantify hierarchical areole loop nesting via recursive minimum-width vein removal on the planar dual graph",
            "reported_in_source: Murray (1926) derives minimum-work pipe scaling r_parent^3 = sum r_child^3, while Price et al. (2013) measure 349 cleared leaves (1,514,771 junctions) showing a transition from Murray's law in minor veins (gamma ~ 3, area ratio ~ 1.25) to area-preserving branching in major veins (gamma ~ 2, area ratio ~ 1.01)",
            "reported_in_source: Runions et al. (2005) define open auxin space-colonization (Eq. 1) via Voronoi nearest-vein neighborhoods and closed reticulate venation (Eq. 2-3) via Toussaint Relative Neighborhood Graph (RNG) neighborhoods with persistent tagged-source anastomosis",
            "transfer_boundary: Direct comparison of simulated planar dual areole nesting and Strahler bifurcation scaling against segmented leaf skeleton specimens and Price et al. (2013) / Ronellenfitsch et al. (2015) empirical benchmarks" ;
        pk:anatomicalStructure "Auxin flux vein / phyllotactic primordium in Ginkgo biloba" ;
        pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "4. Polar Auxin & Turgor Stress" ;
        pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "III. Phyta (Embryophyta)" ;
        pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Open & Reticulate Venation" ;
        pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Murray Exponent alpha" ;
        pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Angiospermae & Gymnospermae" ;
        pk:biologicalGenus "Ginkgo" ;
        pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.12.3.207>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1145/1073204.1073251>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1004680>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0037994>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0085420> ;
        pk:geologicalAgeMa 0e+00 ;
        pk:geologicalPeriod "Holocene (Extant)" ;
        pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-18-venation-audit-v2-runions-leaf-venation-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-18-venation-audit-v2-runions-leaf-venation-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-18-venation-audit-v2-runions-leaf-venation-3>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-18-venation-audit-v2-runions-leaf-venation-4>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-18-venation-audit-v2-runions-leaf-venation-5>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-18-venation-audit-v2-runions-leaf-venation-6>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-18-venation-audit-v2-runions-leaf-venation-7> ;
        pk:hypothesisType "Auxin Space-Colonization, Murray's Minimum-Work Vascular Law & Planar Dual Loop Nesting" ;
        pk:phenomenonScaleTier "7_organism_cm" ;
        pk:phenomenonSizeLog10Meters -1.903e+00 ;
        pk:phenomenonSizeMeters 1.25e-02 ;
        pk:sameSpeciesClaim <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-ginkgo-biloba-bioelectric-polarity>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-ginkgo-biloba-biomineral-accretion>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-ginkgo-biloba-branching-tree>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-ginkgo-biloba-clock-wavefront>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-ginkgo-biloba-collective-stigmergy>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-ginkgo-biloba-elastic-buckling>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-ginkgo-biloba-flux-canalization>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-ginkgo-biloba-morphogen-condensation>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-ginkgo-biloba-turing-wavelength>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-ginkgo-biloba-vertex-packing> ;
        pk:speciesTaxon <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/taxon/ginkgo-biloba> ;
        pk:weightOfEvidence 9.13e-01 .

    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-runions-pavement-cell-lobing> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Sapala et al. (2018) & Fu et al. (2005) ROP2-ROP6 interdigitated puzzle-shaped pavement cell lobing, Largest Empty Circle (LEC) turgor stress scaling, reduced pressurized periclinal membrane-shell and depth-resolved anticlinal wall buckling (Arabidopsis thaliana (cotyledon & leaf epidermal pavement cells))" ;
        dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/runions-pavement-cell-lobing-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/runions-pavement-cell-lobing-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/runions-pavement-cell-lobing-3>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/runions-pavement-cell-lobing-4>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/runions-pavement-cell-lobing-5> ;
        schema:about "Arabidopsis thaliana (cotyledon & leaf epidermal pavement cells)" ;
        schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Full 3D finite-element shell modelling of dome deflection coupled to anticlinal wall growth anisotropy, discrete microtubule stochastics, or any digitised amplitude-vs-depth measurement from confocal stacks",
            "reconstructed_in_script: (Pass 3) Depth-resolved anticlinal wall strip: outer-junction forcing by the ROP2-ROP6 wall displacement, Robin inner face (beta sweep 0 .. clamped), sparse FD Laplace solve vs modal closed form (1.2 %), dominant k = 8 mode inner/outer gain 0.028 (e^-1 penetration 4 um of H = 15 um), depth-distributed-forcing ablation (inner/outer 0.70)",
            "reconstructed_in_script: (Pass 3) Reduced Foppl uniform-tension pressurised periclinal membrane solve -T lap(z) = P on the rasterised footprint with self-consistent tension T = T0 + E h eps/(1-nu), T0 = P H / 2, verified against the closed-form disk (0.9 %) and the inscribed-disk bound (18/18), used to TEST the LEC stress proxy: Pearson r(sigma_m, R_LEC) = 0.982 but fitted exponent 0.51 and isotropic/WT ratio 1.73 vs the proxy's 3.32",
            "reconstructed_in_script: 196-node periodic anticlinal boundary coupled ROP2-RIC4 / ROP6-RIC1-KTN1 reaction-diffusion PDE integrator (intracortical r = -0.9899, trans-wall r = 0.9998, 24.5 um lobe wavelength, exact intercellular area conservation)",
            "reconstructed_in_script: Automated DoG + zero-compactness watershed segmentation of 10 interlocking puzzle cells from the SHA-256-locked Arabidopsis leaf epidermis micrograph (mean S = 0.720, min S = 0.626; mean L = 1.316 in this environment vs 1.506 recorded by v2)",
            "reconstructed_in_script: Exact 2D Euclidean Distance Transform R_LEC and ConvexHull solidity/lobeyness across A in [250, 4500] um^2 for a compact branched WT puzzle construction (band + alternating staggered finger lobes; aspect 2.6 at 4500 um^2), unlobed isotropic cells, ktn1/ric1 and rop2 rop4 mutants, and parallel-file monocot epidermis",
            "reported_in_source: Armour et al. (2015) Plant Cell 27:2484-2500: lobe formation involves differential growth of periclinal and anticlinal walls in 3D (depth context; no amplitude-vs-depth table is used here)",
            "reported_in_source: Fu et al. (2005) Cell 120:687-700 & Lin et al. (2013) Curr Biol 23:290-297: antagonistic cortical ROP2-RIC4 (actin lobe outgrowth) and ROP6-RIC1-KTN1 (katanin-mediated microtubule neck bundling) polarisation in antiphase across shared anticlinal cell walls; lobeyness collapse in rop2 rop4 RNAi and ktn1/ric1 mutants",
            "reported_in_source: Sapala et al. (2018) eLife 7:e32794: outer periclinal cell wall tensile stress in pressurised FEM cell templates increases with the Largest Empty Circle radius (thin-wall proxy sigma_max ~ P R_LEC / h, Box 1 & Fig. 3); interdigitated puzzle lobing pins R_LEC near ~11.4 um as cell area expands to 4500 um^2 whereas isotropic polygonal/mutant cells grow as sqrt(A/pi)",
            "transfer_boundary: The WT footprint is a deterministic geometric construction whose constants (lobe half-width 0.62 r_t, tip 1.25x, pitch 3.0 r_t, band fraction polynomial) were tuned to the vendored benchmark series, not grown by the spring-remodelling simulator of Sapala et al. (2018); the ROP2-ROP6 PDE does not feed the polygon",
            "transfer_boundary: The depth law (sinh/cosh modal attenuation) is a prediction of a prestressed-strip model verified against its own analytic solution; the inner-face anchoring beta = 2 is a modelling choice and no depth-resolved specimen measurement is vendored",
            "transfer_boundary: The periclinal 'shell' is a uniform-tension membrane with an analytic clamped-edge bending boundary layer on the 2D footprint, not a bending-coupled 3D finite-element shell; E = 300 MPa, nu = 0.3, H = 15 um and T0 = PH/2 are order-of-magnitude assumptions (flagged in the vendored JSON), so the absolute stresses (34 vs 59 MPa) and the 1.73x ratio are model-conditional" ;
        pk:anatomicalStructure "Auxin flux vein / phyllotactic primordium in Arabidopsis thaliana" ;
        pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "4. Polar Auxin & Turgor Stress" ;
        pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "III. Phyta (Embryophyta)" ;
        pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Spirals, Veins & Puzzle Cells" ;
        pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Golden Angle / Auxin Flux" ;
        pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Angiospermae & Gymnospermae" ;
        pk:biologicalGenus "Arabidopsis" ;
        pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2004.12.026>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cub.2013.01.022>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41477-019-0500-2>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1105/tpc.114.126664>,
            <https://doi.org/10.7554/eLife.01967>,
            <https://doi.org/10.7554/eLife.32794> ;
        pk:geologicalAgeMa 0e+00 ;
        pk:geologicalPeriod "Holocene (Extant)" ;
        pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-pavement-cell-lobing-audit-v3-runions-pavement-cell-lobing-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-pavement-cell-lobing-audit-v3-runions-pavement-cell-lobing-10>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-pavement-cell-lobing-audit-v3-runions-pavement-cell-lobing-11>,
