    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Sheth et al. (2012) Science distal Hoxa13/Hoxd11-13 + Gli3 dose modulation of Turing digit wavelength on a fan-shaped embryonic autopod, with Pass 3 AER-FGF8 mitogenic outgrowth on a deforming Lagrangian mesh (Vertebrate embryonic autopod (Mus musculus distal Hox/Gli3 allelic series & postaxial hexadactylous autopod radiograph))" ;
        dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly-3>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly-4>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly-5> ;
        schema:about "Vertebrate embryonic autopod (Mus musculus distal Hox/Gli3 allelic series & postaxial hexadactylous autopod radiograph)" ;
        schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: 3D limb bud geometry, cell-level mechanics, Sox9/Bmp/Wnt three-node kinetics, quantitative reproduction of Sheth et al.'s Fig. 2G digit-period measurements (not vendored), or hour-calibrated developmental time",
            "reconstructed_in_script: Sheth et al. (2012) linear dispersion, k_c(H) and the cubic-saturated two-component PDE on a 1D Neumann arc and a 2D fixed-width polar fan (Pass 2), plus the Pass 3 AER-FGF8 kinematic growing fan in ALE form with dilution, mesh-relative advection, physical-metric angular modes, backward-Euler radial diffusion, Lagrangian tracers, AER regression and ablation, a g_max sweep and the quasi-static digit-number/width law; 6-genotype allelic series; dual negative controls; radiograph digit-ray segmentation; 5 Lean 4 theorems",
            "reported_in_source: Boehm et al. (2010): limb bud proliferation is distally biased but a proliferation gradient alone is insufficient to explain bud shape",
            "reported_in_source: Crampin, Gaffney & Maini (1999): on a growing domain the reaction-diffusion equations acquire an advection term and a dilution term -(div v) u; patterns lag the fixed-domain wavelength and transition by peak insertion / frequency doubling",
            "reported_in_source: Sheth et al. (2012): progressive loss of distal Hox (Hoxa13, Hoxd11-13) in a Gli3-null background shrinks the digit period (wavelength) of a Turing-type mechanism, raising digit number from 5 to ~14 at roughly constant autopod width (Figs. 1-3)",
            "reported_in_source: Summerbell (1974): AER excision arrests distal outgrowth; the earlier the excision the more proximal the truncation",
            "transfer_boundary: Digit-ray (stripe) orientation is imposed by PD/AP diffusion anisotropy D_r = 0.05 D rather than derived from the Fgf/Wnt proximodistal modulation of Raspopovic et al. (2014)",
            "transfer_boundary: Growth is kinematic: g(r,t) is prescribed by the mitogen field and div v = g; no elastic/viscous constitutive law, stress balance or oriented cell behaviour is solved (Boehm et al. 2010 show these matter for shape)",
            "transfer_boundary: The 1D arc and fixed-width fan solvers seed the target cosine mode (-0.08 cos(n_target s)); only the Pass 3 growing fan evolves from seeded noise alone, and it shows a growth-induced wavelength lag (N_grow = 3.5 WT, 13.0 null vs law 5 / 14)",
            "transfer_boundary: k_c(H) = 14 - 9H and g_u(H) = 200 f_u + 25 k_c^4 - 4.5|tr J_kc| are closure ansaetze that interpolate the allelic series and pin sigma_max ~ 4.5; they are not fitted to Sheth et al.'s supplementary parameter values" ;
        pk:anatomicalStructure "Morphogen gradient & pre-cartilage condensation zone in Mus musculus" ;
        pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "2. Morphogen + Condensations" ;
        pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "I. Enaima (Vertebrata)" ;
        pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Skeletal Rays & Joints" ;
        pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "French-Flag / PSHM Thresholds" ;
        pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Mammalia (Zootoka)" ;
        pk:biologicalGenus "Mus" ;
        pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1006/bulm.1999.0131>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2005.10.016>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1179047>,
