    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-sick-wnt-dkk-hair-follicle> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Sick et al. (2006) & Andl et al. (2002) WNT/DKK reaction-diffusion hair follicle spacing, secondary wave insertion, transgenic phenotypes & (Pass 3) 3D dermal condensate FGF20/BMP4 chemotaxis with hair peg downgrowth (Embryonic mouse (Mus musculus) epidermal hair follicle placode lattice with dermal condensate formation and hair peg downgrowth; K14-Wnt / Dkk1 / Fgf20-null / BMP4-excess genotypes)" ;
        dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/sick-wnt-dkk-hair-follicle-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/sick-wnt-dkk-hair-follicle-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/sick-wnt-dkk-hair-follicle-3>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/sick-wnt-dkk-hair-follicle-4>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/sick-wnt-dkk-hair-follicle-5>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/sick-wnt-dkk-hair-follicle-6> ;
        schema:about "Embryonic mouse (Mus musculus) epidermal hair follicle placode lattice with dermal condensate formation and hair peg downgrowth; K14-Wnt / Dkk1 / Fgf20-null / BMP4-excess genotypes" ;
        schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: A deforming epithelial interface or tissue mechanics of invagination, DC -> epidermis feedback (DC-derived Noggin/FGF), follicle-type specification by DC size, calibration of slab depth or peg depth to micrometres, or numerical parity with Sick et al.'s own simulation parameters",
            "reconstructed_in_script: (Pass 3) 3D dermal slab beneath the WT placode field: FGF20 sourced at z = 0 by the placodes, BMP4 produced by the dermis, Keller-Segel chemotaxis with volume filling in conservative face-flux form, per-placode hair-peg depth ODE, WT / Fgf20-null / chemotaxis-null / BMP4-excess genotypes, chi_f sweep, dermal linear stability, seam-aware placode counting",
            "reconstructed_in_script: Saturating Gierer-Meinhardt WNT/DKK PDE with exact steady state, Jacobian and d_c = (sqrt2+1)^2; 1D primary wave -> 2x expansion -> secondary insertion (4 -> 8); 2D WT / K14-Wnt / enlarged / Dkk1 / equal-diffusion regimes; Dkk1 dosage and domain-length sweeps; optical-density segmentation of the vendored specimen",
            "reported_in_source: Andl et al. (2002): ectopic Dkk1 blocks follicle initiation (no placodes)",
            "reported_in_source: Botchkarev et al. (1999), Mou et al. (2006): BMP4 inhibits follicle induction / dermal condensation; Noggin/EDA antagonise it",
            "reported_in_source: Glover et al. (2017): dermal cells aggregate directly beneath placodes by directed migration toward placode FGF20",
            "reported_in_source: Huh et al. (2013): placode-derived FGF20 is required for primary and secondary dermal condensates; Fgf20-null placodes form but do not progress",
            "reported_in_source: Paus et al. (1999): ordinal morphological stages placode -> hair germ (with DC) -> hair peg",
            "reported_in_source: Sick et al. (2006): WNT (short-range activator) and DKK (long-range inhibitor) form a Turing/Meinhardt reaction-diffusion pair that sets pelage follicle spacing; K14-Dkk1 overexpression reduces/abolishes follicles, altered WNT/DKK balance enlarges or crowds placodes, and a secondary follicle wave inserts between primary follicles as the skin grows",
            "transfer_boundary: All parameters are dimensionless and chosen to produce the qualitative regimes; none of D_w, D_h, mu, rho, kappa, D_f, mu_f, chi_f, chi_b, D_rho, v_peg is traced to a measured value or to Sick et al.'s SOM parameter table",
            "transfer_boundary: The K14-Wnt regime changes D_w, D_h and kappa together with rho_w, so it is a 'denser lattice' preset rather than a pure WNT-overexpression perturbation",
            "transfer_boundary: The dermal coupling is one-way (placodes -> dermis); the epidermis stays planar and peg downgrowth is a scalar depth per placode; stage thresholds 25%/50% of slab depth are a model convention",
            "transfer_boundary: The vendored specimen is a Gad1 whole-mount in situ of E12.5-E13.5 vibrissa/hair placodes (Maddox & Condie 2004), not a pelage pattern from Sick et al.; the PDE lattice (15 placodes, NN-spacing CV 0.086) and the specimen (16 segmented placodes, CV 0.323) agree in count only approximately and disagree in regularity" ;
        pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Mus musculus" ;
        pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
        pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "I. Enaima (Vertebrata)" ;
        pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
        pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
        pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Mammalia (Zootoka)" ;
        pk:biologicalGenus "Mus" ;
        pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1007/BF00289234>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(70)90092-5>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/S1534-5807(02)00167-3>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/11078>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1046/j.1523-1747.1999.00740.x>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0600825103>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1101/gad.198945.112>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1130088>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1186/1471-213X-4-4>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pbio.2002117> ;
        pk:geologicalAgeMa 0e+00 ;
        pk:geologicalPeriod "Holocene (Extant)" ;
        pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-wnt-dkk-hair-follicle-audit-v3-sick-wnt-dkk-hair-follicle-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-wnt-dkk-hair-follicle-audit-v3-sick-wnt-dkk-hair-follicle-10>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-wnt-dkk-hair-follicle-audit-v3-sick-wnt-dkk-hair-follicle-11>,
