    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Sumper (2002) & Lenoci-Camp (2008) hierarchical Cahn-Hilliard diatom biosilica phase separation (Pass 3: centrifugal precipitation front + 3-stage single-domain quench) (Coscinodiscus wailesii (Centric marine diatom frustule valve pores: foramen, cribrum, cribrella; radial costae))" ;
        dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-3>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-4>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-5> ;
        schema:about "Coscinodiscus wailesii (Centric marine diatom frustule valve pores: foramen, cribrum, cribrella; radial costae)" ;
        schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Quantitative agreement with measured C. wailesii costae spacing or bifurcation count, the exact Furukawa crossover speed, cribrum-per-foramen multiplicities of 7-19 (model gives 4.8 at 512^2), SDV chemistry, or online verification of the Furukawa (1992) and Schmid & Volcani (1983) DOIs",
            "reconstructed_in_script: Pass 2 two-stage hierarchy, dispersion relation, eps sweep, SEM segmentation of 139 foramina / 74 cribrum pores, hexatic |psi_6| and 3-tier log-linear scaling (L124-L171, L244-L331, L730-L975)",
            "reconstructed_in_script: Radial quench front a(r,t) = tanh((R0 + v t - r)/w) with lagging solidification front R_s = R - lag lambda_c on a disc, conserved thermal noise, margin gradient-tensor anisotropy A, front Peclet number v/(lambda_c sigma_max), 5-speed ablation and 3-seed isotropic null (L346-L580)",
            "reconstructed_in_script: Semi-implicit spectral Cahn-Hilliard solver with exact zero-mode mass conservation, extended with a spatially varying bulk term phi^3 - a(x) phi and a zero-mobility frozen mask with total-mass re-projection (L178-L243)",
            "reconstructed_in_script: Three-stage single-domain 512^2 quench with per-tier eps from lambda_c inversion at 12.5 nm/px, eroded parent-pore chambers with frozen walls, per-tier counts, nested multiplicities, nearest-neighbour pitches and equivalent diameters (L587-L724)",
            "reported_in_source: Furukawa (1992): a quench front moving at speed v through a binary mixture produces lamellae perpendicular to the front at slow speeds and parallel to the front at fast speeds, with an isotropic limit as v -> infinity",
            "reported_in_source: Lenoci & Camp (2008): a two-stage quenched Cahn-Hilliard model with solidified silica walls reproduces nested foramen/cribrum pore hierarchies; linear spinodal dispersion sigma(k) = M k^2 (1 - 3 phi0^2 - eps^2 k^2)",
            "reported_in_source: Schmid & Volcani (1983): C. wailesii valve morphogenesis proceeds centrifugally from the pattern centre with radial costae branching toward the margin",
            "reported_in_source: Sumper (2002): LCPA/silica liquid-liquid phase separation inside the SDV yields three self-similar hexagonal pore tiers (foramen d_1 = 1250 nm / a_1 = 1850 nm; cribrum d_2 = 220 / a_2 = 380 nm; cribrella d_3 = 42 / a_3 = 75 nm)",
            "transfer_boundary: Costae (phi0 = 0 rib layer) and areolae (phi0 = -0.30 droplet layer) are separate simulations; the model does not produce both in one domain",
            "transfer_boundary: Front speed, solidification lag (1.0 lambda_c), noise amplitude (0.005), front width (2.0) and R0 (8) were selected from ~24 exploratory runs to reach the radial regime; the stage durations (290, 160, 100 steps) and erosions (0, 3, 1 px) of the 3-stage model were tuned from 4 trial runs for nested-count visibility. None of these values is from the cited papers",
            "transfer_boundary: Frozen-silica conservation is global (leaked spectral flux spread uniformly over all mobile pixels), not local; the 3-stage cribrella sit at the grid floor (d_3 = 3.4 px target, 3.7 px measured), so their pitch/diameter are resolution-biased upward",
            "transfer_boundary: The costae model is validated against its own isotropic null and the sign of A, not against a specimen: the vendored SEM shows the valve face at three magnifications and no margin, so no empirical A or rib spacing exists in the package" ;
        pk:anatomicalStructure "Biomineralized shell whorl / spicule / test in Coscinodiscus wailesii" ;
        pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "8. Crystal Accretion & TPMS" ;
        pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "IV. Protista & Monera" ;
        pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Coiled Shells, Spicules & Gyroids" ;
        pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Raup (W,D,S) / Gyroid Mean H=0" ;
        pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Mineralized Protists (Silica/Calcite)" ;
        pk:biologicalGenus "Coscinodiscus" ;
        pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/0378-4371(92)90111-2>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1021/la7022784>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1063/1.1744102>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1111/j.0022-3646.1983.00387.x>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1070026>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1166/jnn.2006.174> ;
        pk:geologicalAgeMa 0e+00 ;
        pk:geologicalPeriod "Holocene (Extant)" ;
        pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-audit-v3-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-audit-v3-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-10>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-audit-v3-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-11>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-audit-v3-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-12>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-audit-v3-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-13>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-audit-v3-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-14>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-audit-v3-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-audit-v3-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-3>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-audit-v3-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-4>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-audit-v3-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-5>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-audit-v3-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-6>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-audit-v3-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-7>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-audit-v3-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-8>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-audit-v3-sumper-diatom-frustule-phase-sep-9> ;
        pk:hypothesisType "Fourth-Order Cahn-Hilliard Spinodal Phase Separation PDE & Hierarchical Hexagonal Packing" ;
        pk:phenomenonScaleTier "7_organism_cm" ;
        pk:phenomenonSizeLog10Meters -1.531e+00 ;
        pk:phenomenonSizeMeters 2.943e-02 ;
        pk:speciesTaxon <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/taxon/coscinodiscus-wailesii> ;
        pk:weightOfEvidence 8.9e-01 .

    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-tailbud-neuromesodermal-jamming> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Mongera et al. (2018) & Kim et al. (2021) zebrafish tailbud active fluid-to-solid jamming transition & yield-stress axis elongation (Danio rerio (zebrafish tailbud mesodermal progenitor zone MPZ & presomitic mesoderm PSM))" ;
        dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/tailbud-neuromesodermal-jamming-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/tailbud-neuromesodermal-jamming-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/tailbud-neuromesodermal-jamming-3>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/tailbud-neuromesodermal-jamming-4>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/tailbud-neuromesodermal-jamming-5> ;
        schema:about "Danio rerio (zebrafish tailbud mesodermal progenitor zone MPZ & presomitic mesoderm PSM)" ;
        schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Does not model 3D notochord vacuolation turgor mechanics, anterior somite epithelialization clefting, an FGF8/Wnt morphogen determination front, Delta-Notch phase coupling, or a full axisymmetric/3D Stokes-Bingham solve with fibronectin traction boundary conditions.",
            "reconstructed_in_script: (Pass 3) Her1/Her7 clock phase advection in the tip frame with a mechanical arrest gate sigma_y/sigma_A >= 4 (x_arrest = 161.1 um > x_jam = 81.0 um), Cooke-Zeeman somite length S = (v_elong + 0.45) * 23.5 min = 46.2 um, frozen her1 stripe wavelength 46.2 um measured on the kymograph, per-regime arrest fronts (cdh2 and ablation: none), and somite-border fibronectin feedback into the sheath profile.",
            "reconstructed_in_script: (Pass 3) Quasi-3D fibronectin sheath: f_FN(x) profile, hoop equilibrium eps_r = max(0, sigma_A - sigma_y)/(K_FN f_FN + K_t), equilibrium radius R_eq(x), influx-weighted channeling chi (0.951 WT, 0.907 itga5 MO, 0.736 fn1a;fn1b MO) multiplying the elongation speed, tailbud width ratio (1.04 / 1.08 / 1.24), 12-point fn_scale sweep (monotonic), and a diagnostic wall-friction force F_drag.",
            "reconstructed_in_script: Continuous posterior-to-anterior active-foam & Bingham viscoplastic solver across x in [0, 300] um (`solve_ap_jamming_profile`, r_sigma_y = 0.9989, r_kT1 = 0.9922, jamming crossover x* = 81.0 um) and 2D U-shaped tailbud cellular flow simulator across 5 experimental regimes (WT Control, cdh2 Morphant, Blebbistatin, SU5402, Zero-Backstop Ablation; v_elong r = 0.9748, L-R asymmetry r = 0.9851).",
            "reconstructed_in_script: Nuclear-seeded Voronoi tessellation and regional interstitial space segmentation of the Danio rerio posterior tailbud lightsheet micrograph (`zebrafish_tailbud_psm_specimen.jpg`, IDR0051, N = 391 nuclei, <z> = 5.88, AP compaction r = 0.9915).",
            "reported_in_source: Dray et al. (2013) Current Biology 23:1335-1341 Figs. 1-4: a fibronectin matrix wraps the tailbud and PSM; fn1a;fn1b double morphants and itga5 morphants lose this boundary, elongate the trunk more slowly and show altered posterior tissue shape and mechanics (the script vendors these as APPROXIMATE ratios, v/v_WT ~0.70 / ~0.82, width ~1.20 / ~1.08, +/-25%).",
            "reported_in_source: Herrgen et al. (2010) / Soroldoni et al. (2014): the zebrafish her1/her7 clock period is ~23.5 min at 28 C and clock waves slow and compress toward the anterior PSM before arresting into somite stripes (Cooke-Zeeman S = v_front T).",
            "reported_in_source: Kim et al. (2021) Nature Physics 17:859-866 & Mongera et al. (2018) Fig. 4: active tension fluctuations fluidize the MPZ (sigma_A > sigma_y) via frequent T1 neighbor exchanges, whereas the jammed solid A-PSM (sigma_y >> sigma_A) serves as an internal mechanical backstop that rectifies MPZ progenitor addition into unidirectional posterior elongation and preserves left-right symmetry; N-cadherin (cdh2) knockdown expands phi_ECS > 14%, unjamming the PSM, slowing elongation, and inducing bilateral body-axis asymmetry.",
            "reported_in_source: Mongera et al. (2018) Nature 561:401-405 Figs. 1-4: along the posterior-to-anterior axis of the zebrafish tailbud, extracellular space fraction phi_ECS(x) decreases from ~14.5% in the posterior Mesodermal Progenitor Zone (MPZ) to ~4.9% in the Anterior Presomitic Mesoderm (A-PSM), driving cell packing phi_pack = 1 - phi_ECS across the rigidity-percolation threshold phi_c approx 0.860 and elevating ferrofluid-measured yield stress sigma_y(x) from ~11 Pa to ~118 Pa while active Myosin-II tension fluctuations sigma_A(x) decline from ~50 Pa to ~13 Pa.",
            "transfer_boundary: 2D dorsal-ventral optical-plane projection of the 3D U-shaped zebrafish posterior tailbud and paraxial presomitic mesoderm; the fibronectin sheath is a thin-rod axisymmetric reduction (one radius per AP position), not a 3D boundary mesh.",
            "transfer_boundary: The clock is a phase oscillator with a prescribed frequency profile and a mechanical arrest gate (Lambda_arrest = 4, a modelling choice standing in for the FGF/Wnt determination front and Yap mechanosensitivity), not the Lewis (2003) her1/her7 delay-differential oscillator; v_PSM-shortening = 0.45 um/min and the ~47 um somite length are approximate anchors.",
            "transfer_boundary: The sheath channeling argument (influx stored in radial dilation is lost to elongation) is a transient-window argument, not a steady-state Stokes balance; K_FN and K_t are calibrated to the approximate Dray et al. (2013) ratios; the dynamic ECM friction F_drag does not feed back on v_elong." ;
        pk:anatomicalStructure "Segmentation clock somite / metamere unit in Danio rerio" ;
        pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "3. Phase/Delay Oscillators" ;
        pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "I. Enaima (Vertebrata)" ;
        pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Periodic Somites & Segments" ;
        pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Somite Length S = u·T_clock" ;
        pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Pisces (Ichthyes)" ;
        pk:biologicalGenus "Danio" ;
        pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0960-9822(03)00534-7>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2017.08.043>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cub.2010.06.034>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cub.2013.05.052>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/nmeth.4101>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41567-021-01215-1>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-018-0479-2>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1253089>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.090381> ;
        pk:externalAtlasDataset <https://daniocell.nichd.nih.gov/>,
            <https://mapzebrain.org/>,
            <https://zebrahub.ds.czbiohub.org/>,
            <https://zfin.org/> ;
        pk:fossilLineageGroup "Danionin Pigment Evolution Series" ;
        pk:geologicalAgeMa 0e+00 ;
        pk:geologicalPeriod "Holocene (Extant)" ;
