    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Wolfram (1984) Rule 30 & Meinhardt–Klingler (1987) Conus textile Pigmentation (Conus textile Linnaeus, 1758 (textile cone snail))" ;
        dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-3>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-4>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-5> ;
        schema:about "Conus textile Linnaeus, 1758 (textile cone snail)" ;
        schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Infinite-horizon proof of the open 2019 Wolfram Rule 30 Prize Problems #1-#3 (verifies finite-horizon statistics through t = 1024 and exact diagonal periods through k = 414)",
            "reconstructed_in_script: Exact Boolean and GF(2) ANF Rule 30 evolution, 1024-step single-seed light-cone, Jen (1990) left-bijective reconstruction and k=0..414 diagonal period-doubling cascade (k = 0, 3, 8, 29, 400), directional Boolean damage-cone ensemble, Meinhardt-Klingler PDE kymograph and lesion scar simulation, and 3D Raup Conus shell projection validated against segmented OSU Conus textile photography",
            "reported_in_source: Jen (1990) proves left-bijective spatial invertibility a_{t,i-1} = a_{t+1,i} XOR (a_{t,i} OR a_{t,i+1}) and the left-cone diagonal period-doubling cascade d_k(t+1) = d_{k-2}(t) XOR (d_{k-1}(t) OR d_k(t)) gated by all-zero synchronizing barriers d_{k-1} = 0",
            "reported_in_source: Meinhardt & Klingler (1987) formulate a 1D mantle-edge activator-substrate-hormone reaction-diffusion PDE generating self-extinguishing pigment triangles and V-shaped lesion recovery wakes",
            "reported_in_source: Wolfram (1983, 1984, 2002) introduces elementary cellular automaton Rule 30 (a_{t+1,i} = a_{t,i-1} XOR (a_{t,i} OR a_{t,i+1})) as a discrete generative model of Conus textile tent pigmentation and poses the 2019 Rule 30 Prize Problems on the center column a_{t,0} (OEIS A051023)",
            "transfer_boundary: Cross-model 1D space-time defect-front kymograph comparison linking Rule 30 / Meinhardt mantle wakes to Zhang-Goldstein-Levin (2025) frozen-defect cell sorting and Cervera-Levin-Mafe (2021) bioelectric domain-wall propagation" ;
        pk:anatomicalStructure "Biomineralized shell whorl / spicule / test in Conus textile" ;
        pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "8. Crystal Accretion & TPMS" ;
        pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "II. Anaima (Invertebrata)" ;
        pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Cellular Automaton Triangles" ;
        pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Defect Annihilation Slope" ;
        pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Ostrakoderma (Mollusca & Echinodermata)" ;
        pk:biologicalGenus "Conus" ;
        pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/0167-2789(90)90169-P>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0022-5193(87)80101-7>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/311419a0>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1103/RevModPhys.55.601> ;
        pk:geologicalAgeMa 0e+00 ;
        pk:geologicalPeriod "Holocene (Extant)" ;
        pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-18-conus-audit-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-18-conus-audit-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-18-conus-audit-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-3>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-18-conus-audit-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-4>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-18-conus-audit-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-5>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-18-conus-audit-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-6>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-18-conus-audit-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-7> ;
        pk:hypothesisType "Elementary Cellular Automata (GF(2)), Neurosecretory Mantle Threshold Automaton & Reaction-Diffusion PDE" ;
        pk:phenomenonScaleTier "7_organism_cm" ;
        pk:phenomenonSizeLog10Meters -1.385e+00 ;
        pk:phenomenonSizeMeters 4.125e-02 ;
        pk:speciesTaxon <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/taxon/conus-textile> ;
        pk:weightOfEvidence 8.73e-01 .

    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-wolpert-french-flag-morphogen> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Wolpert (1969) French Flag positional information, Tickle-Wolpert (1975) chick limb ZPA digit duplication, Ben-Zvi-Barkai (2010) scaling & 2D AER-FGF / ZPA-Shh limb bud paddle (Chick embryo (Gallus gallus domesticus) wing bud & embryonic blastoderm)" ;
        dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/wolpert-french-flag-morphogen-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/wolpert-french-flag-morphogen-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/wolpert-french-flag-morphogen-3>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/wolpert-french-flag-morphogen-4>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/wolpert-french-flag-morphogen-5>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/wolpert-french-flag-morphogen-6>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/wolpert-french-flag-morphogen-7>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/wolpert-french-flag-morphogen-8> ;
        schema:about "Chick embryo (Gallus gallus domesticus) wing bud & embryonic blastoderm" ;
        schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Digit condensation or Turing-type periodicity, temporal integration of Shh exposure (Harfe 2004), a dorsoventral axis or 3D geometry, measured growth curves of the chick wing bud, quantitative Fgf4 / Shh expression levels, or a mechanistic derivation of AER and ZPA position",
            "reconstructed_in_script: 1D linear source-sink and SDD solvers (analytic + explicit PDE, RMSE 7.6e-6), 6-stage growth-scaling sweep with expansion-repression, 5-regime 1D ZPA suite (wild type, full / attenuated / weak anterior graft, ablation) read by a morphogen-valley digit rule, 400-trial Monte Carlo positional-error test, radial segmentation of the vendored 72 h embryo photograph",
            "reconstructed_in_script: Pass 3: explicit 2D finite-difference solver for FGF and Shh on a growing paddle mask (dx = 12.5 um) with zero-flux boundaries, Michaelis-form Shh<->FGF feedback, AER-driven distal apposition growth, graft dose series, AER excision at five stages, ZPA ablation, a rectangle verification against the 1D cosh steady state, 8 new reference-anchored measurements and 7 new Lean 4 theorems",
            "reported_in_source: Ben-Zvi & Barkai (2010): an expander produced where morphogen is low scales the decay length with domain size",
            "reported_in_source: Laufer et al. (1994) and Niswander et al. (1994): Shh in the ZPA and Fgf4 in the posterior AER maintain each other (Shh lost after AER removal, rescued by FGF4 bead; ectopic anterior Fgf4 after a ZPA graft); Crossley et al. (1996): Fgf8 is expressed along the whole ridge",
            "reported_in_source: Saunders (1948) and Summerbell (1974): AER removal arrests outgrowth and truncates the limb at a level that is progressively more distal the later the excision; Summerbell, Lewis & Wolpert (1973): proximo-distal values are laid down by time spent in the distal progress zone",
            "reported_in_source: Tickle, Summerbell & Wolpert (1975) and Tickle (1981): a posterior ZPA specifies wing digits 2-3-4; an anterior graft gives the mirror duplication 4-3-2-2-3-4, and the digit specified next to a weaker graft advances 2 -> 3 -> 4 with polarizing-cell number; Riddle et al. (1993): Shh mediates ZPA activity",
            "reported_in_source: Wolpert (1969): positional information read from a monotone morphogen gradient against thresholds gives size-invariant French-Flag proportions under linear source-sink diffusion; Crick (1970): synthesis-diffusion-degradation gives lambda = sqrt(D/k) and the positional-error law sigma_x = sigma_c / |dc/dx|",
            "transfer_boundary: Digit identity is read from the instantaneous distal Shh concentration against the Pass 2 thresholds normalised to the wild-type peak; the proximo-distal segment is read from the truncation fraction of the wild-type length via a 1/3-2/3 trisection, and the Saunders / Summerbell comparison is to an ordinal stage -> segment summary (+/- 1 stage between studies), not to digitised truncation data",
            "transfer_boundary: The 2D model is a reduced phenomenological coupling: the production rates s_F, s_S, feedback gain g_S and half-saturations K_S, K_FS, K_g are tuned so that wild-type FGF ~ 1 and L_final ~ 660 um, not taken from any paper; the developmental clock is compressed (12 h of model time spans HH18 -> HH28, ~5x faster than in ovo) while keeping tau_relax << tau_growth",
            "transfer_boundary: The paddle geometry is prescribed (fixed AP width 500 um, elliptical 150 um cap); the AER is the distal-facing rim row and the ZPA is the posterior-margin mesenchyme within 120 um of the rim by construction, so their positions are inputs, not emergent; new lattice rows appear with zero concentration (no proliferation field)",
            "transfer_boundary: The specimen is a whole-egg 72 h embryo photograph whose radial area-vasculosa profile is used as a proxy gradient; no limb bud image or Shh / Fgf in situ is compared with the 2D output" ;
        pk:anatomicalStructure "Morphogen gradient & pre-cartilage condensation zone in Gallus gallus" ;
        pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "2. Morphogen + Condensations" ;
        pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "I. Enaima (Vertebrata)" ;
        pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Skeletal Rays & Joints" ;
        pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "French-Flag / PSHM Thresholds" ;
        pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Aves (Ornithes)" ;
        pk:biologicalGenus "Gallus" ;
        pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1002/jez.1401080304>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/0092-8674(93)90626-2>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/0092-8674(94)90030-2>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0022-5193(69)80016-0>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0092-8674(00)80999-X>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/225420a0>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/244492a0>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/254199a0>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/289295a0>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/371609a0>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0912734107> ;
        pk:geologicalAgeMa 0e+00 ;
        pk:geologicalPeriod "Holocene (Extant)" ;
        pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-french-flag-morphogen-audit-v3-wolpert-french-flag-morphogen-1>,
