    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling-code-traceability> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Campas et al. (2010) PNAS affine scaling-and-shear transformation + Abzhanov et al. (2004, 2006) Bmp4/Calmodulin beak morphogenesis + Soons et al. (2010-2015) reduced FEM fracture risk — Code-to-model traceability: 88/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Credited: the module header maps each law to Campas/Abzhanov/Fritz/Soons and to the Lean 4 module `MathOfBiology.Loop_070` (L1-L64); Section 4b opens with a design banner (L584-L605) and every FEM function carries a docstring naming the source (Gibson-Ashby L637, Soons load cases L987, Herrel/Campas bite forces L1075, Soons 2012 ablation L1178); the math-KG YAML registers equations 4-5 with single-range `code_locus` values pointing at the current lines. Deductions: uncited geometry constants — lower-mandible factors (L198), 3D half-width exponent (L213), base dimensions 11.4/7.6/6.8 mm and Gaussian field centres/widths (L397-L405) (-4); the structural-peak exclusion zones, tip plate depth and contact-patch width are coded as defaults without a citation (L666-L719, L785-L861) (-3); `mean_tapered_beam_tip_over_base_ratio` and `section_fem_over_beam_*` (L1120-L1124) are computed but surfaced only in a note (-2); the comparison figure's bite-force axis still cites 'Herrel et al.' without a year/venue (L1740) (-1); `--verify-only` duplicates `--self-test` (L2178) (-2)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "2021-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling.py L198–L213: Lower-mandible factors (-0.34, 0.88, 0.90) and 3D half-width 0.48 x^0.82 are model inventions without a source <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8a7928d7/2021-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling.py#L198-L213>",
            "2021-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling.py L397–L405: Bmp4/CaM Gaussian field centres/widths and base dimensions 11.4/7.6/6.8 mm are uncited <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8a7928d7/2021-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling.py#L397-L405>" ;
        ns1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling-code-traceability-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling-code-traceability-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling-code-traceability-3> ;
        ns1:hasScore 8.8e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling-model-fidelity> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Campas et al. (2010) PNAS affine scaling-and-shear transformation + Abzhanov et al. (2004, 2006) Bmp4/Calmodulin beak morphogenesis + Soons et al. (2010-2015) reduced FEM fracture risk — Model fidelity to source: 90/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Credited: exact upper-triangular affine group and analytic inverse (L154-L172), Bmp4/CaM field and RCAS suite (L377-L461), and the new reduced FEM — a correct vectorised Q4 plane-stress formulation (2x2 Gauss, symmetric positive-definite D, exact linearity 2F -> 2 sigma) verified against Euler-Bernoulli and Timoshenko (L744-L782, L785-L861, L935-L971), Gibson-Ashby E_trab = E_s (BV/TV)^2 (L636-L641), a two-material shell/core map (L722-L735), three Soons-type load cases (L974-L1064) and 5 machine-checked Lean theorems. Deductions: the 14-species 'empirical' profiles are the forward transform plus Gaussian noise (L266-L272), so the headline collapse and negative control are circular (-5); the remediation item asked for a micro-CT 3D fracture solver and received a 2D sagittal plane-stress section with uniform out-of-plane thickness W_mm (L763-L782), no crack model, and an artificial 0.7 mm solid-keratin tip clamp (L684) that dominates the tip-biting peaks (-3); the `bmp4_index` used for the r_Bmp4 = 0.9997 correlation is linear in `s_D` by construction (L349-L351) (-1); lower-mandible (-0.34, 0.88, 0.90; L198) and 3D half-width (0.48 x^0.82; L213) factors are uncited model inventions (-1)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "2021-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling.py L266–L272: 14-species 'empirical' profiles are forward_transform_beak_surface() output plus rng.normal(0, 0.0024 s_D) — the collapse tests the inverse of the same transform <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8a7928d7/2021-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling.py#L266-L272>",
            "2021-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling.py L680–L684: Tip clamped to tip_solid_depth_mm (0.7 mm solid keratin) because the x^1.85 culmen is ~1 % of basal depth at x = 0.1 L; this plate dominates the 10.8x tip/base ratio <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8a7928d7/2021-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling.py#L680-L684>" ;
        ns1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling-model-fidelity-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling-model-fidelity-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling-model-fidelity-3>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling-model-fidelity-4>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling-model-fidelity-5>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling-model-fidelity-6> ;
        ns1:hasScore 9e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling-morphometric-validation> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Campas et al. (2010) PNAS affine scaling-and-shear transformation + Abzhanov et al. (2004, 2006) Bmp4/Calmodulin beak morphogenesis + Soons et al. (2010-2015) reduced FEM fracture risk — Morphometric validation: 84/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Credited: 19 measurements, each with `reference_value`, `unit`, `method` and `reference_source` (L1845-L2061); the 10 Pass 3 measurements include two analytic FEM verifications (0.9925, 0.9905), a mesh convergence (0.0045), a 14-species tapered-beam slope (0.971, r = 0.9986), the Soons-2010 homeostasis ratio 0.432, the tip/base ratio 10.8, the oblique ratio 0.899, keratin shielding -0.036, BV/TV ablation 4.235 and a bone fracture-risk index 0.017; notes honestly state where the model disagrees with the recalled Soons claim. Deductions: the headline collapse metrics validate synthetic data (L266-L272) (-5); the RCAS reference value is computed from `D_over_L_obs` that are Law-2 formula outputs, not Abzhanov measurements (L1915-L1917) (-3); the negative-control reference 0.092 (L1905) and Certhidea shear RMS reference 0.012 (L1955) are the script's own output rounded, and r_DL reference 0.98 (L1945) is unsourced (-3); none of the FEM stresses or risk indices are compared with a measured or digitised stress value (every Pass 3 anchor is analytic, a null, or 'transcribed offline') (-3); the tip/base reference 3.07 is a naive lever estimate that disagrees with the value by design (L2014-L2019) (-1); convergence is checked for one species/case only (L1215-L1227) (-1)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "2021-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling.py L1905–L1905: Negative-control reference_value 0.092 is the script's own output (0.0937) rounded <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8a7928d7/2021-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling.py#L1905-L1905>",
            "2021-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling.py L1915–L1917: RCAS reference_value = bmp.D_over_L_obs / nog.D_over_L_obs, where the 'obs' values are Law-2 formula outputs (ratio 3.8687 vs 'obs' 3.8745) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8a7928d7/2021-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling.py#L1915-L1917>",
            "2021-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling.py L1945–L1955: r_DL reference 0.98 unsourced ('Gould 1845 & Campas Fig. 1'); Certhidea shear RMS reference 0.012 equals the script's 0.0120 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8a7928d7/2021-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling.py#L1945-L1955>" ;
        ns1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling-measurement-14-species-cantilever-bending-stiffness-i-beam-w-d-3-12-l-vs-bite-force-correlation>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling-measurement-14-species-universal-affine-scaling-and-shear-collapse-correlation-campas-et-al-2010>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-alberti-avian-beak-darwin-scaling-measurement-14-species-universal-affine-scaling-and-shear-collapse-rms-residual-campas-et-al-2010-fig-3>,
