        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "The 3D geometry is now imported from the SHA-256-locked specimen itself: `reconstruct_opt_visual_hull` (L759-800) reads the AP and DV half-width profiles of the Fig. 2F dorsal and posterior St0/St1 silhouettes (scale anchored by L_PD(St0) = 1020 um; the two views give independent St1 PD lengths 1391 vs 1386 um) and every FEM scenario is scored by dorsal-silhouette IoU against the specimen St1 hull (`silhouette_iou_vs_specimen`, L1224-1252): flank influx 0.847 > WT active stress 0.770 > Model I 0.683 > St0 baseline 0.625; Panel F overlays FEM WT and the specimen hull, Panel P all four. Scored down from 93 because the hull is a two-view elliptical approximation rather than the OPT iso-surface, and because the specimen disagrees with the reference table on St1/St0 PD (1.364 vs 1.422) and on DV thickness (926 vs 580 um) — a discrepancy the script measures and reports but cannot resolve." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-specimen-match> ;
