        rdfs:label "Brodland (2002) / Krieg et al. (2008) / Maître et al. (2012) Differential Interfacial Tension Hypothesis (DITH) and zebrafish germ-layer cortical tension sorting, with time-dependent Nodal/TGF-beta coupling (Pass 3) — Model fidelity to source: 92/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Brodland (2002) Eq. (1) is implemented exactly in `compute_dith_tensions` (L136-L184) and now also in continuous per-cell form in the Nodal-coupled sorter: `_cell_pair_J` (L840-L847) rebuilds the bond matrix every MCS from gamma_i0 = beta_i and gamma_ij = kappa|beta_i - beta_j|, which is Brodland's law with omega_ij = beta_i + beta_j - gamma_ij, and Lean theorem 5 proves the closure always satisfies the Krieg regime-I inequality 0 < gamma_ij < |gamma_i0 - gamma_j0|. The Nodal coupling (L232-L334) is a recognisable reduced morphogen model: exponential range, first-order temporal rise from sphere stage, two-threshold Hill dose response mirroring Krieg's own lefty1 / cyclops / cyclops+casanova induction, first-order cortex relaxation; Lean theorems 4 and 6 prove monotonicity/bounds of the dose map and non-overshoot of the relaxation step. Deductions: the static regimes (L496-L508) use j_hom = 4.0 for both E-E and M-M contacts, discarding the gamma_EE = 70 / gamma_MM = 150 that `compute_dith_tensions` returns, so the static lattice energy is a Steinberg-type J matrix and not Brodland's full DITH energy (-4); the Nodal field is 1D and exposure is frozen to the tier of origin (L826, L893), with no Lefty feedback or epiboly (-3); kappa = 2/3 is a phenomenological closure tuned to gamma_EM = 30 (-1)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "2002-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting.py L496–L508: Static regimes: j_hom = 4.0 shared by E-E and M-M bonds; gamma_EE / gamma_MM from compute_dith_tensions are not used in the energy <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8beed34/2002-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting.py#L496-L508>" ;
        ns1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-model-fidelity-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-model-fidelity-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-model-fidelity-3>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-model-fidelity-4> ;
        ns1:hasScore 9.2e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-morphometric-validation> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Brodland (2002) / Krieg et al. (2008) / Maître et al. (2012) Differential Interfacial Tension Hypothesis (DITH) and zebrafish germ-layer cortical tension sorting, with time-dependent Nodal/TGF-beta coupling (Pass 3) — Morphometric validation: 88/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "`measure_morphoeval()` (L1595-L1702) returns 13 measurements with non-null references: the 8 v2 ones (gamma_EM = 30, beta_M - beta_E = 45, wild-type Delta_r = +0.3807 vs 0.34, caMLCK Delta_r = -0.3282 vs -0.34, Blebbistatin 0, 3-layer gap 0.4237 vs 0.42, Young-Dupré 0.866, profile r = 0.9301 vs 0.92) and 5 new Nodal ones: shield mesendoderm tiers 5 (ref 5), shield endoderm tiers 2 (ref 2), hierarchy established 4.87 hpf (ref <= 6.0), Nodal-coupled Delta_r = +0.3504 (ref 0.34), Nodal-null |Delta_r| = 0 (ref 0). The hard-coded \"p=0.0001\" strings of v2 are gone (L1625 now states single-seed / no replicate statistics; L1660 reports the computed Pearson p). Deductions: the two tier-count references and the 0.34 / 0.42 radial anchors are recalled approximate literature values, not digitised from a figure or table, and the hierarchy reference is only an upper bound (-7); all sorting metrics come from one seed with no replicate spread (-3); the Nodal tier counts are partly tautological because lambda and K_M were chosen to hit them (-2)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "2002-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting.py L1666–L1680: Tier-count references (5, 2) are recalled approximate values; method strings say so <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8beed34/2002-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting.py#L1666-L1680>" ;
        ns1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-measurement-blebbistatin-control-radial-separation>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-measurement-camlc-cortex-reversal-radial-separation>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-measurement-dith-wildtype-gamma-em>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-measurement-krieg-2008-spreading-tension-diff>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-measurement-maitre-2012-young-dupre-contact-radius-half-tension>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-measurement-nodal-cortical-tension-hierarchy-established-hpf>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-measurement-nodal-coupled-internalization-radial-sep-7hpf>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-measurement-nodal-endoderm-tier-count-at-shield-6hpf>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-measurement-nodal-mesendoderm-tier-count-at-shield-6hpf>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-measurement-nodal-null-mzoep-radial-sep>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-measurement-specimen-vs-dith-radial-profile-pearson-r>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-measurement-three-germ-layer-ectoderm-endoderm-radial-gap>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-measurement-wildtype-radial-core-shell-separation>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-morphometric-validation-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-brodland-differential-interfacial-tension-sorting-morphometric-validation-2> ;
