    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-caleo-cajal-dendritic-wiring-code-traceability> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Cuntz et al. (2010) PLoS Comput. Biol. & Cuntz et al. (2007) PNAS Ramón y Cajal minimum-wiring and conduction-delay greedy Steiner dendritic trees + Rall's 3/2 diameter power law + (Pass 3) Rall passive-cable electrotonics coupled to a Morris-Lecar dendritic Ca2+ spike hotspot — Code-to-model traceability: 95/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "The module docstring (L1-73) maps every governing equation — greedy cost, 2D/3D scaling, Rall 3/2, lambda_DC and the Koch AC reduction, the Morris-Lecar ODEs — to its paper and to the five Lean 4 theorems by name, and each Pass 3 function carries a docstring naming the equation it implements and the ablation it exposes (L352-368, L425-461). The math-KG YAML registers equations 1-5 with single-range `code_locus` pins re-pointed to the shifted lines, and every measurement `source` names the theorem it leans on. Deductions: the JSON `linear_superposition_note` (L62) attributes exact superposition to \"Lean 4 Theorem 5\" whereas the script and the Lean file number it Theorem 4 (`rall_passive_membrane_linear_superposition`) and Theorem 5 is the length-constant bound (-2); the docstring Lean line pins for Theorems 1-3 (L36-67, L85-113, L127-147) are approximate against the 216-line module (theorem heads at L38, L90, L136) and Theorems 4-5 carry no line pin (-2); `evaluate_cuntz_pareto_sweep` cites no figure for the benchmark arrays it compares against (-1)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "datasets/cajal_dendritic_wiring/electrotonic_ca_spike_reference.json L62–L62: linear_superposition_note cites 'Lean 4 Theorem 5' for the superposition result that the script and Lean module number Theorem 4 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/datasets/cajal_dendritic_wiring/electrotonic_ca_spike_reference.json#L62-L62>" ;
        ns1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-caleo-cajal-dendritic-wiring-code-traceability-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-caleo-cajal-dendritic-wiring-code-traceability-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-caleo-cajal-dendritic-wiring-code-traceability-3> ;
        ns1:hasScore 9.5e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-caleo-cajal-dendritic-wiring-model-fidelity> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Cuntz et al. (2010) PLoS Comput. Biol. & Cuntz et al. (2007) PNAS Ramón y Cajal minimum-wiring and conduction-delay greedy Steiner dendritic trees + Rall's 3/2 diameter power law + (Pass 3) Rall passive-cable electrotonics coupled to a Morris-Lecar dendritic Ca2+ spike hotspot — Model fidelity to source: 94/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "The Cuntz (2007, 2010) greedy MST solver with bottom-up Rall (1959) 3/2 diameter accumulation (`grow_cuntz_dendritic_tree`, L165-281), the random spanning-tree ablation (L282-313), the 8-point bf Pareto sweep (L716-769) and the 2D/3D Wen-Chklovskii scaling regressions (L770-828) are unchanged from v2 and remain faithful. Pass 3 adds a genuinely coupled passive/active model: the Rall DC length constant and Koch (1999) Eq. 2.37 AC reduction (`rall_length_constant_um`, L352-368) are the textbook formulas, every edge receives X_e = l_e / lambda_f(d_e) from the Rall diameters (`compute_tree_electrotonics`, L371-388), and the Morris-Lecar equations (L425-461) are correctly transcribed with the two ablation switches that isolate the regenerative g_Ca term. Deductions: the hotspot is a single isopotential compartment with the canonical barnacle Hopf parameter set (C = 20 uF/cm2, V1-V4, phi) rather than Purkinje P-type Ca2+ kinetics, so the 4.28x gain and the 5.24 ms window are properties of a generic excitable membrane placed at the LCA, not of a Purkinje dendrite (-3); attenuation uses the semi-infinite exp(-X) factor (L483-484), which is only exact for Rall-matched cylinders seen from the soma, whereas here it is applied centripetally from tips toward a branch node (-2); the scaling-law sweep runs at bf = 0.15 (L791, L801) while every other panel uses the Purkinje regime bf = 0.20 (-1). Five Lean 4 theorems (0 sorrys) back the greedy cost trade-off, the 3/2 law, tree topology, exact passive superposition and lambda_f <= lambda_DC." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "2007-caleo-cajal-dendritic-wiring.py L425–L461: Vectorised forward-Euler Morris-Lecar Ca2+/K+ hotspot with g_ca_scale = 0 and freeze_w ablations; parameters are the canonical barnacle Hopf set, not a Purkinje P-type fit <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/2007-caleo-cajal-dendritic-wiring.py#L425-L461>" ;
