        ns1:evidenceAgainst "datasets/nacre_screw_dislocation_spirals/cholesteric_fracture_reference.json L1–L82: Pass 3 reference table with provenance_note 'transcribed offline ... must be re-verified' (L4) and empirical_targets flagged approx (L68-L79) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/datasets/nacre_screw_dislocation_spirals/cholesteric_fracture_reference.json#L1-L82>" ;
        ns1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-cartwright-nacre-screw-dislocation-spirals-source-traceability-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-cartwright-nacre-screw-dislocation-spirals-source-traceability-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-cartwright-nacre-screw-dislocation-spirals-source-traceability-3> ;
        ns1:hasScore 8.8e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-cartwright-nacre-screw-dislocation-spirals-specimen-match> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Cartwright & Checa (2007), Cartwright et al. (2009) & BCF (1951) nacre screw-dislocation spirals, Frank-Read target loops, chitin pore mineral-bridge columnar vs sheet transition, 3D cholesteric chitin precursor coupling and brick-and-mortar tablet-sliding fracture — Morphological realism / specimen match: 86/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "The SHA-256-pinned public-domain SEM mother-of-pearl specimen is still segmented by DoG seam detection and Delaunay coordination (h_0 = 0.5000 um at 0.019867 um/px, 328 seams, CV 0.29; Z = 6.01; aspect 3.24) and shown in panels E-F of the comparison figure; Pass 3 adds an x-z section through the screw core with white membranes and yellow mineral fill, a director-twist panel and a brick-and-mortar RVE GIF whose geometry (L_ov = 7.8 um, h = 0.5 um, Phi = 0.95) is taken from the SEM-anchored h_0 (+3 for the new visual comparison surface). Deductions: the reference values the SEM Z and aspect ratio are compared against (5.96 and 3.2436) are the script's own Pass 2 outputs copied into the measurement block — SEM Z has since drifted to 6.01 under the current scipy and still 'passes' a 5.5-6.4 band — so two of the three specimen metrics are self-referential (-6); the Pass 3 'membrane period vs SEM h_0' measurement uses the script's own segmentation as its reference and is flagged as such but remains intra-script (-2); the fracture RVE is compared with Jackson's numbers for Pinctada, not with any morphometric read from the Haliotis specimen (tablet waviness, overlap length, mortar thickness are literature assumptions), so the mechanical panels are not specimen-matched (-4); no Cartwright et al. (2009) spiral / target micrograph is vendored for the morphospace panels, as in v2 (-2)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-specimen-match> ;
