    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-economou-palate-ruguga-turing-model-fidelity> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Economou et al. (2012) FGF10/FGF7-SHH activator-inhibitor Turing stripe mechanism at mammalian palatal growth zones, coupled to quasi-static epithelial plate ridge elevation — Model fidelity to source: 88/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Credited: exact FGF-SHH Jacobian, dispersion curve and equal-diffusion control (L183-237); 9-stage intercalation (L240-291); 2D growing-shelf RD with incision barriers (L516-737); and the new Law 4 plate coupling that is mathematically correct and exactly solved (transfer stiffness L391-402, DCT solver L405-429 certified against the FD operator L440-454, rectified thickening load L457-465, in-loop feedback L645-647 and L684-688), with 5 Lean theorems (0 sorrys). Deductions: the coronal-cut, FGF10-bead and cyclopamine outcomes are seeded by condition-specific initial patterns (mediolateral cos modulation and q_gz at L606-615, q_high + bead halo at L616-627, q_cyc at L628-633) so those phenotypes are not emergent consequences of the barrier or rate change (-5); the x spacing is rescaled by dx_eff = dx (q / 1.24) (L338, L600, L619, L631), decoupling the integrated wavelength (3.37) from the dispersion lambda_c (3.22) and from the plate's physical dx (-3); the plate is a linear 2.5D reduction with assumed dimensionless constants and one-way coupling by default (chi_m = 0), not the 3D FEM invagination requested (-4)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "2012-economou-palate-ruguga-turing.py L598–L600: dx_eff = dx * (q_ap / 1.24) rescaling: grid wavelength 3.37 vs dispersion lambda_c 3.22 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2012-economou-palate-ruguga-turing.py#L598-L600>",
            "2012-economou-palate-ruguga-turing.py L606–L633: Condition-specific initial conditions encode the coronal / bead / cyclopamine outcomes rather than letting them emerge <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2012-economou-palate-ruguga-turing.py#L606-L633>" ;
        ns1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-economou-palate-ruguga-turing-model-fidelity-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-economou-palate-ruguga-turing-model-fidelity-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-economou-palate-ruguga-turing-model-fidelity-3> ;
        ns1:hasScore 8.8e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-economou-palate-ruguga-turing-morphometric-validation> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Economou et al. (2012) FGF10/FGF7-SHH activator-inhibitor Turing stripe mechanism at mammalian palatal growth zones, coupled to quasi-static epithelial plate ridge elevation — Morphometric validation: 92/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "`measure_morphoeval()` now returns 14 reference-anchored measurements (L1429-1590): the 9 Pass 2 metrics plus mechanical ridge count (9 vs 9), crest/Shh-stripe phase offset (0.0226 vs 0 lambda), crest duty cycle against a value measured on the vendored specimen with the same estimator (0.423 vs 0.493; right shelf 0.444), kappa-sweep Spearman rho (-1.00 vs -1) and chi_m-sweep count robustness (9.0 vs 9). Deductions: three Pass 2 reference values remain self-referential (coronal bifurcation 0.4695 at L1545 and specimen CV 0.1843 at L1585 are the script's own outputs; in-phase r = 0.96 at L1515 is an eyeballed figure value) (-5); ridge amplitude is dimensionless so no height comparison with histology exists (-3)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "2012-economou-palate-ruguga-turing.py L1545–L1585: Self-referential reference values 0.4695 and 0.1843 carried from Pass 2 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2012-economou-palate-ruguga-turing.py#L1545-L1585>" ;
        ns1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-economou-palate-ruguga-turing-measurement-2d-wild-type-palatal-shelf-transverse-rugae-count-8-1-7b>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-economou-palate-ruguga-turing-measurement-biological-specimen-left-palatal-shelf-transverse-rugae-count>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-economou-palate-ruguga-turing-measurement-biological-specimen-palatal-rugae-inter-stripe-spacing-cv-left-shelf>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-economou-palate-ruguga-turing-measurement-biological-specimen-right-palatal-shelf-transverse-rugae-count>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-economou-palate-ruguga-turing-measurement-coronal-surgical-cut-bifurcation-spot-index-vs-intact-wild-type>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-economou-palate-ruguga-turing-measurement-equal-diffusion-negative-control-rugae-count-d-a-d-h-0-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-economou-palate-ruguga-turing-measurement-fgf-shh-critical-turing-wavelength-lambda-c>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-economou-palate-ruguga-turing-measurement-in-phase-mesenchymal-fgf-vs-epithelial-shh-spatial-correlation-r-fgf-shh>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-economou-palate-ruguga-turing-measurement-mechanical-ridge-count-from-quasi-static-epithelial-plate-elevation-wt>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-economou-palate-ruguga-turing-measurement-ridge-amplitude-monotonic-attenuation-with-bending-stiffness-kappa-spearman-rho>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-economou-palate-ruguga-turing-measurement-ridge-crest-duty-cycle-fwhm-spacing-simulated-plate-ridges-vs-segmented-specimen-rugae>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-economou-palate-ruguga-turing-measurement-ridge-crest-to-shh-stripe-phase-offset-wt-fraction-of-ruga-wavelength>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-economou-palate-ruguga-turing-measurement-ruga-8-growth-zone-sequential-intercalation-correlation-8-1-7b-e12-0-e15-5>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-economou-palate-ruguga-turing-measurement-two-way-chemo-mechanical-feedback-robustness-wt-rugae-count-across-chi-mech-sweep>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-economou-palate-ruguga-turing-morphometric-validation-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-economou-palate-ruguga-turing-morphometric-validation-2> ;
