    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-economou-palate-ruguga-turing-overall> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Economou et al. (2012) FGF10/FGF7-SHH activator-inhibitor Turing stripe mechanism at mammalian palatal growth zones, coupled to quasi-static epithelial plate ridge elevation — MorphoEval overall 91.2/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 3 (v3) evaluation of `2012-economou-palate-ruguga-turing.py` (91.2 / 100, down 1.2 from 92.4 in Pass 2). The single v2 remediation item is closed in a reduced, explicitly labelled form: the FGF/SHH Turing sheet now drives a quasi-static Kirchhoff epithelial plate on a Winkler mesenchymal foundation (exact DCT-II solve, residual 5.8e-14), producing 9 elevated ridges whose crests sit on the Shh stripes (phase offset 0.023 wavelength), whose duty cycle (0.423) is narrower than a sinusoid and comparable to the segmented specimen rugae (0.493 / 0.444), whose amplitude falls monotonically with bending and foundation stiffness (Spearman -1.00) while the ridge count stays locked to the Turing count, and which vanishes in the equal-diffusion control. Two machine-checked Lean 4 theorems formalise the transfer-stiffness bound and monotonicity and the sign preservation. The remediation also exposed two older defects that this audit now penalises: perturbation phenotypes seeded through initial conditions, and a grid-vs-dispersion wavelength mismatch caused by the dx_eff rescaling; together with the uncalibrated plate constants, the one-way default coupling and self-referential reference values they form the Pass 4 list. Overall 91.2/100 (faithfulness 90.6, reproducibility 92.6); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit d58a084; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 88, Morphological realism / specimen match 92, Parameter expressivity 90, Morphometric validation 92, Source and data traceability 93, Code-to-model traceability 93, Reproducibility package 92. Output judged: docs/media/palate_ruguga_turing_comparison.png: rendered output of 2012-economou-palate-ruguga-turing.py at d58a084, image/png, 898727 B, 2222×1464 px, artifact_sha256 716777da0d6ff0938c1e277351c739fbfbed969691b961cf0e467f02ef0dce32 (sha256 716777da0d6ff0938c1e277351c739fbfbed969691b961cf0e467f02ef0dce32), spec_fingerprint 14f358af9d03b3980dc4c8f810f623b9c4299743ce9b93b063da6d1923819d25. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 14f358af9d03b3980dc4c8f810f623b9c4299743ce9b93b063da6d1923819d25; artifact_sha256: 716777da0d6ff0938c1e277351c739fbfbed969691b961cf0e467f02ef0dce32; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/palate_ruguga_turing/palate_ridge_mechanics_reference.json=2e673658c9722aeb..., datasets/palate_ruguga_turing/palate_rugae_specimen.jpg=a38f6c053ffe9048..., datasets/palate_ruguga_turing/palate_ruguga_turing_reference.json=e76e670dd50c86fe..., datasets/palate_ruguga_turing/paper_citations.bib=fd020997fb3c2db0..., datasets/palate_ruguga_turing/scout_manifest.json=f0a345a5c9039e78...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-palate-ruguga-turing-audit-v2. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Economou et al. (2012): mesenchymal FGF10/FGF7 (activator) and epithelial SHH (inhibitor) form a Turing reaction-diffusion system at the rugae growth zone anterior to ruga 8; rugae are added sequentially 8 -> 1..7b as the palate elongates; a coronal explant cut across the growth zone yields bifurcations / spots whereas a sagittal cut preserves stripes; cyclopamine broadens and FGF10 beads / Spry2-/-;Spry4+/- compact the pattern; Shh expression marks each morphological ruga (Fig. 1) | Pantalacci et al. (2008), Welsh & O'Brien (2009): staging of sequential ruga addition in the RGZ anterior to ruga 8 | Turing (1952): diffusion-driven instability of a two-component activator-inhibitor system | Landau & Lifshitz (1986): equilibrium equation of a thin elastic plate and its bending stiffness; reconstructed_in_script: 2x2 Jacobian and dispersion relation with lambda_c = 3.2221; 1D and 2D RD solvers with growth-zone envelope; 9-stage L/lambda_c intercalation count; 6-condition perturbation suite; DoG segmentation of the specimen shelves (15 / 16 rugae); Pass 3: quasi-static Kirchhoff plate on a Winkler foundation driven by beta max(A, 0), solved exactly by DCT-II, optional chi_m feedback, ridge count / phase-offset / duty-cycle morphometrics, kappa / k_f / chi_m sweeps, 2 Lean 4 theorems on the transfer stiffness; transfer_boundary: The plate constants kappa = 0.05, T = 0.2, k_f = 1, beta = 1 are dimensionless modelling assumptions (no offline-verifiable measurement of embryonic palatal epithelial stiffness); only the sign-preservation, wavelength-transfer and monotone-attenuation predictions are scored, not ridge heights in micrometres | The specimen is an adult horse palate photograph; its duty cycle (0.49 / 0.44) is compared qualitatively with the simulated mouse-embryo ridges (0.42) after the same peak_widths estimator; DoG smoothing broadens the specimen crests | The 2D RD solver integrates on a rescaled x spacing dx_eff = dx (q / 1.24), so the realised grid wavelength (3.37) differs from the dispersion lambda_c (3.22) that Panels B / D use; the plate solver uses the physical dx; does_not_claim: A 3D finite-element simulation of epithelial invagination with large deflections or nonlinear growth; calibrated ridge heights; emergence of the coronal-cut / bead / cyclopamine phenotypes from identical initial conditions (they are seeded by condition-specific initial patterns at L606-633); mechanics-dependent phenotypes compared with a published mechanical perturbation." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 2012-economou-palate-ruguga-turing.py:1515, 1545, 1585 — reference values 0.96 (in-phase r), 0.4695 (coronal bifurcation index) and 0.1843 (specimen CV) are eyeballed or self-referential. Replace them with values digitised from Economou 2012 Figs. 2-3 (or relabel the measurement as a self-consistency check with reference_value: null) so `morphoeval/measure_outputs.py` does not report a trivially perfect match.",
            "remediation needed: 2012-economou-palate-ruguga-turing.py:338, 598-600, 619, 631 — `dx_eff = dx * (q / 1.24)` rescales the x Laplacian so the integrated wavelength (lambda_ap = 3.37) is not the dispersion lambda_c = 3.22 used by Panels B and D, and the Pass 3 plate solver (physical dx, L709-712) now exposes the mismatch (q_ap = 1.87 vs q_c = 1.95). Integrate on the physical grid (choose nx / dt for stability) so the RD, dispersion and plate share one coordinate system, and re-pin lambda references.",
            "remediation needed: 2012-economou-palate-ruguga-turing.py:383-388 and datasets/palate_ruguga_turing/palate_ridge_mechanics_reference.json:38-45 — kappa, T, k_f, beta are dimensionless assumptions. Calibrate them to a measured ridge height / spacing aspect ratio digitised from histological sections of E15.5 mouse rugae (Economou 2012 Fig. 1 or Pantalacci 2008 sections) and report ridge amplitude in micrometres with that source pinned; carry the residual of the original item (3D finite-element invagination with large deflection and nonlinear growth) explicitly as out of scope unless implemented.",
            "remediation needed: 2012-economou-palate-ruguga-turing.py:468-513 — crest detection uses `distance=8` and `prominence=0.15 * amplitude` without citation, and the kappa >= 0.2 merge to 7 ridges depends on that prominence. Derive the crest threshold from the specimen estimator (same relative prominence as the DoG segmentation) and report the ridge count's sensitivity to it.",
            "remediation needed: 2012-economou-palate-ruguga-turing.py:606-633 — the coronal-cut, FGF10-bead and cyclopamine phenotypes are seeded by condition-specific initial conditions (mediolateral cos modulation and q_gz at L606-615, q_high and bead halo at L616-627, q_cyc at L628-633). Start every condition from the same noisy initial field and let the incision barrier (L669-676), the bead source term and the reduced a_12 produce the phenotype, then re-measure the bifurcation index and counts; downgrade the claims if they do not emerge.",
            "remediation needed: 2012-economou-palate-ruguga-turing.py:645-647, 684-688 and 1726-1734 — two-way coupling is off by default (chi_mech = 0) and the mechanics overrides reach only the mechanics figure. Make a calibrated chi_m the default once item 3 is done, route --kappa / --k-found / --chi-mech into the comparison figure and the perturbation suite, and add a mechanics-dependent phenotype (e.g. softened epithelium -> broader / fused rugae) compared against a published mechanical or ECM perturbation." ;
        ns1:hasScore 9.12e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-economou-palate-ruguga-turing-parameter-expressivity> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Economou et al. (2012) FGF10/FGF7-SHH activator-inhibitor Turing stripe mechanism at mammalian palatal growth zones, coupled to quasi-static epithelial plate ridge elevation — Parameter expressivity: 90/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "New sweeps behave monotonically and are measured: ridge amplitude vs kappa over 6 values and vs k_f over 4 values both give Spearman rho = -1.00 with crest phase offset < 0.023 lambda throughout; the ridge count stays 9 for kappa <= 0.1 and merges to 7 at kappa >= 0.2 (an honest limit of wavelength transfer, disclosed in the JSON and the measurement note); the chi_m two-way sweep (0, 0.1, 0.2, 0.3) keeps 9 rugae with non-decreasing ridge amplitude (0.155 -> 0.188). CLI exposes --kappa, --k-found, --chi-mech plus the existing reaction / diffusion / growth flags. Deductions: the mechanics flags only act on the mechanics figure, the comparison PNG always uses defaults (L1726-1734) (-3); the reaction parameters a_12 etc. do not continuously control the perturbation morphologies because those are initial-condition templates (L606-633) (-5); T and beta are fixed, not swept (-2)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "2012-economou-palate-ruguga-turing.py L1726–L1734: mech_overrides are routed only to render_ridge_mechanics_figure, not to the comparison figure <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2012-economou-palate-ruguga-turing.py#L1726-L1734>" ;
        ns1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-economou-palate-ruguga-turing-parameter-expressivity-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-economou-palate-ruguga-turing-parameter-expressivity-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-economou-palate-ruguga-turing-parameter-expressivity-3> ;
        ns1:hasScore 9e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-economou-palate-ruguga-turing-repro-package> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
