    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-overall> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Feugier, Mochizuki & Iwasa (2005) PIN1 efflux carrier canalization on a Lockhart (1965)-growing hexagonal leaf blade with Scarpella et al. (2004/2006) procambial commitment: sequential 1°→4° vein-order emergence, open trees vs closed areoles vs decelerating no-branching — MorphoEval overall 91.9/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 3 (v3) evaluation of `2005-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization.py` (overall weighted score 91.9/100, down from 93.1/100 in v2). The Pass 2 remediation item is closed: a new Section 3b couples the Feugier (2005) hexagonal PIN1 carrier-flux ODEs to a Lockhart (1965) yield-threshold growing blade mesh (allometric mask, marginal cell birth, four stages 2.0-7.0 DAG) and produces sequential 1°→2°→3°→4° vein-order emergence (4/4 orders) with beta_1 = 0 at every stage for the accelerating open-tree regime, beta_1 = 4 closed areoles under the Scarpella (2004) irreversible commitment lock, a diffuse all-polarized sheet (vein fraction 0.86) under decelerating Phi (Feugier result 2), and nothing under k_1 = 0. Three new Lean 4 theorems (Lockhart yield-threshold growth, growth-event Betti-1 bookkeeping, commitment-lock monotonicity) bring the file to 6 theorems with 0 sorrys; `measure_morphoeval()` grows to 15 measurements and `--self-test` to 15 checks (27 s). The pass also corrects the record: the primary citation (236(4):366-375), the withdrawn \"Model B → closed loops\" attribution to Feugier, and the relabelling of Panels A-B as a templated scaffold. The net score falls because v2 had credited those defects as supporting evidence and because the new growing-blade reference values (`growing_blade_reference.json`) are internally authored expectations rather than externally digitised stage-resolved areole counts. Overall 91.9/100 (faithfulness 91.3, reproducibility 93.3); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit d58a084; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1, lean 4.35.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 91, Morphological realism / specimen match 90, Parameter expressivity 94, Morphometric validation 92, Source and data traceability 92, Code-to-model traceability 94, Reproducibility package 94. Output judged: docs/media/carrier_driven_canalization_comparison.png: rendered output of 2005-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization.py at d58a084, image/png, 1263498 B, 2310×1428 px, artifact_sha256 74b39f5757cc4cb7020ab8f336cc4b70b0c34685f5c9d809bf4214e79583dd22 (sha256 74b39f5757cc4cb7020ab8f336cc4b70b0c34685f5c9d809bf4214e79583dd22), spec_fingerprint d5956a07207a9a97703c7b3ba0b06fe87ba07192a5b48400bfa9427bfa87a2c3. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: d5956a07207a9a97703c7b3ba0b06fe87ba07192a5b48400bfa9427bfa87a2c3; artifact_sha256: 74b39f5757cc4cb7020ab8f336cc4b70b0c34685f5c9d809bf4214e79583dd22; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/carrier_driven_canalization/carrier_driven_canalization_reference.json=2f5e49e4cb5437bf..., datasets/carrier_driven_canalization/growing_blade_reference.json=400f277d561dfd8c..., datasets/carrier_driven_canalization/leaf_tip_venation_loops_specimen.jpg=e54c8add6cf7c916..., datasets/carrier_driven_canalization/paper_citations.bib=648885997eb3e2ee..., datasets/carrier_driven_canalization/scout_manifest.json=1de2b4f4c53ac234...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-carrier-driven-canalization-audit-v2. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Feugier, Mochizuki & Iwasa (2005) J. Theor. Biol. 236(4):366-375 hexagonal leaf lamina auxin S_i and directional PIN1 carrier P_ij ODEs with conserved total cellular carrier pool P_total = P_{i,cyt} + sum_{j=1}^6 P_ij; accelerating carrier-response functions Phi(J) produce branching vein patterns while linear or decelerating Phi produce no branching; conserved-pool competition yields higher auxin in veins than surrounding tissue | Scarpella, Francis & Berleth (2004) Development 131:3445-3455: vein orders form sequentially (midvein, then secondaries, tertiaries, quaternaries) during blade expansion; preprocambial domains extend as freely ending strands and fuse with pre-existing veins; procambial identity, once acquired, is not lost | Scarpella, Marcos, Friml & Berleth (2006) Genes & Development 20:1015-1027 ProPIN1:PIN1-GFP imaging showing epidermal PIN1 convergence points and transient bipolar PIN1 cells bridging strands into closed areoles | Lockhart (1965) J. Theor. Biol. 8:264-275: irreversible cell expansion rate (1/V)dV/dt = phi * max(0, P - Y) with wall extensibility phi, turgor P and yield threshold Y; reconstructed_in_script: Emergent growing-blade module (`simulate_growing_blade_canalization`): Feugier Eqs. 1-6 integrated on a 26x22 hexagonal mesh whose active blade mask expands by the Lockhart area law A(t) = A_0 exp(phi[(P-Y_0)t - kappa t^2/2]) (A(7)/A(2) = 2.399, arrest at 8 DAG) through four stages (2.0, 3.5, 5.0, 7.0 DAG) with marginal cell birth; 1°, 2°, 3°, 4° vein orders emerge sequentially (4 of 4 orders) with beta_1 = 0 at every stage in the accelerating open-tree regime, beta_1 = 4 closed areoles at 7 DAG under the Scarpella (2004) commitment lock, vein-cell fraction 0.86 (no discrete strands) under decelerating Phi, and no veins under k_1 = 0 | Commitment-delay expressivity sweep tau_commit in {0.5, 1, 2, 4, 8} giving monotone non-increasing beta_1 (Spearman rho = -1.0) | 6-face hexagonal intracellular PIN1 pool conservation and face-competition algebra (`verify_hexagonal_pool_conservation_and_face_competition`): pool error 0.0, winner-take-all share 0.9978 (ref 0.9960), saturated bipolar share 0.5221 (ref 0.5180), 6-regime Pearson r = 0.9999 | Templated topology scaffold (`simulate_hexagonal_venation_models`, Panels A-B): vein paths placed by a shortest-path template, ODEs relaxed on the scaffold, Betti-1 = 0 vs 16 graph readouts — relabelled in Pass 3 as a scaffold / Law 1 & Law 3 check, NOT an emergent result | Automated ridge + chromatic warmth segmentation of the cleared dicot leaf tip venation skeleton specimen (`leaf_tip_venation_loops_specimen.jpg`, CC BY-SA 4.0, 539x351 px): vein density 0.3585, Betti-1 = 205 closed areoles, mean compactness 0.7749 +- 0.0191 SE; transfer_boundary: 2D hexagonal cellular lattice with Lockhart area growth and marginal cell addition mapped to a cleared dicot leaf venation skeleton; blade growth is applied to the area/mask only (no per-cell anisotropic expansion, no carrier dilution by growth) | The 'closed areole' mechanism is Scarpella (2004/2006) procambial commitment, implemented as a sustained-flux lock, not a Feugier (2005) result; does_not_claim: 3D viscoelastic cell-wall FEM, turgor-driven anisotropic cell expansion, or stress feedback on PIN1 polarity | That Feugier et al. (2005) report closed loops under saturating Phi (withdrawn in Pass 3: the paper reports no branching under decelerating Phi, which the `decelerating_no_branching` regime reproduces) | Quantitative agreement of the simulated areole count (beta_1 = 4 on a 407-cell blade) with the specimen's 205 areoles; only the topological class (open tree vs reticulate) is compared." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Add per-cell biomechanics to the growth coupling: `blade_mask_at_growth_fraction` (L795-813) grows the blade only by marginal cell birth; implement Lockhart expansion per cell (anisotropic hexagon dilation along the Kuchen 2012 polarity field) with carrier dilution P_ij <- P_ij * A_old/A_new, and prove a Lean lemma that dilution preserves the Law 1 pool identity.",
            "remediation needed: Anchor the growing-blade metrics externally: digitise stage-resolved areole / vein-order counts from Kang & Dengler (2004) and Scarpella et al. (2004) Fig. 1 into `growing_blade_reference.json` (`expected_outcomes`, currently internally authored) and tighten `growing_blade_decelerating_vein_cell_fraction` (L1373-1382) and `growing_blade_committed_reticulate_betti1_final` (L1360-1371) tolerances accordingly.",
            "remediation needed: Replace the stage-index gate on the commitment lock (`commitment_on = regime == ... and s_idx >= 1`, L979) by an auxin-history criterion (e.g. cumulative flux through the face exceeding a threshold), and let the midvein emerge from a basal sink + apical source without the pre-placed apex convergence point (L948).",
            "remediation needed: Retire the templated Pass 2 scaffold from the headline figure: replace Panels A-B (`render_outputs`, titles at L1664 and L1673, data from `simulate_hexagonal_venation_models` L421-693) with the emergent open-tree and committed growing-blade final stages, and re-anchor the two scaffold measurements `model_a_open_tree_betti1_loops` (L1286) and `model_b_closed_reticulate_betti1_loops` (L1296) to emergent values or drop them.",
            "remediation needed: Strand width: emergent 3°/4° strands in `docs/media/carrier_driven_canalization_growth_stages.png` are 2-3 cells wide; add a single-file procambial strand-width measurement to `_vein_graph_from_fields` (L815-860) with a Scarpella (2006) reference of 1 cell and tune P_vein / lateral competition until it is met." ;
        ns1:hasScore 9.19e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-parameter-expressivity> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Feugier, Mochizuki & Iwasa (2005) PIN1 efflux carrier canalization on a Lockhart (1965)-growing hexagonal leaf blade with Scarpella et al. (2004/2006) procambial commitment: sequential 1°→4° vein-order emergence, open trees vs closed areoles vs decelerating no-branching — Parameter expressivity: 94/100" ;
