    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-repro-package> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Feugier, Mochizuki & Iwasa (2005) PIN1 efflux carrier canalization on a Lockhart (1965)-growing hexagonal leaf blade with Scarpella et al. (2004/2006) procambial commitment: sequential 1°→4° vein-order emergence, open trees vs closed areoles vs decelerating no-branching — Reproducibility package: 94/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "15-check `run_self_test()` (L1796-1903, ~27 s) verifies SHA-256 integrity of 5 files, parameter agreement with the vendored JSON, the corrected citation string, Laws 1-3, the Lockhart closed form vs Euler integration and arrest, growing-blade pool/antisymmetry residuals, monotone cell birth, 4/4 sequential orders, open-tree beta_1 = 0 at all stages with one component, committed beta_1 >= 1 with locked bipolar cells and none at stage 1, decelerating fraction >= 0.85 and > 2x open tree, k_1 = 0 ablation, monotone tau_commit sweep (rho <= -0.9), and 15 deterministic measurements across two calls. Default render regenerates both PNGs and the 16-frame GIF in ~21 s. Debit: wall-clock and determinism depend on the seeded RNG for newborn-cell carrier noise (seed 2005) and no cross-platform tolerance is stated for the committed beta_1 = 4." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-repro-package> ;
