    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-source-traceability> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Feugier, Mochizuki & Iwasa (2005) PIN1 efflux carrier canalization on a Lockhart (1965)-growing hexagonal leaf blade with Scarpella et al. (2004/2006) procambial commitment: sequential 1°→4° vein-order emergence, open trees vs closed areoles vs decelerating no-branching — Source and data traceability: 92/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "`datasets/carrier_driven_canalization/` now vendors 8 BibTeX entries with DOIs/PMIDs (`paper_citations.bib`, L1-90), a corrected reference JSON, the new `growing_blade_reference.json` with a bibliographic-correction record and six primary sources, and the specimen; all 5 files are SHA-256-verified at runtime (`verify_dataset_integrity`, L117-143). The corrected Feugier record (236(4):366-375, PMID 15899502) is cross-checked in the self-test. Debit: the v1/v2 record carried a wrong volume/issue/pages and a result attribution the paper does not make, both of which v2 scored 95 — the correction is credited here, the two-pass miss is not forgiven in full." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-source-traceability> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/source-traceability" ;
