    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-overall> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Goriely & Tabor (1998) PRL / Gerbode et al. (2012) Science Kirchhoff elastic rod tendril perversion, G-fiber overwinding & Pass 3 thigmotropic contact coiling — MorphoEval overall 91.7/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 3 (v3) evaluation of `1998-goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature.py` (overall weighted score ~91.7/100, down from 93.1 in v2). The single v2 remediation item is closed in reduced form: a new implicit overdamped discrete-rod section 3b simulates contact-gated thigmotropic coiling around a rigid cylindrical support with Coulomb support friction and self-contact friction, producing N_wrap = 2.86 turns after 30 min (no-support control 0.31, kappa0 stays 0), first full wrap at 4.75 min, max support penetration < 0.025 mm, max axial strain < 2 %, F_hold(mu) = {0.0005, 0.108, 0.212, 0.27} mN monotone in mu with the frictionless coil slipping at the first load increment, 11 active self-contact pairs with min non-adjacent distance / 2a = 0.989 in the stacked-turns scenario, and wraps(R_s = 2) / wraps(R_s = 1) = 0.64. The Pass 2 results are unchanged (pitchfork r = 0.9974, |Delta_Lk| = 0, soft overwinding r = 0.9806, 4-species r = 0.9999, specimen CV = 0.298). The score goes down because re-verification shows the v2 audit misquoted two measurements (Gerbode peak overwinding 0.7171 vs ref 0.58 and kappa_0 0.4976 vs ref 0.65 mm^-1, not 0.5873 and 0.6545), and because the six new measurements are internal controls or scheme-consistency checks rather than comparisons with measured contact-coiling data. Overall 91.7/100 (faithfulness 90.7, reproducibility 94.0); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 8a7928d7; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 92, Morphological realism / specimen match 90, Parameter expressivity 94, Morphometric validation 88, Source and data traceability 94, Code-to-model traceability 94, Reproducibility package 94. Output judged: docs/media/tendril_perversion_intrinsic_curvature_comparison.png: rendered output of 1998-goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature.py at 8a7928d7, image/png, 1061305 B, 2757×1458 px, artifact_sha256 57eed032cffcc9361a1a8fa3afc14d6c5377dfa2d824686d569b7ebc68f50f73 (sha256 57eed032cffcc9361a1a8fa3afc14d6c5377dfa2d824686d569b7ebc68f50f73), spec_fingerprint 68cb059282e6586e1c698e0a2073f9ca8cb2a88dda3dd3ce0c564cd556b97a7e. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 68cb059282e6586e1c698e0a2073f9ca8cb2a88dda3dd3ce0c564cd556b97a7e; artifact_sha256: 57eed032cffcc9361a1a8fa3afc14d6c5377dfa2d824686d569b7ebc68f50f73; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/tendril_perversion_intrinsic_curvature/paper_citations.bib=2529ebe7e9abea2f..., datasets/tendril_perversion_intrinsic_curvature/scout_manifest.json=801e196968b34405..., datasets/tendril_perversion_intrinsic_curvature/tendril_perversion_helix_specimen.jpg=14409d193142442d..., datasets/tendril_perversion_intrinsic_curvature/tendril_perversion_intrinsic_curvature_reference.json=8af7ac3175f6890f..., datasets/tendril_perversion_intrinsic_curvature/thigmotropic_contact_coiling_reference.json=f55d9cfe319f0366...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-audit-v2. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Goriely & Tabor (1998) / McMillen & Goriely (2002): an intrinsically curved Kirchhoff rod with both ends held undergoes a supercritical pitchfork bifurcation below T_c = B kappa_0^2 / (1 + Gamma) into two opposite-handed helices joined by a perversion, with zero net link | Gerbode et al. (2012): the cucumber tendril's G-fiber ribbon sets the intrinsic curvature; soft tendrils (Gamma < 1) overwind under axial stretch while lignified ones unwind; coil radius and pitch scale across species | Darwin (1865) Ch. IV: tendrils curve toward a touched side within tens of seconds, complete a wrap around a thin stick within minutes to about an hour, and grasp thin supports more readily than thick ones (qualitative) | Jaffe & Galston (1968): thigmotropic coiling is a contact-triggered, propagating growth response; Euler (1762): the capstan law exp(mu Theta) for a flexible line on a cylinder; reconstructed_in_script: Timoshenko bilayer kappa_0, exact T_c, 161-node L-BFGS-B Kirchhoff perversion solver with zero-link enforcement and negative controls; 10-point pitchfork sweep; soft vs lignified overwinding; 4-species scaling; DoG segmentation of the SHA-256-locked Passiflora caerulea specimen (Pass 2) | Pass 3: 61-node inertia-free discrete rod with contact-gated intrinsic curvature pointing toward the support axis, implicit backward-Euler incremental potential (L-BFGS-B), rigid-cylinder penalty contact, penalty self-contact, lagged-normal Coulomb friction on support and self-contact, quasi-static grip test vs mu*sum(N) and exp(mu Theta); no-support, frictionless, friction-sweep, support-radius-sweep and stacked-turns scenarios; transfer_boundary: The contact solver is a separate bending-only rod: it has no material-frame twist, so Gamma = C/B plays no role in contact coiling and the perversion (zero-link) physics of section 3 is not coupled to it | mu_support, mu_self, kappa_contact, tau_thigmo, v_signal, the 55 deg approach angle and the initial placement touching the support at 25 % of L are provenance-tagged assumptions; the only empirical anchors for Pass 3 are Darwin's qualitative timings and support-size statements | Friction uses normal forces lagged one macro step; F_hold / mu*sum(N) = 0.67 is a consistency check of the scheme, not an experiment; N_wrap counts loose loops that enclose but do not touch the support (contact fraction 33 % of nodes); does_not_claim: Circumnutation or support-search before first touch, a measured tendril-on-wood friction coefficient, compliant or rough or finite-length supports, G-fiber lignification time course, or a validated time-to-wrap (tau_thigmo and v_signal were chosen inside Darwin's 5-60 min window and the model's 4.75 min falls slightly below it)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 1998-goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature.py:1221, 897-899 and 2051-2056 — housekeeping: the section-6 banner still says '6-Panel'; `_last_objective`, `_mat_dir`, `_last_opt_message` are unused and `last_objective` is unbound when t_end_min < dt_min; the determinism check covers only a 5 min horizon. Also morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_064_tendril_perversion_intrinsic_curvature.lean:1-12 — the header lists only the three Pass 2 sources although Laws 4-5 cite Darwin (1865), Jaffe & Galston (1968) and Euler (1762).",
            "remediation needed: 1998-goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature.py:1841-1850 and 1831-1840 — the time-to-first-wrap measurement (4.75 min vs reference 32.5 min) is set by the assumed tau_thigmo = 5 min and v_signal = 5 mm/min and falls below Darwin's 5-60 min window, and N_wrap uses the no-support control as its reference. Pass 4: either digitise a quantitative time course (e.g. Jaffe & Galston 1968 Fig. or Isnard & Silk 2009 Table) into the JSON and fit tau_thigmo/v_signal to it, or move both entries out of `measure_morphoeval()` into a 'predictions' list so the quick gate does not count them as reference-anchored.",
            "remediation needed: 1998-goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature.py:1925-1933 and 1955-1963 — the Gerbode soft peak overwinding (0.7171 vs 0.58 turns, +24 %) and the G-fiber bilayer kappa_0 (0.4976 vs 0.65 mm^-1, -23 %) miss their references by about a quarter; v2 misquoted both. Pass 4: revisit `compute_g_fiber_intrinsic_curvature` (L164-L181) bilayer thickness/modulus ratio against Gerbode et al. (2012) Fig. 2 and the overwinding amplitude in `evaluate_gerbode_overwinding_regimes` (L1040-L1088), and report the deviations in the figure.",
            "remediation needed: 1998-goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature.py:483-514 and 1588-1591 — `_wrap_statistics` counts winding of every distal node about the support axis, so N_wrap = 2.86 with only 33 % of nodes in contact includes loose loops (mean loop radius > R_s + a), yet panel G's title reports \"N = 2.9\" without the qualifier. Pass 4: report tight wraps (nodes with rho < R_s + a + tol) separately from enclosing loops, add a contact-feedback growth law so kappa0 keeps rising until contact (the JSON `residual_remediation` already proposes this), and label panel G accordingly.",
            "remediation needed: 1998-goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature.py:596-909 vs 249-411 — the contact-coiling rod is a separate bending-only discrete rod with no material-frame twist, so Gamma = C/B (the quantity that drives Laws 2-3) plays no role in contact coiling and the zero-link perversion physics is never solved together with support contact. Pass 4: add a twist degree of freedom (Cosserat / Bishop-frame twist angle per edge) to the section 3b rod, or drive section 3 `relax_kirchhoff_perversion_rod` with the contact-gated kappa0 and a cylinder constraint, and show that a tethered tendril wrapping a support still forms a perversion.",
            "remediation needed: 1998-goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature.py:741-761 and 1851-1860 — Coulomb friction uses normal forces lagged one macro step, so F_hold / mu*sum(N) = 0.67 is partly a numerical artefact of the lag plus partial contact; the self-test accepts any value in (0.1, 1.5) (L2044). Pass 4: iterate the normal force to self-consistency within each macro step (or use a semi-smooth Newton / augmented-Lagrangian contact step), then tighten the acceptance band and report the capstan-law comparison exp(mu Theta) as a measurement.",
            "remediation needed: morphoeval/cloud/dispatches/slot-064.json `slug` (\"human-brain-folding-3d\") and the pass3 run yaml `paper` field (Tallinen et al. 2016) do not describe this tendril script; both are campaign metadata outside this slot's writable files (`init` sets the run paper). Flagged for the campaign coordinator rather than edited." ;
        ns1:hasScore 9.17e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-parameter-expressivity> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Goriely & Tabor (1998) PRL / Gerbode et al. (2012) Science Kirchhoff elastic rod tendril perversion, G-fiber overwinding & Pass 3 thigmotropic contact coiling — Parameter expressivity: 94/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 2 sweeps retained (10 tension levels across the pitchfork L982-L1038, soft vs lignified Gamma L1040-L1088, 4 species L1091-L1141). Pass 3 adds a 4-point friction sweep with frictionless control, a 4-point support-radius sweep, a no-support control and a stacked-turns scenario (`evaluate_thigmotropic_contact_coiling` L911-L976), 20 contact-model parameters in `THIGMO_DEFAULTS` (L446-L470) and six new CLI flags `--mu --mu-self --R-support --kappa-contact --approach-angle --tau-thigmo` wired through `thigmo_overrides` into both renderers (L2075-L2080, L2102-L2121); `--kappa0/--B/--Gamma/--L` now also reach `render_growth_gif` (L2119). Deductions: the support-radius sweep shows no sharp enclosure threshold at R* = 1/kappa_contact - a (wraps(2 mm)/wraps(1 mm) = 0.64, the model still winds loosely around thick supports), so the one qualitatively testable Darwin statement is not reproduced as a transition (-3); tau_thigmo and v_signal are exposed but no sweep shows how time-to-wrap depends on them (-2); `--kappa-contact` is not propagated to the Pass 2 panels, which is correct but means the two models cannot be co-varied from the CLI (-1)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
        ns1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-parameter-expressivity-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-parameter-expressivity-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-parameter-expressivity-3>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-parameter-expressivity-4> ;
        ns1:hasScore 9.4e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-repro-package> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Goriely & Tabor (1998) PRL / Gerbode et al. (2012) Science Kirchhoff elastic rod tendril perversion, G-fiber overwinding & Pass 3 thigmotropic contact coiling — Reproducibility package: 94/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "`self_test()` (L1987-L2068) runs 12 checks: the 8 Pass 2 checks plus (9) contact coiling N_wrap > 1.5 vs control < 0.5 with kappa0 = 0, penetration < 0.1 a, strain < 2 %; (10) F_hold monotone in mu, frictionless slip, F_hold/mu*sum(N) in (0.1, 1.5); (11) stacked turns activate self-contact and stay within 15 % of the rod diameter; (12) two-run bitwise determinism of the implicit contact solver (L2051-L2056). Verified this round: PASSED all 12 checks in ~85 s; the default render completes in ~45 s and writes the 4 media files listed under output/extra_outputs; dataset integrity is fail-closed; results are memoised in `_THIGMO_CACHE` by full parameter tuple. Deductions: the determinism check runs only a 5 min horizon, not the 30 min default (-2); the self-test takes ~85 s, dominated by the friction and radius sweeps, with no `--quick` path (-2); no requirements lock file pins the environment that produced the committed media (-1); the Pass 3 PNG is gitignored (`*.png`), so the committed repo does not carry the new figure (-1)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-repro-package> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/repro-package" ;
        ns1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-repro-package-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-repro-package-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-repro-package-3> ;
        ns1:hasScore 9.4e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-source-traceability> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Goriely & Tabor (1998) PRL / Gerbode et al. (2012) Science Kirchhoff elastic rod tendril perversion, G-fiber overwinding & Pass 3 thigmotropic contact coiling — Source and data traceability: 94/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "`datasets/tendril_perversion_intrinsic_curvature/` now vendors 5 SHA-256-pinned files (`EXPECTED_SHA256` L110-L127, verified fail-closed by `verify_dataset_integrity` L141-L153): the Pass 2 reference JSON, specimen JPG, scout manifest and bib, plus the new `thigmotropic_contact_coiling_reference.json` in which every value carries a provenance tag (literature / derived / assumption / prediction), Darwin's (1865) Ch. IV timings and support-size statement are quoted with the caveat that they are approximate readings, and a `residual_remediation` list is recorded. The bib gains Jaffe & Galston (1968), Isnard & Silk (2009) and Euler (1762); the README section 5 documents the Pass 3 model and states that the new DOIs were not re-verified offline. Deductions: the two new DOIs could not be verified offline (-2); Darwin's \"25 s to visible curvature\" and \"5-60 min to full wrap\" are approximate readings without page pinpoints (-2); Euler (1762) has no DOI and the capstan law is cited without a page (-1); the bib is pinned but is itself an authored file, so pinning does not establish provenance (-1)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-source-traceability> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/source-traceability" ;
        ns1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-source-traceability-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-source-traceability-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-source-traceability-3>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-source-traceability-4> ;
        ns1:hasScore 9.4e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-specimen-match> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Goriely & Tabor (1998) PRL / Gerbode et al. (2012) Science Kirchhoff elastic rod tendril perversion, G-fiber overwinding & Pass 3 thigmotropic contact coiling — Morphological realism / specimen match: 90/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Unchanged specimen pipeline: the SHA-256-locked CC BY-SA Passiflora caerulea tendril JPG is segmented into backbone, 50 helical turn apices and the perversion zone (`segment_tendril_perversion_specimen` L1144-L1220) and shown in panel E; 4-species coil radius/pitch match (r = 0.9999). Pass 3 adds panels G/H and a 4-panel thigmotropic figure + GIF whose 3D rod wraps a grey cylinder in a visually plausible helix. Deductions: there is no empirical specimen of a tendril wrapped on a support, so the new coiling output is compared only with the no-support control and Darwin's prose (-5); with 33 % of nodes in contact and a mean loop radius above R_s + a, panel G's \"N = 2.9\" includes loose loops that enclose but do not touch the support, so the figure reads tighter than the statistics support (-3); specimen pitch CV 0.298 vs the 0.22 reference is a Pass 2 carry-over that the model does not explain (-2); panel H overlays F_hold(mu) and N_wrap(R_s) on one axes with a secondary top axis, and panel C of the thigmotropic PNG has a legend that partly overlaps the curves (cosmetic)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-specimen-match> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/specimen-match" ;
        ns1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-specimen-match-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-specimen-match-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-specimen-match-3>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-specimen-match-4>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-specimen-match-5>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-goriely-tendril-perversion-intrinsic-curvature-specimen-match-6> ;
        ns1:hasScore 9e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-code-traceability> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Yang et al. (2022) & Donnay & Pawson (1969) biogenic single-crystal calcite TPMS echinoderm stereom (Diamond D, Gyroid G, Primitive P), Gibson-Ashby cellular mechanics, nanoindentation twin-band arrest FEM & syncytial ACC templating — Code-to-model traceability: 91/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Credit: the header docstring (L1-80) maps Sections 4b and 6b to the ten sources and the six Lean theorems, states the reductions (2D, one twin family, no r/f slip, no fracture) and flags refs 5-10 as offline-recalled; function docstrings cite the equation or paper step for the FEM, pile-up and templating code; model constants carry inline provenance comments (L117-138); the math-KG YAML registers equations 5-6 with single-range lean_locus / code_locus. Deductions: the Pass 2 [111] projection docstring claims to follow Yang et al. Figs. 2-3 while the implementation integrates a partial period and the dislocation is an ansatz whose comment asserts a winding of 1.0 that is simply assigned (L552-555, L591-592) (-3); the E/10 'cleavage scale' line (L1714-1716) is a scale marker presented beside measured quantities (-1); DEFAULT_TAU_TWIN_MPA = 500 (L118) is a scale parameter whose role is explained in the comment but the pile-up head stress at this tau in a 6 um strut (147 GPa) is unphysical and not flagged in the panel (-1). Net -1 from v2." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "models/2020-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid.py L1714–L1716: e_cleave = E/10 drawn as a 'cleavage scale' marker — a scale line, not a measured cleavage stress <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/models/2020-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid.py#L1714-L1716>",
            "models/2020-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid.py L552–L555: DEFECT: docstring claims Yang et al. Figs. 2-3 projections while the code integrates a partial [111] period and hard-codes the Burgers winding <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/models/2020-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid.py#L552-L555>" ;
        ns1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-code-traceability-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-code-traceability-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-code-traceability-3> ;
        ns1:hasScore 9.1e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-model-fidelity> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Yang et al. (2022) & Donnay & Pawson (1969) biogenic single-crystal calcite TPMS echinoderm stereom (Diamond D, Gyroid G, Primitive P), Gibson-Ashby cellular mechanics, nanoindentation twin-band arrest FEM & syncytial ACC templating — Model fidelity to source: 91/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Credit: the Pass 2 3D nodal TPMS level sets, implicit-surface H/K and odd-inversion/half-fraction results remain correct (L287-478); the new FEM implements a genuine small-strain crystal-plasticity scheme — Q4 plane-strain stiffness (L670-689), Schmid resolved shear on two e-twin variants, perfectly plastic criterion with twin-shear exhaustion, initial-strain iteration with a single LU factorisation per structure, displacement-controlled flat punch, lattice vs monolith at equal depth (L692-868, L908-974) — and the pile-up scaling is the Eshelby-Frank-Nabarro formula (L871-905); the templating model encodes the Politi secondary-nucleation vs primary-nucleation distinction and the Beniash / Vidavsky vesicle-delivery picture (L1155-1269). Deductions: the Pass 2 [111] projection integrates along w in [0, 2 pi) instead of the full [111] period 2 pi sqrt(3) (L558), so Panel D's hexagonal contrast is a partial-period artefact, and its edge dislocation is a phase-winding ansatz with burgers_winding = 1.0 hard-coded (L582-592) (-4); the FEM is a 2D plane-strain honeycomb section of a 3D stretching-dominated lattice with one twin family, |tau| used for both twin senses (L798-802), no r/f slip, isotropic elasticity and no fracture, so it cannot be compared with Yang et al.'s load-depth or twin-band data (-3); the templating kinetics are unfitted model choices and the template is the adult honeycomb rather than a larval triradiate spicule (-2). Net -2 from v2." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "models/2020-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid.py L549–L603: DEFECT: [111] projection integrates w over [0, 2 pi) (L558) rather than the full 2 pi sqrt(3) period — projected D density is uniform over the full period; edge dislocation is an ansatz with burgers_winding = 1.0 hard-coded (L592) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/models/2020-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid.py#L549-L603>",
            "models/2020-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid.py L798–L802: Twin criterion uses |tau| for both variants and both senses — calcite e-twinning is polar; no r/f slip <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/models/2020-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid.py#L798-L802>" ;
        ns1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-model-fidelity-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-model-fidelity-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-model-fidelity-3>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-model-fidelity-4> ;
        ns1:hasScore 9.1e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-morphometric-validation> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Yang et al. (2022) & Donnay & Pawson (1969) biogenic single-crystal calcite TPMS echinoderm stereom (Diamond D, Gyroid G, Primitive P), Gibson-Ashby cellular mechanics, nanoindentation twin-band arrest FEM & syncytial ACC templating — Morphometric validation: 86/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Credit: `measure_morphoeval()` (L1842-2028) now returns 16 reference-anchored measurements; the 7 new ones (L1863-1934) report a non-trivial FEM result (max lamella 2.78 um against the geometric arrest bound a_0/sqrt(6) = 6.04 um; twinned-area ratio 0.123 against the phi = 0.50 null; k ratio 0.193) and the templating result (IoU 0.753 against 1.0 with the 0.418 flux-matched control in the method string). Deductions: the headline Pass 2 validation — 12-species r = 0.9997 (L1938-1947) — is circular because the table's e_rel_obs equals e_rel_pred +/- 0.002 by construction (-5); the Gibson-Ashby 2.0x at phi = 0.5 (L1988-1997) is the algebraic identity C phi/(C phi^2), chi = -4 (L1978-1987) is a lookup (L446-453) not computed from the field, and Z = 0 (L1998-2007) is assigned via get_tpms_nodal_strut_vectors(\"none\") (L441) (-3); several Pass 3 references are weak: the stiffness ratio reference 0.19 is Gibson-Ashby stretching although the 2D honeycomb is bending-dominated (L1895-1903), the pore-arrest fraction 0.26 vs ideal 1.0 includes notch-singularity elements at hexagon vertices (L1885-1893), the largest-domain fraction measures 0.766 against a reference of 1.0 (the single chance primary-nucleation event at k_1 = 1e-7 seeds a second domain holding 23% of the crystalline pixels; the self-test's `domains <= 2` does not catch this and the Phase A handoff reported it as ~0.999) (L1915-1923), and the ACC-fraction reference 0.0 is asymptotic rather than a literature time point (L1925-1934) (-3); the specimen a_0 reference is self-referential (L2018-2027) (-1). Net -6 from v2." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "datasets/crinoid_stereom_gyroid/crinoid_stereom_gyroid_reference.json L86–L98: DEFECT: cross_taxa_echinoderm_stereom_table has no per-row figure/table/DOI provenance; TPMS-type assignments (e.g. Cidaris rugosa 'Primitive P') unsupported <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/datasets/crinoid_stereom_gyroid/crinoid_stereom_gyroid_reference.json#L86-L98>",
            "models/2020-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid.py L1885–L1903: Pass 3 references of limited strength: pore-arrest ideal 1.0 vs 0.26 (notch-vertex twinning), stiffness ratio reference 0.19 = stretching C phi while the honeycomb section is bending-dominated (GA 2.3 (t/l)^3 = 0.288 noted in the source string) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/models/2020-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid.py#L1885-L1903>",
            "models/2020-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid.py L1915–L1923: DEFECT: largest-domain fraction measures 0.766 (measurements.yaml) vs reference 1.0 — a chance primary event seeds a 23% second domain; the self-test's domains <= 2 (L2130) does not catch it <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/models/2020-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid.py#L1915-L1923>",
            "models/2020-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid.py L1938–L1947: DEFECT: 12-species Pearson r = 0.9997 is circular — reference-table e_rel_obs is e_rel_pred +/- 0.002 for every row <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/models/2020-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid.py#L1938-L1947>",
            "models/2020-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid.py L1978–L2007: DEFECT: chi = -4 is a genus lookup (L446-453), 2.0x Gibson-Ashby ratio is the identity C phi/(C phi^2), pinch-off Z = 0 is assigned via the 'none' strut set (L441) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/models/2020-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid.py#L1978-L2007>" ;
        ns1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-measurement-12-species-echinodermata-tpms-vs-labyrinthic-stereom-relative-modulus-correlation-e-e-s>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-measurement-3d-schwarz-diamond-tpms-implicit-surface-mean-curvature-h-on-zero-level-set>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-measurement-3d-schwarz-diamond-tpms-zero-level-set-solid-volume-fraction-phi-c-0>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-measurement-acc-fraction-of-spicule-mineral-remaining-after-48-h-of-templated-secondary-nucleation-transformation>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-measurement-crinoid-ossicle-sem-specimen-segmented-solid-calcite-volume-fraction-crinoid-stereom-ossicle-specimen-jpg>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-measurement-crinoid-ossicle-sem-specimen-segmented-trabecular-lattice-period-a-0-crinoid-stereom-ossicle-specimen-jpg>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-measurement-elastic-flat-punch-indentation-stiffness-ratio-of-the-111-diamond-lattice-section-to-the-monolithic-single-crystal>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-measurement-gibson-ashby-stretching-tpms-phi-1-vs-bending-foam-phi-2-stiffness-amplification-at-phi-0-50>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-measurement-largest-crystallographic-domain-fraction-of-spicule-calcite-under-secondary-nucleation-dominated-acc-calcite-transformation>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-measurement-nanoindentation-fem-fraction-of-lattice-twinned-elements-adjacent-to-a-strut-pore-interface-free-surface-arrest>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-measurement-nanoindentation-fem-twin-band-max-lamella-run-length-in-the-111-diamond-lattice-section-at-4x-monolith-twin-onset-depth>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-measurement-nanoindentation-fem-twinned-area-confinement-ratio-lattice-monolith-at-equal-indentation-depth-4x-onset>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-measurement-schwarz-diamond-z-4-tetrahedral-inter-strut-angle-arccos-1-3-in-protoreaster-nodosus>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-measurement-super-threshold-pinch-off-ablation-negative-control-nodal-strut-valence-c-1-35>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-measurement-syncytial-membrane-templating-fidelity-iou-mineral-tpms-template-after-48-h-of-acc-vesicle-delivery>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-measurement-tpms-unit-cell-euler-characteristic-chi-2-2g-for-genus-g-3-bicontinuous-stereom>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-morphometric-validation-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-morphometric-validation-2> ;
