    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-grieneisen-root-auxin-reflux-fountain-model-fidelity> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Grieneisen et al. (2007) Nature & Mähönen et al. (2014) Nature reverse-fountain root tip auxin reflux capacitor solved on a cellular PIN-permeability lattice, with a growing dividing cellular lattice and gravistimulated PIN3/PIN7 bending (Friml 2002, Band 2012) — Model fidelity to source: 92/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "The Grieneisen (2007) cellular PIN-permeability reflux model is now actually solved (`build_pin_lattice_operator` L178-288 assembles the sparse operator with rootward stele, shootward epidermal, inward lateral and apolar columella permeabilities, passive exchange, turnover and the shoot source; `solve_cellular_auxin_steady_state` L291-295), the Mähönen (2014) PLETHORA solver runs on variable-length rows with growth dilution (`solve_plethora_gradient` L334-362), the growing lattice divides cells explicitly (`simulate_growing_cellular_lattice` L542-636) and gravistimulation is a g-biased statocyte efflux split (L253-263) feeding sine-law bending (`simulate_gravitropic_bending` L641-716). Six machine-checked Lean 4 theorems (0 sorrys) cover the laws. Two points below v2 because the v2 remediation asked for vertex/CPM mechanics and the delivered growth/bending are reduced kinematic models with uniform row lengths and an imposed 40 degree tipping point." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
        ns1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-grieneisen-root-auxin-reflux-fountain-model-fidelity-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-grieneisen-root-auxin-reflux-fountain-model-fidelity-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-grieneisen-root-auxin-reflux-fountain-model-fidelity-3>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-grieneisen-root-auxin-reflux-fountain-model-fidelity-4>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-grieneisen-root-auxin-reflux-fountain-model-fidelity-5> ;
        ns1:hasScore 9.2e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-grieneisen-root-auxin-reflux-fountain-morphometric-validation> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Grieneisen et al. (2007) Nature & Mähönen et al. (2014) Nature reverse-fountain root tip auxin reflux capacitor solved on a cellular PIN-permeability lattice, with a growing dividing cellular lattice and gravistimulated PIN3/PIN7 bending (Friml 2002, Band 2012) — Morphometric validation: 89/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "`measure_morphoeval()` (L841-1038) returns 16 measurements, each with a reference value, unit and uncertainty: flux-conservation error, WT QC amplification, log-amplitude r over six regimes (0.919), decapitation retention (0.925), ablation peak shift, WT z_MZ (240 um), six-regime z_MZ r (-0.331, with the 5-regime r > 0.9 excluding NPA reported alongside), three growing-lattice metrics against Beemster & Baskin / Dello Ioio anchors, three gravitropism metrics against Friml / Band anchors, and three specimen metrics. Four points below v2 because the comparisons are now honest: the six-regime z_MZ correlation is negative, the tipping point is 2.8x slower than Band (2012), the growth rate is ~2x below the literature anchor, and the regime benchmarks remain synthetic." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
