        ns1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation-model-fidelity> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Hannezo et al. (2017) Cell & Scheele et al. (2017) Nature unifying theory of branching morphogenesis via branching and annihilating random walks (BARW) — Model fidelity to source: 92/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "The core BARW rules (persistent migration, Poisson A -> 2A, trail deposition, R_a annihilation) are implemented in 2D (L236-489) and now in 3D (L823-1029) with the nematic alignment torque du = lambda (f.u)(f - (f.u)u) dt and a unit-sphere persistent random walk; the exact Catalan critical GW pmf (L196-234), the 1D Fisher-KPP mean field (L491-582), neutral Moran drift with hypergeometric splits (L1074-1157) and the inflating capsule (L891-903) are all recognisable reductions of the cited papers, and 6 Lean theorems machine-check the algebraic identities (0 sorry). Deductions: the 1D PDE uses uncited constants 1.82 k_a, 0.55 v_0 and v_drift = 0.35 v_0 (L510, L530-531) tuned to make the plateau hit k_b/k_a (-3); the 3D model needed a birth-vertex exemption (L934-938) absent from the 2D model, so the two simulators implement different annihilation rules (-2); the fat pad is a cylinder, not Bordeu's slab, and deposited ducts are not advected with the inflating sphere (-2); the WT 2D tree at seed 2017 has only N_b = 12 and other seeds give N_b from 1 to 70, so the 2D model sits at the edge of extinction (-1)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "2017-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation.py L510–L531: Uncited PDE calibration constants v_drift = 0.35 v0, 1.82 ka, 0.55 v0 that set the wake plateau <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/74d06a5c/2017-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation.py#L510-L531>" ;
        ns1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation-model-fidelity-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation-model-fidelity-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation-model-fidelity-3>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation-model-fidelity-4>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation-model-fidelity-5> ;
        ns1:hasScore 9.2e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation-morphometric-validation> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Hannezo et al. (2017) Cell & Scheele et al. (2017) Nature unifying theory of branching morphogenesis via branching and annihilating random walks (BARW) — Morphometric validation: 86/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "`measure_morphoeval()` (L1799-1998) reports 14 metrics with reference values, units and dispersion statistics: q_branch 0.480 (ref 0.5), tau = 1.4418 (ref 1.5, computed p-value L227), honest generational r = 0.924 against the measured pooled ensemble (L641-661; replaces the hand-fitted Pass 2 curve), i_inf = 0.28695 (ref 0.28571), hyper-branching 8.82x, R_a = 0 explosion +49 tips, specimen N_term = 34 and r/R_max = 0.7833, and six Pass 3 metrics: 3D cylinder q_b = 0.4937 (ref 0.5), sphere tau = 1.438 (ref 1.49), S_iso = 0.054 (ref 0), S gain 0.576, clonal f_bar = 0.119 (ref 0.125), tau_clone = 1.66 (ref 1.5). Deductions: the hyper-branching reference 2.00 (L1897) is missed by 4.4x and the \"hypo\" tree is a dead stalk (L_total = 28), yet the metric is presented as a pass (-4); i_inf vs k_b/k_a is a self-calibration via L510/L530-531 (-3); the sphere tau regresses bins with count >= 2 over S in [3, 45] of a single tree (L1824-1831) and the clone tail uses sizes 1..25 with r = -0.93 (L1198-1201) — both small-sample exponents (-3); S(lambda) monotonicity rests on one seed per lambda and the cylinder trees at lambda = 0.2, 0.4 have N_b = 4 and 2 (-2); g = 1 of the generational profile is q = 1 by construction and the reference profile is labelled \"obs\" without digitisation provenance (-2)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "2017-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation.py L1198–L1201: Clone-size tail regression over sizes 1..25 with count >= 2; r = -0.93 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/74d06a5c/2017-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation.py#L1198-L1201>",
            "2017-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation.py L1824–L1831: Sphere tau regression on count >= 2 bins over S in [3, 45] of one tree (small-sample exponent) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/74d06a5c/2017-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation.py#L1824-L1831>",
            "2017-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation.py L1897–L1897: Hyper-branching reference 2.00 vs measured 8.82 — model/reference mismatch scored as a pass <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/74d06a5c/2017-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation.py#L1897-L1897>" ;
        ns1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation-measurement-1d-mean-field-barw-homeostatic-wake-duct-density-i-inf>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation-measurement-2d-barw-self-terminated-topological-branching-fraction-q-branch-wt>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation-measurement-3d-barw-nematic-ecm-order-parameter-s-in-the-true-isotropic-control-chi-0-lambda-0>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation-measurement-3d-cylindrical-fat-pad-barw-topological-branching-fraction-q-branch-ecm-lambda-0-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation-measurement-3d-ecm-alignment-sweep-nematic-order-gain-s-lambda-0-2-s-lambda-0-in-spherical-mesenchyme>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation-measurement-3d-spherical-mesenchyme-barw-subtree-size-power-law-exponent-tau-kidney-regime>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation-measurement-attenuated-tgf-beta-r-a-1-75-vs-wild-type-r-a-3-5-ductal-hyper-branching-ratio>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation-measurement-clonal-neutral-drift-martingale-duct-length-weighted-labelled-fraction-vs-induced-fraction-f-0>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation-measurement-critical-galton-watson-subtree-size-power-law-exponent-tau>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation-measurement-generational-branching-probability-q-branch-g-correlation-across-3-organs>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation-measurement-mouse-branched-ductal-specimen-active-distal-tip-count-n-term>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation-measurement-mouse-branched-ductal-specimen-peripheral-active-tip-radial-localization-r-r-max>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation-measurement-non-annihilating-r-a-0-ablation-unarrested-active-tip-explosion-delta>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hannezo-branching-random-walk-annihilation-measurement-single-cell-clone-size-tail-exponent-tau-clone-labelled-ductal-segments-per-surviving-clone>,
