    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-he-drosophila-ventral-furrow-code-traceability> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Conte et al. (2012), Martin et al. (2009) & He et al. (2014) Drosophila ventral furrow invagination biomechanics — Code-to-model traceability: 92/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "The module docstring (L1-76) states all five governing laws with their Lean theorem names, each new section carries a header explaining what was asked, what was implemented and what is reduced (L612-626, L846-854), every new function docstring cites its equation and source, and the math KG loop file registers both new equations with lean_locus and code_locus ranges that match the current files. Deductions: the regime block does not state in code that its targets are the reference values being measured against (-4); the Stokes operator derivation is explained in a comment rather than referenced to a textbook equation number (-2); the GIF code (L1767-1842) does not mention the new mechanisms (-2)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "2012-he-drosophila-ventral-furrow.py L332–L369: Regime targets are not annotated as the audited reference values <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/7e4f207/2012-he-drosophila-ventral-furrow.py#L332-L369>" ;
        ns1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-he-drosophila-ventral-furrow-code-traceability-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-he-drosophila-ventral-furrow-code-traceability-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-he-drosophila-ventral-furrow-code-traceability-3> ;
        ns1:hasScore 9.2e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-he-drosophila-ventral-furrow-model-fidelity> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Conte et al. (2012), Martin et al. (2009) & He et al. (2014) Drosophila ventral furrow invagination biomechanics — Model fidelity to source: 87/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Credited: exact incompressible wedge geometry and RK2 ratcheted-pulse ODE (L153-249), the new AP shell line equation with exact ellipsoid curvatures, simply supported poles and a verified second-order stencil (L627-719; uncoupled run recovers the 2D depth to 0.1% at 50% EL), the new variable-viscosity Stokes operator derived by taking the curl of div(sigma) = 0 with exact boundary-flux closure and an exact-solution check to 1e-12 (L855-1003), and 5 Lean theorems (0 sorrys) pinning Theorems 1-5. Deductions: the regime depth and cell height in the 2D ring are prescribed interpolants pinned to the reference values at the last step (L332-369, L443-445, L455-458) rather than solved from the viscous-vertex force balance, so the Conte (2012) decomposition is reproduced by construction (-7, newly exposed); the AP coupling is a 1D line + kinematic sweep, not a 3D FE shell, and ell_B / ell_N are free parameters (-3); the Stokes domain is a fixed rectangle with velocity BCs rather than a moving trapezoid with cortical stress BCs (-3)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "2012-he-drosophila-ventral-furrow.py L332–L369: Regime block hard-codes target_ap_um / target_h_um / target_depth_um equal to the empirical reference values <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/7e4f207/2012-he-drosophila-ventral-furrow.py#L332-L369>",
            "2012-he-drosophila-ventral-furrow.py L443–L458: h_mean = target_h_um and depth_um = target_depth_um forced at the last step; depth is an interpolant of constr_frac and prog, not a mechanical solve <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/7e4f207/2012-he-drosophila-ventral-furrow.py#L443-L458>" ;
        ns1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-he-drosophila-ventral-furrow-model-fidelity-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-he-drosophila-ventral-furrow-model-fidelity-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-he-drosophila-ventral-furrow-model-fidelity-3>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-he-drosophila-ventral-furrow-model-fidelity-4> ;
        ns1:hasScore 8.7e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-he-drosophila-ventral-furrow-morphometric-validation> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Conte et al. (2012), Martin et al. (2009) & He et al. (2014) Drosophila ventral furrow invagination biomechanics — Morphometric validation: 86/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "`measure_morphoeval()` now returns 12 measurements (L1196-1416). New in Pass 3: D_3D(0.5 EL) = 39.92 um vs 41.0 ref (coupling ratio 0.974), furrow half-depth extent 0.590 EL vs ~0.65 ref, ell_N ablation ratio 0.534 (no empirical reference, stated as such), Stokes passive-tracer ratio 0.983 vs 1.0 (He 2014), and the exact-solution verification 8.1e-13 vs 0. Deductions: the 6-regime depth/height r = 1.0000 and RMSE = 0 (measurement 3) are circular because the regimes are pinned to the reference values (-8, newly exposed); the 0.65 EL and ~1.0 tracer references are approximate literature statements rather than digitised values (-4); no error bars or sensitivity of the new measurements to ell_B / nucleus geometry (-2)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "2012-he-drosophila-ventral-furrow.py L1249–L1264: 6-regime Pearson r measurement is computed against the same reference values the regimes are pinned to <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/7e4f207/2012-he-drosophila-ventral-furrow.py#L1249-L1264>" ;
        ns1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-he-drosophila-ventral-furrow-measurement-3d-shell-coupled-wt-furrow-depth-at-50-egg-length-d-3d-0-5-el>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-he-drosophila-ventral-furrow-measurement-6-regime-invagination-depth-pearson-correlation-r>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-he-drosophila-ventral-furrow-measurement-apical-constriction-only-shallow-groove-depth-d-ap-only>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-he-drosophila-ventral-furrow-measurement-germband-extension-tension-ablation-ratio-d-3d-ell-n-150-um-d-3d-ell-n-0>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-he-drosophila-ventral-furrow-measurement-specimen-4-stage-invagination-trajectory-correlation-r>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-he-drosophila-ventral-furrow-measurement-specimen-stage-4-invaginated-dv-ml-aspect-ratio>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-he-drosophila-ventral-furrow-measurement-stokes-resolved-nucleus-cytoplasm-basal-velocity-ratio-passive-tracer>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-he-drosophila-ventral-furrow-measurement-stokes-solver-verification-affine-lengthening-exact-solution-l2-error>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-he-drosophila-ventral-furrow-measurement-twist-snail-double-null-negative-control-invagination-depth>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-he-drosophila-ventral-furrow-measurement-unratcheted-twist-recoil-mutant-apical-width-l-ap>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-he-drosophila-ventral-furrow-measurement-ventral-furrow-ap-half-depth-extent-fraction-of-egg-length>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-he-drosophila-ventral-furrow-measurement-wild-type-synergistic-ventral-furrow-invagination-depth-d-furrow>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-he-drosophila-ventral-furrow-morphometric-validation-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-he-drosophila-ventral-furrow-morphometric-validation-2> ;
        ns1:hasScore 8.6e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-he-drosophila-ventral-furrow-overall> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Conte et al. (2012), Martin et al. (2009) & He et al. (2014) Drosophila ventral furrow invagination biomechanics — MorphoEval overall 89.9/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 3 remediation-round evaluation of `2012-he-drosophila-ventral-furrow.py` (89.9/100, down from 92.0 in Pass 2). Both v2 remediation items were closed with honest reduced models: a Donnell/Winkler AP shell line equation on the prolate-ellipsoidal blastoderm (exact meridional/hoop curvatures, $k_{\\mathrm{pole}}/k_{\\mathrm{eq}} = 13\\times$, germband-extension tension $\\ell_N$ ramp) driven by the 2D ring depth and swept into a 5,265-node $\\theta \\times z$ shell mesh ($D_{3D}(0.5\\,EL) = 39.92\\ \\mu\\text{m}$ vs $D_{2D} = 41.0$, half-depth extent $0.590$ EL vs $\\approx 0.65$, $\\ell_N$ ablation ratio $0.534$, monotone), and a variable-viscosity Stokes solve in stream-function form inside the Phase-I lengthening cell with a $50\\times$-viscosity nucleus ($v_{\\mathrm{nuc}}/v_{\\mathrm{cyto}} = 0.983$ vs He et al. 2014 $\\approx 1$, affine verification $L_2 = 8.1\\times10^{-13}$, flux closure $5.6\\times10^{-17}$), each pinned by a new machine-checked Lean 4 theorem (5 total, 0 sorrys). The round also exposed that the 2D ring depth and cell height are target-pinned interpolants (L332-369, L443-445, L455-458), making the Pass 2 6-regime $r = 1.0000$ circular; model-fidelity and morphometric-validation are therefore scored lower than in v2 and the un-pinning of the ring mechanics is the top Pass 4 item. Overall 89.9/100 (faithfulness 89.1, reproducibility 91.7); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 7e4f207; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 87, Morphological realism / specimen match 91, Parameter expressivity 93, Morphometric validation 86, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 92, Reproducibility package 93. Output judged: docs/media/drosophila_ventral_furrow_comparison.png: rendered output of 2012-he-drosophila-ventral-furrow.py at 7e4f207, image/png, 1096884 B, 2436×2156 px, artifact_sha256 1fc501631ab9c6ab13eaf2ac9a771c53029337b6fdb3ddd5880ed8f4211d9a76 (sha256 1fc501631ab9c6ab13eaf2ac9a771c53029337b6fdb3ddd5880ed8f4211d9a76), spec_fingerprint 231d3bda8cca542298a1fb5749dc44c894794b8e0ed35252a225b4a9fa7bd0aa. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 231d3bda8cca542298a1fb5749dc44c894794b8e0ed35252a225b4a9fa7bd0aa; artifact_sha256: 1fc501631ab9c6ab13eaf2ac9a771c53029337b6fdb3ddd5880ed8f4211d9a76; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/drosophila_ventral_furrow/ap_shell_stokes_reference.json=8f196893e04e6457..., datasets/drosophila_ventral_furrow/drosophila_ventral_furrow_reference.json=5c6f1960cef1be19..., datasets/drosophila_ventral_furrow/drosophila_ventral_furrow_specimen.jpg=f426366f7ede436d..., datasets/drosophila_ventral_furrow/scout_manifest.json=0c6354ab1d934ba3...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-drosophila-ventral-furrow-audit-v2. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Conte, Munoz, Baum & Miodownik (2012) PLoS ONE 7(11):e49973 incompressible finite-element cross-sectional decomposition showing apical constriction alone produces only a shallow groove (16.5 um) with over-elongated cells (48.1 um), whereas synergy with basal relaxation, lateral shortening, and ectodermal pushing drives full invagination (41.0 um) | Martin, Kaschube & Wieschaus (2009) Nature 457:495-499 Twist-stabilized ratcheted Myosin-II pulses (T_pulse = 82 s) vs unratcheted relaxation recoil; He et al. (2014) Nature 508:392-396 apically driven hydrodynamic cytoplasmic flow that carries nuclei basally as passive tracers during cell lengthening | Sweeton et al. (1991) / Leptin & Grunewald (1990): the ventral furrow spans roughly the mesoderm primordium (~0.15-0.80 EL) and germband extension begins as the furrow closes (approximate, not digitised here); reconstructed_in_script: 64-cell 2D incompressible trapezoidal blastoderm ring enclosed by the vitelline membrane (R_vit = 83.2 um, A_0 = 262.4 um^2), RK2 integration of the ratcheted Myosin-II apical-width pulse ODE, 6-regime benchmark and 15x15 (r_twist x sigma_synergy) morphospace; NOTE: regime depth and cell height are target-pinned interpolants, not emergent mechanics | [Pass 3] Reduced 3D AP shell: Donnell/Winkler elastic line ell_B^4 D'''' - ell_N^2 D'' + k_rel(z) D = D_2D(t) chi_meso(z) on the prolate ellipsoid (exact kappa_z, kappa_theta; k_pole/k_eq = 13x), driven by the ring depth at each snapshot with a germband-extension tension ramp, swept into a 65x81 theta x z shell mesh; sweeps over ell_N (0-150 um, ablation ratio 0.53, monotone) and a/b (1.5-4.0) | [Pass 3] Variable-viscosity Stokes flow (stream-function form, 35x192 grid, 6,110 unknowns) inside the Phase-I lengthening mesoderm cell with incompressible-trapezoid boundary kinematics, a 50x-viscosity nucleus (v_nuc/v_cyto = 0.983, rigid-body CV 0.004), exact affine verification (L2 8.1e-13) and a Phase-I nuclear trajectory (4.5 um basal displacement over 16.2 um lengthening) | Automated 4-stage confocal cross-section segmentation and ventral apical Myosin-II red enrichment analysis on drosophila_ventral_furrow_specimen.jpg (DV/ML = 1.0496 -> 0.9217, MyoII enrichment = 1.63x, trajectory r = 0.9993); transfer_boundary: The AP coupling is a 1D elastic line with a curvature-weighted Winkler foundation and a kinematic circumferential sweep; ell_B = 22 um and the WT ell_N ramp to 30 um are model assumptions not measured in any cited paper, and N_GB is not calibrated to Lye et al. (2015) ablation recoil | The Stokes solve is 2D on a fixed rectangle frozen at t = 1.8 min with velocity (not stress) boundary data; nucleus size/position are order-of-magnitude values; the He et al. (2014) comparison is the qualitative passive-tracer ratio ~1, not a digitised velocity field | The 2D ring depth that drives both new layers is pinned to the Conte (2012) / Martin (2009) reference values at the last step, so the 6-regime r = 1.0000 is a consistency check of the calibration, not an independent prediction; does_not_claim: A 3D finite-element shell with coupled membrane/bending stresses, a moving-boundary (ALE) or 3D Stokes solve with cortical actomyosin stress boundary conditions, emergent (un-pinned) invagination depth from the viscous-vertex mechanics, or subcellular Rho1/Rok reaction-diffusion signaling." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 2012-he-drosophila-ventral-furrow.py:332-369, 443-445, 455-458 — the ring depth and cell height are target-pinned interpolants (`target_depth_um`, `target_h_um` equal to the reference values; `depth_um = target_depth_um * min(1, ...)` and forced at the last step). Replace with an actual force balance on the 64-cell ring (apical/basal/lateral line tensions gamma_ap, gamma_ba, gamma_lat + vitelline contact + yolk pressure, overdamped vertex dynamics) so that D_furrow and h emerge, and re-score the 6-regime comparison as a prediction rather than a calibration check.",
            "remediation needed: 2012-he-drosophila-ventral-furrow.py:578-624 — the 15x15 morphospace is an analytic surrogate (`ap_factor`, `d_val`, `h_val`) rather than ring re-simulation; once the ring mechanics are un-pinned, regenerate the morphospace by running the ring at each (r_twist, sigma_synergy) grid point.",
            "remediation needed: 2012-he-drosophila-ventral-furrow.py:646-719 and 721-793 — the AP coupling is one-way (ring -> line) and kinematic in theta: D(z) is swept with a fixed Gaussian pocket shape and there is no membrane/bending stress feedback from the AP profile onto the ring. Upgrade to a two-way coupled thin-shell (Koiter or Donnell) solve on the theta x z mesh with the active apical tension as a surface load, or at minimum make the pocket width a function of D(z).",
            "remediation needed: 2012-he-drosophila-ventral-furrow.py:855-1003 — the Stokes domain is a fixed rectangle at a single instant (t = 1.8 min) with velocity boundary data; the nucleus is an elliptical viscosity inclusion of assumed size/position. Move to a moving-boundary (ALE or level-set) trapezoid solved at every Phase-I step with an apical actomyosin stress BC and a force-free rigid nucleus (Lagrange multiplier), and compare the resolved nuclear trajectory to digitised nuclear positions from He et al. (2014) Fig. 1.",
            "remediation needed: datasets/drosophila_ventral_furrow/ap_shell_stokes_reference.json:54-62 — ell_B = 22 um and the WT ell_N ramp to 30 um are uncalibrated assumptions; the ablation ratio measurement has no reference. Calibrate N_GB / k_eq from published laser-ablation recoil during germband extension (Lye et al. 2015; Collinet et al. 2015) and ell_B from the blastoderm bending modulus, and digitise the furrow AP extent from a ventral-view micrograph (Sweeton et al. 1991 Fig. 1) instead of the 0.65 EL literature estimate.",
            "remediation needed: datasets/drosophila_ventral_furrow/paper_citations.bib:45-83 — the Sweeton (1991), Leptin & Grunewald (1990) and Lye (2015) DOIs were added offline and flagged unverified; verify them (and add Collinet et al. 2015) when network access is available." ;
        ns1:hasScore 8.99e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-he-drosophila-ventral-furrow-parameter-expressivity> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Conte et al. (2012), Martin et al. (2009) & He et al. (2014) Drosophila ventral furrow invagination biomechanics — Parameter expressivity: 93/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "The 6-regime evaluator and the 15x15 (r_twist x sigma_synergy) morphospace are retained, and Pass 3 adds two genuine physical sweep axes with monotone, theorem-backed behaviour: germband-extension tension ell_N in {0, 25, ..., 150} um reduces D(0.5 EL) monotonically from 41.0 to 21.9 um (ablation ratio 0.534; Theorem 4) and lengthens the half-depth extent, and egg aspect ratio a/b in {1.5, ..., 4.0} raises the polar stiffening ratio monotonically. Deductions: the 15x15 morphospace is still an analytic surrogate rather than re-running the ring (L578-624) (-4); the nucleus viscosity ratio and position are not swept (-3)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
