    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-honda-dichotomous-tree-branching-specimen-match> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Honda (1971) J. Theor. Biol. & Honda & Fisher (1978) Science 3D recursive dichotomous tree branching, effective leaf area optimization, Leonardo da Vinci pipe-model area conservation, and solar-elevation ray tracing of tiered crowns vs latitude — Morphological realism / specimen match: 90/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Vendors and SHA-256-verifies the Botanic Garden Meise Pagoda Dogwood specimen (960x1280 px), segments variegated foliage shelves and detects 7 horizontal pagoda tiers and 25 Y-bifurcations (`segment_cornus_controversa_specimen`, L829-969), and Pass 3 adds the specimen's inter-tier spacing / tier half-width s/R = 0.376 +- 0.134 over 6 tier pairs (`measure_specimen_tier_spacing`, L786-824) which is overlaid as a band on the E(s/R) curves and as a tier-spacing overlay panel in the new solar figure. The specimen is compared with the model in both PNGs. Deductions: the junction acceptance windows 12-50 deg / 30-82 deg and beta in [0.65, 1.45] (L933-935) pre-filter the Y-fork statistics toward the Honda & Fisher range, so theta_1 = 22.40, theta_2 = 50.93 and beta = 0.9533 are partially prescribed (-4); ROI box, foliage percentile 72 and wood percentile 78 (L843, L850, L871) are hand-tuned to this one image (-2); the s/R ratio is a projected photographic quantity without perspective or tilt correction, and the foliage column-density threshold 0.15 and +-12 px band (L786-801) are unsourced (-2); the specimen reference values the measurements are compared against are regressions of this script's own earlier output (-2)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-specimen-match> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/specimen-match" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "1976-honda-dichotomous-tree-branching.py L933–L935: Junction acceptance windows 12-50 / 30-82 deg and beta in [0.65, 1.45] pre-select forks inside the expected Honda & Fisher range <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/1976-honda-dichotomous-tree-branching.py#L933-L935>" ;
        ns1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-honda-dichotomous-tree-branching-specimen-match-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-honda-dichotomous-tree-branching-specimen-match-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-honda-dichotomous-tree-branching-specimen-match-3>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-honda-dichotomous-tree-branching-specimen-match-4> ;
        ns1:hasScore 9e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-code-traceability> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Hubaud, Regev, Mahadevan & Pourquié (2017) excitable FitzHugh-Nagumo segmentation clock gated by YAP mechanotransduction, with FGF/Wnt clock-and-wavefront arrest and stiffness-LATS-YAP kinetics (Pass 3) — Code-to-model traceability: 91/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Each Pass 3 section header and docstring names the law, the source and the Lean theorem it implements (Sections 4b-4d), the math KG registers six equations with lean_locus and code_locus, and the figure panels, measurements and self-test checks are labelled by law. Deductions: the FGF gate form g(F) = F^h/(F_thr^h + F^h) with F_thr = 0.15, h = 4 and gamma_F = 1.6 is traced to no equation or figure of any cited paper (-4); the mechanical constants E_50 = 10 kPa, A_50 = 500 um^2, m = 3, k_exp = 1/12, k_PP = 1/20 and tau_actin = 8 min are declared as module constants without citations (-3); the Kuramoto phase is an atan2 around the fixed point, which is not a protophase correction and is uncited (-1); the ensemble/logistic mismatch at L447-456 is undocumented (-1)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "2016-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation.py L720–L723: Defect: Hill gate g(F) and its F_thr / h_F defaults are not traced to a published equation <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2016-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation.py#L720-L723>",
            "2016-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation.py L957–L965: Defect: mechanical constants E_50, h_E, A_50, m_L, r0, k_exp, k_PP, tau_actin, overexpression factor declared without source citations <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2016-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation.py#L957-L965>" ;
        ns1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-code-traceability-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-code-traceability-2> ;
        ns1:hasScore 9.1e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-model-fidelity> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Hubaud, Regev, Mahadevan & Pourquié (2017) excitable FitzHugh-Nagumo segmentation clock gated by YAP mechanotransduction, with FGF/Wnt clock-and-wavefront arrest and stiffness-LATS-YAP kinetics (Pass 3) — Model fidelity to source: 93/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "The published FHN fast-slow core, YAP gate and 2D excitable PDE are unchanged and verified (Laws 1-3, L171-604). Pass 3 adds the two missing mechanisms the v2 audit asked for and proves their governing identities in Lean (Theorems 4-6): the regressing exponential Fgf8 gradient (Dubrulle 2001) gating I_eff with an arrest criterion that reproduces S = v_wf T to 0.3% and the analytic front offset to 0.4% (L707-886), and a three-state YAP import/export/phosphorylation cycle whose monotonicity in tension and LATS is proved cross-multiplied (L954-1139). Deductions: the FGF gate gamma_F (g(F) - 1) is additive and phenomenological rather than an Fgf8/Wnt3a/Hes7 circuit, and gamma_F had to be raised from 0.8 to 1.6 for the excitable waves to actually arrest at the front, which is a tuned rather than derived number (-3); the 6-regime benchmark's 200-cell ensemble (L447-453) is computed but never used - the predicted oscillating fraction is a logistic of the deterministic I_eff with a hand-set margin 0.115 and width 0.125 (L451-456), so the r = 0.9976 reflects two fitted constants rather than ensemble dynamics (-3); the cascade keeps a LATS branch that Dupont (2011) found largely dispensable for the stiffness response (disclosed, -1)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "2016-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation.py L447–L456: Defect: 200-cell ensemble osc_mask is computed but pred_frac is a hand-tuned logistic of the deterministic I_eff (margin 0.115, width 0.125); the ensemble only feeds a reporting field <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2016-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation.py#L447-L456>" ;
        ns1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-model-fidelity-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-model-fidelity-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-model-fidelity-3>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-model-fidelity-4>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-model-fidelity-5>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-model-fidelity-6> ;
        ns1:hasScore 9.3e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-morphometric-validation> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Hubaud, Regev, Mahadevan & Pourquié (2017) excitable FitzHugh-Nagumo segmentation clock gated by YAP mechanotransduction, with FGF/Wnt clock-and-wavefront arrest and stiffness-LATS-YAP kinetics (Pass 3) — Morphometric validation: 93/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "`measure_morphoeval()` (L1218-1352) now returns 11 reference-anchored measurements: the five v2 ones plus stripe spacing S vs v_wf T and the ~100 um mouse somite anchor, the Cooke-Zeeman slope vs T, the cascade RMSE vs the regime table, E_crit vs the Dupont bracket, the LatA onset latency vs one clock period, and the Kuramoto R vs complete synchrony with an uncoupled control; each carries a unit, method and note with the ablation / sweep numbers. Deductions: several new references are analytic or bracket values rather than measured specimen numbers (S vs v_wf T is a self-consistency check of the chain against its own tail-bud period; E_crit's 5.3 kPa 'reference' is a geometric midpoint; the LatA onset reference is an upper bound) (-4); the mouse somite length anchor is an order-of-magnitude value with no digitised Gomez (2008) table vendored (-2); the specimen CV 0.201 is never contrasted with the model CV 0.024 (-1)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
        ns1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-measurement-6-regime-yap-notch-perturbation-oscillating-cell-fraction-pearson-correlation-r>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-measurement-cooke-zeeman-sweep-slope-ds-dv-wf-across-5-wavefront-speeds>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-measurement-critical-nuclear-yap-excitability-threshold-y-nuc-crit-at-j-dll1-0>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-measurement-dll1-notch-juxtacrine-coupling-kuramoto-order-parameter-r-at-j-max-0-15>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-measurement-fgf-wnt-wavefront-arrested-somite-stripe-spacing-s-model-1d-ap-excitable-chain>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-measurement-fitzhugh-nagumo-supercritical-hopf-bifurcation-threshold-u-h>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-measurement-latrunculin-a-dynamic-rescue-oscillation-onset-latency-after-f-actin-depolymerisation>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-measurement-latrunculin-a-yap-inhibited-autonomous-oscillation-period-t-osc>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-measurement-predicted-critical-substrate-stiffness-e-crit-for-spread-psm-cells-y-nuc-y-nuc-crit>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-measurement-vertebrate-somite-psm-specimen-bilateral-somite-spacing-s-obs>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-measurement-yap-mechanotransduction-cascade-y-nuc-rmse-across-5-wild-type-hubaud-regimes>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-morphometric-validation-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-morphometric-validation-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-morphometric-validation-3> ;
        ns1:hasScore 9.3e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-overall> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Hubaud, Regev, Mahadevan & Pourquié (2017) excitable FitzHugh-Nagumo segmentation clock gated by YAP mechanotransduction, with FGF/Wnt clock-and-wavefront arrest and stiffness-LATS-YAP kinetics (Pass 3) — MorphoEval overall 91.8/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 3 post-remediation evaluation of `2016-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation.py` (91.8/100, v2 91.7). Both v2 remediation items are closed: the excitable FHN core is now coupled along a 1D anteroposterior axis to an explicit regressing Fgf8/Wnt gradient through a Hill gate on I_eff, so that the clock arrests at a moving determination front and freezes a Mesp2-like stripe pattern whose spacing (101.7 um) matches the Cooke-Zeeman law v_wf T (102.0 um) across a 5-point v_wf sweep (slope 144.8 min vs T 145.7 min, r 0.99998), with lambda_F controlling PSM length (407-735 um) but not S, gamma_F controlling whether excitable pulses leak anteriorly (802 um at 0.8, 0 um at the default 1.6) and uniform FGF abolishing the stripes; and nuclear YAP is now produced by a substrate-stiffness -> F-actin -> LATS1/2 -> YAP phosphorylation / import cascade calibrated on the five wild-type regimes (RMSE 0.054), predicting E_crit = 12.6 kPa inside the Dupont (2011) 0.7-40 kPa bracket and a dynamic Latrunculin A ignition 30.8 min after F-actin loss, while J_Dll1 became an explicit juxtacrine Dll1-Notch coupling that synchronises a heterogeneous ring (R 0.27 -> 0.80). Three new Lean 4 theorems (Theorems 4-6) back the new mathematics (6 total, 0 sorrys). The round also surfaced the next layer of defects: the 200-cell ensemble in the 6-regime benchmark is decorative (the predicted fraction is a hand-tuned logistic of I_eff), the vendored specimen is a chick embryo SEM filed as mouse with no um scale, the FGF gate and several mechanical constants are uncited modelling choices, the cascade cannot reproduce the non-monotonic Y-27632 vs high-density pair, and the PSM clock has no phase gradient outside ~50 um of the front. Overall 91.8/100 (faithfulness 91.5, reproducibility 92.4); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit d58a084; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 93, Morphological realism / specimen match 88, Parameter expressivity 95, Morphometric validation 93, Source and data traceability 94, Code-to-model traceability 91, Reproducibility package 92. Output judged: docs/media/yap_excitable_segmentation_comparison.png: rendered output of 2016-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation.py at d58a084, image/png, 1578308 B, 2775×2475 px, artifact_sha256 b03f6304bef6d56658a46a97e5ad6da8f0d2c23af33d12f3eadf74f3fcac9db6 (sha256 b03f6304bef6d56658a46a97e5ad6da8f0d2c23af33d12f3eadf74f3fcac9db6), spec_fingerprint eb7a0a2051924df9834d2292bd3eca5cca883f40d58bf2c4618667071ccac50f. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: eb7a0a2051924df9834d2292bd3eca5cca883f40d58bf2c4618667071ccac50f; artifact_sha256: b03f6304bef6d56658a46a97e5ad6da8f0d2c23af33d12f3eadf74f3fcac9db6; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/yap_excitable_segmentation/mouse_psm_somites_specimen.jpg=8b80971796cb29e2..., datasets/yap_excitable_segmentation/scout_manifest.json=852a6ed7852f291d..., datasets/yap_excitable_segmentation/yap_excitable_segmentation_reference.json=afec7ed9c8b4fd64...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-yap-excitable-segmentation-audit-v2. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Hubaud, Regev, Mahadevan & Pourquie (2017) Cell 171:668-682 FitzHugh-Nagumo excitable oscillator model of primary mouse presomitic mesoderm (PSM) cells gated by nuclear YAP mechanotransduction | Quiescent excitable state in isolated spread fibronectin PSM cells (high nuclear YAP) rescued into ~140 min autonomous LuVeLu oscillations by Latrunculin A, Y-27632 (Rockout), or Yap1 inhibition, and blocked by constitutively active Yap5SA | Cooke & Zeeman (1976) clock-and-wavefront law S = v_wf T; Dubrulle, McGrew & Pourquie (2001) posterior-high fgf8 mRNA gradient regressing with axis elongation and positioning the determination front; Dupont et al. (2011) YAP/TAZ cytoplasmic on ~0.7 kPa and nuclear on ~40 kPa fibronectin hydrogels under Rho/F-actin control; Wada et al. (2011) stress fibres inhibit LATS1/2; reconstructed_in_script: Analytical cubic nullcline continuation, Jacobian spectrum, and supercritical Hopf bifurcation diagram across Y_nuc in [0, 1] (|u_H| = 0.9675, Y_crit = 0.6109) | RK4 single-cell & ensemble simulations across all 6 Hubaud et al. (2017) perturbation regimes (Pearson r = 0.9976, RMSE = 0.0469) plus subthreshold vs suprathreshold single-pulse excitability | 2D reaction-diffusion mPSM target-wave PDE solver with Yap5SA constitutive block control and bilateral somite DoG peak segmentation on mouse_psm_somites_specimen.jpg (47.14 px mean spacing, CV = 0.2010) | [Pass 3] 1D anteroposterior excitable chain with juxtacrine Dll1-Notch coupling and a regressing Fgf8/Wnt gradient: arrest front g(F) = g_crit, frozen-phase Mesp2-like switch, 8 stripes with S = 101.7 um vs v_wf T = 102.0 um (CV 0.024), 0 um anterior pulse leak at gamma_F = 1.6 (802 um at 0.8), v_wf / lambda_F / gamma_F sweeps and uniform-FGF ablation (0 stripes) | [Pass 3] Stiffness -> F-actin tension -> LATS1/2 -> three-state YAP kinetics cascade fitted to the five wild-type regimes (RMSE 0.054), E_crit = 12.6 kPa, dynamic Latrunculin A rescue (onset 30.8 min, period 142.5 min), and a 48-cell Dll1-Notch ring synchrony sweep (Kuramoto R 0.27 -> 0.80); transfer_boundary: Fast-slow 2-variable FitzHugh-Nagumo phenomenological reduction of the Notch/FGF/Wnt/YAP mouse PSM segmentation clock compared with a dorsal chick-embryo somite SEM (Wikimedia 'Aves_Neural_tube_and_somites_in_chick_embryo.jpg', filed as mouse_psm_somites_specimen.jpg) whose px spacing has no um calibration | The FGF/Wnt gate acts additively on I_eff (gamma_F (g(F) - 1)) and the determination front is defined by the Hopf margin, which is a reduced reading of Hubaud et al. (2017) Fig. 7 and of the clock-and-wavefront literature, not an equation published in the source paper; the chain is 1D with no cell flow, convergent extension or mediolateral extent | The YAP cascade is a lumped ODE keeping both a LATS-dependent branch (Wada 2011) and a LATS-independent tension-driven import branch; Dupont et al. (2011) reported the stiffness response as largely LATS-independent, and the E_50 = 10 kPa, A_50 = 500 um^2, m = 3, k_exp, k_PP, tau_actin constants are modelling choices, not measured values; does_not_claim: Explicit molecular transcriptional-translational delay equations for Hes7/Lfng/Axin2, a PSM-wide period/phase gradient (Lauschke 2013 kinematic waves are only reproduced within ~50 um of the front), 3D focal-adhesion traction force microscopy, or the mouse somite AP length beyond an order-of-magnitude anchor (~100 um, Gomez et al. 2008)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 2016-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation.py:447-456 — the 200-cell ensemble (y_samples, j_samples, osc_mask) is computed but `pred_frac` is a logistic of the deterministic I_eff with a hand-set detection margin (0.115) and width (0.125), so the 6-regime Pearson r = 0.9976 reflects two tuned constants rather than ensemble dynamics. Use the ensemble fraction (np.mean(osc_mask), or RK4 on each sampled cell) as the prediction, or derive the margin/width from the ensemble sigma_Y / sigma_J, and report the fit honestly.",
            "remediation needed: 2016-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation.py:687-701 and 621-684 — the J_max -> Kuramoto R sweep is not strictly monotone (it saturates: 0.802 at J_max = 0.20 vs 0.801 at 0.30, Spearman 0.94) and the phase is an atan2 around the fixed point rather than a protophase-corrected phase; use a Hilbert / protophase estimator, average over several seeds and heterogeneity levels, and compare with Riedel-Kruse (2007) or Hubaud (2017) dissociation-reaggregation synchrony data.",
            "remediation needed: 2016-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation.py:720-748 — the FGF/Wnt gate g(F) = F^h/(F_thr^h + F^h) with F_thr = 0.15, h = 4 and gamma_F = 1.6 is a phenomenological additive term on I_eff; gamma_F had to be tuned from 0.8 to 1.6 for the excitable pulses to arrest at the front. Replace it with (or calibrate it against) an explicit Fgf8/Wnt3a -> Hes7/Lfng input taken from a cited model, and vendor the Dubrulle (2001) fgf8 gradient profile as a fixture.",
            "remediation needed: 2016-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation.py:750-886 — the clock is quasi-synchronous across the PSM and only slows within ~50 um of the front (Panel G), so the Lauschke (2013) phase-gradient / kinematic travelling waves are not reproduced. Add a posterior-to-anterior period gradient (e.g. tau_v(x) or I_eff(x) ramp) and measure the wave speed and phase-gradient wavelength against Lauschke et al. (2013) mPSM values.",
            "remediation needed: 2016-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation.py:957-965 and 1000-1031 — the cascade constants (E_50 = 10 kPa, A_50 = 500 um^2, m = 3, k_exp = 1/12, k_PP = 1/20, tau_actin = 8 min, 2x Yap5SA overexpression) and the per-regime mechanical inputs are uncited modelling assignments, and the tension-only cascade cannot reproduce the non-monotonic Y-27632 (0.30) vs high-density mPSM (0.18) pair (RMSE floor 0.054). Vendor Dupont (2011) / Wada (2011) measured values, add a density / contact-inhibition term, and store the fitted (alpha_T, kappa_LATS, T_L) as a pinned fixture.",
            "remediation needed: datasets/yap_excitable_segmentation/yap_excitable_segmentation_reference.json:50-58 and 2016-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation.py:1173-1214 — the vendored SEM is a chick embryo ('Aves_Neural_tube_and_somites_in_chick_embryo.jpg') filed as mouse_psm_somites_specimen.jpg, with no um per px scale, so neither the organism nor the 100 um stripe spacing can be compared with it. Add a correctly named mouse PSM specimen (or relabel as chick and change the organism claim), record a scale, and compare S_model (um) with the specimen in um." ;
        ns1:hasScore 9.18e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-parameter-expressivity> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Hubaud, Regev, Mahadevan & Pourquié (2017) excitable FitzHugh-Nagumo segmentation clock gated by YAP mechanotransduction, with FGF/Wnt clock-and-wavefront arrest and stiffness-LATS-YAP kinetics (Pass 3) — Parameter expressivity: 95/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Every new morphospace parameter is swept and behaves monotonically as claimed: v_wf -> S linearly (5 points, slope 144.8 min = T, r 0.99998), lambda_F -> PSM length (407 / 571 / 735 um vs analytic 410 / 574 / 737) with S unchanged, gamma_F -> anterior pulse leak (802 um at 0.8, 0 um at >= 1.2), uniform FGF -> 0 stripes, E_sub -> Y_nuc monotone with E_crit inside the Dupont bracket, J_max -> Kuramoto R (0.27 -> 0.80, Spearman 0.94), plus the v2 Y_nuc bifurcation sweep and 6-regime suite. New CLI flags --v-wf, --lambda-F and --E-sub expose the two mechanisms. Deductions: the J_max -> R relation is not strictly monotone (it saturates: 0.802 at 0.20 vs 0.801 at 0.30; Spearman 0.94) and the ring uses a tau_v CV fixed at 0.04 (-3); the sweeps are reported as numbers and one scatter panel, without rendered stripe patterns along the v_wf sweep (-2)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
        ns1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-parameter-expressivity-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-parameter-expressivity-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-parameter-expressivity-3>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-parameter-expressivity-4> ;
        ns1:hasScore 9.5e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-repro-package> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Hubaud, Regev, Mahadevan & Pourquié (2017) excitable FitzHugh-Nagumo segmentation clock gated by YAP mechanotransduction, with FGF/Wnt clock-and-wavefront arrest and stiffness-LATS-YAP kinetics (Pass 3) — Reproducibility package: 92/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Deterministic seeds (2016) throughout, bitwise determinism asserted for both the 2D PDE and the new 1D chain, a least-squares calibration that is deterministic from fixed initial guesses, --self-test with the Pass 3 checks (stripe count, CV, S vs v_wf T, PSM length vs analytic, ablation, sweep slope, lambda_F invariance, wave arrest vs leak control, cascade RMSE, regime states, E_crit bracket, LatA onset, R monotonicity, 11 measurements with reference values) passing in ~6 s, and the default invocation regenerating the PNG and GIF in ~13 s. Deductions: no requirements lock file is vendored for this slot (-4); the GIF/PNG are not asserted byte-identical across runs (only the model arrays are) (-2); the calibration result depends on scipy.optimize internals and is not pinned by a stored fitted-parameter fixture (-2)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-repro-package> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
