            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-specimen-match-3> ;
        ns1:hasScore 8.8e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-ibrahim-vascular-angiogenesis-notch-code-traceability> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Bentley, Gerhardt & Bates (2008) PLoS Comput. Biol., Hellström et al. (2007) Nature & Jakobsson et al. (2010) Nat. Cell Biol. VEGF-VEGFR2-Dll4-Notch1 tip/stalk salt-and-pepper lateral inhibition and angiogenic sprouting, coupled to lumenized Poiseuille flow, wall-shear pruning and arteriovenous specification (Pass 3) — Code-to-model traceability: 88/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "The module docstring (L1-100) maps every governing equation of Sections 2-3b to its paper and to the five Lean theorems with file#line pins; the Section 3b banner (L519-535) states the reduced-model scope and residuals explicitly; `pries_shear_set_point_pa`, `solve_poiseuille_network`, `fit_murray_exponent` and `simulate_perfused_plexus_remodeling` cite Pries 1995/1998, Murray 1926, Chen 2012 and Franco 2015 in their docstrings; the math-KG YAML registers equations 1-5 with single-range code loci. Deductions: the Hill templates in `evaluate_notch_gain_sweep` (L1337-1349) and the regime branches at L313-380 are not documented as prescriptions in the module docstring, which still describes the sweep as reproducing the benchmark (-5); the lumenization coefficients and AV gains are uncited (-3); Panel E legend still reads \"Simulated (Pass 2)\" (L1831) and the lumen docstring (L680-681) is wrong about DAPT (-2); the counter-current comment at L761-765 claims a position-independence that the WT result contradicts (-2)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "2021-ibrahim-vascular-angiogenesis-notch.py L1828–L1832: Panel E legend still says 'Simulated (Pass 2)'; refs_primary hard-coded here rather than read from the reference JSON <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/2021-ibrahim-vascular-angiogenesis-notch.py#L1828-L1832>",
            "2021-ibrahim-vascular-angiogenesis-notch.py L761–L765: Comment claims counter-current layout makes competition calibre- rather than position-dependent; WT survivors cluster near the inlet with one 9 um rung <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/2021-ibrahim-vascular-angiogenesis-notch.py#L761-L765>" ;
        ns1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-ibrahim-vascular-angiogenesis-notch-code-traceability-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-ibrahim-vascular-angiogenesis-notch-code-traceability-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-ibrahim-vascular-angiogenesis-notch-code-traceability-3> ;
        ns1:hasScore 8.8e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-ibrahim-vascular-angiogenesis-notch-model-fidelity> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Bentley, Gerhardt & Bates (2008) PLoS Comput. Biol., Hellström et al. (2007) Nature & Jakobsson et al. (2010) Nat. Cell Biol. VEGF-VEGFR2-Dll4-Notch1 tip/stalk salt-and-pepper lateral inhibition and angiogenic sprouting, coupled to lumenized Poiseuille flow, wall-shear pruning and arteriovenous specification (Pass 3) — Model fidelity to source: 85/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Credited: the Brillouin k = pi stability verifier (L182-224), the M = 16 VEGFR2-Dll4-Notch1 + 2D sprouting solver (L245-483), and the new hemodynamic layer — an exact Poiseuille/Kirchhoff resistor solve (L773-845), the Pries set point tau_e(P) implemented as published (L641-662), log-sensing adaptation with metabolic stimulus and shrinkage bias plus topological pruning (L912-1198), a Notch -> lumen coupling point (L665-690), and the shear-only-shunt / uniform-shear / no-flow ablations (L1210-1240) whose outcomes match Pries 1998 and Chen 2012 qualitatively; five Lean 4 theorems (0 sorrys) formalise the mechanisms. Deductions: `evaluate_notch_gain_sweep` simulates only k_t = 0 and returns closed-form Hill templates (`hill_rec`, `hill_alt`, L1337-1349) for the other 7 points, so Panel C and measurement 7 are not model output (-6); `simulate_vessel_notch_sprouting` carries regime-specific hard-coded branches — the Dll4+/- quartet mask forcing 75% tips (L313, L327-333, L370), a prescribed high-VEGF sinusoid (L339), hand-set mosaic targets n_target[14]/[15] (L347-348), and the DAPT state overwritten each step (L378-380) — so the benchmark regimes are steered rather than emergent (-6); the WT Murray exponent is 3.53 (+18%) and the remodelled bed keeps one dominant proximal rung at the 9 um radius clip, contradicting the counter-current comment (L761-765) that competition is calibre- not position-dependent (-2); the AV readout is one-way (no shear -> Dll4/Notch feedback), the ladder topology is imposed and the plexus is quasi-static with constant viscosity (-1, disclosed at L525-534)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "2021-ibrahim-vascular-angiogenesis-notch.py L1308–L1377: evaluate_notch_gain_sweep: only k_t = 0 calls the simulator; k_t > 0 uses closed-form Hill templates hill_rec / hill_alt (L1337-1349) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/2021-ibrahim-vascular-angiogenesis-notch.py#L1308-L1377>",
            "2021-ibrahim-vascular-angiogenesis-notch.py L313–L380: Regime-specific hard-coded branches: is_dll4_haplo quartet mask (L313, L327-333), 0.78*d_target (L370), high-VEGF osc_drive sinusoid (L339), mosaic n_target[14]/[15] (L347-348), DAPT state forced each step (L378-380) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/2021-ibrahim-vascular-angiogenesis-notch.py#L313-L380>" ;
        ns1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-ibrahim-vascular-angiogenesis-notch-model-fidelity-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-ibrahim-vascular-angiogenesis-notch-model-fidelity-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-ibrahim-vascular-angiogenesis-notch-model-fidelity-3>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-ibrahim-vascular-angiogenesis-notch-model-fidelity-4>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-ibrahim-vascular-angiogenesis-notch-model-fidelity-5>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-ibrahim-vascular-angiogenesis-notch-model-fidelity-6> ;
        ns1:hasScore 8.5e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-ibrahim-vascular-angiogenesis-notch-morphometric-validation> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Bentley, Gerhardt & Bates (2008) PLoS Comput. Biol., Hellström et al. (2007) Nature & Jakobsson et al. (2010) Nat. Cell Biol. VEGF-VEGFR2-Dll4-Notch1 tip/stalk salt-and-pepper lateral inhibition and angiogenic sprouting, coupled to lumenized Poiseuille flow, wall-shear pruning and arteriovenous specification (Pass 3) — Morphometric validation: 83/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "`measure_morphoeval()` (L2045-2223) now returns 14 reference-anchored measurements; the five new hemodynamic metrics (L2078-2131) are WT median capillary wall shear stress 1.0555 Pa (ref 1.5, band 1-2), emergent Murray exponent 3.5264 (ref 3.0), max Kirchhoff residual 6.7e-26 m^3/s (ref 0), DAPT/WT perfused-density ratio 1.625 (ref 1.5, band 1.3-2.0) and WT AV segregation index 1.0 (ref 1.0; DAPT 0.5, no-flow 0.5), all with units, method, source and reference pulled from the SHA-256-pinned JSON; the nine Pass 2 values are unchanged. Deductions: measurement 7 (sweep Pearson r = 0.998, L2192-2201) is a template fit, not a simulation-vs-benchmark statistic (-5); measurements 8-9 (L2202-2221) use reference values 0.1967 and 0.8406 that are the script's own segmentation outputs, so they are self-referential (-4); measurements 1-6 compare regimes whose outcomes are steered by hard-coded branches (L313-380) to the benchmarks they were steered to (-3); the Murray exponent misses the band [2.7, 3.3] by 0.23 and the self-test widens the band by +/-0.4 to pass (L2307-2308) (-2); the AV index is saturated so measurement 14 hitting 1.0 is weakly discriminating, and three references are bands/qualitative rather than points (-3)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "2021-ibrahim-vascular-angiogenesis-notch.py L2192–L2201: Measurement 7: Pearson r of the Section 4 sweep, whose k_t > 0 points are templates (circular) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/2021-ibrahim-vascular-angiogenesis-notch.py#L2192-L2201>",
            "2021-ibrahim-vascular-angiogenesis-notch.py L2202–L2221: Measurements 8-9: reference_value 0.1967 / 0.8406 are the script's own specimen segmentation outputs, not external values <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/2021-ibrahim-vascular-angiogenesis-notch.py#L2202-L2221>",
            "2021-ibrahim-vascular-angiogenesis-notch.py L2306–L2309: Self-test widens the Murray band by +/-0.4 (k = 3.53 vs band [2.7, 3.3]) to pass <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/2021-ibrahim-vascular-angiogenesis-notch.py#L2306-L2309>" ;
        ns1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-ibrahim-vascular-angiogenesis-notch-measurement-dapt-notch-blockade-k-t-0-0-all-tip-hypersprouting-fraction>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-ibrahim-vascular-angiogenesis-notch-measurement-dll4-haploinsufficiency-heterozygote-tip-cell-fraction>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-ibrahim-vascular-angiogenesis-notch-measurement-high-uniform-vegf-overload-synchronous-dll4-oscillation-cv>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-ibrahim-vascular-angiogenesis-notch-measurement-huvec-angiogenic-sprouting-plexus-specimen-sprouting-tip-to-junction-ratio>,
