    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-meinhardt-echinoderm-pentaradial-symmetry-specimen-match> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Morris (2012), Mooi & David (1998/2008), Lovén (1874), Duboc et al. (2005), Luo & Su (2012) & Meinhardt (2008) echinoderm bilateral-to-pentaradial hydrocoel ring symmetry breaking with Ocular Plate Rule test growth — Morphological realism / specimen match: 89/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Credited: the Tripneustes gratilla test segmentation (L916-962) is unchanged and now shares a single polar chromaticity + azimuthal FFT pipeline (`polar_c5_harmonics`, L759-800) with the synthetic OPR test projection (L739-756), so the specimen and the model are measured identically; the specimen's ambulacral duty cycle (0.575) calibrates the synthetic ambulacral width; the 9-panel comparison figure places the specimen (Panel E), its spectrum (Panel F) and the plated dome / harmonics inset (Panels G, I) side by side; the OPR figure insets both images. Deductions: a synthetic exactly five-fold test has C_5 ~ 1 regardless of plate kinetics, so the 0.9964 vs 0.9255 comparison discriminates nothing about the accretion model (-4); detected synthetic ray angles [7, 80, 138, 210, 281] are noisy because the synthetic profile has flat tops (-2); the species mismatch (header organism S. purpuratus, specimen and \"trigeminate\" argument T. gratilla) persists (-3); no plate-level comparison (plate counts per column, plate outlines) is made against the specimen, which is the morphology the new solver actually produces (-3)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-specimen-match> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/specimen-match" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "models/2005-meinhardt-echinoderm-pentaradial-symmetry.py L1630–L1636: Aboral C_5 measurement uses the specimen's own C_5 as reference and the specimen-calibrated duty cycle; near-trivial for an exactly 5-fold synthetic test <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a69596cc/models/2005-meinhardt-echinoderm-pentaradial-symmetry.py#L1630-L1636>" ;
        ns1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-meinhardt-echinoderm-pentaradial-symmetry-specimen-match-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-meinhardt-echinoderm-pentaradial-symmetry-specimen-match-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-meinhardt-echinoderm-pentaradial-symmetry-specimen-match-3>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-meinhardt-echinoderm-pentaradial-symmetry-specimen-match-4> ;
        ns1:hasScore 8.9e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing-code-traceability> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Menshykau & Iber (2013), Zubkov et al. (2015) & Watanabe & Costantini (2004) kidney ureteric bud GDNF-RET-Wnt11 Turing branching morphogenesis with stromal BMP4/7-Gremlin1-FGF7 feedback and reduced-3D ampulla necking — Code-to-model traceability: 89/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "The module docstring (L1-67) maps every section to its source equations and the Pass 3 additions name their functions, the Lean laws and the honesty control; the math-KG loop file registers Laws 4 and 5 with Lean declarations, variables, roles and `code_locus` line ranges (`menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing.yaml`, L93-129); the Lean file's Law 4/5 headers state the Python function each theorem formalises (L159-205); `solve_ampulla_cap_imex` carries an explicit HONESTY NOTE about the seeded staircase (L342-346) and the removed hand-placed buds are documented in place (L756). Deductions: the calibration constants `gain_wt_ref`, `g_ref`, `size_jitter_sd` (L726-728), `R_TIP_WT_DEFAULT`, `TIP_RADIUS_SIGNAL_EXPONENT` (L102-103), the Gaussian amplitudes/widths (L774-789) and the saturating cubic (L403) are flagged as model choices but cite no derivation (-5); `compute_turing_phase_space` is dead code with a nonsensical `sigma_proxy` (L297-301) (-3); Lean Law 3 `tip_splitting_peaks` (L122) caps at m = 3 while the Python band map has a 4th polydomain band (-2); the math-KG `code_locus` ranges will drift as the script is edited (-1)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "2012-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing.py L297–L301: Dead sigma_proxy expression multiplies a term by 0.0; compute_turing_phase_space never called <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/2012-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing.py#L297-L301>",
            "morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_054_kidney_ureteric_bud_gdnf_ret.lean L122–L126: tip_splitting_peaks caps at 3 peaks; the m = 4 polydomain band has no Lean coverage <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_054_kidney_ureteric_bud_gdnf_ret.lean#L122-L126>" ;
        ns1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing-code-traceability-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing-code-traceability-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing-code-traceability-3> ;
        ns1:hasScore 8.9e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing-model-fidelity> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Menshykau & Iber (2013), Zubkov et al. (2015) & Watanabe & Costantini (2004) kidney ureteric bud GDNF-RET-Wnt11 Turing branching morphogenesis with stromal BMP4/7-Gremlin1-FGF7 feedback and reduced-3D ampulla necking — Model fidelity to source: 84/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "The core Menshykau & Iber (2013) receptor-ligand system (steady state, flux cancellation, dispersion relation, lambda_c = 0.4726) is implemented correctly (L163-270) and the three Pass 3 additions are genuine mechanisms rather than relabelled prescriptions: the stromal gain law is a monotone BMP/Gremlin1/FGF7 function (L649-667) whose spatial fields (L774-789) set the per-tip ampulla radius and hence rho_tip and the splitting multiplicity (L835-852), the moving boundary advances the dome with the JSON growth law v_n = v0 max(0, R^2 G - S_thr) and re-solves the cap PDE on the current arc (L587-647), and the axis-selection argument compares Re sigma(2 pi/L) along the two principal arcs (L491-537). Deductions: the band-seeded cap solver seeds the cosine mode of the band-predicted m (L367-378), so the m = 1..4 staircase is an initial-condition artefact, and the noise-seeded control (L380-383) selects [2, 3, 5, 5] because the two-lobe mode sits on the rising flank of sigma(k) (-6); the hypoplasia parameter set b = 0.45 has Tr J_0 > 0 and is outside the Turing regime, now labelled (L1204) but still used for the hypoplasia tree (-3); the moving boundary is 1D on the dome with no curvature/surface-tension term, no re-meshing and no 3D, and the 90 deg dihedral rests on `daughter_long_axis_parallel` (L544, L569) rather than dynamics (-3); the cap kinetics use a saturating cubic R^2 G/(1 + 0.18 (R - R*)^2) (L403) that is not in the paper (-2); BMP4/BMP7 share one quasi-static field and `compute_turing_phase_space` (L272-310) is dead code with a term multiplied by 0.0 (L299) (-2)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "2012-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing.py L1204–L1204: Panel A labels the hypoplasia set b = 0.45 as Tr J_0 > 0, outside the Turing regime; the hypoplasia tree still uses it <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/2012-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing.py#L1204-L1204>",
            "2012-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing.py L272–L310: compute_turing_phase_space is never called and sigma_proxy multiplies a term by 0.0 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/2012-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing.py#L272-L310>",
            "2012-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing.py L367–L383: Band-seeded cosine initial condition for the predicted m versus the noise-seeded honesty control; the staircase is conditioned on its own seed <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/2012-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing.py#L367-L383>" ;
        ns1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing-model-fidelity-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing-model-fidelity-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing-model-fidelity-3>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing-model-fidelity-4>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing-model-fidelity-5> ;
        ns1:hasScore 8.4e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing-morphometric-validation> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Menshykau & Iber (2013), Zubkov et al. (2015) & Watanabe & Costantini (2004) kidney ureteric bud GDNF-RET-Wnt11 Turing branching morphogenesis with stromal BMP4/7-Gremlin1-FGF7 feedback and reduced-3D ampulla necking — Morphometric validation: 76/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "`measure_morphoeval()` (L1413-1589) now reports 14 metrics with references and dispersion statistics: lambda_c = 0.4726 (exact), WT tip Pearson r = 0.9903 (p ~ 1e-5) and Horton-Strahler R_b, generational angle RMSE 2.92 deg, Spry1-/- and bead ratios, hypoplasia ratio 0.3125 (ref 0.4), specimen 12/6 tips, plus six Pass 3 metrics (noise-seeded staircase agreement 0/4, necking index 0.2025, dihedral 90.0 deg (ref 90), Grem1-/- 0.4375 (ref 0.08), Fgf7-/- 1.00 (ref 0.70), Bmp4+/- 1.8125 (ref 1.20)), all bitwise deterministic across two runs. The honesty control is credited for being reported rather than hidden. Deductions: the band-seeded \"4/4 exact mode matches\" metric is circular and the honest control scores 0/4 (-6); angle RMSE is self-referential because half-angles are prescribed from the same table (L856) (-4); the Watanabe & Costantini generation table and the perturbation means (28.5, 5.2, 21.0 tips; 0.88/0.12 fractions) and the Pearson reference 0.9985 are not traceable to a figure or table (-5); three new stromal ratios miss their qualitative references by 2-5x and Spry1-/- overshoots 3.875 vs 2.19 after removing hand-placed buds (-5); the necking index has no reference value; conditions use different RNG streams (SHA-256 of the condition name, L719) so WT vs mutant are not seed-matched (-2); the 90 deg dihedral match is guaranteed by the orientation assumption (-2)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "2012-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing.py L1438–L1450: Noise-seeded staircase gives [2, 3, 5, 5] vs band map [1, 2, 3, 4]: the Pass 2 4/4 metric was conditioned on its seed <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/2012-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing.py#L1438-L1450>",
            "2012-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing.py L719–L719: Per-condition RNG seed = SHA-256 digest of the condition name; WT vs perturbation comparisons are not seed-matched <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/2012-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing.py#L719-L719>",
            "2012-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing.py L856–L859: Prescribed generational half-angles make the angle-RMSE metric self-referential <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/2012-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing.py#L856-L859>" ;
        ns1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing-measurement-bmp4-reduced-stromal-inhibition-e12-5-tip-ratio-vs-wt-ectopic-supernumerary-budding>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing-measurement-e11-0-e13-5-wild-type-ureteric-bud-tip-count-correlation-pearson-r-vs-watanabe-costantini-2004>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing-measurement-fgf7-stromal-growth-factor-loss-e12-5-tip-ratio-vs-wt>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing-measurement-gdnf-and-prr-ub-hypoplastic-e12-5-ureteric-tip-reduction-ratio-vs-wt-control>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing-measurement-generational-ureteric-bifurcation-angle-rmse-across-e11-5-e13-5-vs-no-sink-ablation-control>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing-measurement-grem1-stromal-bmp-de-repression-failure-e12-5-tip-ratio-vs-wt>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing-measurement-mean-dihedral-rotation-angle-between-successive-splitting-planes-anisotropic-dome-cascade-4-generations>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing-measurement-moving-boundary-ampulla-necking-index-of-the-wt-dichotomous-cap-1-r-cleft-r-lobe>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing-measurement-noise-seeded-ampulla-tip-splitting-peak-count-agreement-with-the-band-map-1-2-3-4-honesty-control>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing-measurement-segmented-e12-5-mouse-metanephros-gfp-ureteric-bud-tip-count-panel-a-wild-type-control>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing-measurement-segmented-e12-5-mouse-metanephros-wt-to-mutant-ureteric-tip-multiplicity-ratio-panel-a-vs-panel-b>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing-measurement-spry1-hyper-branching-exogenous-gdnf-bead-supernumerary-e12-5-tip-count-ratio-vs-wt-control>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing-measurement-ureteric-ampulla-tip-splitting-mode-transition-accuracy-across-rho-tip-pi-r-tip-lambda-c>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing-measurement-wild-type-gdnf-ret-homogeneous-steady-state-signaling-r-2-g-critical-turing-wavelength-lambda-c>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing-morphometric-validation-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing-morphometric-validation-2> ;
