    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney-overall> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Menshykau & Iber (2013) & Short et al. (2014) GDNF-RET-Wnt11-Sprouty1 kidney ureteric bud Turing branching morphogenesis — MorphoEval overall 88.1/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 3 (v3) evaluation of `2014-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney.py` (overall weighted score 88.1/100, down from 92.8 in v2). The single v2 remediation item — couple the 3D tree to a phase-field / moving-boundary model of the expanding renal capsule and nephrogenic zone — is closed in a reduced, honestly labelled form: a steady diffuse-domain GDNF field on a fixed 36x36x39 grid inside an expanding spherical capsule with a nephrogenic-zone production shell and RET tip sinks, coupled to the tree by chemotaxis, moving-boundary confinement, interstitial dilation and GDNF-gated arrest. The coupling demonstrably matters: 67 % of E15.5 tips lie in the nephrogenic zone (decoupled v2 tree 11 %, with 80 % outside the capsule), a half-rate capsule suppresses the tip count to 198/293 through 103 vs 7 gated arrests, and the field is 2.15x enriched in the nephrogenic zone. Two Lean theorems (confinement bound, crowding-arrest monotonicity) are machine-checked, the self-test grows to 9 checks and 12 measurements, and three CLI flags plus the previously dead --D-ratio are wired. The lower score reflects what the remediation exposed rather than regressions: E15.5 tips 293 vs 354 observed (RMSE 23.3; v2's perfect fit came from a hard-coded WT branch_prob = 1.0 that is now removed), capsule constants that are order-of-magnitude anchors, a capsule radius prescribed from the observed tip counts, self-referential generation lengths/angles, a fragile Horton-Strahler R_b (2.18 at gate 0.15, 2.35 at 0.18), a specimen micrograph from a prorenin-receptor study with an unsourced pErk fold reference, and CLI overrides that do not reach the perturbation suite, sweep or capsule figure. Overall 88.1/100 (faithfulness 87.0, reproducibility 90.5); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 028758bc; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 90, Morphological realism / specimen match 84, Parameter expressivity 90, Morphometric validation 86, Source and data traceability 88, Code-to-model traceability 90, Reproducibility package 93. Output judged: docs/media/gdnf_ret_ureteric_kidney_comparison.png: rendered output of 2014-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney.py at 028758bc, image/png, 945447 B, 2742×1446 px, artifact_sha256 9f98460186b4bdf7797ab875a51788dba9d5afea8d89977769eda0675a4efdc0 (sha256 9f98460186b4bdf7797ab875a51788dba9d5afea8d89977769eda0675a4efdc0), spec_fingerprint f9c1a998913eff873333397950c9abd3c6d935d905ec30d2d429a949264e57cf. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: f9c1a998913eff873333397950c9abd3c6d935d905ec30d2d429a949264e57cf; artifact_sha256: 9f98460186b4bdf7797ab875a51788dba9d5afea8d89977769eda0675a4efdc0; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/gdnf_ret_ureteric_kidney/gdnf_ret_ureteric_kidney_reference.json=b624d595c12fdf8d..., datasets/gdnf_ret_ureteric_kidney/kidney_ureteric_tree_specimen.jpg=dceaf5044c7014e4..., datasets/gdnf_ret_ureteric_kidney/paper_citations.bib=3eb2da09bd233938..., datasets/gdnf_ret_ureteric_kidney/renal_capsule_phase_field_reference.json=8959f600edc5b3b8..., datasets/gdnf_ret_ureteric_kidney/scout_manifest.json=60b78a1876b45c42...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney-audit-v2. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Menshykau & Iber (2013): a ligand-receptor (GDNF-RET) Schnakenberg-type Turing mechanism on the ureteric bud epithelium selects elongation, bifurcation or trifurcation according to the ampulla geometry; GDNF is produced by the cap mesenchyme and bound by epithelial RET | Short et al. (2014): OPT tip counts across E11.5-E15.5 (2 to 354 tips), Horton-Strahler R_b 2.08 and R_L 1.38, stereotyped early branching followed by a spatially regulated nephrogenic-zone programme in which all tips reside beneath the renal capsule | Watanabe & Costantini (2004), Basson et al. (2005), Miyazaki et al. (2000), Shakya et al. (2005): GDNF-bead attraction, Spry1-/- supernumerary budding, BMP4 stalk inhibition and Gdnf-/-/Ret-/- renal agenesis; reconstructed_in_script: 4-species GDNF-RET-Wnt11-Sprouty1 reaction-diffusion solver on a 1D periodic ampulla ring with m = 1..4 mode selection (L212-L361); a 3D stochastic ureteric tree across g = 1..8 with Horton-Strahler ordering (L366-L457, L655-L914); a steady diffuse-domain GDNF field inside an expanding spherical renal capsule with nephrogenic-zone production shell and RET tip sinks (L526-L604) coupled to the tree by chemotaxis, confinement, interstitial dilation and GDNF-gated arrest; a 6-condition capsule coupling sweep (L990-L1051); a 5-condition perturbation suite at g = 5 (L1057-L1101); colour-threshold segmentation of a vendored E12.5 micrograph (L1107-L1215); transfer_boundary: The capsule is a sphere on a fixed Eulerian grid with isotropic dilation, not a moving-mesh finite-element model of the kidney; its radius R_cap(g) is prescribed from the Short (2014) observed tip numbers (L509-L519, L750), so the moving boundary is partly data-driven rather than emergent | Per-generation segment lengths and branch angles are read from the reference table (L743-L747); the tree reproduces the ordering of tip counts, not an independent prediction of the generation-wise geometry | The capsule constants (300/550 um anchors, 110 um nephrogenic zone, 150 um GDNF decay length, kappa_tip 2.0, gate 0.15, chi 0.35) are modelling assumptions tagged as such in renal_capsule_phase_field_reference.json, not literature table values; does_not_claim: A deforming tetrahedral/FEM mesh of capsule and nephrogenic zone, anisotropic tissue growth, an ellipsoidal kidney, epithelial mechanics, cell-level nephron induction, or quantitative reproduction of the specimen micrograph's pErk1/2 fold (the 2.40 reference is unsourced)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 2014-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney.py:1193-1198 and 1812-1821 — the pErk1/2 ROIs are hard-coded pixel boxes that ignore `panel_d_f_wt_if_roi_xyxy` in the reference JSON, and the measured fold 38.65 is compared with an unsourced `reference_value: 2.40`. Read the ROIs from the JSON, state a sourced reference or mark the measurement as uncalibrated.",
            "remediation needed: 2014-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney.py:1230-1234, 1589-1597 and 990-997 — CLI overrides reach only the g=1..8 tree; the perturbation suite, Panel H sweep and the capsule figure take `seed` only, and the `no_capsule` ablation changes chemotaxis, confinement, gate and dilation at once. Propagate overrides and add single-factor ablations (confinement-only, gate-only, dilation-only).",
            "remediation needed: 2014-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney.py:1622-1678 — `render_growth_gif` draws every generation frame with the final (dilated) node positions, so early frames show already-stretched segments. Record per-generation node snapshots during growth and animate those.",
            "remediation needed: 2014-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney.py:1798 and datasets/gdnf_ret_ureteric_kidney/paper_citations.bib — Shakya et al. (2005) Dev. Cell 8:65-74 is cited in a measurement source string but absent from the bib; add it (and update the SHA-256 pin) and verify the DOI 10.1016/j.devcel.2004.11.008.",
            "remediation needed: 2014-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney.py:1807-1808 and datasets/gdnf_ret_ureteric_kidney/gdnf_ret_ureteric_kidney_reference.json — the vendored Wikimedia micrograph is from a prorenin-receptor (PRR UB-/-) study, not a GDNF/RET or Short (2014) specimen, and the \"published 12 tips, cohort mean 13.2 +/- 0.5\" has no verifiable citation. Either vendor a CC-licensed GDNF/RET-perturbation specimen or relabel the panel as a generic E12.5 ureteric tree.",
            "remediation needed: 2014-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney.py:1826 — `self_test` docstring says \"8-check ... Pass 2 (v2)\" while the suite has 9 checks and prints \"Pass 3 v3\"; the ampulla PDE geometry at 232-260 is a periodic 1D ring described as a \"semicircular dome\". Update both docstrings.",
            "remediation needed: 2014-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney.py:427-436 and 1849 — `compute_horton_strahler_metrics` drops the last ratio and falls back to R_b = 2.0, and the 1.90-2.30 self-test window passes only at gate 0.15 (R_b = 2.35 at gate 0.18 or chi = 0). Compute R_b by log-linear regression over all orders with >= 2 streams and report its sensitivity to the gate.",
            "remediation needed: 2014-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney.py:479-489 and datasets/gdnf_ret_ureteric_kidney/renal_capsule_phase_field_reference.json:15-28 — the capsule anchors (300 / 550 um), nephrogenic-zone thickness 110 um, GDNF decay length 150 um, kappa_tip 2.0, gate 0.15, chi 0.35, hilum offset 0.62 and margin 22 um are tagged as assumptions. Trace at least the capsule radii and nephrogenic-zone thickness to a measured source (Short 2014 OPT volumes or a histology table) and add a sensitivity sweep over gate and chi showing how R_b and the tip count respond.",
            "remediation needed: 2014-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney.py:509-519 and 750 — `renal_capsule_radius_um` interpolates R_cap(g) from the OBSERVED Short (2014) tip number of the same generation, so the moving boundary is data-prescribed and the Panel C tip-count comparison is not independent of the reference. Drive the capsule radius from simulated state (e.g. cumulative tip count or an interstitial growth law R_cap(t) with its own anchor) and report the comparison as a prediction.",
            "remediation needed: 2014-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney.py:705-709 and 772-778 — trifurcation constants 0.08 / 0.24 / 0.22, stage factors 1.28 / 0.72 and branch probability 0.99 * gain^0.42 have no cited source; the E15.5 tip count is 293 vs 354 observed (RMSE 23.3) and g=5 WT is 36 vs 40.2. Either calibrate these against the Short (2014) table with the calibration stated, or expose them as documented parameters.",
            "remediation needed: 2014-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney.py:743-747 and 956-957 — per-generation `segment_length_um` and `branch_angle_deg` are read from the reference table, so the segment-length Pearson r is circular; recorded generation lengths are at formation while Strahler lengths include later dilation (752-761). Derive segment length from the ampulla PDE / capsule geometry or drop the length correlation from the measurement list.",
            "remediation needed: 2014-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney.py:752-761 and 526-604 — the capsule is a sphere on a fixed Eulerian grid with isotropic dilation; the kidney is ellipsoidal with anisotropic growth and the ureteric epithelium is not a separate phase. Residual of the v2 item: implement a deforming (moving-mesh) capsule / nephrogenic-zone domain or at least an ellipsoidal capsule with anisotropic dilation." ;
        ns1:hasScore 8.81e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney-parameter-expressivity> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Menshykau & Iber (2013) & Short et al. (2014) GDNF-RET-Wnt11-Sprouty1 kidney ureteric bud Turing branching morphogenesis — Parameter expressivity: 90/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 3 adds a 6-condition capsule coupling sweep (coupled, no-chemotaxis, decoupled, capsule x0.6 / x0.5 / x1.3) whose outputs move monotonically with capsule growth (198 < 268 < 293 tips; NZ fraction 0.95 > 0.90 > 0.67 > 0.58), the `grow_ureteric_tree_3d` signature exposes `capsule_growth`, `chemotaxis_weight`, `capsule_confinement`, `gdnf_gate` (L663-L666), `evaluate_short_2014_generations` forwards them, and the CLI gains `--capsule-growth`, `--chemotaxis`, `--no-capsule` while `--D-ratio` (dead in v2) is now wired. The 4 ampulla regimes, 8 generations and 5 perturbation conditions are retained. Deductions: CLI overrides affect only the g = 1..8 tree (Panels A, C, F, G); the perturbation suite, Panel H sweep and the capsule figure take `seed` only and ignore them (-4); the `no_capsule` ablation changes chi, confinement, gate and dilation simultaneously, so only `no_chemotaxis` isolates a single coupling (-3); the gate value 0.15 is not sweepable from the CLI although R_b is sensitive to it (-1). Net: 92 -> 90." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "2014-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney.py L1230–L1234: `render_comparison_figure` passes overrides only to the ampulla modes and the g=1..8 tree; `evaluate_perturbation_suite(seed)` and `evaluate_capsule_coupling_sweep(seed)` ignore them <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/2014-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney.py#L1230-L1234>",
            "2014-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney.py L993–L993: `no_capsule` condition sets chemotaxis 0, capsule False and gate 0 at once — a conflated ablation <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/2014-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney.py#L993-L993>" ;
        ns1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney-parameter-expressivity-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney-parameter-expressivity-2> ;
        ns1:hasScore 9e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney-repro-package> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Menshykau & Iber (2013) & Short et al. (2014) GDNF-RET-Wnt11-Sprouty1 kidney ureteric bud Turing branching morphogenesis — Reproducibility package: 93/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "`--self-test` passes 9 checks in 6.9 s (SHA-256 integrity of 5 files + capsule JSON consistency, Turing criterion, harmonics [1,2,3,4], Short scaling and Strahler windows, agenesis control, perturbation ordering, specimen segmentation, two-run bitwise determinism of PDE, tree and field, and the new 10-assertion capsule-coupling check including the hilum fixed point and zero GDNF outside the capsule); `measure_morphoeval()` length is asserted (12); the full default render writes the PNG, the capsule PNG and the GIF in 7.3 s; all outputs are seeded and deterministic. Deductions: the self_test docstring is stale (-1); the R_b window 1.90-2.30 is satisfied only at the default gate so the determinism guarantee is narrower than it looks (-1); the capsule figure and sweep cannot be regenerated under the CLI overrides (-1); no pinned requirements lock file for this script (-1). Net: 93 -> 93." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-repro-package> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/repro-package" ;
        ns1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney-repro-package-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney-repro-package-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney-repro-package-3> ;
        ns1:hasScore 9.3e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney-source-traceability> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Menshykau & Iber (2013) & Short et al. (2014) GDNF-RET-Wnt11-Sprouty1 kidney ureteric bud Turing branching morphogenesis — Source and data traceability: 88/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "`datasets/gdnf_ret_ureteric_kidney/` carries 5 primary DOIs in `paper_citations.bib`, the scout manifest, the reference JSON, the specimen image and now `renal_capsule_phase_field_reference.json`, all 5 SHA-256-pinned and verified fail-closed at every run (`verify_dataset_integrity`, L87-L104; `load_capsule_reference` cross-checks the JSON against `CAPSULE_PARAMS`, L107-L119). The new JSON tags every capsule constant with a status string (approximate anchor / modelling assumption / numerical), which is the right way to disclose unsourced values. Deductions: Shakya et al. (2005) is cited in a measurement source string (L1798) but is absent from `paper_citations.bib` (-2); the specimen \"published 12 tips, cohort mean 13.2 +/- 0.5\" (L1808) and the pErk reference 2.40 (L1817-L1818) have no verifiable citation (-3); none of the capsule constants is traced to a table or figure (-2). Net: 95 -> 88." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-source-traceability> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/source-traceability" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "2014-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney.py L1798–L1818: Shakya 2005 cited but not in the bib; specimen 'cohort mean 13.2 +/- 0.5' and pErk reference 2.40 unsourced <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/2014-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney.py#L1798-L1818>" ;
        ns1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney-source-traceability-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney-source-traceability-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney-source-traceability-3> ;
        ns1:hasScore 8.8e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney-specimen-match> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Menshykau & Iber (2013) & Short et al. (2014) GDNF-RET-Wnt11-Sprouty1 kidney ureteric bud Turing branching morphogenesis — Morphological realism / specimen match: 84/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "The 8-panel figure now shows the coupled 3D tree, the ampulla modes, the g = 1..8 scaling, the perturbation suite, the specimen segmentation, a mid-plane capsule GDNF slice with capsule / nephrogenic-zone contours and confined tips (Panel G), and the ablation bars (Panel H); the dedicated capsule-coupling figure contrasts the E13.0 and E15.5 coupled trees with the decoupled v2 tree, 80 % of whose tips lie outside the nominal capsule — a visually convincing demonstration that the coupling is what keeps tips in the nephrogenic zone. Specimen segmentation still finds 13 WT vs 6 mutant tips. Deductions, which the v2 audit did not apply: the vendored Wikimedia micrograph is from a prorenin-receptor (PRR UB-/-) study, not a GDNF/RET or Short (2014) specimen, so the \"mutant\" panel is not the Gdnf/Ret perturbation the model simulates (-4); the measured pErk1/2 fold of 38.65 is compared with a reference of 2.40 whose source string is unsourced, a 16x discrepancy left unexplained (-3); the pErk ROIs are hard-coded pixel boxes that ignore the ROI stored in the reference JSON (-1); the GIF draws every generation frame with the final dilated node positions, so early frames show already-stretched segments (-1); the E15.5 coupled tree has 293 tips vs the 354 the figure's own Panel C reports as observed (-2). Net: 91 -> 84." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-specimen-match> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/specimen-match" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "2014-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney.py L1622–L1678: GIF uses final (dilated) node positions for every generation frame <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/2014-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney.py#L1622-L1678>",
            "2014-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney.py L1812–L1821: pErk1/2 fold 38.65 vs `reference_value: 2.40` whose source is an unsourced description string; specimen is from a PRR study, not GDNF/RET <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/2014-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney.py#L1812-L1821>" ;
        ns1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney-specimen-match-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney-specimen-match-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney-specimen-match-3>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney-specimen-match-4> ;
        ns1:hasScore 8.4e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-code-traceability> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Metzger et al. (2008) & Menshykau et al. (2012, 2014) mouse lung stereotyped branching modes (Domain D, Planar P, Orthogonal O), FGF10-SHH-Ptch1 Turing mode selection, pleura-confined diffuse-domain FGF10 cavity and stochastic postnatal septation — Code-to-model traceability: 93/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "The module docstring (L1-66) maps every section to its source and to the five Lean laws, and names the honest reduction of each Pass 3 item; section banners for 3b and 4b (L612-636, L1046-1065) carry the model equations; every new function has a docstring citing the equation or phase it implements; the math KG loop file (115 lines) registers Laws 4-5 with Lean theorem names, Lean code excerpts and Python code loci, and the loci of Laws 1-3 were refreshed to the new line numbers. Deductions: the self_test docstring (L1897-1906) still describes the Pass 2 7-item list and omits blocks 7-8 (-2); the tuned-constant comment on L117 points to an external handoff note rather than stating the sensitivity in the code (-2); the `--self-test` help string still says 'Pass 2' (L2009) (-1); the measurement for the transition position attributes the 0.5 bound to Metzger Fig. 3 in its `reference_source` string before admitting it is assigned (-2)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "2008-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching.py L1896–L1906: self_test docstring still lists the Pass 2 seven items; blocks 7-8 undocumented in the docstring <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/2008-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching.py#L1896-L1906>" ;
        ns1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-code-traceability-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-code-traceability-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-code-traceability-3>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-code-traceability-4> ;
        ns1:hasScore 9.3e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-model-fidelity> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Metzger et al. (2008) & Menshykau et al. (2012, 2014) mouse lung stereotyped branching modes (Domain D, Planar P, Orthogonal O), FGF10-SHH-Ptch1 Turing mode selection, pleura-confined diffuse-domain FGF10 cavity and stochastic postnatal septation — Model fidelity to source: 92/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "The Metzger (2008) 3D D/P/O grammar with the 4m + 1 tip law and the Menshykau (2012, 2014) FGF10-SHH-Ptch1 dispersion relation are implemented as in Pass 2 (L183-442, L448-611). Pass 3 adds a genuine mechanism for the margin/interior mode switch: the ligand equation is solved in a diffuse-domain cavity (Li et al. 2009 formulation, Dirichlet F = 0 beyond the pleura via the (1 - psi) F / tau penalty, L656-702), the tip acts as a Ptch1 sink (R^2 = 1 + 3 exp(-r^2/0.25^2)), and the P/O decision is the sign of the supply anisotropy (`decide`, L806-839); the solver is checked against the exact slab closed form with monotone first-order convergence (L704-747). The septation module is an exact-increment Yule process with the Mund (2008) phase structure (L1106-1172) and its mean law is proved in Lean (Law 5). Deductions: the cavity is a quasi-2D cross-section with a prescribed 15 %/generation dilation (L780-782) rather than a 3D moving boundary, tips are not advected by grad F and the pleura does not respond to the tree (-2); the switch depends on the tuned pair h_mid = 1.0 / A_c = 0.05 (L117, L123) and on three further unsourced constants (L119-121) (-2); `simulate_fgf10_shh_mode_switch` clips R and F to [0.1, 3.2] every step (L578-579), uses an unjustified `diff_scale = 0.25` for the domain case (L568), and its seed profiles hard-code the final peak spacing, so the apical-vs-lateral outcome is largely prescribed by the initial condition (-2, pre-existing, not scored in Pass 2)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "2008-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching.py L116–L123: PLEURA_* and RECEPTOR_* constants: h_mid = 1.0 and A_c = 0.05 are tuned (comment on L117); growth 0.15, gamma 4.0, tip gain 2.0 unsourced <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/2008-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching.py#L116-L123>",
            "2008-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching.py L568–L579: diff_scale = 0.25 for the domain case and per-step clipping of R, F to [0.1, 3.2] in the spectral Turing solver <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/2008-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching.py#L568-L579>" ;
        ns1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-model-fidelity-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-model-fidelity-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-model-fidelity-3>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-model-fidelity-4>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-model-fidelity-5>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-model-fidelity-6> ;
        ns1:hasScore 9.2e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-morphometric-validation> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Metzger et al. (2008) & Menshykau et al. (2012, 2014) mouse lung stereotyped branching modes (Domain D, Planar P, Orthogonal O), FGF10-SHH-Ptch1 Turing mode selection, pleura-confined diffuse-domain FGF10 cavity and stochastic postnatal septation — Morphometric validation: 87/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "`measure_morphoeval()` reports 13 entries (L1739-1893): the 8 Pass 2 metrics plus the slab-check relative error 0.0261 (ref 0), the P/O transition position 0.54 (ref 0.5 convention), the emergent dihedral RMSE 3.13 deg (ref 0; 8/8 mode accuracy; non-circular, the observed dihedral is never fed back), the ensemble P36 alveolar count 2.32e6 (ref 2.3e6, explicitly labelled a calibration target) and the per-unit CV 0.9978 (ref 0.9999, Yule law). The lineage validation now grows each tree with the pleura policy instead of the observed dihedral (L969-1044), which closes the Pass 2 circularity. Deductions: the E11-E14.5 tip-count r = 1.0000 is self-referential because the benchmark event counts reproduce 2 + sum(D + P + O) exactly (`pred_tips`, L1004-1011) (-4); the `reference_value`s 0.481834 (isotropy contrast, L1838) and 1.4172 (lambda_T, L1848) are the model's own outputs recorded as references, unchanged since Pass 2 (-3); the adult alveolar count is fitted with 1 dof, so only the CVs, control, plateau and bulk/continued partition are tests and no per-age Mund (2008) count is compared (-3); the lung-level CV (0.028 vs 0.040 law) rests on 12 seeds and the self-test only bounds it below 0.1 (-1); the transition position reference 0.5 is a convention written into the dataset JSON, not a measured value (-2)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "2008-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching.py L1004–L1011: pred_tips = 2 + cumulative D+P+O events from the benchmark table whose event counts were back-filled to match, giving r = 1.0000 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/2008-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching.py#L1004-L1011>",
            "2008-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching.py L1834–L1852: reference_value 0.481834 (L1838) and 1.4172 (L1848) are the script's own outputs, not literature values <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/2008-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching.py#L1834-L1852>" ;
        ns1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-measurement-compound-lobar-scaffold-d-4-o-o-active-distal-tip-count-4m-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-measurement-diffuse-domain-fgf10-solver-relative-error-vs-closed-form-slab-profile-eps-0-025>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-measurement-emergent-pleura-confined-dihedral-rmse-vs-8-e12-5-e14-5-lineages>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-measurement-empirical-e11-0-e14-5-developmental-distal-tip-count-pearson-r>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-measurement-empirical-e12-5-e14-5-mouse-lung-dihedral-angle-rmse-8-lineages>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-measurement-fgf10-shh-ptch1-turing-critical-wavelength-lambda-t>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-measurement-optimal-dihedral-rotation-angle-delta-phi-maximizing-3d-inter-tip-clearance>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-measurement-planar-vs-orthogonal-transverse-3d-tip-isotropy-contrast-sigma-y-sigma-x>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-measurement-pleura-confined-margin-to-interior-p-o-transition-position-x-l-x>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-measurement-segmented-bronchial-daughter-to-parent-lumen-caliber-ratio-r-d-r-0>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-measurement-segmented-mammalian-bronchial-tree-specimen-junction-angle-mean>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-measurement-septation-per-terminal-unit-alveolar-count-coefficient-of-variation-at-p36>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-measurement-stochastic-septation-adult-alveolar-count-at-p36-ensemble-mean>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-morphometric-validation-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-morphometric-validation-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-morphometric-validation-3> ;
        ns1:hasScore 8.7e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-overall> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Metzger et al. (2008) & Menshykau et al. (2012, 2014) mouse lung stereotyped branching modes (Domain D, Planar P, Orthogonal O), FGF10-SHH-Ptch1 Turing mode selection, pleura-confined diffuse-domain FGF10 cavity and stochastic postnatal septation — MorphoEval overall 88.5/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 3 (v3 remediated) evaluation of `2008-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching.py` (overall down slightly from 91.1 in Pass 2 despite both v2 remediation items being closed, because the round exposed defects that Pass 2 had not scored). The script now couples the Metzger (2008) D/P/O grammar to a diffuse-domain FGF10 cavity bounded by a dilating pleura (L612-963) so that the margin -> Planar / interior -> Orthogonal switch is emergent (position sweep x*/L_x = 0.54, critical half-thickness h* = 0.944 l0, slab-check error 0.026 with first-order convergence), replaces the circular Pass 2 lineage dihedral comparison with an emergent one (RMSE 3.13 deg, 8/8 mode accuracy, emergent isotropy vs hull flatness r = 0.996), and extends the grammar beyond E16.5 with an exact-increment Yule septation ensemble (632 units x 12 seeds, P36 = 2.32e6 vs the 2.3e6 calibration target, unit CV 0.998 vs Yule 0.9999, deterministic no-septation control frozen at 632). Five Lean 4 theorems (0 `sorry`s) are machine-checked, 13 morphometrics are measured, and the 8-block self-test passes in ~4.4 s with two-run bitwise determinism. Against that: the pleura half-thickness and anisotropy threshold are tuned so the transition sits mid-lobe; each lineage's lobe position is assigned from its class label; the E11-E14.5 benchmark table has no per-row provenance and its r = 1.0000 tip-count fit is self-referential; two Pass 2 reference values are the model's own outputs; the Turing PDE clips R and F to [0.1, 3.2] every step and its seed profiles prescribe the final peak spacing; `--seed` is parsed but never used; and the three new DOIs are unverified. Overall 88.5/100 (faithfulness 87.1, reproducibility 91.7); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 028758bc; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 92, Morphological realism / specimen match 82, Parameter expressivity 90, Morphometric validation 87, Source and data traceability 89, Code-to-model traceability 93, Reproducibility package 93. Output judged: docs/media/lung_stereotyped_branching_modes_comparison.png: rendered output of 2008-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching.py at 028758bc, image/png, 760057 B, 2950×1350 px, artifact_sha256 39a638e50c464718f55cb5a04c00c6dbe57169032a3a3896d1e76a6400bec3d4 (sha256 39a638e50c464718f55cb5a04c00c6dbe57169032a3a3896d1e76a6400bec3d4), spec_fingerprint d02b0c3844bcaa108ea9ec4bb8fce374a8da22fe6801db1a8256bba00a9e901f. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: d02b0c3844bcaa108ea9ec4bb8fce374a8da22fe6801db1a8256bba00a9e901f; artifact_sha256: 39a638e50c464718f55cb5a04c00c6dbe57169032a3a3896d1e76a6400bec3d4; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/lung_stereotyped_branching_modes/bronchial_tree_specimen.jpg=3247bc8c35eddcad..., datasets/lung_stereotyped_branching_modes/lung_stereotyped_branching_modes_reference.json=860ab1e53046d2e7...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-lung-stereotyped-branching-modes-audit-v2. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Metzger et al. (2008): the E11-E15 mouse bronchial tree is built from three stereotyped subroutines — Domain Branching, Planar Bifurcation (confined to lobe edges/margins) and Orthogonal Bifurcation (lobe interiors) — composed in a genetically encoded sequence | Menshykau et al. (2012, 2014): an FGF10 / SHH-Ptch1 receptor-ligand Turing system on a growing epithelial domain selects between apical (bifurcation) and lateral (domain) budding, and mesenchymal geometry biases the direction of outgrowth | Mund, Stampanoni & Schittny (2008): mouse alveolarisation proceeds in a bulk phase P4-P21 and a continued phase P14-P36; Knust et al. (2009): the adult C57BL/6 mouse lung holds ~2.3e6 alveoli; reconstructed_in_script: 3D Bishop-frame D/P/O grammar with the 4m + 1 tip law and a 181-point dihedral sweep; the Menshykau dispersion relation and a 1D spectral PDE mode switch; a quasi-2D diffuse-domain FGF10 cavity bounded by a dilating lens-shaped pleura with the tip as Ptch1 sink, whose supply anisotropy chooses P (0 deg) vs O (90 deg) at each bifurcation; an exact-increment Yule septation ensemble seeded by the grammar's extrapolated E16.5 terminal-unit count; chromatic segmentation and skeletonisation of a bronchial-tree image; transfer_boundary: The pleura model is a transverse cross-section (z-invariant) with a prescribed, tree-independent dilation; tips choose P/O from the field but are not advected by grad F, and the pleura does not deform in response to the tree — the v2 item asked for a 3D moving-boundary phase-field/BEM, which this is not | lambda_bulk is fitted to the adult alveolar count, so the P36 total is a calibration, not a prediction; the 632 terminal units at E16.5 are a log-linear extrapolation of the vendored E11-E14.5 timecourse table; lambda_cont / lambda_bulk = 0.12 and birth at E19.5 are assumptions | The 'specimen' is a Wikimedia medical illustration of human bronchioles/alveoli, not a mouse E11-E15 lung; its junction angles are compared with the model's reference angles but cannot validate the mouse grammar; does_not_claim: A 3D moving-boundary mesenchyme, tip chemotaxis, per-age alveolar counts from Mund (2008), digitised Metzger (2008) lineage coordinates, or an independent prediction of the adult alveolar number." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 2008-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching.py:1-26, 1806 and lung_stereotyped_branching_modes_reference.json:29-42 — the Li (2009), Mund (2008) and Knust (2009) DOIs are cited from memory and flagged unverified; Yule (1925) has no DOI. Verify the three DOIs against the publishers' records when network access is available, add the Yule (1925) DOI (Phil. Trans. R. Soc. B 213:21-87), and clear the `verification` flags.",
            "remediation needed: 2008-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching.py:1004-1011 and 1834-1852 — the E11-E14.5 tip-count r = 1.0000 is self-referential (benchmark event counts reproduce 2 + sum(D+P+O) exactly) and reference_value 0.481834 / 1.4172 are the model's own outputs recorded as references. Digitise the observed tip counts from Metzger (2008) Fig. 1 with per-stage provenance and replace the two self-referential reference_values with literature values or mark them `reference_source: model` so the measurement is not read as a validation.",
            "remediation needed: 2008-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching.py:1116-1191 — lambda_bulk is fitted (1 dof) to the Knust (2009) adult count, so the P36 total is a calibration; lambda_cont / lambda_bulk = 0.12 and birth at E19.5 are assumed; no per-age alveolar count is compared. Transcribe the Mund (2008) per-age alveolar numbers (P4, P7, P10, P14, P21, P36) into the dataset JSON with figure provenance, fit lambda_bulk on the early points only and hold out the later ones as a prediction.",
            "remediation needed: 2008-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching.py:116-123 and 780-782 — h_mid = 1.0 and A_c = 0.05 are tuned so the single-tip P/O transition lands at x*/L_x = 0.54 (h_mid = 0.9 makes the whole lobe planar, 1.1 flips only the outer 10 %); the cavity dilation 0.15/generation, gamma = 4.0 and tip gain 2.0 are unsourced. Add a 2D sweep of (h_mid, A_c) reporting x* and the lineage mode accuracy as a function of both, source h_mid from a measured E12.5 lobe section aspect ratio, and state the sensitivity in the code rather than in an external note.",
            "remediation needed: 2008-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching.py:2024 and 2033-2047 — `--seed` is parsed but never passed to render_outputs, so RANDOM-RANDOM control trees always use seed 2008. Forward the seed (also to run_dihedral_angle_sweep and simulate_postnatal_septation) and add a self-test asserting that two different seeds change the random control but not the deterministic metrics.",
            "remediation needed: 2008-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching.py:553-579 — the spectral Turing solver clips R and F to [0.1, 3.2] every step, the seed profiles hard-code the final peak spacing (1.42 / 0.80), and diff_scale = 0.25 is applied only to the domain case; Panel C (ax_c, L1483) shows the traces saturating at the clip bounds. Remove the clipping (or justify it as a positivity projection and report how often it binds), seed from small random noise with a fixed RNG, and derive the domain/apical diffusion contrast from the Menshykau (2014) geometry rather than a constant.",
            "remediation needed: 2008-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching.py:841-844 and 969-1044 — the per-lineage emergent dihedral uses a single isolated tip at generation 1 while the flatness comparison uses the full policy tree; the two can disagree at mid-lobe positions (tree mean 45 deg). Report both predictors per lineage, flag disagreements, and add Panel G legend/inset placement that does not occlude the lens or the upper-right cavity.",
            "remediation needed: 2008-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching.py:989 with lung_stereotyped_branching_modes_reference.json:123-221 — `lobe_cross_section_position_norm` (0.90 margin / 0.15 interior) is assigned from the Metzger lineage class, so the 8/8 emergent mode accuracy tests 'margin -> planar, interior -> orthogonal' given the label. Replace the assigned positions with coordinates digitised from Metzger (2008) Fig. 3 lineage maps (or an independent lobe atlas) with per-row figure provenance, and report accuracy on positions that were not used to build the model.",
            "remediation needed: datasets/lung_stereotyped_branching_modes/bronchial_tree_specimen.jpg with 2008-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching.py:1237-1346 and 1874-1891 — the SHA-256-pinned 'specimen' is a human medical illustration (Lynch/Jaffe), not a mouse E11-E15 lung, so the junction-angle and caliber comparisons are drawing-vs-model. Add a CC-licensed mouse embryonic lung image (e.g. an E12.5-E14.5 whole-mount or lobe section) as a second pinned specimen, segment it, and compare the emergent P/O trees and the lens cross-section aspect ratio against it; keep the current image but relabel it as an illustration." ;
        ns1:hasScore 8.85e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-parameter-expressivity> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Metzger et al. (2008) & Menshykau et al. (2012, 2014) mouse lung stereotyped branching modes (Domain D, Planar P, Orthogonal O), FGF10-SHH-Ptch1 Turing mode selection, pleura-confined diffuse-domain FGF10 cavity and stochastic postnatal septation — Parameter expressivity: 90/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 2's dihedral sweep, mode-sequence comparison and equal-diffusion control remain (L385-442, L521-611). Pass 3 adds two genuine mechanistic sweeps: the subtree root across the lobe cross-section x0/L_x in [0, 0.9] with emergent dihedral, tree isotropy and anisotropy reported (margin-interior transition x*/L_x = 0.54; L880-925), and the lobe half-thickness with a critical h* = 0.944 l0 and monotone anisotropy (L928-963); plus a far-tip FGF10 ablation and the deterministic no-septation control (L1175-1191). Four new CLI flags (`--pleura-half-thickness`, `--anisotropy-threshold`, `--septation-seeds`, `--septation-cont-fraction`, L2017-2023) are wired through `render_outputs` (L2033-2047). Deductions: `--seed` (L2024) is parsed but never passed to `render_outputs`, so the RANDOM trees always use the hard-coded 2008 seed (-4); the anisotropy threshold and tip gain are swept only implicitly through the position sweep, and no sweep shows how x* moves with A_c or h_mid even though the handoff documents that it is sensitive to them (-4); the septation continued/bulk ratio is a CLI input, not a swept or fitted quantity (-2)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "2008-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching.py L2033–L2047: render_outputs call: pleura and septation flags forwarded, args.seed not forwarded (dead flag) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/2008-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching.py#L2033-L2047>" ;
        ns1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-parameter-expressivity-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-parameter-expressivity-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-parameter-expressivity-3> ;
        ns1:hasScore 9e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-repro-package> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Metzger et al. (2008) & Menshykau et al. (2012, 2014) mouse lung stereotyped branching modes (Domain D, Planar P, Orthogonal O), FGF10-SHH-Ptch1 Turing mode selection, pleura-confined diffuse-domain FGF10 cavity and stochastic postnatal septation — Reproducibility package: 93/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "`--self-test` passes in ~4.4 s with 8 blocks (L1896-2004): SHA-256 integrity, 4m + 1 law, dihedral optimum, Turing dispersion and equal-diffusion ablation, lineage correlation, specimen segmentation, two-run bitwise determinism, and the new block 7 (slab convergence < 5 %, centre -> orthogonal / margin -> planar, anisotropy monotone, 0.3 <= x* <= 0.9, 8/8 mode accuracy, far-tip ablation, determinism; L1953-1976) and block 8 (mean-field agreement < 6 %, frozen control, no alveoli before P4, unit CV in [0.8, 1.2], lung CV < 0.1, P36 within 6 % of target, exact closed-form calibration, determinism; L1978-2003). The default render regenerates both media files in ~5.3 s; the pinned environment (Python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0) matches the venv. Deductions: the dead `--seed` flag means a documented reproducibility control does nothing (-3); the lung-CV bound (< 0.1) and the P36 tolerance (6 %) are loose relative to the reported values (-2); `docs/media` is git-ignored so the regenerated PNG/GIF are not pinned by hash in the repository (-2)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-repro-package> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/repro-package" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "2008-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching.py L2024–L2024: --seed parsed with default 2008 but never forwarded to render_outputs <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/2008-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching.py#L2024-L2024>" ;
        ns1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-repro-package-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-repro-package-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-repro-package-3> ;
        ns1:hasScore 9.3e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-source-traceability> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Metzger et al. (2008) & Menshykau et al. (2012, 2014) mouse lung stereotyped branching modes (Domain D, Planar P, Orthogonal O), FGF10-SHH-Ptch1 Turing mode selection, pleura-confined diffuse-domain FGF10 cavity and stochastic postnatal septation — Source and data traceability: 89/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "The dataset directory keeps the SHA-256-pinned specimen and JSON (runtime check `verify_dataset_integrity`, L145-167), and the JSON (307 lines, dataset_id -v2) now carries three additional sources, a `lobe_cross_section_position_norm` per lineage row, a `pleura_confinement_reference` block that states plainly that the position is ASSIGNED from the Metzger lineage class and that the paper gives no quantitative pleural distance (L274-287), and a `postnatal_alveolarization_reference` block (L288-307); `paper_citations.bib` gains three entries (L47-81) and the README is updated. The header docstring lists all 7 sources with DOIs (L1-26). Deductions: the three new DOIs (Li 2009, Mund 2008, Knust 2009) were cited offline from memory and are flagged `unverified` in the JSON (L29-42), bib and docstring (L26) — they could not be checked in this audit either (-4); the `empirical_mouse_lung_lineage_benchmarks` and `developmental_timecourse_e11_to_e15` tables (L110-273) still have no per-row figure/table provenance and their hull-flatness values look synthetic (-4); Yule (1925) is cited in a measurement source without DOI (L1806) and `margin_position_norm_min = 0.5` (L277) is a convention presented alongside paper-derived values (-2); the specimen's Wikimedia provenance is correct but the image is not of the organism studied (-1)." ;
