    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-source-traceability> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Moulton, Goriely & Chirat (2015) & Chirat et al. (2013) hierarchical mollusc aperture spine folding and fractal frond serration — Source and data traceability: 88/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Credit: 5 dataset files are SHA-256-pinned in `EXPECTED_SHA256` (L105-124) and verified fail-closed at every run by `verify_dataset_integrity()` (L136-150), including the new `pass3_koiter_cord_thickness_reference.json` (L119-121); `pass3_citations.bib` adds Koiter (1966), Manor et al. (2008) and re-cites Rudraraju et al. (2019) with the explicit note that DOIs could not be re-verified offline; the dataset README has a Pass 3 section that labels both closures as reduced and lists the new files and media; the four Pass 2 DOIs are unchanged. Deductions: the manor2008 DOI `10.1209/0295-5075/83/10005` is recalled from memory and unverified, and koiter1966 has no DOI (-2); the modelling constants have no source — E = 12 MPa, K_s = 0.48 vs K_s_eff = 1.98 (L163, L213, L677), h = 0.42 / 0.0708 / 0.0245 mm (L182-183), Koiter `onset_excess = 0.15` (L686), `varix_halfwidth_mm = 5.0` (L681), `kappa_3 = 0.28 k^2 P_c` (L726, L1083), the height law 4.8 sqrt(gamma - gamma_c) (L368, L747), `eps_cord = 0.15` and the 0.35 thickness floor (L1031) (-5); the cross-taxa `*_obs` columns and the per-species h_1, h_2 values in the reference JSON (L114-150) cite no measurement (-3); only a Murex pecten photograph is vendored although Chicoreus ramosus is half of the organism field (-2)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-source-traceability> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/source-traceability" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "datasets/mollusc_aperture_spine_buckling/mollusc_aperture_spine_buckling_reference.json L114–L150: Cross-taxa table h1/h2/obs values have no measurement provenance <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/datasets/mollusc_aperture_spine_buckling/mollusc_aperture_spine_buckling_reference.json#L114-L150>",
            "models/2015-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling.py L677–L690: Koiter defaults K_s_eff = 1.98, varix_halfwidth_mm = 5.0, onset_excess = 0.15 — modelling choices without a cited source <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/models/2015-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling.py#L677-L690>" ;
        ns1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-source-traceability-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-source-traceability-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-source-traceability-3> ;
        ns1:hasScore 8.8e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-specimen-match> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Moulton, Goriely & Chirat (2015) & Chirat et al. (2013) hierarchical mollusc aperture spine folding and fractal frond serration — Morphological realism / specimen match: 86/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Credit: the SHA-256-locked *Murex pecten* specimen is now used quantitatively twice — DoG comb segmentation (n = 16, CV = 0.2092; `segment_murex_specimen`, L559-634) and, new in Pass 3, its 15 inter-spine spacings drive the inverse-WKB thickness profile h(u)/h_bar = (lambda/lambda_bar)^(4/3) that is then tested against the graded comb (panel I, L1486-1517; CV 0.112 emergent vs 0.209 specimen); the specimen is visible in panels F and I of the 3x3 figure and the Koiter surface in panel G shows cord-registered spines in 3-D (`render_pass3_koiter_figure`, L1573-1649). Deductions: every *Chicoreus ramosus* claim (frond cascade, h(s) across instars) has no specimen — the Pass 2 item explicitly asked for Chicoreus thickness data and the closure uses a Murex photograph (-6); the two-harmonic thickness fit has R^2 = 0.29 and is floored at 0.35 (L1031), so the inferred h_max/h_min = 1.71 is weakly constrained, and the first segmented spacing (find_peaks distance = 26 px, L585) is plausibly a spurious peak that inflates the gradient (-4); the emergent graded-comb CV (0.112) reaches only about half the specimen CV (-2); the cord-locking GIF and Koiter surface are compared with no muricid varix photograph (-2)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-specimen-match> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/specimen-match" ;
        ns1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-specimen-match-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-specimen-match-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-specimen-match-3>,
