    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-nakamasu-zebrafish-three-cell-stripes-specimen-match> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Nakamasu et al. (2009) 3-variable zebrafish pigment-cell reaction-diffusion network + Volkening-Sandstede iridophore S/L agents on a growing flank, laser-ablation polarity & leopard (cx41.8) spot-to-stripe morphospace — Morphological realism / specimen match: 90/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Panel I shows an emergent (not templated) adult flank with 4 dark stripes separated by 3 interstripes whose dense iridophores sit in the light bands — the same 4-stripe count the specimen segmentation finds (Panel F, L954-1030) and a plausible rendering of the X0/X1D/X1V sheets of Frohnhöfer 2013 / Singh 2014; Panels E-G keep the SHA-256-locked Danio rerio photograph, its segmented stripes and the standardized profile comparison. Deductions: no juvenile-stage specimen images are vendored, so the 2 -> 4 ontogeny is compared with a qualitative normal table rather than with pictures (-5); dense iridophore coverage of X1D/X1V is sparse compared with the contiguous sheets seen in vivo, and loose iridophores are few (loose fraction 0.02) (-3); the GIF is the model alone with no specimen frame (-2)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-specimen-match> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/specimen-match" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "docs/media/zebrafish_three_cell_stripes_growth.gif (generated output, not in repo): 8-frame growing-flank GIF (SL 7.2 -> 18 mm) with agents and dorsoventral profiles; no juvenile specimen frames — docs/media/zebrafish_three_cell_stripes_growth.gif: rendered output of 2009-nakamasu-zebrafish-three-cell-stripes.py at 3aaa03d, image/gif, 387895 B, 1056×440 px, 8 frames, artifact_sha256 2e85b27819c7e94524233f2180f0de10d3ae2797b2ecc37e5725541b68aa02a5 (sha256 2e85b27819c7e94524233f2180f0de10d3ae2797b2ecc37e5725541b68aa02a5), spec_fingerprint 53d32e73f4ffa155070025683029f96e36562f3bf4bf95b4d073d237a096b1d2" ;
        ns1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-nakamasu-zebrafish-three-cell-stripes-specimen-match-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-nakamasu-zebrafish-three-cell-stripes-specimen-match-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-nakamasu-zebrafish-three-cell-stripes-specimen-match-3> ;
        ns1:hasScore 9e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing-code-traceability> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Wiggs et al. (1997), Li et al. (2011) & Eskandari et al. (2015) cylindrical bilayer mucosal folding, period-doubling & Poiseuille airway resistance, coupled to a Weibel (1963) bronchial-tree impedance network with Venegas (2005) flow-stretch feedback — Code-to-model traceability: 85/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "The module header (L1-90) maps each law to its paper and to the five Lean theorems, every new tree function carries a docstring naming its source (Weibel 1963 model A, Poiseuille, Venegas 2005 feedback, Macklem & Mead 1967 for the small-airway check), the math-KG registration (`morphoeval/math_kg_loops/nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing.yaml`) lists 5 equations with single-range `code_locus` / `lean_locus` pins that match the current file, and the 14 self-test checks are numbered and commented against the laws. Deductions: the blending weights 0.88/0.12, 0.85/0.15 and 0.75/0.25 (L420, L430, L437, L627-632) are not explained anywhere as reference prescription, so a reader of the \"L-BFGS-B relaxation\" docstring is misled about what is computed (-7); the spectral-operator and energy coefficients (L366-371 and the surrounding weights) and the constants 0.0085, 0.7110, 0.25 (L130, L217, L221) have no derivation or citation (-4); the Li 2011 title inconsistency between header and Lean docstring (-2); the seed-paper author list in the v2 audit header (\"Auguste,imba\") is a pre-existing documentation defect carried in the campaign prompt (-2)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "2018-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing.py L366–L371: Spectral operator weights 0.25/0.75 and surrounding energy coefficients have no citation <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8a7928d7/2018-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing.py#L366-L371>",
            "2018-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing.py L436–L438: Reference blending is uncommented as such; docstring presents the function as an energy relaxation <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8a7928d7/2018-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing.py#L436-L438>" ;
        ns1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing-code-traceability-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing-code-traceability-2> ;
        ns1:hasScore 8.5e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing-model-fidelity> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Wiggs et al. (1997), Li et al. (2011) & Eskandari et al. (2015) cylindrical bilayer mucosal folding, period-doubling & Poiseuille airway resistance, coupled to a Weibel (1963) bronchial-tree impedance network with Venegas (2005) flow-stretch feedback — Model fidelity to source: 80/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Credited: the cylindrical bilayer wavenumber law m* = c_cyl (R_0/h_m)(3 mu_s/mu_m)^(1/3) (L204-223), the inextensible-perimeter lumen-area occlusion and Hagen-Poiseuille (A_0/A)^2 law (L225-243) and its vectorised twin shared with the tree (L245-276), and the new tree: Weibel model-A geometry (L734-785), R = 8 eta L / (pi r^4) (L787-791), exact bottom-up series-parallel impedance with top-down flow split (L794-823, conservation error <= 3e-16, homogeneous identity to 1e-9), per-branch m* and area fraction, saturating Venegas feedback with under-relaxed fixed-point iteration (L852-1009) and the analytic small-airway share (L826-850). Five Lean 4 theorems formalise the scaling, occlusion, Poiseuille, bifurcation-scaling and feedback-monotonicity laws. Deductions: the ring minimiser's headline outputs are prescribed — a_norm = 0.88 target + 0.12 computed (L436-438) and pd_sim = 0.85 pd_obs + 0.15 FFT (L430) whenever reference values are passed, which is the default (L516-517) — so the phenotype A/A_0 = 0.253 and R_flow/R_0 = 15.65 are not solutions of the stated energy (-8); the plotted profile is 75 % analytic template + 25 % minimiser (L420) and the spectral operator / energy weights (L366-371 and the 1.60, 0.35, 2.20, 0.68, 1.35, 0.32 coefficients) are unsourced tuning (-4); wall_coupling = (1+0.0085 h_m)^-0.5, C_CYL_CURVATURE = 0.7110 and epsilon_c = 0.25 (3 mu_s/mu_m)^(2/3) (L130, L217, L221) are fitted to the 12-point table rather than derived (-3); the tree is Poiseuille-only with generation-independent h_m/R_0 and m*, no Pedley correction, compliance or cartilage limit, and the 0.12 area floor inherited by `lumen_area_fraction_vectorized` saturates closed branches at 69x so the asthma defect fraction non-monotonically drops from 0.35 to 0.30 between eps = 0.28 and 0.34 in the tree GIF (-5)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "2018-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing.py L215–L222: wall_coupling 0.0085 and epsilon_c prefactor 0.25 are unsourced fitted constants <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8a7928d7/2018-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing.py#L215-L222>",
            "2018-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing.py L416–L421: u_combined = 0.75*(analytic base_wave + sulcus_cusp) + 0.25*u_rel: plotted rosette is mostly template <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8a7928d7/2018-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing.py#L416-L421>",
            "2018-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing.py L426–L440: pd_sim = 0.85*pd_ratio(observed) + 0.15*FFT and a_norm = 0.88*target_a_norm + 0.12*a_calc: phenotype outputs are prescribed, not relaxed <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8a7928d7/2018-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing.py#L426-L440>" ;
        ns1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing-model-fidelity-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing-model-fidelity-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing-model-fidelity-3>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing-model-fidelity-4> ;
        ns1:hasScore 8e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing-morphometric-validation> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Wiggs et al. (1997), Li et al. (2011) & Eskandari et al. (2015) cylindrical bilayer mucosal folding, period-doubling & Poiseuille airway resistance, coupled to a Weibel (1963) bronchial-tree impedance network with Venegas (2005) flow-stretch feedback — Morphometric validation: 80/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "`measure_morphoeval()` (L1606-1776) returns 15 reference-anchored measurements, 6 new: homogeneous tree / single-airway identity 1.000000 (ref 1.0), Weibel pure-Poiseuille small-airway share 0.4291 (analytic ref 0.43; Macklem-Mead 0.10-0.20 stated), Severe Asthma heterogeneous VDef 0.3503 (Venegas ~0.30, range 0.20-0.40), Healthy VDef 0.0449 at identical sigma/kappa (ref 0.0), asthma/healthy whole-tree amplification 2.80 (ref 3.66) and defect run-length clustering 1.25 (null 1.0); the Pass 2 collapse statistics (r = 0.9986, p = 8.9e-14, alpha = -1.04 ± 0.02), the three m* values and the specimen metrics remain. Deductions: the phenotype A/A_0, R_flow/R_0 (15.65 vs 16.52) and period-doubling measurements are 85-88 % the reference value by construction (L430, L436-438), so their agreement is not a validation (-8); the 2.80 vs 3.66 amplification measurement mixes two single-airway sources (the reference table's 16.52/4.51 vs the closed-form law's 11.77/4.72 = 2.49 that the tree actually uses), so the stated \"above the lower bound\" claim holds only relative to 2.49 and the printed reference is weak (L1756-1765) (-4); the 12-point collapse r is partly circular because the table's m_obs values are largely model-derived and the law's constants were fitted to the same table (-4); the specimen fold count and circularity are compared to themselves (-2); the Venegas comparison is to a single scalar (defect volume fraction) with no PET-image morphometric and sigma is assumed (-2)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "2018-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing.py L1756–L1765: Asthma/healthy tree amplification 2.80 compared to 3.66 = 16.52/4.51 from a different single-airway source than the tree's own law (2.49) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8a7928d7/2018-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing.py#L1756-L1765>",
            "2018-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing.py L612–L635: sim_*_A_norm / sim_*_R_flow = 0.85*reference + 0.15*simulated feeding Panel C and the constriction-curve comparison <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8a7928d7/2018-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing.py#L612-L635>" ;
        ns1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing-measurement-12-point-3-species-bronchial-fold-wavenumber-scaling-correlation-human-bovine-ovine>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing-measurement-chronic-bronchitis-remodeled-circumferential-fold-mode-number-m>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing-measurement-healthy-bronchiole-heterogeneous-bronchospasm-ventilation-defect-fraction-at-identical-sigma-kappa-epsilon-mean-0-28>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing-measurement-healthy-thin-walled-bronchiole-circumferential-fold-mode-number-m>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing-measurement-histology-specimen-segmented-inward-mucosal-fold-count-m-obs-bronchiole-mucosal-rosette-specimen-jpg>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing-measurement-histology-specimen-segmented-rosette-lumen-circularity-4-pi-a-p-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing-measurement-homogeneous-bronchospasm-whole-tree-single-airway-poiseuille-resistance-ratio-identity-severe-asthma-epsilon-0-28>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing-measurement-log-log-inverse-mucosal-thickness-scaling-exponent-alpha-m-h-m-r-0-alpha>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing-measurement-relaxed-asm-negative-control-epsilon-theta-0-open-lumen-area-fraction-a-lumen-a-0>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing-measurement-severe-asthma-hagen-poiseuille-airflow-resistance-amplification-r-flow-r-0-at-epsilon-theta-0-28>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing-measurement-severe-asthma-healthy-whole-tree-resistance-amplification-under-heterogeneous-bronchospasm-epsilon-mean-0-28>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing-measurement-severe-asthma-heterogeneous-bronchospasm-ventilation-defect-fraction-epsilon-mean-0-28-sigma-0-10-kappa-0-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing-measurement-severe-asthma-ventilation-defect-spatial-clustering-mean-contiguous-defect-run-length-random-bernoulli-expectation>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing-measurement-severe-asthmatic-airway-remodeling-circumferential-fold-mode-number-m>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing-measurement-weibel-model-a-pure-poiseuille-small-airway-g8-g16-d-2-mm-share-of-conducting-airway-resistance>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-nelson-airway-mucosal-creasing-morphometric-validation-1>,
