    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-newman-limb-chondrogenesis-turing-model-fidelity> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Newman & Frisch (1979) Science 3D Helmholtz/Turing standing-wave eigenmodes and proximodistal 1 -> 2 -> 3 skeletal chondrogenesis in developing Gallus gallus wing bud — Model fidelity to source: 94/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Retains the exact Newman & Frisch (1979) Eqs. (1)-(7) dispersion relation (`compute_newman_dispersion`, L161-271) and the 1D/2D nonlinear DCT-II IMEX solvers (L274-468). Pass 3 adds the requested 3D moving boundary (L847-1152): Lagrangian P1 FEM in z with advection a(z) = int S dz, dilution and bisection refinement (L1045-1108), a moving distal boundary, DST-II Dirichlet dorsal/ventral ectoderm (L898), active-zone kinetics with k_PD^2 from the actual discrete PD operator (L668-692) and fu chosen by bisection so the fastest linear mode is exactly m^2 + k_DV^2 + k_PD^2 (L695-770), plus three new Lean theorems (Helmholtz budget, FGF8 window depth, Hill-2 monotonicity). It is held at 94 rather than raised because the remediation exposed structural limits: (i) pattern selection is not growth-sensitive — the S_max = 0 sweep run (zero outgrowth) still yields [1, 2, 3] (L1204-1209), so the moving boundary sets element lengths only; (ii) the Table 1 map m(L_PD) (L186-191) is still an empirical input and the m-increment joint/interzone is an imposed field reset (L1006-1012); (iii) the AP/DV cross-section is spectral on a box (header L567-600), not a FEM mesh of the paddle-shaped bud; (iv) post-excision kinetics are held by rule (L991-997)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "1979-newman-limb-chondrogenesis-turing.py L1006–L1012: Joint/interzone on m increment is an imposed reset of the active + apical field to noise (documented, not emergent) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/1979-newman-limb-chondrogenesis-turing.py#L1006-L1012>",
            "1979-newman-limb-chondrogenesis-turing.py L1204–L1209: S_max sweep: S = 0 (no outgrowth) still produces [1, 2, 3] — element count is clock-set, growth-insensitive <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/1979-newman-limb-chondrogenesis-turing.py#L1204-L1209>",
            "1979-newman-limb-chondrogenesis-turing.py L186–L191: Table 1 mode map m(L_PD) thresholds 375/190/125 um remain an empirical input to the kinetics (not derived from hyaluronate -> D_eff) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/1979-newman-limb-chondrogenesis-turing.py#L186-L191>" ;
        ns1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-newman-limb-chondrogenesis-turing-model-fidelity-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-newman-limb-chondrogenesis-turing-model-fidelity-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-newman-limb-chondrogenesis-turing-model-fidelity-3> ;
        ns1:hasScore 9.4e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-newman-limb-chondrogenesis-turing-morphometric-validation> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Newman & Frisch (1979) Science 3D Helmholtz/Turing standing-wave eigenmodes and proximodistal 1 -> 2 -> 3 skeletal chondrogenesis in developing Gallus gallus wing bud — Morphometric validation: 93/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "`measure_morphoeval()` (L1671-1836) now reports 14 reference-backed measurements: the 8 Pass 2 items (unchanged values) plus 3D record total elements 6 vs 6, L_PD(24 h) 250.2 vs 250 um, L_PD(48 h) 128.6 vs 140 um (-8.1 %, the 3-point clock fit's residual), excision at 0 h -> 1 vs 1, excision at 24 h -> 3 vs 3, and record AP spacing ratio 1.484 vs 1.5. The L_PD(48 h) miss and the fact that the excision series is partly a consequence of the imposed m-map timing keep this below the mid-90s." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "1979-newman-limb-chondrogenesis-turing.py L639–L665: Hyaluronidase clock fit to Table 1 (tau_H = 37.0 h) — L_PD(48 h) = 128.6 um vs 140 um reference is an 8 % residual of the one-parameter exponential <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/1979-newman-limb-chondrogenesis-turing.py#L639-L665>" ;
        ns1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-newman-limb-chondrogenesis-turing-measurement-3d-moving-boundary-intact-aer-total-skeletal-elements-in-the-frozen-record-1-2-3>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-newman-limb-chondrogenesis-turing-measurement-3d-record-zeugopod-to-autopod-anteroposterior-spacing-ratio-m-2-m-3>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-newman-limb-chondrogenesis-turing-measurement-equal-diffusion-du-dv-and-hyaluronate-excess-fu-1-5-negative-control-amplitude>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-newman-limb-chondrogenesis-turing-measurement-hh20-stylopod-pde-condensation-count-m-l-pd-500-um>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-newman-limb-chondrogenesis-turing-measurement-hh24-zeugopod-pde-condensation-count-m-l-pd-250-um>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-newman-limb-chondrogenesis-turing-measurement-hh27-chick-wing-autopod-pde-condensation-count-m-l-pd-140-um>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-newman-limb-chondrogenesis-turing-measurement-hh28-chick-hindlimb-autopod-pde-condensation-count-m-l-pd-115-um>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-newman-limb-chondrogenesis-turing-measurement-intact-aer-2d-wing-bud-total-skeletal-elements-stylopod-1-zeugopod-2-autopod-3>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-newman-limb-chondrogenesis-turing-measurement-moving-boundary-active-progress-zone-depth-l-pd-at-24-h-hh24>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-newman-limb-chondrogenesis-turing-measurement-moving-boundary-active-progress-zone-depth-l-pd-at-48-h-hh27>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-newman-limb-chondrogenesis-turing-measurement-moving-boundary-aer-excision-at-t-0-h-hh20-cumulative-skeletal-elements>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-newman-limb-chondrogenesis-turing-measurement-moving-boundary-aer-excision-at-t-24-h-hh24-cumulative-skeletal-elements>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-newman-limb-chondrogenesis-turing-measurement-progress-zone-mode-number-l-ap-lambda-ap-vs-pde-element-count-pearson-r>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-newman-limb-chondrogenesis-turing-measurement-segmented-gallus-gallus-wing-specimen-zeugopod-to-autopod-spacing-ratio>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-newman-limb-chondrogenesis-turing-morphometric-validation-1> ;
        ns1:hasScore 9.3e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-newman-limb-chondrogenesis-turing-overall> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Newman & Frisch (1979) Science 3D Helmholtz/Turing standing-wave eigenmodes and proximodistal 1 -> 2 -> 3 skeletal chondrogenesis in developing Gallus gallus wing bud — MorphoEval overall 93.8/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 3 (v3) post-remediation evaluation of `1979-newman-limb-chondrogenesis-turing.py` (overall weighted score: 93.8 / 100 (93.85 unrounded), up +1.5 from 92.3 / 100 in Pass 2). The single Pass 2 remediation item is closed in a reduced, explicitly scoped form: Section 4b adds a 3D moving-boundary wing bud whose proximodistal axis is a Lagrangian P1 finite-element mesh advected by FGF8-graded Hill-2 proliferation beneath the AER (dilution, h-refinement, moving distal boundary), with DCT-II/DST-II spectral Galerkin anteroposterior/dorsoventral cross-sections, a one-parameter hyaluronidase clock fitted to Newman & Frisch Table 1 (tau_H = 37.0 h, max |rel err| 4.6 %), three FGF8 zones (apical refractory / active progress zone / frozen record), active-zone Turing kinetics from the paper's 3D Helmholtz relation using the lowest eigenvalue of the actual discrete PD operator, and AER-excision and parameter sweeps. The intact run deposits a 3D skeletal record of [1, 2, 3] elements (DV core-mode purity 0.99, record AP spacing ratio 1.484 vs 1.5 theory / 1.407 specimen), reproduces L_PD(24 h) = 250.2 um (Table 1: 250) and L_PD(48 h) = 128.6 um (Table 1: 140), and the Summerbell (1974) excision-time series 1/1/3/3/3/6 elements for t_exc = 0/8/16/24/32/40 h. Six Lean 4 theorems (3 new) are machine-checked with 0 sorrys. The remediation also exposed that the element count is set by the clock rather than by growth (S_max = 0 still gives [1, 2, 3]), that the Table 1 mode map and the joint reset remain imposed, and that the cross-section is a spectral box rather than a FEM paddle; these are carried as Pass 4 items and model-fidelity is held flat rather than raised. Overall 93.8/100 (faithfulness 93.2, reproducibility 95.3); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit d58a084; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 94, Morphological realism / specimen match 92, Parameter expressivity 95, Morphometric validation 93, Source and data traceability 96, Code-to-model traceability 95, Reproducibility package 95. Output judged: docs/media/limb_chondrogenesis_turing_comparison.png: rendered output of 1979-newman-limb-chondrogenesis-turing.py at d58a084, image/png, 707529 B, 2285×1972 px, artifact_sha256 2b43fb710f9364839582f078db91b045664d7fb980ac6db71e8db52a90870e53 (sha256 2b43fb710f9364839582f078db91b045664d7fb980ac6db71e8db52a90870e53), spec_fingerprint ccb5850b44c8ca2f5f2646ec40a4758c3d46ded6705df0c966f6d163508ab9c2. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: ccb5850b44c8ca2f5f2646ec40a4758c3d46ded6705df0c966f6d163508ab9c2; artifact_sha256: 2b43fb710f9364839582f078db91b045664d7fb980ac6db71e8db52a90870e53; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/limb_chondrogenesis_turing/chick_wing_skeleton_specimen.jpg=771e26f9fe8c813d..., datasets/limb_chondrogenesis_turing/fgf8_moving_boundary_reference.json=b4fefaace1e7a1b3..., datasets/limb_chondrogenesis_turing/limb_chondrogenesis_turing_reference.json=c30d742bbf2a990a..., datasets/limb_chondrogenesis_turing/paper_citations.bib=21dad0bab5186d67..., datasets/limb_chondrogenesis_turing/scout_manifest.json=7f3605aa11f5e077...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-limb-chondrogenesis-turing-audit-v2." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Make proximodistal mode selection growth-sensitive: derive the Table 1 map m(L_PD) (L186-191) and the active-zone fu (L695-770) from a hyaluronate density field (Toole 1972) advected and diluted on the same Lagrangian mesh instead of thresholds on L_PD, so that the S_max = 0 run (L1204-1209) no longer yields [1, 2, 3] with zero outgrowth.",
            "remediation needed: Reduce the L_PD(48 h) residual (128.6 vs 140 um, L639-665) by fitting the hyaluronidase clock to a dense Summerbell (1976) elongation series rather than three Table 1 points, and report the fit's confidence interval in measurement 10.",
            "remediation needed: Replace the DCT-II/DST-II spectral box cross-section (L898-907, header L567-600) with an unstructured 3D P1 finite-element mesh on a paddle-shaped bud outline with anteroposterior widening (Zhu et al. 2010 geometries), keeping the moving distal boundary.",
            "remediation needed: Replace the imposed joint/interzone reset on m increment (L1006-1012) with an emergent interzone: e.g. a Gdf5/Wnt9a-type inhibitor released where the deposited record saturates, or the mechanical clefting of Loop 018, and verify that the 1 -> 2 -> 3 compartments still separate.",
            "remediation needed: Replace the post-excision kinetics-hold rule (L991-997) with an explicit distal cell-death zone (Rowe & Fallon 1982, ~200 um) and FGF8 bead rescue (Niswander et al. 1993) so the Summerbell (1974) series and partial rescue are predicted rather than rule-driven." ;
        ns1:hasScore 9.38e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

