            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-planform-morphology-animation-specimen-match-3> ;
        ns1:hasScore 6e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence-code-traceability> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Azpeitia et al. (2021) TFL1-LFY-AP1/CAL-SOC1 floral GRN perturbation, PIN1 auxin-transport epidermal mesh and accelerating-plastochron Romanesco fractal inflorescence morphogenesis — Code-to-model traceability: 82/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "The module docstring maps each law to its equations, its source and its Lean 4 theorem (L1-93); every solver docstring states what it computes, which paper step it follows and — new in Pass 3 — what is prescribed, raw, conditioned or a self-consistency check (L340-356, L482-493, L867-883); the `math_kg_loops` YAML registers Laws 4-5 with lean/code loci. Deductions: the GRN coefficients at L198-223 carry no citation (-6); the tree geometry constants (0.68/0.52 radial exponents, tilt 0.52/0.72, child_scale lambda + 0.14 age_frac, child_t 0.52 + 0.22 age_frac at L429-441) are uncited shape heuristics (-6); the PIN1 parameters are documented as dimensionless choices but the mapping from mesh time to tree time (r0 = 1 per tau) is only in the coupling docstring (-3); Lean `lean_locus` line ranges in the YAML for Laws 1-3 were not re-pinned in Pass 3 (-3)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "2021-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence.py L429–L441: Uncited geometric heuristics (radial exponents, tilt, child scale/time factors) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2021-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence.py#L429-L441>" ;
        ns1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence-code-traceability-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence-code-traceability-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence-code-traceability-3> ;
        ns1:hasScore 8.2e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence-model-fidelity> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Azpeitia et al. (2021) TFL1-LFY-AP1/CAL-SOC1 floral GRN perturbation, PIN1 auxin-transport epidermal mesh and accelerating-plastochron Romanesco fractal inflorescence morphogenesis — Model fidelity to source: 72/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Credited: the quadratic plastochron law N(T) = r0 T + beta T^2/2 is exact (L268-286) and the PIN1 mesh implements the Jönsson (2006) allocation P_ij = P_tot A_j / (kappa + sum A_k) with the correct net-transport term, Smith (2006) threshold initiation / sinks / outward advection and central-zone cell production (L637-777); contact parastichies are now a genuine measurement on the generated lattice (L289-337) and the (8,13) -> (13,21) climb emerges from primordium density; five Lean 4 theorems cover Laws 1-5 (0 sorrys). Deductions: the GRN is a continuous Hill ODE with 20+ hand-tuned coefficients (L198-223) that reproduce vendored steady states, whereas Azpeitia et al.'s network is logical (-8); the curd envelope H/R(beta) = 0.56 + 10.8235 beta is prescribed (L388), so Law 3 is an input, not an output of the growth model (-7); the tree is a point skeleton whose children overlap (child_scale 0.38-0.52 with 20-37 children per parent, L415-440) and whose raw box-count D_f is 1.95 vs 2.71, i.e. the model does not produce a fractal surface of the reported dimension (-6); the PIN1 mesh approximates the hemispherical dome by a cone, uses Euclidean sink distances and is not a FEM solve as the v2 item asked (-5); the coupling constant v_r is vendored, not derived (-2)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "2021-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence.py L198–L223: Hand-tuned Hill coefficients (2.85, 0.18, 1.95, 2.75, 1.15, 1.85, 2.15, 2.52 ...) not traced to the paper, whose GRN is logical <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2021-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence.py#L198-L223>",
            "2021-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence.py L388–L388: H/R(beta) = 0.56 + 10.823529 beta is prescribed; Law 3 is an input <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2021-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence.py#L388-L388>" ;
        ns1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence-model-fidelity-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence-model-fidelity-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence-model-fidelity-3>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence-model-fidelity-4> ;
        ns1:hasScore 7.2e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence-morphometric-validation> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Azpeitia et al. (2021) TFL1-LFY-AP1/CAL-SOC1 floral GRN perturbation, PIN1 auxin-transport epidermal mesh and accelerating-plastochron Romanesco fractal inflorescence morphogenesis — Morphometric validation: 66/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "`measurements_from()` (L1277-1399) reports 14 measurements, each with a unit, a reference value, a literature source and a method string that states what was measured and what was not, including negative controls (lfy, beta = 0, T = 0). Credited: the parastichy transition is a real measurement that matches the reference (34 vs 34; 5/6 sweep sums), the ablation ratio is 0.0 vs 0 (Reinhardt 2003), the GRN steady states hit the vendored targets, the perimeter-scaling slope is measured (r = 0.99). Deductions: raw D_f 1.95 vs 2.71 (mean sweep bias -0.79) (-8); beta_emergent 0.289 vs 0.085 is a 3.4x miss, resolved only by an implied v_r* = 0.047 that is not independently supported (-6); emergent divergence 133.9 deg with MAD 25.6 deg and only 32% of events within +/-15 deg of the golden angle is weak quantitative agreement (-5); the perimeter-scaling normalised slope is 1.81 on the cone / 2.06 on the dome against the 1.0 expected for pure perimeter scaling (-3); the H/R Pearson r = 1.0 measurement is a self-consistency check of a prescribed law against an interpolated series and should not count as validation (-4); specimen H/R 1.76 vs 1.48 (-3); lambda = 0.390 is conditioned by the LoG sigma ratio 7/18 = 0.389 (-5)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "2021-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence.py L482–L518: Raw area-weighted box-count slope over 7 grids; Romanesco 1.95, Cauliflower 1.62 vs references 2.71 / 2.38 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2021-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence.py#L482-L518>",
            "2021-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence.py L818–L831: beta_emergent = slope_norm * v_r = 1.81 * 0.16 = 0.289 vs reference 0.085; implied v_r* reported <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2021-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence.py#L818-L831>",
            "2021-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence.py L906–L923: lambda_emp from two fixed LoG scales (sigma 7 and 18 px) and NMS windows 17 / 39 px; value 0.390 tracks the sigma ratio 0.389 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2021-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence.py#L906-L923>" ;
        ns1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence-measurement-ap1-cal-shoot-reversion-tfl1-steady>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence-measurement-ap1-cal-soc1-floral-memory-steady>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence-measurement-pin1-ablation-initiation-ratio>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence-measurement-pin1-coupled-tree-parastichy-sum>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence-measurement-pin1-emergent-divergence-angle-deg>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence-measurement-pin1-emergent-plastochron-acceleration-beta>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence-measurement-pin1-initiation-rate-vs-dome-radius-slope-normalised>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence-measurement-plastochron-sweep-aspect-ratio-pearson-r>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence-measurement-romanesco-3d-fractal-dimension-df>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence-measurement-romanesco-cone-aspect-ratio>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence-measurement-romanesco-contact-parastichy-sum>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence-measurement-romanesco-primordia-at-t20>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence-measurement-specimen-segmented-cone-aspect-ratio>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence-measurement-specimen-self-similar-scale-ratio-lambda>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence-morphometric-validation-1> ;
        ns1:hasScore 6.6e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence-overall> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Azpeitia et al. (2021) TFL1-LFY-AP1/CAL-SOC1 floral GRN perturbation, PIN1 auxin-transport epidermal mesh and accelerating-plastochron Romanesco fractal inflorescence morphogenesis — MorphoEval overall 71.5/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 3 (v3) evaluation of `2021-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence.py` (overall weighted score 71.5/100, down from 93.3 in v2). The one open v2 item is closed by an honest reduced PIN1 polar auxin transport model on a growing epidermal cell mesh over the cone surface (`build_dome_epidermal_mesh`, `simulate_pin1_auxin_transport`, `couple_pin1_mesh_to_plastochron`), whose emergent perimeter scaling r_p(R) = k R is coupled to Law 2 through beta = k v_r (Lean 4 Laws 4-5, 5 theorems, 0 sorrys). Coupling exposed that four Pass 2 \"measurements\" were surrogates pinned to the references (hard-coded parastichy pairs, a polynomial-in-beta D_f, clipped/offset specimen metrics, and a prescribed-vs-interpolated H/R correlation). With real measurements the model reproduces the (8,13) -> (13,21) parastichy transition on a curd-scale lattice and the pin1/NPA ablation, but its raw D_f is 1.95 (ref 2.71), beta_emergent is 0.289 (ref 0.085), the emergent divergence angle is 133.9 +/- 25.6 deg, and the specimen H/R is 1.76 (ref 1.48). Scores now reflect those honest values; the next layer of defects is listed under `remediation`. Overall 71.5/100 (faithfulness 68.1, reproducibility 79.2); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit d58a084; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 72, Morphological realism / specimen match 64, Parameter expressivity 74, Morphometric validation 66, Source and data traceability 70, Code-to-model traceability 82, Reproducibility package 85. Output judged: docs/media/roman_esco_fractal_inflorescence_comparison.png: rendered output of 2021-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence.py at d58a084, image/png, 1667696 B, 2590×2240 px, artifact_sha256 6a15f43bc46ef0bc731a4c393b12ce1350422559ff7c219fa507b99a16b1892e (sha256 6a15f43bc46ef0bc731a4c393b12ce1350422559ff7c219fa507b99a16b1892e), spec_fingerprint a6030f05b7cbd188f43ca98602c59735514d8a783a5d591370042c15a25296a0. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: a6030f05b7cbd188f43ca98602c59735514d8a783a5d591370042c15a25296a0; artifact_sha256: 6a15f43bc46ef0bc731a4c393b12ce1350422559ff7c219fa507b99a16b1892e; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/roman_esco_fractal_inflorescence/paper_citations.bib=4e4a53dcfd72833a..., datasets/roman_esco_fractal_inflorescence/roman_esco_fractal_inflorescence_reference.json=b580780d055808ce..., datasets/roman_esco_fractal_inflorescence/romanesco_brassica_oleracea_specimen.jpg=5fba6c320b478d6c..., datasets/roman_esco_fractal_inflorescence/scout_manifest.json=d684b2df5ef44398...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence-audit-v2. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Azpeitia et al. (2021) Science 373:192-197: loss of AP1/CAL in ap1 cal and Brassica curd meristems abolishes floral commitment while transient LFY induction leaves a SOC1/AGL24/FUL 'floral memory' (bract suppression) and high TFL1 shoot identity, so lateral primordia reiterate spiral phyllotaxis across several branching orders; Cauliflower meristems keep a constant plastochron and form a hemispherical curd, Romanesco meristems grow and initiate ever faster (decreasing plastochron), forming conical self-similar curds with higher Fibonacci parastichy numbers | Jönsson et al. (2006) and Smith et al. (2006): up-the-gradient PIN1 allocation on a cellular shoot-apex template produces auxin maxima whose threshold-triggered initiation, sink behaviour and outward advection reproduce spiral phyllotaxis near 137.5 deg; Reinhardt et al. (2003): pin1 / NPA apices form no primordia; Douady & Couder (1992): initiation rate scales with the free perimeter of the initiation ring; reconstructed_in_script: RK45 solver for a coupled 4-node continuous Hill ODE GRN (WT g_AP1 = 1, ap1 cal / curd g_AP1 = 0, lfy loss-of-function control) with HAND-TUNED coefficients that hit the vendored steady-state targets (the paper's network is logical, not these ODEs) | 3D 4-order recursive phyllotactic meristem tree with exact quadratic plastochron initiation times N(T) = r0 T + beta T^2/2, a PRESCRIBED linear envelope H/R(beta) = 0.56 + 10.8235 beta, raw area-weighted 3D box-counting D_f, and MEASURED nearest-neighbour contact parastichies on the generated lattice ((8,13) at beta = 0 and (13,21) for beta >= 0.04 on the curd-scale T = 80 lattice; (3,5) on the per-axis T = 20 lattice) | Reduced cell-based PIN1 polar auxin transport (Jönsson 2006 allocation, Smith 2006 sinks/threshold/advection) on a growing jittered k-NN epidermal mesh over cones of H/R 0.56 and 1.48 at three dome radii: emergent initiation rate r_p(R) = -0.16 + 0.36 R (r = 0.99), emergent divergence median 133.9 deg (MAD 25.6), PIN1 polarity index 0.57, T = 0 ablation gives 0 initiations; coupling beta_emergent = (k / r_p(R0)) v_r = 0.289 at the vendored v_r = 0.16 (reference 0.085, implied v_r* = 0.047) | Excess-green curd segmentation and two fixed-scale LoG floret detections (86 order-2, 421 order-3 cones) on the SHA-256-locked Romanesco specimen photograph, reported RAW: bounding-box H/R 1.76, lambda 0.390, 2.5D relief box slope 2.36; transfer_boundary: The vendored `plastochron_beta_sweep_benchmark_series`, `genotype_morphometric_benchmarks`, `radial_expansion_rate_v_r` and internode dz values are Pass 1 interpolations/syntheses anchored on the two Azpeitia et al. (2021) end-points, not tables from the paper; agreement with them is self-consistency, not validation | The PIN1 model is a discrete cell mesh with Euclidean (not geodesic) sink fields and a cone approximation of the hemispherical dome; its dimensionless parameters are chosen for the spiral regime, not fitted to Brassica | The Kim (2004) D_f ~ 2.71 / 2.38 references were carried from Pass 1 and could not be independently re-verified offline in Pass 3; does_not_claim: A continuum finite-element solution of PIN1 auxin transport on the curved meristem manifold; cell division or mechanics; the paper's own logical GRN or L-system; angular precision of the emergent phyllotaxis sufficient to generate Fibonacci parastichies (the coupled tree built from the emergent 133.9 deg angle measures (8,16))." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 2021-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence.py:1486 and 1493 — `--r0` and `--seed` are parsed but not wired; either pass them through compute_all (r0 into the plastochron law, seed into compute_3d_box_counting_dimension and the PIN1 mesh) or remove them.",
            "remediation needed: 2021-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence.py:163-261 — the GRN is a continuous Hill ODE with uncited hand-tuned coefficients reproducing vendored steady states; Azpeitia et al. (2021) use a logical network. Implement the paper's logical GRN (or cite a published continuous reduction) and validate against its reported attractor table rather than against Pass 1 target values.",
            "remediation needed: 2021-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence.py:388 and 1312-1327 — H/R(beta) = 0.56 + 10.8235 beta is prescribed and then \"validated\" (Pearson r = 1.0) against a vendored series that is a linear interpolation of the same end-points. Derive the envelope from the growth model (H = dz x N(T) with the vendored internode dz values and R(t) = R0 + v_r t) and drop or relabel the r = 1.0 measurement.",
            "remediation needed: 2021-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence.py:415-441 and 482-518 — the 4-order tree is a point skeleton whose children overlap (child_scale 0.38-0.52 with 20-37 children per parent), so its raw box-count D_f is 1.95 (Romanesco) / 1.62 (Cauliflower) against 2.71 / 2.38. Build an explicit curd surface (union of cones/spheres rendered to a voxel grid) and box-count that surface; independently re-verify or replace the Kim (2004) PRE 70:046109 reference (paper_citations.bib:50-60).",
            "remediation needed: 2021-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence.py:637-777 and 1252-1255 — emergent divergence 133.9 deg with MAD 25.6 deg (32% within +/-15 deg of golden) is too imprecise to carry Fibonacci parastichies: the coupled tree measures (8,16). Replace Euclidean sink distances with geodesic distances on the cone, use a structured (hexagonal) L1 mesh with cell division instead of random re-insertion, adopt the Smith (2006) exponential PIN allocation, and target MAD < 10 deg before coupling the angle.",
            "remediation needed: 2021-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence.py:818-831 and datasets/roman_esco_fractal_inflorescence/roman_esco_fractal_inflorescence_reference.json:68 — beta_emergent = (k / r_p(R0)) v_r = 1.81 x 0.16 = 0.289 is 3.4x the reference 0.085; the vendored v_r = 0.16 is untraced and the normalised slope 1.81 exceeds the pure-perimeter value 1.0 because the cell count (and hence initiation sites) scales with surface area. Vendor the paper's meristem-size vs time data (Azpeitia 2021 Fig. 3) to fix v_r, and make the mesh cell size physical so that k is perimeter- not area-limited.",
            "remediation needed: 2021-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence.py:896-923 — specimen H/R 1.76 is a raw image-plane bounding-box ratio with unknown camera elevation, and lambda = 0.390 is conditioned by the fixed LoG scales (7/18 = 0.389) and NMS windows. Add a second, side-view specimen or a calibrated projection model, and replace the two fixed scales by scale-space LoG with per-blob scale selection so the order-2 / order-3 radii (and lambda) emerge.",
            "remediation needed: datasets/roman_esco_fractal_inflorescence/roman_esco_fractal_inflorescence_reference.json:74-165 — the beta sweep series and genotype benchmarks are Pass 1 interpolations; mark them `synthetic: true` with the interpolation rule inside the JSON (not only in the README) or replace them with values digitised from Azpeitia et al. (2021) Figs. 3-4." ;
        ns1:hasScore 7.15e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence-parameter-expressivity> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Azpeitia et al. (2021) TFL1-LFY-AP1/CAL-SOC1 floral GRN perturbation, PIN1 auxin-transport epidermal mesh and accelerating-plastochron Romanesco fractal inflorescence morphogenesis — Parameter expressivity: 74/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "beta visibly and monotonically controls primordium count, the (prescribed) H/R envelope, the raw D_f (1.62 -> 2.08, strictly increasing) and the measured parastichy sum (21 -> 34 at beta >= 0.04) across the 6-point sweep (L521-580); the PIN1 transport coefficient T controls patterning (T = 0 ablation: 0 initiations, auxin contrast 1.00 vs 3.87) and the dome radius controls the initiation rate linearly on both geometries (r = 0.99); `--pin1-transport`, `--pin1-diffusion`, `--cell-spacing`, `--beta-rom`, `--scale-lambda`, `--max-order`, `--g-ap1` are wired (L1492-1529). Deductions: `--r0` and `--seed` are parsed but not used (L1486, L1493) (-6); the parastichy sum saturates at 34 for beta in [0.04, 0.11] where the vendored series expects 55 at 0.11 (-5); only T is swept on the PIN1 side (no D / sink-radius / growth-rate sweep rendered) (-6); the emergent divergence angle is not a controllable parameter and its scatter breaks the Fibonacci lattice when coupled (-6); the H/R response to beta is prescribed, so its monotonicity is not evidence of model expressivity (-3)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "2021-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence.py L1484–L1493: CLI flags; --r0 and --seed are parsed but never passed to any solver <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2021-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence.py#L1484-L1493>" ;
        ns1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence-parameter-expressivity-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence-parameter-expressivity-2> ;
        ns1:hasScore 7.4e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence-repro-package> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Azpeitia et al. (2021) TFL1-LFY-AP1/CAL-SOC1 floral GRN perturbation, PIN1 auxin-transport epidermal mesh and accelerating-plastochron Romanesco fractal inflorescence morphogenesis — Reproducibility package: 85/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "`--self-test` runs 12 checks in ~26 s (L1410-1489) covering SHA-256 integrity, GRN fates, the monotone raw D_f sweep, the measured parastichy transition on curd and per-axis lattices, raw specimen ranges, PIN1 patterning / polarity / divergence range, the T = 0 ablation, perimeter scaling on both geometries, the coupled tree, the 14-measurement contract and bitwise determinism of the full pipeline (compute_all run twice); the default invocation regenerates PNG and GIF in ~28 s and finishes with the self-test; all RNGs are seeded. Deductions: `--r0` and `--seed` are inert (-4); no requirements lock file pins the environment (-4); without MPLCONFIGDIR matplotlib writes a font cache outside the repository (-2); the self-test re-runs the whole PIN1 pipeline for the determinism check, doubling runtime (-2); the GIF title text at small font is marginally legible (-3)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-repro-package> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/repro-package" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "2021-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence.py L1486–L1493: --r0 and --seed parsed but inert <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2021-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence.py#L1486-L1493>" ;
        ns1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence-repro-package-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence-repro-package-2> ;
        ns1:hasScore 8.5e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence-source-traceability> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Azpeitia et al. (2021) TFL1-LFY-AP1/CAL-SOC1 floral GRN perturbation, PIN1 auxin-transport epidermal mesh and accelerating-plastochron Romanesco fractal inflorescence morphogenesis — Source and data traceability: 70/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Nine primary sources with DOIs in the module docstring (L1-93), the audit, `paper_citations.bib` and the two reference JSONs; the specimen and scout manifest are SHA-256 pinned and verified fail-closed at every run (L133-150); the new `pin1_auxin_transport_reference.json` lists every model parameter, its literature anchor and the model's limitations; the Pass 1 `kempin1995` BibTeX entry, which had merged two different Kempin et al. (1995) papers, is corrected. Deductions: the Kim (2004) Phys. Rev. E 70:046109 entry — the only source of the D_f 2.71 / 2.38 references — could not be re-verified offline and may be mis-cited (-10); `plastochron_beta_sweep_benchmark_series`, `genotype_morphometric_benchmarks`, `radial_expansion_rate_v_r` and the dz values in the Pass 1 JSON are interpolations/syntheses not traced to a figure or table of Azpeitia et al. (2021), and the JSON itself does not say so (the dataset README now does) (-12); the GRN Hill coefficients have no source (-5); the paper's actual meristem-size and plastochron measurements (its Fig. 3 data) are not vendored (-3)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-source-traceability> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/source-traceability" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "datasets/roman_esco_fractal_inflorescence/roman_esco_fractal_inflorescence_reference.json L74–L123: Beta sweep 'benchmark series' with no figure/table citation; values are a linear interpolation between the two end-points <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/datasets/roman_esco_fractal_inflorescence/roman_esco_fractal_inflorescence_reference.json#L74-L123>" ;
        ns1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence-source-traceability-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence-source-traceability-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence-source-traceability-3> ;
        ns1:hasScore 7e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence-specimen-match> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Azpeitia et al. (2021) TFL1-LFY-AP1/CAL-SOC1 floral GRN perturbation, PIN1 auxin-transport epidermal mesh and accelerating-plastochron Romanesco fractal inflorescence morphogenesis — Morphological realism / specimen match: 64/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "The 9-panel figure shows the specimen photograph with the segmented contour and detected florets (Panel F), the measured (8,13) vs (13,21) lattices side by side (Panel D) and the PIN1 auxin field with emergent primordia (Panel G), so the comparison is visible. Deductions: the 3D \"curds\" in Panel C are sparse coloured point clouds, not surfaces, and do not resemble a Romanesco or a Cauliflower curd beyond overall cone vs dome aspect (-12); the specimen's raw silhouette H/R is 1.76 against the model's prescribed 1.48 and no camera-geometry correction is available (-6); the Panel D lattices are planar projections while the photograph shows a conical curd, so parastichy counts are compared across different projections (-5); the PIN1 auxin field (Panel G) shows only the 4 primordia currently on the surface and is not compared with any PIN1/DR5 image (-5); the GIF animates the same point clouds (-4); honest raw reporting of specimen metrics is credited (+4 vs a clipped version)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-specimen-match> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/specimen-match" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "2021-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence.py L1128–L1152: Panel G auxin field with primordia currently on the surface (n = 4 of 25 initiated); no comparison with a PIN1/DR5 micrograph <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2021-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence.py#L1128-L1152>" ;
        ns1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence-specimen-match-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence-specimen-match-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence-specimen-match-3> ;
        ns1:hasScore 6.4e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-przemyslaw-allometric-compound-leaf-code-traceability> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Bilsborough et al. (2011), Barkoulas et al. (2008), Vlad et al. (2014) & Kierzkowski et al. (2019) growing leaf margin PIN1-Auxin-CUC2-RCO feedback loop: emergent integrated-contour dissection, growing cellular spring-lattice lamina with Mitchison-canalized veins and microtubule-anisotropic growth, and Cardamine hirsuta specimen segmentation — Code-to-model traceability: 80/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "The module docstring (L1-80) maps all five laws to their Lean theorems with verified line loci and states the Pass 3 changes, the honest outcome and the model's limits; `GrowingLaminaSpringMesh` and the new helpers carry per-step citations (Mitchison, Scarpella, Hamant, Sampathkumar, Kierzkowski); the math-KG yaml (`przemyslaw-allometric-compound-leaf.yaml`, 5 equations) has lean_locus and code_locus entries that were re-checked against the current file. Deductions: several docstrings and the Section 2 header still call the prescribed-template margin signal a \"reaction-transport PDE\" (L154-186) (-8); v2 line references elsewhere in the repository (v2 audit, KG) now point at shifted lines (-4); panel titles in the growth GIF still read as validation rather than template output (-4); mesh parameter defaults are documented only in the signature, not in the docstring (-4)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "2011-przemyslaw-allometric-compound-leaf.py L154–L186: simulate_growing_margin_feedback_pde is still documented as a reaction-transport PDE although its peaks are a Gaussian template (see HONESTY NOTE L187) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2011-przemyslaw-allometric-compound-leaf.py#L154-L186>" ;
        ns1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-przemyslaw-allometric-compound-leaf-code-traceability-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-przemyslaw-allometric-compound-leaf-code-traceability-2> ;
        ns1:hasScore 8e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-przemyslaw-allometric-compound-leaf-model-fidelity> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Bilsborough et al. (2011), Barkoulas et al. (2008), Vlad et al. (2014) & Kierzkowski et al. (2019) growing leaf margin PIN1-Auxin-CUC2-RCO feedback loop: emergent integrated-contour dissection, growing cellular spring-lattice lamina with Mitchison-canalized veins and microtubule-anisotropic growth, and Cardamine hirsuta specimen segmentation — Model fidelity to source: 72/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Loops 1-3 of Bilsborough et al. (2011) are implemented as exact algebraic laws on a 1D margin profile (L154-317), the margin contour is now genuinely integrated from the Loop 3 outgrowth velocity (`integrate_margin_outgrowth`, L417-475; emergent I_D L476-523) and the new `GrowingLaminaSpringMesh` (L654-1137) is a real overdamped elastic solver (Hookean springs + area penalty, L999-1025) with rest-length growth from an anisotropic tensor (L1027-1065), a screened-Poisson growth field (L872-887), Mitchison canalization on sparse linear solves (L905-927) and a flux-connected vein topology check (L929-947); 5 Lean 4 theorems (3 v2 + Hamant partition L164-192 + Mitchison feedback L206-224) mirror the code. Deductions: the auxin convergence peaks are a prescribed Gaussian template (L198-216; disclosed L187-194), so Loop 1 is verified only as an identity and tooth number/spacing are inputs (-10); the remediation asked for a 3D FE vertex mesh and the delivered lamina is 2D, without thickness, division or adaxial/abaxial layers (-8); the stress-feedback lamina anisotropy is implemented (L985-990) but disabled by default (a_lamina = 0.0, L706) because it destabilised the explicit relaxation (-5); the equal-duration growth law cannot produce leaflet-level dissection (sweep ceiling 0.427, L1186-1215) (-5)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "2011-przemyslaw-allometric-compound-leaf.py L187–L216: HONESTY NOTE and convergence_drive: auxin peaks are prescribed Gaussians at u = +-0.22 k; PIN1 up-the-gradient transport is not solved <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2011-przemyslaw-allometric-compound-leaf.py#L187-L216>",
            "2011-przemyslaw-allometric-compound-leaf.py L705–L706: a_vein = 0.20 but a_lamina = 0.0: the Sampathkumar (2014) stress-feedback channel is switched off by default <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2011-przemyslaw-allometric-compound-leaf.py#L705-L706>" ;
        ns1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-przemyslaw-allometric-compound-leaf-model-fidelity-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-przemyslaw-allometric-compound-leaf-model-fidelity-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-przemyslaw-allometric-compound-leaf-model-fidelity-3> ;
        ns1:hasScore 7.2e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-przemyslaw-allometric-compound-leaf-morphometric-validation> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Bilsborough et al. (2011), Barkoulas et al. (2008), Vlad et al. (2014) & Kierzkowski et al. (2019) growing leaf margin PIN1-Auxin-CUC2-RCO feedback loop: emergent integrated-contour dissection, growing cellular spring-lattice lamina with Mitchison-canalized veins and microtubule-anisotropic growth, and Cardamine hirsuta specimen segmentation — Morphometric validation: 55/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "`measure_morphoeval()` (L1339-1570) returns 20 measurements, every one with unit, reference_value, reference_source, uncertainty and method; all dissection indices are emergent and the circular Pass 2 r = 0.998 is explicitly withdrawn (L1426-1434). Lean-mirrored identities (L1216-1249) and mesh-validity metrics (inverted elements 0, residual 1e-3) are included. Deductions: At WT is a calibration (kappa_n tuned to 0.228, L426), not a prediction (-5); Ch WT misses by 0.53, mir164a-4 by 0.21 and the rco/At WT order is inverted, so the only free predictions fail (-15); the emergent r = 0.807 has p = 0.052 (-5); the specimen measurements' references are self-referential (-7); the MT-ablation effect (delta I_D 0.029) and the vein-axial stretch ratio (1.04 vs 1.02 control) are within the resolution-limit noise of a one-vertex tooth (-8); the `cuc2_mutant_smooth` measurement's reference uncertainty was widened to 0.012 so that 0.000 vs 0.012 passes (-5)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "2011-przemyslaw-allometric-compound-leaf.py L1415–L1424: cardamine_wt_compound_dissection_index_ID = 0.254 vs reference 0.785 is reported as OUT-OF-PREDICTION rather than fitted <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2011-przemyslaw-allometric-compound-leaf.py#L1415-L1424>",
            "2011-przemyslaw-allometric-compound-leaf.py L426–L427: kappa_n = 0.50 calibrated on the At WT datum: the At WT measurement is a fit <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2011-przemyslaw-allometric-compound-leaf.py#L426-L427>" ;
        ns1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-przemyslaw-allometric-compound-leaf-measurement-arabidopsis-wt-auxin-cuc2-antiphase-r>,
