    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-raspopovic-bmp-sox9-wnt-digits-overall> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Raspopovic et al. (2014) 3-node Bmp-Sox9-Wnt Turing digit patterning network modulated by distal FGF on a moving-boundary FEM limb-bud outgrowth mesh — MorphoEval overall 84.0/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 3 (v3) evaluation of `2014-raspopovic-bmp-sox9-wnt-digits.py` (84.0/100; v2 96.3, v1 56.8). The single v2 remediation item is closed: Section 3b couples the 3-node network to a genuine moving-boundary P1 finite-element limb-bud mesh (2496 nodes / 4750 triangles) with a conservative ALE lumped-mass update that realises the Crampin-Gaffney-Maini dilution term exactly, implicit diffusion with the stiffness re-assembled on the deformed mesh, and AER-anchored FGF/Hoxd wavelength modulation. From unbiased noise the growing bud produces 5 unbranched Sox9 rays (bifurcation range 0 in 3/3 seeds; 0.67 without the modulation), out-of-phase ligands (r = -0.978 / -0.994), and sequential ray addition 2 -> 4 -> 5 as the distal arc grows 11.9 -> 20.1. The solver is verified against the analytic dispersion relation (2.2 % at q_c), the dilution law (slope -1.000, rho_c 0.265 vs 0.261) and the arc-length law (monotone, slope 0.225 vs 0.250); three new Lean theorems formalise these laws. The overall score nevertheless falls because the re-read exposed that the v2 2D fan result was mode-seeded and masked, the v2 FGF/Hox collapse rests on a fitted exponent that contradicts the network's own dispersion relation, and the LDN / CHIR counts are capped by hand; the FEM layer's own reductions (prescribed fan, uniform stretch, analytic references, interior ray insertion) are priced in as well. Overall 84.0/100 (faithfulness 81.9, reproducibility 88.9); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit d58a084; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 82, Morphological realism / specimen match 81, Parameter expressivity 84, Morphometric validation 82, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 86, Reproducibility package 90. Output judged: docs/media/bmp_sox9_wnt_digits_comparison.png: rendered output of 2014-raspopovic-bmp-sox9-wnt-digits.py at d58a084, image/png, 1351556 B, 2453×2288 px, artifact_sha256 22b27c34b46a015ca80913991f77bbaec823119454402539c53eb86847740d91 (sha256 22b27c34b46a015ca80913991f77bbaec823119454402539c53eb86847740d91), spec_fingerprint fcc019aeaf38ae13b447dccbc8f276f80745d761e03ea95627ecad0617dd1321. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: fcc019aeaf38ae13b447dccbc8f276f80745d761e03ea95627ecad0617dd1321; artifact_sha256: 22b27c34b46a015ca80913991f77bbaec823119454402539c53eb86847740d91; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/bmp_sox9_wnt_digits/bmp_sox9_wnt_digits_reference.json=c0444b665610be2e..., datasets/bmp_sox9_wnt_digits/limb_bud_outgrowth_fem_reference.json=3db7c9493f12c2b3..., datasets/bmp_sox9_wnt_digits/paper_citations.bib=88ff32a60b567060..., datasets/bmp_sox9_wnt_digits/paper_citations_pass3.bib=eab1e111424c9ac1..., datasets/bmp_sox9_wnt_digits/scout_manifest.json=f990b473b6a93cfa..., datasets/bmp_sox9_wnt_digits/sox9_limb_digits_specimen.jpg=533f621904d6f2ce...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-bmp-sox9-wnt-digits-audit-v2. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Raspopovic et al. (2014): a 3-node network of cell-autonomous Sox9 with diffusing Bmp and Wnt (Sox9 represses both ligands, Bmp activates and Wnt represses Sox9) is Turing-unstable without ligand self-activation; Sox9 digit stripes are out of phase with Bmp and Wnt; on the growing autopod a distal FGF / Hoxd gradient that lengthens the wavelength keeps the stripes unbranched, and the growing-domain simulations were run on a realistic limb-bud growth map (Marcon et al. 2011) | Sheth et al. (2012): digit number scales with autopod width / Hox dosage through the Turing wavelength | Crampin, Gaffney & Maini (1999): on a growing domain every species acquires the dilution term -(div u) c and modes are inserted sequentially as the domain lengthens | Boehm et al. (2010): finite-element limb-bud growth; a proliferation gradient alone does not explain the bud shape | Farin et al. (2013): E12.5 Sox9 / E13.5 Col2a1 WISH of wild-type (5) and Tbx2-/- (6) digit condensations (the vendored specimen) | Shubin & Alberch (1986): the digital arch forms posterior to anterior with the marginal digit I last; reconstructed_in_script: 3-node and reduced 2-diffuser Jacobians, dispersion relation and D = 0 control (Laws 1-3); 1D distal-arc explicit solver; 2D polar-fan finite-difference solver carried from v2; 7-regime FGF/Hox table; 6-condition perturbation suite; DoG + chromogen segmentation of the WISH specimen (5 WT vs 6 Tbx2-/- rays) | Pass 3: P1 finite-element solver on a Lagrangian / ALE polar-fan mesh with a moving AER boundary, implicit diffusion, conservative lumped-mass dilution, re-assembled stiffness, AER-anchored wavelength modulation with three modes, FEM verification against the analytic dispersion relation, growth-dilution sweep, final-arc sweep, 3 x 3 modulation ablation, 9 new reference-anchored measurements and 3 new Lean theorems (Laws 4-6); transfer_boundary: The mesh is a prescribed polar fan (r_prox = 4.2, R: 5.0 -> 8.4, theta_max = 0.38 pi) with a uniform radial Lagrangian stretch and an exponential-then-capped outgrowth law; there is no proliferation field, no realistic bud outline, no dorsoventral axis and no measured growth kinetics | The FGF / Hoxd modulation enters as D ∝ (r / R(t))^2 (lambda ∝ r / R(t)); this is the unique modulation that keeps sigma_max fixed while scaling lambda with the arc, not an equation of Raspopovic et al. (2014), whose supplementary modulation functions were not retrieved | All new reference values are analytic consequences of the baseline parameters (dispersion relation, Lean Laws 4-6) or qualitative statements from the papers; no digitised stripe count, growth curve or width-vs-digit-number data are vendored | The v2 7-regime FGF/Hox collapse depends on a fitted exponent (3.12) in a diffusion scaling that the network itself does not produce; the v2 LDN / CHIR digit counts are capped by hand; the v2 2D polar-fan result is mode-seeded and cosmetically masked (all three are disclosed here and carried as Pass 4 items); does_not_claim: A reproduction of the Raspopovic et al. (2014) supplementary growing-domain simulations, measured outgrowth kinetics of the mouse limb bud, the posterior-to-anterior order of digit condensation (the model inserts new rays in the interior), chondrogenic condensation mechanics, 3D geometry, or digit identity." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 2014-raspopovic-bmp-sox9-wnt-digits.py:1088-1120 and 1993-2000 — the arc sweep gives 2, 4, 5, 5, 6 against the integer law 3, 4, 5, 6, 7 (exact 2/5) and the self-test only requires |slope - 1/lambda| < 0.08. Report the band of admissible counts per arc (from the dispersion band sigma > 0.9 sigma_max) and tighten the test, or average over seeds.",
            "remediation needed: 2014-raspopovic-bmp-sox9-wnt-digits.py:1721-1812 and datasets/bmp_sox9_wnt_digits/limb_bud_outgrowth_fem_reference.json — eight of nine Pass 3 references are analytic / model-internal. Vendor measured anchors (Sheth 2012 width vs digit number, Raspopovic Fig. 4 stripe counts with and without modulation) and compare the FEM ray width, spacing CV and taper with the segmented specimen rays.",
            "remediation needed: 2014-raspopovic-bmp-sox9-wnt-digits.py:303-365 (L318 d_scale = (k_bs_eff / k_bs)^3.12 * fgf_scale^2) with datasets/bmp_sox9_wnt_digits/bmp_sox9_wnt_digits_reference.json `fgf_hox_wavelength_scaling` — the 7-regime wavelength collapse is produced by a fitted exponent; with D fixed the network shortens lambda_c as k_bs rises (5.02 -> 3.27 for k_bs 1.0 -> 3.2). Retrieve the Raspopovic et al. (2014) supplementary modulation functions, re-derive which parameter the FGF / Hox gradients modulate, and re-score the table without a fitted exponent.",
            "remediation needed: 2014-raspopovic-bmp-sox9-wnt-digits.py:476-594 (L526-528 mode seeding, L549-550 radial diffusion x 0.0008, L514 / L560-567 cosmetic envelope) — the v2 2D polar-fan solver imposes its 5-ray result. Remove it (or rerun it from noise with isotropic diffusion) and drop the '2D fan-shaped autopod ... digit ray count' measurement (L1855-1864) in favour of the FEM measurement, or label it explicitly as seeded.",
            "remediation needed: 2014-raspopovic-bmp-sox9-wnt-digits.py:617-629 and 644-649 — per-condition basal Sox9 offsets and the min(1, ...) / min(2, ...) caps hard-code the LDN-193189 and CHIR99021 digit counts. Derive the counts from the solver with a single condensation threshold and report the failures if the network does not reproduce them.",
            "remediation needed: 2014-raspopovic-bmp-sox9-wnt-digits.py:712-718 and 871 (fan map, R(t) = min(R1, R0 exp(g t)), uniform stretch) — the limb-bud geometry and kinematics are prescribed. Vendor the Boehm et al. (2010) / Marcon et al. (2011) outgrowth kinetics and bud outline (or digitise Raspopovic Fig. 4 stage outlines), drive the mesh by a proliferation field and compare L_arc(t) with the measured width.",
            "remediation needed: 2014-raspopovic-bmp-sox9-wnt-digits.py:915-923 with measurement L1796-1811 — new rays are inserted in the interior (0/3 marginal; eta = -0.25, +0.47, +0.11) and marginal half-rays sit on the straight fan boundary, whereas the digital arch adds the marginal digits last and the specimen's digits I / V are inset. Add a rounded outline with margin competence loss (or a Shh / Gli3 anterior-posterior bias) and re-measure the insertion order.",
            "remediation needed: Repro: add a requirements.lock for the recorded environment (python 3.14.7 / numpy 2.5.4 / scipy 1.16.3 / matplotlib 3.10.7 / Pillow 12.0.0), set MPLCONFIGDIR inside the script when the default is unwritable, and tighten the FEM tolerances (sigma 0.05 -> 0.03, slope 0.08 -> 0.04) in self_test (L1974-1977, L1999-2000)." ;
        ns1:hasScore 8.4e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-raspopovic-bmp-sox9-wnt-digits-parameter-expressivity> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Raspopovic et al. (2014) 3-node Bmp-Sox9-Wnt Turing digit patterning network modulated by distal FGF on a moving-boundary FEM limb-bud outgrowth mesh — Parameter expressivity: 84/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 3 adds three sweeps that behave as the formal laws predict: the dilution rate rho lowers sigma_eff linearly (slope -1.000, r = -1.000, threshold 0.265 vs 0.261; L1033-1085), the final arc length raises the distal ray count monotonically (2, 4, 5, 5, 6 over L_arc 12..28, Spearman 0.97, slope 0.225 vs 0.250; L1088-1120), and the modulation mode controls branching (scaled 0.00 < material 0.67 = none 0.67 mean bifurcation range over 3 seeds; L1123-1139); `--growth-rate` and `--fgf-mode` are wired through render_comparison_figure (L2029-2036, L1264-1268). Deductions: the arc sweep matches the integer law in only 2/5 cases because noise-driven mode selection in this broad-band network is +/- 1 ray (-5); the v2 7-regime FGF/Hox panel is a fitted curve (L318) and the LDN / CHIR counts are capped by hand (L644-649), so two of the nine panels do not demonstrate parameter control by the model (-7); the growth rate is swept only through the dilution proxy, not through full FEM runs at several g (-4)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "2014-raspopovic-bmp-sox9-wnt-digits.py L644–L649: LDN / CHIR digit counts capped by min(1, ...) / min(2, ...) (deduction) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2014-raspopovic-bmp-sox9-wnt-digits.py#L644-L649>" ;
        ns1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-raspopovic-bmp-sox9-wnt-digits-parameter-expressivity-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-raspopovic-bmp-sox9-wnt-digits-parameter-expressivity-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-raspopovic-bmp-sox9-wnt-digits-parameter-expressivity-3> ;
        ns1:hasScore 8.4e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-raspopovic-bmp-sox9-wnt-digits-repro-package> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Raspopovic et al. (2014) 3-node Bmp-Sox9-Wnt Turing digit patterning network modulated by distal FGF on a moving-boundary FEM limb-bud outgrowth mesh — Reproducibility package: 90/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "`--self-test` runs 12 checks in 55 s (L1908-2017): SHA-256 of 6 files, Laws 1-3, FGF table, perturbation ordering, specimen segmentation, 1D determinism, FEM stiffness / mass / dispersion / ALE checks, 5 unbranched rays with out-of-phase ligands and sequential addition, ablation ordering, dilution slope and threshold, arc monotonicity, and bitwise FEM determinism from a fresh integration (L2002-2005); the default render takes 41 s and writes both artefacts; all parameters are exposed in argparse (L2020-2062). Deductions: no lock file pins the interpreter / numpy / scipy / matplotlib / Pillow versions, and the v2 audit recorded versions that differ from the venv (-5); when `~/.matplotlib` is not writable the run emits font-cache warnings and writes a temporary cache, which the script does not control via MPLCONFIGDIR (-2); the self-test tolerance on the arc slope (0.08) and the 5 % sigma tolerance are lenient relative to the 2.2 % achieved (-2); the GIF palette is quantised from the first frame, so byte identity across Pillow versions is not guaranteed (-1)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-repro-package> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/repro-package" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "2014-raspopovic-bmp-sox9-wnt-digits.py L1993–L2000: Lenient tolerances: |slope - 1/lambda| < 0.08, Spearman > 0.9 (deduction) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2014-raspopovic-bmp-sox9-wnt-digits.py#L1993-L2000>" ;
        ns1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-raspopovic-bmp-sox9-wnt-digits-repro-package-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-raspopovic-bmp-sox9-wnt-digits-repro-package-2> ;
        ns1:hasScore 9e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-raspopovic-bmp-sox9-wnt-digits-source-traceability> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Raspopovic et al. (2014) 3-node Bmp-Sox9-Wnt Turing digit patterning network modulated by distal FGF on a moving-boundary FEM limb-bud outgrowth mesh — Source and data traceability: 90/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "All 8 sources carry DOIs in the module docstring (L7-38), the two BibTeX files and the dataset README; six dataset files are SHA-256 pinned and verified fail-closed on every run (L135-182), including the new reference table and the Pass 3 BibTeX file, kept separate so the v2 digests are unchanged. Deductions: the Raspopovic et al. (2014) supplementary growth maps and modulation functions were not retrieved, so the FEM layer's provenance is to secondary descriptions (-4); no digitised data from Boehm (2010), Marcon (2011) or Sheth (2012) are vendored and the reference table was written in this loop (-4); the v2 reference JSON's FGF/Hox table pairs k_bs_eff with lambda_obs in a direction the model does not produce and carries no per-row source pointer (-2)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-source-traceability> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/source-traceability" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "datasets/bmp_sox9_wnt_digits/limb_bud_outgrowth_fem_reference.json L7–L11: not_vendored list: growth kinetics, bud outline and the paper's modulation functions are absent (deduction) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/datasets/bmp_sox9_wnt_digits/limb_bud_outgrowth_fem_reference.json#L7-L11>" ;
        ns1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-raspopovic-bmp-sox9-wnt-digits-source-traceability-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-raspopovic-bmp-sox9-wnt-digits-source-traceability-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-raspopovic-bmp-sox9-wnt-digits-source-traceability-3> ;
        ns1:hasScore 9e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-raspopovic-bmp-sox9-wnt-digits-specimen-match> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Raspopovic et al. (2014) 3-node Bmp-Sox9-Wnt Turing digit patterning network modulated by distal FGF on a moving-boundary FEM limb-bud outgrowth mesh — Morphological realism / specimen match: 81/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Panel F still segments the SHA-256-locked Farin et al. (2013) WISH image (L1145-1245: 5 WT E12.5 Sox9 rays, 5 WT E13.5 Col2a1 rays, 6 Tbx2-/- rays, spacing CV 0.155) and Panel A now places a genuinely emergent 5-ray FEM limb bud beside it (L1311-1332), with the outgrowth sequence (Panel G, L1520-1552), the bifurcating ablation (Panel H, L1555-1574) and an 8-frame GIF of the growing mesh (L1622-1695). The rays run unbranched from wrist to AER and are out of phase with Bmp, as in the paper's Fig. 2 and 4. Deductions: the FEM bud is a sharp-cornered sector, not the rounded paddle of the specimen, and its marginal rays sit on the anterior / posterior boundary as half-rays whereas the specimen's digits I and V are inset behind an interdigital margin (-8); no quantitative side-by-side of the FEM rays with the specimen (ray width, spacing CV, taper) is made — the specimen metrics are compared only with the v2 1D / fan solvers (-5); the v2 2D fan panel has been replaced, but the ablation panel's 'none' case shows 4 vs 3 rays rather than the clear Y-splits of the paper's unmodulated simulation (-3); the GIF right panel is the 1D profile, not the FEM ligand fields (-3)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-specimen-match> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/specimen-match" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "2014-raspopovic-bmp-sox9-wnt-digits.py L712–L718: Fan geometry with straight radial margins: marginal half-rays at the boundary unlike the specimen (deduction) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2014-raspopovic-bmp-sox9-wnt-digits.py#L712-L718>" ;
        ns1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-raspopovic-bmp-sox9-wnt-digits-specimen-match-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-raspopovic-bmp-sox9-wnt-digits-specimen-match-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-raspopovic-bmp-sox9-wnt-digits-specimen-match-3> ;
        ns1:hasScore 8.1e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling-code-traceability> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Richman et al. (1975) & Tallinen et al. (2014, 2016) neo-Hookean constrained cortical expansion and sulcal creasing instability, with a Pass 3 3D hemispheric Swift-Hohenberg surface surrogate — Code-to-model traceability: 84/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "The module header maps Laws 1-6 to their papers and to the 6 Lean theorems by name (L34-74); every Pass 3 function carries a docstring naming the equation and source (GSH Eq. 1 of Stoop 2015 at L526-538, Lyapunov functional at L507-509, Fischl & Dale thickness range, honeycomb bound), the honesty note (L376-388) states exactly what is and is not emergent, and the math-KG YAML registers equations 4-6 with single-range `code_locus` pins. Deductions: the GI growth law is written with exponent 0.85 in Panel C and the GIF (L1175, L1532) but 0.88 in the solver (L267) — the plotted curve is not the curve the solver uses (-5); constants 1.603 / 0.88 / 0.22 / 0.65 / 0.18 / 2.8 / 4.2 in the 2D solver (L265-288) are uncited (-5); eps_scale 0.5 and g2 0.35 are documented but not derived (-3); the Y- junction raster ignores the polar caps (|lat| > 60 deg) and the longitude wrap of `ndi.label`, which is not stated in the docstring (-3)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "1975-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling.py L1175–L1175: Panel C GI law uses exponent 0.85 while the solver (L267) uses 0.88 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/1975-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling.py#L1175-L1175>",
            "1975-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling.py L1532–L1532: GIF GI curve also uses exponent 0.85 — inconsistent with the solver <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/1975-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling.py#L1532-L1532>" ;
        ns1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling-code-traceability-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling-code-traceability-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling-code-traceability-3> ;
        ns1:hasScore 8.4e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling-model-fidelity> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Richman et al. (1975) & Tallinen et al. (2014, 2016) neo-Hookean constrained cortical expansion and sulcal creasing instability, with a Pass 3 3D hemispheric Swift-Hohenberg surface surrogate — Model fidelity to source: 78/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Laws 1-3 (growth excess Delta_g = max(0, g - g_c), lambda = 2 pi h (mu_c / 3 mu_s)^(1/3), GI = 1 + 2 N d / P_hull; L162-189) are Richman's and Zilles's and are machine-checked. The Pass 3 GSH surrogate (L515-576) is a recognised reduced model for film-on-curved-substrate wrinkling (Stoop 2015), its Lyapunov energy (L506-512) decreases in every supercritical stage, its uniform mode is damped and its subcritical null is exact; the cotangent Laplace-Beltrami operator passes kernel, area and l = 1 eigenvalue checks (self-test #9). Deductions: the 2D coronal \"neo-Hookean\" solver is not a buckling model — n_sulci_target = round(P_hull / lambda_theory) (L253), gi_target = 1 + 1.603 dg^0.88 thinness_boost (L266-267) and the cusp profile u_eq (L272-276) are prescribed, and the energy (L290-314) penalises deviation from u_eq, so L-BFGS-B denoises a target rather than selecting a mode (-10); the 3D surrogate imposes k_c(x) and imports depth from the 2D solver (L735-736), so neither wavelength nor amplitude is emergent in 3D and the requested volumetric FEM is absent (-6); the Lissencephaly control has g = 1.14 < g_c so h = 6.5 mm is never exercised — Richman's thick-cortex prediction (longer wavelength) is not tested (-3); eps_scale and g2_curvature_coeff are unsourced (-3); the honesty note (L376-388) and the Lean coverage of all 6 laws prevent a larger deduction." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "1975-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling.py L253–L276: 2D solver prescribes n_sulci_target from P_hull/lambda_theory, gi_target from unsourced constants 1.603/0.88/0.22 and a cusp profile u_eq before minimisation <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/1975-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling.py#L253-L276>",
            "1975-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling.py L290–L314: Energy is a penalty on (u - u_eq) plus bending/slope differences from u_eq: L-BFGS-B relaxes toward the prescribed profile <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/1975-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling.py#L290-L314>",
            "1975-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling.py L735–L736: 3D crease-wall GI uses mean_sulcal_depth_mm from the 2D shell of the same stage — depth is not emergent in 3D <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/1975-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling.py#L735-L736>" ;
        ns1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling-model-fidelity-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling-model-fidelity-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling-model-fidelity-3>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling-model-fidelity-4> ;
        ns1:hasScore 7.8e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling-morphometric-validation> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Richman et al. (1975) & Tallinen et al. (2014, 2016) neo-Hookean constrained cortical expansion and sulcal creasing instability, with a Pass 3 3D hemispheric Swift-Hohenberg surface surrogate — Morphometric validation: 68/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "`measure_morphoeval()` (L1572-1743) returns 15 reference-anchored measurements, 6 new in Pass 3 (L1682-1743) with explicit caveats in their `note` fields. Credited: the GW22 subcritical null is exact (0 junctions, GI_3D = 1), Y-junction count rises 0 -> 21 -> 122 and sulcal components fall 178 -> 40 across GW26 -> GW38 (a genuinely emergent topological result), GI_3D 2.604 vs 2.56, and the gradient sweep reports slope, SE, r and RMSE. Deductions: measurements #1, #3 and #9 (L1592-1621, L1672-1681) compare the Richman formula with `lambda_obs_mm` values that are themselves 4.3633 h in the JSON (L41-276), so r = 1.0000 / alpha = 0.9993 / lambda/h = 4.3642 are formula-vs-formula (-12); measurements #4, #5 and #7 (L1622-1661) report the prescribed 2D targets (lambda_sim 11.20 = P_hull / round(P_hull / lambda_theory), GI_sim = gi_target, 85/28 = the empirical counts), so their agreement is by construction (-8); #10 and #14 are consistency checks because k_c(x) is imposed (stated in the notes) (-3); #12 and #15 have only a mathematical upper bound (honeycomb 2.31) and a \">1\" lower bound as references, with no empirical fetal sulcal-graph value (-3)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "1975-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling.py L1592–L1621: Measurements #1 and #3 regress formula wavelengths against lambda_obs_mm that are formula-generated in the reference JSON (circular r = 1.0000) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/1975-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling.py#L1592-L1621>",
            "1975-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling.py L1622–L1661: Measurements #4, #5, #7 report lambda_sim, GI_sim and sulcus counts that equal the prescribed targets of the 2D solver <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/1975-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling.py#L1622-L1661>",
            "datasets/cortical_gyrification_folding/cortical_gyrification_folding_reference.json L41–L276: Every lambda_obs_mm equals 4.3633 * h_cortex_mm (e.g. GW26 1.65 -> 7.20, mouse 0.88 -> 3.84); no per-value figure/table provenance <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/datasets/cortical_gyrification_folding/cortical_gyrification_folding_reference.json#L41-L276>" ;
        ns1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling-measurement-11-species-mammalian-gyrification-index-scaling-correlation-tallinen-2014-mota-2015>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling-measurement-11-species-mammalian-sulcal-wavelength-scaling-correlation-richman-1975-tallinen-2014>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling-measurement-3d-crease-wall-gyrification-index-gi-3d-1-l-zero-d-mean-a-hull-at-gw38-hemispheric-gsh-planform>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling-measurement-3d-gsh-subcritical-null-y-junctions-and-gi-3d-at-gw22-g-1-12-g-c>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling-measurement-3d-gsh-sulcal-network-percolation-across-ontogeny-largest-sulcal-component-fraction-gw38-gw26>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling-measurement-3d-hemispheric-gsh-surface-gw38-emergent-sulcal-wavelength-lambda-3d-cotangent-laplace-beltrami-10242-nodes>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling-measurement-3d-sulcal-y-junction-density-at-gw38-labyrinth-trivalent-skeleton-nodes-per-lambda-2-lat-60-deg>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling-measurement-coronal-human-brain-specimen-segmented-gyrification-index-gi-specimen-cerebral-cortex-gyri-specimen-jpg>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling-measurement-cross-species-log-log-power-law-exponent-alpha-lambda-h-alpha>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling-measurement-human-gw38-l-bfgs-b-relaxed-neo-hookean-shell-gyrification-index-gi-sim>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling-measurement-human-gw38-l-bfgs-b-relaxed-neo-hookean-shell-sulcal-wavelength-lambda-sim>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling-measurement-polymicrogyria-vs-normogyria-sulcus-frequency-modulation-ratio-richman-et-al-1975>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling-measurement-regional-thickness-gradient-sweep-emergent-anterior-posterior-wavelength-ratio-at-beta-0-3-h-2-08-3-12-mm>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling-measurement-universal-dimensionless-sulcal-wavelength-to-thickness-invariant-lambda-h-across-11-mammals>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling-measurement-zero-growth-lissencephaly-negative-control-gyrification-index-g-g-c-vs-gw38>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling-morphometric-validation-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling-morphometric-validation-2> ;
        ns1:hasScore 6.8e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling-overall> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Richman et al. (1975) & Tallinen et al. (2014, 2016) neo-Hookean constrained cortical expansion and sulcal creasing instability, with a Pass 3 3D hemispheric Swift-Hohenberg surface surrogate — MorphoEval overall 80.2/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 3 (v3) evaluation of `1975-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling.py` (overall weighted score 80.2/100, DOWN from 93.1 in v2). The one v2 remediation item (3D tetrahedral FEM on MRI templates) is closed in an honestly labelled reduced form: a generalized Swift-Hohenberg film-on-curved-substrate planform on a 3D ellipsoidal hemisphere (10 242-node cotangent Laplace-Beltrami) that produces emergent sulcal Y-junctions (0 / 21 / 122 at GW22 / GW26 / GW38), a dimple -> labyrinth percolation transition, a 3D crease-wall GI of 2.604 (obs 2.56, depth imported from the 2D solver) and an emergent regional wavelength that tracks a 1.5x anterior-posterior thickness gradient (slope 1.006). The 3 new Lean theorems verify (6 total, 0 sorrys), the self-test passes 12/12 in 13 s and the 3D solver is bitwise deterministic. The score nevertheless falls because this round's re-read found that the v2 headline validations are circular: the reference JSON's observed wavelengths are 4.3633 h by construction, and the 2D \"neo-Hookean solver\" relaxes toward a prescribed profile whose sulcus count and GI are computed from the formula and unsourced fitted constants (1.603, 0.88, 0.22) before minimisation. Six of the 15 measurements therefore report targets or formula-vs-formula agreement, two of the new 3D measurements are consistency checks (k_c imposed), and two have only mathematical bounds as references. These are now the Pass 4 items. Overall 80.2/100 (faithfulness 78.4, reproducibility 84.4); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 45670cb8; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0, scikit-image 0.26.0, lean 4.35.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 78, Morphological realism / specimen match 82, Parameter expressivity 86, Morphometric validation 68, Source and data traceability 84, Code-to-model traceability 84, Reproducibility package 85. Output judged: docs/media/cortical_gyrification_folding_comparison.png: rendered output of 1975-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling.py at 45670cb8, image/png, 821293 B, 2104×1452 px, artifact_sha256 ca86dd76e3d0c81460ea4a15d6e3c54f90b997c4272caa3b12ede091364d7413 (sha256 ca86dd76e3d0c81460ea4a15d6e3c54f90b997c4272caa3b12ede091364d7413), spec_fingerprint 13499943306506233e29ef0e44d9eb95a08cb36c62618ec286f2346b2d38f941. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 13499943306506233e29ef0e44d9eb95a08cb36c62618ec286f2346b2d38f941; artifact_sha256: ca86dd76e3d0c81460ea4a15d6e3c54f90b997c4272caa3b12ede091364d7413; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/cortical_gyrification_folding/cerebral_cortex_gyri_specimen.jpg=ff9a25e993fd5aad..., datasets/cortical_gyrification_folding/cortical_gyrification_folding_reference.json=94947373ac49d97d..., datasets/cortical_gyrification_folding/paper_citations.bib=c330565c1bac7790..., datasets/cortical_gyrification_folding/scout_manifest.json=7f5410ff8ad2c1ee..., datasets/cortical_gyrification_folding/surface_sh_3d_reference.json=5421bbea0b8fa9e5...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-cortical-gyrification-folding-audit-v2. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Richman et al. (1975): a stiff cortical plate growing on a softer subcortical foundation buckles with wavelength lambda = 2 pi h (mu_c / 3 mu_s)^(1/3), predicting fine folds for thin (microgyric) cortex and broad folds for thick cortex | Tallinen et al. (2014, 2016): multiplicative tangential growth F = F_e G of a neo-Hookean cortex above a critical excess g_c produces cusped sulci; a 3D gel-brain and a tetrahedral FEM on a GW22 MRI template reproduce fetal gyrification GW22-GW34 with GI rising to about 2.5 | Mota & Herculano-Houzel (2015): cortical folding scales universally with surface area and thickness across mammals | Zilles et al. (1988): human whole-hemisphere coronal gyrification index 2.56 +/- 0.08 | Stoop et al. (2015): a stiff film on a soft curved substrate follows a generalized Swift-Hohenberg equation whose curvature-induced quadratic term selects hexagonal dimples at low overstress and labyrinths at high overstress | Fischl & Dale (2000): regional human cortical thickness varies from about 1 mm to 4.5 mm (mean about 2.5 mm) across the hemisphere; reconstructed_in_script: Laws 1-3 (growth excess, cube-root wavelength, GI = 1 + 2 N d / P_hull) as closed-form functions; a 2D coronal shell relaxation (L-BFGS-B) toward a prescribed cusp profile with sulcus count and GI target set from the formula; 11-species and 4-condition sweeps; segmentation of one coronal specimen image | Pass 3: generalized Swift-Hohenberg relaxation on an ellipsoidal hemisphere surface (cotangent Laplace-Beltrami, semi-implicit Euler, Lyapunov energy), regional k_c(x) from a linear thickness gradient, raster skeleton Y-junction counting, marching-triangles iso-contour fundus length, 3D crease-wall GI with depth imported from the 2D solver, 4-point thickness-gradient sweep; transfer_boundary: The 11-species lambda_obs values in the reference JSON are generated from the Richman formula (4.3633 h), so cross-species wavelength agreement (r = 1.0000, alpha = 0.9993, lambda/h = 4.3642) is formula-vs-formula, not model-vs-measurement | The 2D coronal solver's sulcus count, GI target and cusp profile are prescribed before minimisation; L-BFGS-B removes injected noise rather than selecting a buckling mode, so GI_sim, lambda_sim and sulcus counts equal their targets by construction | The 3D surrogate's preferred wavenumber k_c(x) is imposed by the GSH operator; lambda_3D = 11.41 vs 11.33 and the gradient slope 1.006 are consistency checks of the nonlinear planform, and eps_scale = 0.5 / g2_curvature_coeff = 0.35 are tuning constants chosen to place GW26 in the dimple phase and GW38 in the labyrinth phase | The ellipsoid (1.30 R, 0.70 R, 0.95 R) is not an MRI template; Y-junction density has only the honeycomb upper bound 2.31 per lambda^2 as reference; the percolation ratio has only a > 1 lower bound; does_not_claim: A volumetric tetrahedral neo-Hookean FEM, emergent sulcal depth or GI amplitude in 3D, gyral-crown vs fundus thickness differentiation, MRI-template geometry, a Floquet/linear-stability derivation of g_c, or validation of Y-junction density against measured fetal sulcal graphs." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 1975-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling.py:1175 and 1532 vs 267 — the GI growth law is plotted with exponent 0.85 in Panel C and in the GIF but the solver uses 0.88; unify to one sourced exponent (or derive the GI(g) curve from the solver output) so the plotted law is the one computed.",
            "remediation needed: 1975-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling.py:1867-1882 — `--growth-g/--h-cortex/--mu-ratio/--R-brain` are passed only to `render_comparison_figure`; `evaluate_surface_3d_fetal_stages` and `evaluate_regional_thickness_gradient_sweep` receive only `seed` and `subdivisions`. Thread the physical overrides (and eps_scale / g2_curvature_coeff) into the 3D surrogate and add a sweep across the Stoop dimple/labyrinth boundary.",
            "remediation needed: 1975-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling.py:253-276 and 290-314 — the 2D coronal solver prescribes n_sulci_target = round(P_hull / lambda_theory), gi_target = 1 + 1.603 dg^0.88 (2.60/h)^0.22 and a cusp profile u_eq, then minimises a penalty on (u - u_eq); the 28 / 85 sulcus counts, GI_sim 2.5597 and lambda_sim 11.20 reported by measurements #4, #5, #7 are therefore targets, and `energy_drop_ratio` measures noise removal. Replace u_eq with a genuine growth-driven energy (neo-Hookean film strain energy with multiplicative growth g on a Winkler/half-space foundation, random initial condition) so that wavelength, count and GI are selected by the minimiser, and source or remove the constants 1.603 / 0.88 / 0.22.",
            "remediation needed: 1975-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling.py:610-669 — `count_sulcal_y_junctions` rasterises to an equirectangular grid, restricts to |lat| <= 60 deg and uses `ndi.label` without longitude wrap, so junctions and components at the poles and across the seam are miscounted; its only reference is the honeycomb upper bound 2.31 per lambda^2. Count junctions on the mesh skeleton directly (or use periodic labelling) and compare with a published fetal sulcal-graph junction density (e.g. Tallinen 2016 Fig. 4 or a sulcal-pit atlas).",
            "remediation needed: 1975-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling.py:620 with requirements.txt — `skimage.morphology.skeletonize` is a new hard dependency not declared in `requirements.txt` (outside this slot's editable files); add `scikit-image` to the repository requirements (or implement a pure-scipy thinning) and record the exact version in a lock file for this script.",
            "remediation needed: 1975-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling.py:735-736 and 691-714 — the 3D crease-wall GI_3D = 2.604 uses `shell2d[\"mean_sulcal_depth_mm\"]` from the 2D solver, so depth and GI amplitude are not emergent in 3D and no gyral-crown vs fundus thickness differentiation exists. Make depth emergent (e.g. a thin-shell Föppl-von Kármán film with growth on the same mesh, or at minimum a GSH amplitude-to-depth calibration fitted to Tallinen 2016 Fig. 3 rather than imported), and replace the ad-hoc ellipsoid (1.30, 0.70, 0.95) with a vendored, SHA-256-pinned fetal surface template.",
            "remediation needed: 1975-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling.py:991-1034 with 1663-1671 — specimen segmentation thresholds (0.86, 0.08, 14 px, 52nd / 76th percentiles, 62 px band) and the fallback spacings [34, 36, 35] are untraced, P_pial is approximated from distance-transform depths, and the single-section GI 2.81 is compared with the whole-hemisphere mean 2.56. Trace the pial contour directly, report the thresholds' provenance, and compare with a per-section GI reference (Zilles 1988 Fig. 2 profile).",
            "remediation needed: datasets/cortical_gyrification_folding/cortical_gyrification_folding_reference.json:245-254 with 1975-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling.py:924-958 — `lissencephaly_thick_cortex` has g = 1.14 < g_c, so h = 6.50 mm never affects the result and Richman's thick-cortex prediction (longer wavelength, fewer folds at supercritical g) is untested. Add a supercritical thick-cortex condition (h = 6.5 mm, g = 2.15) and assert lambda_sim rises by h-ratio and N_sulci falls.",
            "remediation needed: datasets/cortical_gyrification_folding/cortical_gyrification_folding_reference.json:41-276 with 1975-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling.py:851-922 and 1592-1621 — every `lambda_obs_mm` equals 4.3633 * h exactly (GW26 1.65 -> 7.20, mouse 0.88 -> 3.84), so measurements #1, #3 and #9 (r = 1.0000, alpha = 0.9993, lambda/h = 4.3642) validate the Richman formula against itself. Replace the species and fetal wavelengths with digitised values from Tallinen 2014 Fig. 4 / Mota 2015 supplementary tables (with figure/ table pointers per row), or relabel the rows `lambda_theory_mm` and drop the three circular measurements." ;
        ns1:hasScore 8.02e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling-parameter-expressivity> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Richman et al. (1975) & Tallinen et al. (2014, 2016) neo-Hookean constrained cortical expansion and sulcal creasing instability, with a Pass 3 3D hemispheric Swift-Hohenberg surface surrogate — Parameter expressivity: 86/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Spans 5 fetal stages, 11 species, 4 pathology/ablation conditions (L805-958) and, new in Pass 3, a 4-point anterior-posterior thickness-gradient sweep beta in {0, 0.1, 0.2, 0.3} (L760-802) whose emergent regional wavelength ratio tracks h_ant/h_post (slope 1.006, r = 1.0000), plus `--subdivisions` and `--skip-3d` (L1854-1855). Deductions: `--growth-g/--h-cortex/--mu-ratio/--R-brain` reach only the 2D fetal evaluation (L1867-1877) and not the 3D surrogate (L1879-1882), so the new mechanism cannot be explored from the CLI (-6); the lissencephaly condition varies g, not h, so the thickness axis is not exercised in the pathology sweep (-4); eps_scale and g2 are fixed in the JSON with no sweep across the Stoop dimple/labyrinth boundary (-4)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
