        ns1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling-repro-package> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Richman et al. (1975) & Tallinen et al. (2014, 2016) neo-Hookean constrained cortical expansion and sulcal creasing instability, with a Pass 3 3D hemispheric Swift-Hohenberg surface surrogate — Reproducibility package: 85/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "`self_test()` (L1746-1847) runs 12 checks in 13 s: SHA-256 of 5 files, JSON parity, ablation invariants, fetal monotonicity, 11-species collapse, pathology ordering, specimen segmentation, 2D determinism, and the Pass 3 Laplace-Beltrami sanity (#9), 3D GSH null/Lyapunov/wavelength/junction/GI ordering (#10), gradient sweep (#11) and bitwise 3D determinism (#12); default render is 11.7 s. Deductions: `scikit-image` is now a hard runtime dependency (`from skimage.morphology import skeletonize`, L620, imported lazily inside `count_sulcal_y_junctions`) and is NOT listed in `requirements.txt` — a fresh `pip install -r requirements.txt` environment fails at the 3D stage and in self-test #10 (-7); the self-test tolerances for the 3D stage (8% wavelength, |GI_3D - 2.56| < 0.15) are loose relative to the reported agreement (-2); `.gitignore` excludes `docs/media/*.png`, so neither the regenerated comparison PNG nor the new 3D PNG is tracked and the GIF content is byte-identical to Pass 2 (-3); the exact environment is recorded here but there is no lock file for this script (-3)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-repro-package> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/repro-package" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "1975-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling.py L620–L631: Lazy import of skimage.morphology.skeletonize — new scikit-image dependency not declared in requirements.txt <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/45670cb8/1975-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling.py#L620-L631>" ;
        ns1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling-repro-package-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling-repro-package-2> ;
        ns1:hasScore 8.5e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-richman-cortical-gyrification-buckling-source-traceability> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Richman et al. (1975) & Tallinen et al. (2014, 2016) neo-Hookean constrained cortical expansion and sulcal creasing instability, with a Pass 3 3D hemispheric Swift-Hohenberg surface surrogate — Source and data traceability: 84/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "8 primary sources carry DOIs in the module header (L5-32), in `paper_citations.bib` (now 8 entries incl. stoop2015curvature, fischl2000measuring, cross1993pattern at L56-90) and in the dataset README; all 5 dataset files are SHA-256 pinned (`EXPECTED_SHA256`, L109-126) and verified fail-closed at every run; the new `surface_sh_3d_reference.json` records parameter definitions and the honeycomb-bound derivation (L44-47, L65-66). Deductions: the reference JSON's `lambda_obs_mm` rows are formula-generated, and the fetal `g_tangential`, `GI_obs` and species `GI_obs` values carry no per-value figure/table pointer (-8); eps_scale = 0.5, g2_curvature_coeff = 0.35 and the ellipsoid proportions are stated but unsourced (-4); the 3 new DOIs were written from memory and could not be verified online under the no-network rule (-2); fitted constants 1.603 / 0.88 / 0.22 in the 2D solver are described as \"calibrated to Tallinen\" without a figure or table (-2)." ;
