        ns1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-runions-pavement-cell-lobing-model-fidelity> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Sapala et al. (2018) & Fu et al. (2005) ROP2-ROP6 interdigitated puzzle-shaped pavement cell lobing, Largest Empty Circle (LEC) turgor stress scaling, reduced pressurized periclinal membrane-shell and depth-resolved anticlinal wall buckling — Model fidelity to source: 85/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Credits: exact EDT R_LEC (L215-L265) and the Sapala Laplace proxy, a coupled ROP2-ROP6 RD system (L533-L662), and the new reduced periclinal membrane solver (L723-L838) whose discretisation is verified against the closed-form disk (z_max 0.9 %, mean strain 0.3 %, L900-L906) and whose inscribed-disk bound holds on all 18 footprints (L836), plus the depth strip with FD-vs-modal agreement (L1009-L1158). Deductions: the 'shell' is a uniform-tension Foppl membrane with an analytic edge boundary layer, not a bending-coupled 3D FEM shell, and T0 = PH/2 (L753), E = 300 MPa, nu = 0.3 and H = 15 um are assumptions (-5); the reduced mechanics contradicts the Laplace proxy the script headlines (ratio 1.73 vs 3.32, exponent 0.51 vs 1; L888-L889, L1677-L1683) and the discrepancy is reported but not resolved (-4); the WT footprint is a tuned band-plus-capsule construction (L349-L407) rather than Sapala's emergent spring-remodelling, and the RD wall displacement never feeds the polygon (-4); the v2 ribbon construction (aspect 18.7) shows the LEC pinning mechanism was previously achieved by elongation, so v2's 94 was over-credited (-2 carried as a correction)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "2017-runions-pavement-cell-lobing.py L329–L338: Comment documenting that the v2 WT construction was a 417 x 22 um ribbon (aspect 18.7) and the Pass 3 replacement; the LEC pinning is still geometric, not emergent <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2017-runions-pavement-cell-lobing.py#L329-L338>",
            "2017-runions-pavement-cell-lobing.py L753–L753: T0 = 0.5 * P * H: slab-cell pretension heuristic, not derived from the source model <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2017-runions-pavement-cell-lobing.py#L753-L753>" ;
        ns1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-runions-pavement-cell-lobing-model-fidelity-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-runions-pavement-cell-lobing-model-fidelity-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-runions-pavement-cell-lobing-model-fidelity-3>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-runions-pavement-cell-lobing-model-fidelity-4> ;
        ns1:hasScore 8.5e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-runions-pavement-cell-lobing-morphometric-validation> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Sapala et al. (2018) & Fu et al. (2005) ROP2-ROP6 interdigitated puzzle-shaped pavement cell lobing, Largest Empty Circle (LEC) turgor stress scaling, reduced pressurized periclinal membrane-shell and depth-resolved anticlinal wall buckling — Morphometric validation: 84/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "`measure_morphoeval()` (L1641-L1799) now reports 17 reference-anchored measurements: the 9 v2 metrics (WT R_LEC 11.39 vs 11.4 um, r = 0.986, RMSE 0.26 um; Laplace ratio 3.32; RD r = -0.99 / 0.9998; lambda 24.5 um; mature S 0.655 vs 0.68; ktn1 L 1.111 vs 1.11; specimen S 0.72) plus 8 Pass 3 metrics, of which the shell ratio (1.73 vs 3.32), the sigma-R_LEC exponent (0.51 vs 1) and r (0.98) are genuine tests against the paper's proxy. Deductions: five of the eight new measurements use analytic or model-internal references (disk closed form, inscribed-disk bound, FD-vs-modal error, analytic inner-face gain, junction-forcing control) — solver verification, not biological validation (-8); the depth attenuation has no empirical reference at all (-4); the mature WT lobeyness 1.734 is 0.11 above the 1.62 reference and the lobe count (12) is outside 7.8 +/- 1.6 but neither is reported as a measurement (-3); the specimen lobeyness differs from the v2 record (1.316 vs 1.506) with unchanged code, undermining it as a reference (-1)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "2017-runions-pavement-cell-lobing.py L1774–L1798: Pass 3 depth measurements: FD-vs-modal error, dominant-mode inner/outer gain with ANALYTIC reference, distributed-vs-junction forcing with MODEL-INTERNAL reference — explicitly labelled as having no vendored empirical data <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2017-runions-pavement-cell-lobing.py#L1774-L1798>" ;
        ns1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-runions-pavement-cell-lobing-measurement-anticlinal-depth-fd-vs-modal-rel-err>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-runions-pavement-cell-lobing-measurement-anticlinal-dominant-mode-inner-over-outer-gain>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-runions-pavement-cell-lobing-measurement-anticlinal-inner-over-outer-rms-distributed-vs-junction-forcing>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-runions-pavement-cell-lobing-measurement-anticlinal-lobe-wavelength-um>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-runions-pavement-cell-lobing-measurement-isotropic-vs-puzzle-stress-reduction-ratio>,
