    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-sharon-ripping-leaf-edge-waves-overall> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Sharon et al. (2002) Nature / Audoly & Boudaoud (2003) PRL Non-Euclidean Edge Buckling Cascades in Ruffled Leaf Margins — MorphoEval overall 92.1/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 3 (v3) evaluation of `2002-sharon-ripping-leaf-edge-waves.py` (overall weighted score 92.1/100, down from 93.6 in v2). The single v2 remediation item is closed: the quasi-static non-Euclidean FvK solver is now fed by a spatio-temporal CIN/TCP maturation front, PIN1 up-the-gradient auxin transport and CUC2 PDEs on a growing Lagrangian margin lattice (`simulate_tcp_auxin_margin_development`, L805-L1012); the cascade is re-solved on the developmental <g_0> = 0.6059 (K(0) = -0.001063 mm^-2, M = 4 generations), 27 serrations emerge (12 primary lobes / 15 secondary, hierarchy ratio 3.99, spacing 2.19 mm), and 5 genotype ablations satisfy 6/6 ordinal literature checks (cin <g_0> 2.10x WT and more negative K; TCP-OE 0.44x; cuc2 = pin1 = 0 serrations). Three new Lean 4 theorems (TCP-arrested growth increment, developmental excess metric non-negativity, pairwise PIN1 mass conservation) verify with 0 sorrys. The score falls because this pass surfaces the next layer of defects rather than hiding it: the WT developmental target is self-referential, 4 of 6 new measurements use placeholder / cross-module references, the serration wavelength is a parameter choice, 9 new DOIs are unverified, and the Pass 2 FvK relaxation reproduces its reference table by construction. Overall 92.1/100 (faithfulness 91.8, reproducibility 92.7); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 327729c8; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 93, Morphological realism / specimen match 91, Parameter expressivity 94, Morphometric validation 90, Source and data traceability 91, Code-to-model traceability 93, Reproducibility package 94. Output judged: docs/media/ripping_leaf_edge_waves_comparison.png: rendered output of 2002-sharon-ripping-leaf-edge-waves.py at 327729c8, image/png, 1731094 B, 2775×1680 px, artifact_sha256 d5fb947fa012711aa8cf8764f2abea6d111decc28d191e48affe89c491a8ecda (sha256 d5fb947fa012711aa8cf8764f2abea6d111decc28d191e48affe89c491a8ecda), spec_fingerprint 269fab4dc5e4e98c580cb49e700e990d268686b3f7823f895d6d7cb6898a616e. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 269fab4dc5e4e98c580cb49e700e990d268686b3f7823f895d6d7cb6898a616e; artifact_sha256: d5fb947fa012711aa8cf8764f2abea6d111decc28d191e48affe89c491a8ecda; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/ripping_leaf_edge_waves/lactuca_sativa_edge_waves_specimen.jpg=921d920a85d530f7..., datasets/ripping_leaf_edge_waves/paper_citations.bib=d9c45c59e0864ec3..., datasets/ripping_leaf_edge_waves/ripping_leaf_edge_waves_reference.json=4e4f250a3b7d5939..., datasets/ripping_leaf_edge_waves/scout_manifest.json=9d72416d0542e21c..., datasets/ripping_leaf_edge_waves/tcp_auxin_developmental_reference.json=31eb569d60e0c765...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-ripping-leaf-edge-waves-audit-v2. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Sharon et al. (2002): a free sheet with excess marginal arc length (torn plastic, lettuce, kale) buckles into a self-similar sub-harmonic cascade of edge waves whose wavelength grows linearly with distance from the edge | Audoly & Boudaoud (2003): self-similar cascade scaling lambda_{m+1} = lambda_m / r near a strained boundary | Liang & Mahadevan (2009): saddle-to-ripple transition of a long leaf controlled by the dimensionless metric strain parameter | Nath et al. (2003), Palatnik et al. (2003), Efroni et al. (2008): CIN/TCP transcription factors arrest marginal proliferation basipetally; cin / jaw-D leaves grow excess marginal area and become negatively curved, miR319-resistant TCP flattens | Bilsborough et al. (2011), Nikovics et al. (2006), Koyama et al. (2007), Hay et al. (2006): CUC2-gated PIN1 auxin convergence points position serrations on the growing margin; cuc2 and pin1 margins are smooth | Smith et al. (2006), Jönsson et al. (2006): up-the-gradient PIN1 polarisation generates auxin maxima; reconstructed_in_script: Exponential marginal metric g_yy(x) = 1 + g_0 exp(-x/ell), exact Brioschi K(x) < 0, linear lambda_loc(x), a surrogate L-BFGS-B FvK multi-generation cascade relaxation with flat-metric negative control, 3D mesh reconstruction, 9-station inward profile, 4-system taxon sweep and ExG specimen segmentation (Pass 2) | Pass 3: 1D forward-Euler PDEs on a growing Lagrangian margin lattice for auxin (diffusion + PIN1 up-the-gradient transport + production - decay - growth dilution), CUC2 (repressed by auxin and TCP, gating PIN1) and a basipetal TCP maturation front; interior and marginal growth strains whose ratio gives g_0(y,t); the FvK cascade re-solved on <g_0>; serration tips, primary/secondary hierarchy and emergence time from the kinematic outgrowth field; 5 genotype presets vs a 6-check ordinal phenotype table; transfer_boundary: The gene network parameters (TCP front speed, auxin diffusion/transport/decay, CUC2 kinetics) are Arabidopsis-literature-motivated magnitudes applied to a Lactuca sativa margin; the wild-type calibration target g_0 = 0.64 is the Pass 2 Lactuca mechanical value, so WT agreement is a cross-module self-consistency check, not a measurement | cin/WT = 1.5 and TCP-OE/WT = 0.6 in the reference table are placeholder magnitudes for the ordinal statements '> 1' and '< 1'; the serration-count range [5, 40] is a broad plausibility bound, not a digitised count | The Pass 2 cascade relaxation minimises a surrogate energy whose target slope, aspect constant, penetration targets and activation cutoff are chosen so the output reproduces the reference table; wavelength / penetration r = 1.0000 are by construction; does_not_claim: A 2D growing-sheet FvK or FEM solution with spatially resolved K(x,y) feedback, mechanical feedback on PIN1 polarity, cell division on the stretching lattice, an elastic in-plane solution for serration outgrowth, digitised serration/lobe counts from Bilsborough 2011 or Nath 2003, or online verification of the 9 new DOIs." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 2002-sharon-ripping-leaf-edge-waves.py:1616-1621 — `measure_morphoeval()` takes no arguments and always runs seed 2002 / default genotype, so CLI overrides (--genotype, --g0, --seed) never reach the measurement table. Accept the parsed namespace (or keyword overrides) so measurements are reproducible along every swept axis.",
            "remediation needed: 2002-sharon-ripping-leaf-edge-waves.py:1646, 1656, 1676 and the JSON genotype_phenotype_table — measurements 11, 12 and 14 compare against a placeholder 1.5, a range midpoint 22.5 and a cross-module 3.5. Digitise quantitative serration / lobe counts and cin-vs-WT marginal growth ratios from Bilsborough 2011 (Fig. 1, Fig. 4) and Nath 2003 (Fig. 1-2), store them with uncertainties in the reference table, and SHA-256-pin developmental_citations_pass3.bib.",
            "remediation needed: 2002-sharon-ripping-leaf-edge-waves.py:230-367 — the Pass 2 `relax_foppl_von_karman_cascade` minimises a surrogate energy whose target slope s_target (L307), c_aspect = 1/sqrt(3) (L283), penetration targets (L253), cutoff 4.65 t (L280) and Gamma < 120 gate (L302) reproduce the reference table by construction (r = 1.0000 for wavelength / penetration, lambda_m = lambda_1 / r^(m-1) is an input at L250). Replace with a true FvK energy on a discretised sheet whose cascade ratio and penetration depths are outputs, or relabel the measurements as self-consistency checks.",
            "remediation needed: 2002-sharon-ripping-leaf-edge-waves.py:592, 1242, 401, 415, 1024, 1033 — circular / unsourced constants: the Hosta saddle fallback lmin_s = 39.70 equals the reference value; K(0) = -1.091e-3 is hard-coded in the panel-D title; mesh mode phases, the 0.18 in-plane contraction factor and the 6 mm edge-displacement decay carry no citation. Read the first two from the reference table and either source or expose the rest as documented rendering parameters.",
            "remediation needed: 2002-sharon-ripping-leaf-edge-waves.py:805-1012 and 1014-1034 — the mechanics remain quasi-static and the gene network is 1D along the margin; the FvK cascade is re-solved only on the scalar <g_0> (L962) and the y-modulation sqrt(g_0(y)/<g_0>) (L964) is applied after the fact, while serration outgrowth ds/dt = k_s a (1-m) is kinematic bookkeeping, not an elastic in-plane growth solution. Pass 4: solve a 2D growing-metric FvK on the developmental g_yy(x,y,t) with stress-feedback PIN1 polarity (Heisler 2010 style) so serrations and lobes are mechanical outputs, and register the resulting law in Lean.",
            "remediation needed: 2002-sharon-ripping-leaf-edge-waves.py:812-816 — the serration wavelength (2.19 mm, N_ser = 27) is set by D_a, T_pin, kappa, mu_a chosen in a quick scan for robust patterning. Derive the linear-stability wavelength of the PIN1 up-the-gradient system analytically (or by a numerical dispersion scan), report it as a measurement with its parameter sensitivity, and test it against the digitised serration spacing of Bilsborough 2011.",
            "remediation needed: 2002-sharon-ripping-leaf-edge-waves.py:985-990 and 972 — no growth dilution for CUC2 and no cell division on the stretching lattice (cells enlarge x1.93 over 240 h) and `n_auxin_maxima_timeseries` uses a fixed 1.5 mm material spacing floor. Add cell division when cell length exceeds a threshold (re-meshing the Lagrangian lattice) and dilute CUC2 with the same growth term as auxin.",
            "remediation needed: datasets/ripping_leaf_edge_waves/developmental_citations_pass3.bib and the JSON primary_dois — all 9 new DOIs (10.1126/science.1079354, 10.1038/nature01958, 10.1073/pnas.1015162108, 10.1073/pnas.0510457103, 10.1073/pnas.0509839103, 10.1105/tpc.106.044792, 10.1105/tpc.106.045617, 10.1105/tpc.107.057521, 10.1038/ng1835) were transcribed offline and not verified. Verify each against Crossref in a networked pass and record the verification date in the README.",
            "remediation needed: datasets/ripping_leaf_edge_waves/tcp_auxin_developmental_reference.json (wild_type_calibration.target_g0_mean = 0.64) with 2002-sharon-ripping-leaf-edge-waves.py:828-829 and 1630-1640 — the WT developmental target is the Pass 2 mechanical module's own Lactuca g_0 and gamma_0 = 0.0085/h, beta = 0.75 were tuned to land near it, so measurement 10 is circular. Replace with an independent anchor (digitised marginal/interior growth-rate ratio from Nath 2003 Fig. 2 or Efroni 2008 kinematics) and re-fit gamma_0, beta against it." ;
        ns1:hasScore 9.21e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-sharon-ripping-leaf-edge-waves-parameter-expressivity> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Sharon et al. (2002) Nature / Audoly & Boudaoud (2003) PRL Non-Euclidean Edge Buckling Cascades in Ruffled Leaf Margins — Parameter expressivity: 94/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 2 sweeps (4 cascade generations L431-L514, 9 inward stations L516-L555, 4 sheet systems L557-L629) are retained and Pass 3 adds a genuine biological parameter axis: 5 genotype presets (`GENOTYPE_PRESETS`, L743-L750) scaling TCP front speed, CUC2->PIN1 gain and transport rate, swept by `evaluate_developmental_genotype_sweep` (L1037-L1095) with all 15 kinetic / growth parameters exposed as keyword arguments of `simulate_tcp_auxin_margin_development` (L805-L829), plus CLI `--genotype` and `--skip-developmental` (L1899-L1905) honoured in `main()` (L1927-L1936). Deductions: `measure_morphoeval()` ignores CLI overrides and always runs seed 2002 / defaults (L1616-L1621), so the measurement table cannot be re-expressed along any swept axis (-3); gamma_0 and beta_auxin are not swept, only the genotype presets are (-2); the genotype presets are discrete multipliers rather than a continuous dose-response along v_tcp (-1)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "2002-sharon-ripping-leaf-edge-waves.py L1616–L1621: measure_morphoeval() takes no arguments and always uses seed 2002 / default parameters — CLI overrides do not reach the measurement table <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/327729c8/2002-sharon-ripping-leaf-edge-waves.py#L1616-L1621>" ;
        ns1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sharon-ripping-leaf-edge-waves-parameter-expressivity-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sharon-ripping-leaf-edge-waves-parameter-expressivity-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sharon-ripping-leaf-edge-waves-parameter-expressivity-3>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sharon-ripping-leaf-edge-waves-parameter-expressivity-4> ;
        ns1:hasScore 9.4e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-sharon-ripping-leaf-edge-waves-repro-package> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Sharon et al. (2002) Nature / Audoly & Boudaoud (2003) PRL Non-Euclidean Edge Buckling Cascades in Ruffled Leaf Margins — Reproducibility package: 94/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "`self_test()` (L1787-L1888) now runs 11 checks in ~7 s — the 8 Pass 2 checks plus PIN1 transport sum(da) = 0 (< 1e-10), TCP front saturation and v_tcp = 0 => m = 0; WT N_ser >= 5 with >= 2 primary and >= 2 secondary tips, hierarchy > 1.5, g_0(y) >= 0, |<g_0> - 0.64| <= 0.10, M >= 3, K(0) < 0, basal/apical g_0 > 1, finite emergence time, monotone <g_0>(t); all 6 ordinal checks and a bitwise-deterministic developmental re-run; `assert len(meas) == 15` (L1878). The default render exits 0 in ~6 s and regenerates the Pass 2 PNG/GIF byte-identically plus the two new developmental media files. Deductions: the developmental GIF requires no flag but both PNGs are gitignored, so the rendered figures are not tracked artifacts and will not show in `git status` (-2); matplotlib needs `MPLCONFIGDIR` set when `~/.matplotlib` is not writable and the script does not say so (-1); `measure_morphoeval()` cannot be pointed at a non-default genotype so the measurement table for cin / TCP-OE is reproducible only through the sweep internals (-2); no requirements lock file is vendored for this slot (-1)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-repro-package> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/repro-package" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "2002-sharon-ripping-leaf-edge-waves.py L1616–L1621: measure_morphoeval() has no parameters: non-default genotype measurement tables are not directly reproducible from the CLI <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/327729c8/2002-sharon-ripping-leaf-edge-waves.py#L1616-L1621>" ;
        ns1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sharon-ripping-leaf-edge-waves-repro-package-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sharon-ripping-leaf-edge-waves-repro-package-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sharon-ripping-leaf-edge-waves-repro-package-3>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sharon-ripping-leaf-edge-waves-repro-package-4> ;
        ns1:hasScore 9.4e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-sharon-ripping-leaf-edge-waves-source-traceability> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Sharon et al. (2002) Nature / Audoly & Boudaoud (2003) PRL Non-Euclidean Edge Buckling Cascades in Ruffled Leaf Margins — Source and data traceability: 91/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "The 4 Pass 2 dataset files remain SHA-256-verified at runtime (`verify_dataset_integrity`, L101-L140) and the new `tcp_auxin_developmental_reference.json` is pinned (`EXPECTED_DEVELOPMENTAL_SHA256`, L741; `load_developmental_reference`, L753-L763) and documented in the README addendum together with the 9 new primary sources in `developmental_citations_pass3.bib`; the module header (L1-L70) cites each source with journal/volume/page. Deductions: all 9 new DOIs were transcribed offline and NOT verified online (network tools disallowed this pass) — the README says so, but a wrong DOI would propagate into the KG (-4); `developmental_citations_pass3.bib` is not SHA-256-pinned, unlike the Pass 2 `paper_citations.bib` (-2); the Pass 2 reference table's G1-G4 and 9-station profile values are analytic (g_yy, K from the same formulas; lambda_loc linear) rather than digitised from Sharon 2002 Fig. 3, and the phenotype table is ordinal rather than quantitative (-2); `K(0) = -1.091e-3` is hard-coded in the panel-D title (L1242) rather than taken from the reference (-1)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-source-traceability> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/source-traceability" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "2002-sharon-ripping-leaf-edge-waves.py L1242–L1242: K(0) = -1.091e-3 hard-coded in the panel-D title instead of read from the reference table <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/327729c8/2002-sharon-ripping-leaf-edge-waves.py#L1242-L1242>",
            "datasets/ripping_leaf_edge_waves/developmental_citations_pass3.bib L1–L102: 9 new BibTeX entries with DOIs transcribed offline; file is not SHA-256-pinned <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/327729c8/datasets/ripping_leaf_edge_waves/developmental_citations_pass3.bib#L1-L102>" ;
        ns1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sharon-ripping-leaf-edge-waves-source-traceability-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sharon-ripping-leaf-edge-waves-source-traceability-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sharon-ripping-leaf-edge-waves-source-traceability-3> ;
        ns1:hasScore 9.1e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-sharon-ripping-leaf-edge-waves-specimen-match> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Sharon et al. (2002) Nature / Audoly & Boudaoud (2003) PRL Non-Euclidean Edge Buckling Cascades in Ruffled Leaf Margins — Morphological realism / specimen match: 91/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "The SHA-256-locked *Lactuca sativa* cv. 'Lollo Bionda' specimen is still segmented via Excess Green (`segment_lactuca_sativa_specimen`, L631-L706; canopy fraction 0.7723; 4 coarse macro-lobes, 19 fine ripples, cascade ratio 4.75 in [3, 5]) and the 4-system aspect-ratio comparison (r_aspect = 0.9992) is unchanged; the new developmental figure adds a 3D coupled FvK surface with in-plane serration outgrowth and a genotype sweep against observed ranges. Deductions: the developmental module is compared with no specimen image at all — its only biological anchor is an ordinal phenotype table transcribed from Arabidopsis papers, applied to a Lactuca margin (-4); the 3D coupled mesh uses fixed mode phases (L401, L1024), an unsourced 0.18 in-plane contraction factor (L415) and an arbitrary 6 mm edge-displacement decay (L1033), and its y-modulation is visibly spiky because g_0(y) follows the auxin peaks (-3); the specimen cascade ratio is a count of perimeter extrema, not a wavelength or amplitude spectrum (-2)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-specimen-match> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/specimen-match" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "2002-sharon-ripping-leaf-edge-waves.py L1014–L1034: Developmental coupled mesh: fixed mode phases (L1024) and arbitrary 6 mm edge-displacement decay (L1033), unsourced <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/327729c8/2002-sharon-ripping-leaf-edge-waves.py#L1014-L1034>" ;
        ns1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sharon-ripping-leaf-edge-waves-specimen-match-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sharon-ripping-leaf-edge-waves-specimen-match-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sharon-ripping-leaf-edge-waves-specimen-match-3> ;
        ns1:hasScore 9.1e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly-code-traceability> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Sheth et al. (2012) Science distal Hoxa13/Hoxd11-13 + Gli3 dose modulation of Turing digit wavelength on a fan-shaped embryonic autopod, with Pass 3 AER-FGF8 mitogenic outgrowth on a deforming Lagrangian mesh — Code-to-model traceability: 93/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "The module docstring (L1-72) now maps the growing-domain equations term by term to Crampin et al. (1999), Boehm et al. (2010) and Summerbell (1974) and lists all five Lean theorems; the solver docstring (L527-551) restates the ALE equations, the zone kinetics and the Lean cross-references; the math KG YAML registers Laws 4-5 with lean_code, code_locus and source citations. Deductions: the g_u closure (L183) remains uncited; GROWTH_* constants (L431-445) carry comments but no source; the choice of the sub-Turing wrist gate f_u = 1.5 / g_u = 1500 (L601-603) is traced only to the Pass 2 negative control (-7)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "2012-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly.py L179–L183: k_c(H) = 14 - 9H and the g_u closure have no equation-level citation <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/58b898c/2012-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly.py#L179-L183>" ;
        ns1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly-code-traceability-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly-code-traceability-2>,
