    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-sugimura-tracheal-viscous-fingering-repro-package> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Nelson et al. (2017) Development & Kim et al. (2015) Dev. Cell microfluidic transmural pressure, Laplace epithelial wall stress, ASM peristalsis, 3D ellipsoidal pleural cavity tree, Poiseuille/CFTR luminal pressure network and laryngeal valve cycles driving embryonic lung branching — Reproducibility package: 95/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "12-suite deterministic `self_test()` (L1677-1786) passes in ~0.9 s: SHA-256 integrity, the three Pass 2 Lean laws, sweep correlations, 2D topology, specimen CV, bitwise determinism of `measure_morphoeval()`, and (Pass 3) Poiseuille accumulation and flow conservation, 3D confinement / ablation / 2D consistency / orthogonality, valve monotonicity + Spearman -1 + Jensen gap, and gauge invariance of the 3D and valve solvers. Default render ~3.2 s produces the 3x3 PNG, the 3D PNG and the 12-frame GIF with a fixed seed. Deductions: the self-test tolerance for the FBM mean Delta P (100-280 Pa, L1763) is loose enough to mask a 23 % miss (-2); the specimen suite asserts `== 17` against a self-recorded value rather than an external count (L1718-1722) (-2); `requirements.txt` is repo-wide and no lock file pins the exact numpy/scipy/matplotlib versions used here (-1)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-repro-package> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
