    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-tailbud-neuromesodermal-jamming-specimen-match> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Mongera et al. (2018) & Kim et al. (2021) zebrafish tailbud active fluid-to-solid jamming transition & yield-stress axis elongation — Morphological realism / specimen match: 88/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Panels A5, B1 and B5 still carry the SHA-256-verified IDR0051 *Danio rerio* tailbud lightsheet micrograph with N = 391 segmented nuclei, Voronoi coordination <z> = 5.88 and AP interstitial compaction matching Mongera et al. (2018) with r = 0.9915 (`segment_zebrafish_tailbud_specimen`, L980-1092), and the four 2D regimes in A1-A4 remain visually distinct (jammed anterior plasma colouring vs uniformly fluid cdh2/ablation fields, widened cdh2 envelope). Deductions: the new row C (L1478-1601) compares the sheath envelope, kymograph and frozen stripes only with model references and approximate literature ratios — no fibronectin immunostain or her1 in situ specimen is vendored, so the specimen does not test either new mechanism (-6); the fn1a;fn1b 2D regime is simulated (L1142-1153) but not rendered as a spatial panel, so the predicted wider tailbud is shown only as an envelope curve (-3); the kymograph's posterior synchronous band and anterior frozen stripes are qualitatively right but no comparison image from Soroldoni et al. (2014) is placed beside it (-3)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-specimen-match> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
