    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-tero-physarum-transport-network-repro-package> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Tero et al. (2010) Science & Tero, Kobayashi & Nakagaki (2007) J. Theor. Biol. adaptive Physarum tube conductivity network, shortest-path phase transition, Murray's cube law, Tokyo rail Pareto trade-off, and (Pass 3) peristaltic shuttle-streaming coupling — Reproducibility package: 90/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "`--self-test` runs 11 suites in ~7 s (SHA-256 of 3 files, Kirchhoff conservation, two-path transition, gamma = 0 ablation, graph-computed sweep with bitwise eps = 0 determinism, Murray, specimen CV, peristaltic closure < 1e-12 / reversal / exact 2-per-cycle at eps = 0.05 / O(eps) antisymmetry, second-order transport with a linear null < 1e-12, eps monotonicity, 14-metric bitwise determinism); the default render takes ~6.5 s and writes the PNG and both GIFs; `measure_morphoeval()` accepts a shared results bundle so nothing is computed twice. Deductions: the PNG is gitignored (`*.png`) so the audited figure is not in the repository and must be regenerated (-3); Suite 5 thresholds were loosened to admit the honest values rather than tightened (-2); no requirements lock pins the environment (versions recorded only in this audit) (-3); the self-test's compute_all_results() call is repeated by measure_morphoeval() in Suite 11, so the suite runs the full pipeline twice (-2)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-repro-package> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/repro-package" ;
        ns1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-tero-physarum-transport-network-repro-package-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-tero-physarum-transport-network-repro-package-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-tero-physarum-transport-network-repro-package-3>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-tero-physarum-transport-network-repro-package-4> ;
        ns1:hasScore 9e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-tero-physarum-transport-network-source-traceability> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Tero et al. (2010) Science & Tero, Kobayashi & Nakagaki (2007) J. Theor. Biol. adaptive Physarum tube conductivity network, shortest-path phase transition, Murray's cube law, Tokyo rail Pareto trade-off, and (Pass 3) peristaltic shuttle-streaming coupling — Source and data traceability: 80/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Three vendored inputs are SHA-256-verified at every run (`verify_dataset_integrity`, L112-L150, including the new `peristaltic_shuttle_streaming_reference.json`), the bib has 7 entries, the dataset README has a Pass 3 section (L32-L44) and the new JSON carries explicit `value_provenance` and a `provenance_note`. Deductions: the Kamiya (1981) DOI and the Alim (2013) DOI could not be verified offline and the JSON values T_c = 100 s and lambda*/L = 1 are `recalled` (L6, L30-L36, L52-L58) (-6); `ADAPTATION_TIME_S = 1800 s` (L343), which fixes omega and therefore the absolute shuttle-flux scale, is marked \"unsourced\" (-5); the pre-existing Fig. 3 reference table (8 gamma points with TL/MD/FT/Betti-1) and the Tokyo / Physarum benchmark numbers are not traceable to a specific digitisation — Tero 2010 Fig. 3 plots statistics against I0 for several gamma, not an 8-point gamma scan — so measurements 3-6 are against a reconstruction (-6); the Section 2b banner cites \"Kamiya 1959\" (L301) while the bib and JSON cite Kamiya 1981 (-1); the eps calibration disclosure is credited (+2 net against a larger deduction)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-source-traceability> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/source-traceability" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "2010-tero-physarum-transport-network.py L343–L343: ADAPTATION_TIME_S = 1800 s labelled 'model-scale anchor, unsourced' — sets omega and the osc/steady flux ratio <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/171769b9/2010-tero-physarum-transport-network.py#L343-L343>",
            "datasets/physarum_transport_network/physarum_transport_network_reference.json L1–L186: Pre-existing gamma_phase_transition_sweep_tero2010_fig3 table and Tokyo/Physarum benchmarks without digitisation provenance (Pass 1 reconstruction) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/171769b9/datasets/physarum_transport_network/physarum_transport_network_reference.json#L1-L186>" ;
        ns1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-tero-physarum-transport-network-source-traceability-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-tero-physarum-transport-network-source-traceability-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-tero-physarum-transport-network-source-traceability-3> ;
        ns1:hasScore 8e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-tero-physarum-transport-network-specimen-match> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Tero et al. (2010) Science & Tero, Kobayashi & Nakagaki (2007) J. Theor. Biol. adaptive Physarum tube conductivity network, shortest-path phase transition, Murray's cube law, Tokyo rail Pareto trade-off, and (Pass 3) peristaltic shuttle-streaming coupling — Morphological realism / specimen match: 80/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "The SHA-256-pinned specimen photograph is still segmented into 33 loops with a 3-tier vein hierarchy and Y-junction Murray ratios (`segment_physarum_specimen`, L919-L1025), and the figure now adds the shuttle-streaming time series with ablation (Panel G), net transport vs lambda/L with the Alim line (H), and the eps sweep against the Physarum TL band (I) plus a 24-frame signed-flux GIF. Deductions: the simulated network is a jittered lattice yet Panel A labels its axis \"Kanto West-East coordinate\" and calls the central node Tokyo (L158-L185) (-5); the specimen Betti-1 = 33 and Murray 0.8926 references are the script's own earlier outputs, so \"match\" here is self-agreement (-5); the shuttle-streaming comparison is to definitional / qualitative anchors (2 reversals, \"all tubes oscillate\"), not to a vendored flow-velocity trace or to Alim et al. kymographs (-5); 15 % of trunk tubes keep a steady bias at the default eps, which is reported honestly (-2); the Panel H optimum is shallow and non-unique (1.5 and 2.0 tie at 0.014; 0.25 gives 0.013) and should not be read as confirming lambda ~ L (-3)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-specimen-match> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/specimen-match" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "datasets/physarum_transport_network/peristaltic_shuttle_streaming_reference.json L30–L63: Reference anchors are value_provenance 'recalled' (T_c, lambda/L), 'definitional' (2 reversals) and 'qualitative' (fraction reversing) — weak specimen anchors <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/171769b9/datasets/physarum_transport_network/peristaltic_shuttle_streaming_reference.json#L30-L63>" ;
        ns1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-tero-physarum-transport-network-specimen-match-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-tero-physarum-transport-network-specimen-match-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-tero-physarum-transport-network-specimen-match-3>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-tero-physarum-transport-network-specimen-match-4>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-tero-physarum-transport-network-specimen-match-5> ;
        ns1:hasScore 8e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thomas-coral-calice-septa-insertion-code-traceability> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Milne-Edwards & Haime (1848), Kunth (1869) & Chindapol et al. (2013) Scleractinian coral calice septal insertion, reduced 3D corallum & Keulegan-Carpenter surge morphogenesis — Code-to-model traceability: 91/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "The header docstring (L1-L97) now lists the Pass 3 sources and maps each Pass 3 function to its law; `surge_renewal_efficiency` states in its docstring that the exponential form is a modelling choice; the Pass 3 measurements name their reference source and flag the model-internal one; the math-KG YAML registers Laws 4 and 5 with one `file#La-Lb` range per `code_locus` and refreshed Pass 2 loci. Deductions: the Law 3 rim-modulation constants (0.035, 0.025, 0.42, 0.35, 0.06) in `simulate_scleractinian_calice_2d` carry no citation (-4); the reference JSON cites Chindapol 'Eqs. (1)-(8)' for a flux law that is not Chindapol's (-3); the dissepiment phase/tilt choices in the 3D builder are commented but not sourced (-2)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "2013-thomas-coral-calice-septa-insertion.py L246–L365: simulate_scleractinian_calice_2d: hard-coded rim modulation constants (e.g. 0.035 at L274) without citation <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e651a8b8/2013-thomas-coral-calice-septa-insertion.py#L246-L365>",
            "datasets/coral_calice_septa_insertion/coral_calice_septa_insertion_reference.json L64–L64: Governing-equation section cites Chindapol 'Eqs. (1)-(8)' for a phenomenological flux ansatz <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e651a8b8/datasets/coral_calice_septa_insertion/coral_calice_septa_insertion_reference.json#L64-L64>" ;
        ns1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thomas-coral-calice-septa-insertion-code-traceability-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thomas-coral-calice-septa-insertion-code-traceability-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thomas-coral-calice-septa-insertion-code-traceability-3> ;
