    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-tozluoglu-wing-disc-dome-folding-overall> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Tozluoglu et al. (2019) Dev. Cell & Sui et al. (2018) Nat. Commun. Drosophila wing imaginal disc planar differential growth, basal ECM dome & H/N, H/H, H/P hinge folding (Pass 3: + reduced disc-proper / peripodial / lumen sac) — MorphoEval overall 85.8/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 3 (v3) evaluation of `2020-tozluoglu-wing-disc-dome-folding.py`. The single open v2 item (3D FEM of DP + PE + lumen) was closed in reduced form: a quasi-1D plane-strain three-compartment sac coupling the Pass 2 bilayer disc proper to a tensioned squamous peripodial membrane in unilateral contact and an incompressible lumen whose pressure is closed by prescribed volume (p = 0.62 Pa at 96 h, dome 53.91 um vs ref 54.0, d_HH 19.65 um vs ref 19.4) or imposed (sweep 0-800 Pa; p_half = 372.5 Pa; fold-locus shift 0.000), with a PE-ablation control, provenance-tagged parameters, two Lean 4 theorems and 10/10 passing self-test checks. The round also exposed that the headline fits are largely prescribed: the relaxed surface is tethered to a reference-fitted target shape, the dome-curvature constant is calibrated to the reference, the 7-zone curvature correlation compares hard-coded values, the uniform-growth positional SD is sampled rather than measured from the solved replicates, and the specimen fold loci are window-prescribed. Scores drop accordingly; the Pass 3 additions themselves are honest and well tagged. Overall 85.8/100 (faithfulness 83.8, reproducibility 90.5); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 028758bc; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 82, Morphological realism / specimen match 85, Parameter expressivity 90, Morphometric validation 80, Source and data traceability 88, Code-to-model traceability 90, Reproducibility package 93. Output judged: docs/media/wing_disc_dome_folding_comparison.png: rendered output of 2020-tozluoglu-wing-disc-dome-folding.py at 028758bc, image/png, 642851 B, 2159×1465 px, artifact_sha256 d96fd9da4de81ddd20c5d03b4b0e3e12157621e79cfe3dd7746c18d9ad79ae97 (sha256 d96fd9da4de81ddd20c5d03b4b0e3e12157621e79cfe3dd7746c18d9ad79ae97), spec_fingerprint 2af2500d7102510b3e1d9092d6e108c583a8e75540249273bb0089532f4c3517. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 2af2500d7102510b3e1d9092d6e108c583a8e75540249273bb0089532f4c3517; artifact_sha256: d96fd9da4de81ddd20c5d03b4b0e3e12157621e79cfe3dd7746c18d9ad79ae97; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/wing_disc_dome_folding/drosophila_wing_disc_specimen.jpg=b523296d0ee292e1..., datasets/wing_disc_dome_folding/peripodial_lumen_reference.json=972d43d7d4fc991a..., datasets/wing_disc_dome_folding/scout_manifest.json=0f2a2d1d54a8d262..., datasets/wing_disc_dome_folding/wing_disc_dome_folding_reference.json=c4c99a6cca181df7...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-wing-disc-dome-folding-audit-v2. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Tozluoglu et al. (2019): planar differential growth rates in the third-instar wing disc, together with the basal ECM, position the H/N, H/H and H/P folds precisely; uniform growth gives unpinned buckling; Collagenase flattens the dome and abolishes folds | Sui et al. (2018): differential lateral and basal tension drive H/H vs H/P folding by two distinct mechanisms | McClure & Schubiger (2005): the peripodial epithelium is a thin squamous layer overlying the columnar disc proper (used only for h_PE ~ 3 um; DOI not verified offline) | Mosaliganti et al. (2019): epithelial lumen pressures of ~100-300 Pa in the zebrafish otic vesicle (order-of-magnitude context only; NOT wing-disc data; DOI not verified offline); reconstructed_in_script: L-BFGS-B 2D sagittal apico-basal bilayer with multiplicative growth stretch, stiff BM tether and local fold remodeling (Pass 2); Pass 3 adds a quasi-1D plane-strain sac: neo-Hookean BM shell tension, shallow-cap Laplace dome deflection, tensioned PE membrane in unilateral contact, lumen pressure closed by prescribed volume (bisection) or imposed, an imposed-pressure sweep, a PE-ablation control, 13 measurements and 10 self-test checks; transfer_boundary: The bilayer 'relaxed' surface is tethered to a hand-built target shape (dome envelope, stage scaling and Gaussian cleft depths fitted to the reference table), so the 64-96 h dome and fold-depth correlations largely reproduce the prescription rather than emerge from g(s) | T_PE = 1 mN/m, h_lumen = 12 um, h_margin = 8 um and T_cell = 0.5 mN/m are order-of-magnitude assumptions with no wing-disc measurement; the self-consistent p = 0.62 Pa and p_half = 372.5 Pa are model predictions with no published value to compare; does_not_claim: A 3D finite-element mesh, dorsoventral curvature, PE growth or PE fold mechanics, a measured wing-disc lumen pressure, or an emergent (untethered) fold pattern." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 2020-tozluoglu-wing-disc-dome-folding.py:1061-1082 — `segment_wing_disc_specimen` confines the H/N, H/H and H/P loci to windows [0.22, 0.30], [0.35, 0.43], [0.50, 0.54] and penalises the H/H objective by -0.8 |s - 0.39|; `pouch_frac = s_hp_emp`. Detect the loci without reference-anchored windows (or widen them to the whole hinge and drop the penalty) and report the detection without the prior; record the specimen's genotype / stage / reporter or mark the 'reporter staining' reading as unknown.",
            "remediation needed: 2020-tozluoglu-wing-disc-dome-folding.py:1755 and 1853 — `self_test` docstring '8-point verification suite for Pass 2' and `--self-test` help '8-check verification suite' are stale (10 checks run). Update both; vendor a requirements lock for this script.",
            "remediation needed: 2020-tozluoglu-wing-disc-dome-folding.py:193-211 — `c_finite = 8.395` (L208) is calibrated so the WT dome curvature hits the 0.0128 um^-1 reference; derive the shell curvature from the relaxed surface (kappa = z'' / (1 + z'^2)^1.5 at the pouch apex) or document the constant as a fit with its source.",
            "remediation needed: 2020-tozluoglu-wing-disc-dome-folding.py:354-414 — `solve_wing_disc_sagittal_bilayer` builds `z_target` from a hand-tuned dome envelope (`dome_amp_stage`, L354-368 with per-condition multipliers 0.861 / 0.959 / 1 + 0.092(...)), `fold_stage_scale` (L371-374) and Gaussian cleft depths 15.35/19.95/16.75 um x `remodel_mult` / `jak_mult` (L383-394), then tethers the solution with `k_tether = 1.0` (L414), so the dome r = 0.998 and 15-fold r = 0.995 are prescribed. Replace the target-shape tether by an energy whose fold loci and depths emerge from gamma_s(s, t) = exp(g(s)(t - 64)) and the BM stiffness (e.g. a growth-incompatibility bending energy), or relabel the correlations as 'fit to prescribed target'.",
            "remediation needed: 2020-tozluoglu-wing-disc-dome-folding.py:592-742 and 745-791 — the Pass 3 sac is quasi-1D per unit dorsoventral width; the pressure-mode sweep lets the PE sag > 100 um for p > 10 Pa (an unphysical DP-only response). Carry the v2 item forward: add dorsoventral curvature (axisymmetric shallow-shell or a 3D FEM mesh) for the DP and PE, give the PE a growth law and its own fold mechanics, and bound the PE sag in pressure mode; sweep T_PE and h_lumen since both are untested assumptions.",
            "remediation needed: 2020-tozluoglu-wing-disc-dome-folding.py:879-885 — in `evaluate_developmental_timecourse` the hinge ridge (0.0148 / 0.0151), notum (0.0042) and fold (-0.0020 x depth) zone curvatures are hard-coded, so the 7-zone curvature r = 1.0000 compares the reference with itself. Compute kappa(s) by finite differences of the relaxed `z_apical_um` per zone and report the resulting r honestly.",
            "remediation needed: 2020-tozluoglu-wing-disc-dome-folding.py:958-975 — `evaluate_perturbation_experiments` solves 12 uniform-growth replicates but discards them and appends `rng_rep.uniform(0.18, 0.68)` (L970); the WT pinned SD is `rng_pin.normal(0, fold_position_sd_norm_ref)` (L975), i.e. the reference SD is the generating sigma. Measure the central-fold locus on each solved replicate surface and compute the SD from those; drop the sampled jitter (also fixes `d_hn_sim = float(d_hn_target)` at L474-476).",
            "remediation needed: datasets/wing_disc_dome_folding/wing_disc_dome_folding_reference.json:1-298 — the 64-96 h dome and d_HH timecourse, the 7-zone g(s) / curvature and the perturbation domes (46.5 / 51.8 / 56.4 um, SD 0.142) are not traced to specific figure panels or tables of Tozluoglu et al. (2019) or Sui et al. (2018). Add per-value `source_figure` / `extraction_method` fields or mark the values as synthesised." ;
        ns1:hasScore 8.58e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-tozluoglu-wing-disc-dome-folding-parameter-expressivity> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Tozluoglu et al. (2019) Dev. Cell & Sui et al. (2018) Nat. Commun. Drosophila wing imaginal disc planar differential growth, basal ECM dome & H/N, H/H, H/P hinge folding (Pass 3: + reduced disc-proper / peripodial / lumen sac) — Parameter expressivity: 90/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Credited: 5 stages x 7 zones (L809-903), 6 perturbation conditions including the new `peripodial_ablation` (L906-999), the imposed-pressure sweep over 9 values 0-800 Pa reporting p_half, maximal fold-locus shift and monotonicity (L745-791), and 11 CLI overrides: `--mu-bm`, `--g-pouch`, `--jak-stat-boost`, `--remodeling`, `--seed` plus the new `--lumen-mode`, `--p-lumen`, `--h-lumen`, `--t-pe`, `--ablate-peripodial`, `--skip-sweep` (L1853-1866) wired through `_lumen_kwargs_from_overrides` (L797-806) into timecourse, figure and GIF. Deductions: because the fold family is tethered to a prescribed target (L354-414), the swept growth parameters change amplitudes but cannot move or create folds (-6); `--p-lumen` is silent unless `--lumen-mode pressure` is also passed (L1862) (-2); no sweep over T_PE or h_lumen, the two most uncertain Pass 3 inputs (-2)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
        ns1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-tozluoglu-wing-disc-dome-folding-parameter-expressivity-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-tozluoglu-wing-disc-dome-folding-parameter-expressivity-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-tozluoglu-wing-disc-dome-folding-parameter-expressivity-3> ;
        ns1:hasScore 9e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-tozluoglu-wing-disc-dome-folding-repro-package> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Tozluoglu et al. (2019) Dev. Cell & Sui et al. (2018) Nat. Commun. Drosophila wing imaginal disc planar differential growth, basal ECM dome & H/N, H/H, H/P hinge folding (Pass 3: + reduced disc-proper / peripodial / lumen sac) — Reproducibility package: 93/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Credited: `self_test()` (L1754-1848) runs 10 checks — SHA-256 integrity of 5 files, JSON-to-code parity incl. `H_LUMEN_MEAN_REF_UM` (L1761), Laws 1-3, timecourse correlations, specimen CV, bitwise determinism, and new checks for PE-DP non-penetration (L1818), volume closure, fold-locus invariance, PE-ablation == uncoupled DP (L1824-1828), sweep monotonicity with p_half > 50 Pa and 13 measurements with `reference_value` keys (L1840); a fresh run PASSED all 10 in 11.9 s, the default render takes ~16-18 s and writes the PNG, the new sweep PNG and the GIF; the environment (Python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0) is recorded above. Deductions: stale '8-check' / '8-point' strings (L1755, L1853) (-2); `*.png` is gitignored so the regenerated comparison and sweep PNGs are not versioned and the measurements file is the only fingerprint (-2); no requirements lock file is vendored for this script (-3)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-repro-package> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/repro-package" ;
        ns1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-tozluoglu-wing-disc-dome-folding-repro-package-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-tozluoglu-wing-disc-dome-folding-repro-package-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-tozluoglu-wing-disc-dome-folding-repro-package-3> ;
        ns1:hasScore 9.3e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

