        rdfs:label "Wolpert (1969) French Flag positional information, Tickle-Wolpert (1975) chick limb ZPA digit duplication, Ben-Zvi-Barkai (2010) scaling & 2D AER-FGF / ZPA-Shh limb bud paddle — MorphoEval overall 90.3/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 3 (v3) evaluation of `1969-wolpert-french-flag-morphogen.py` (90.3/100; v2 91.1, v1 41.2). The single v2 remediation item is closed: Section 3b adds a 2D proximo-distal x anteroposterior paddle on which AER FGF (`dF/dt = D lap F - k_F F + s_F AER (1 + g_S S/(S+K_S))`) drives distal apposition growth (`dL/dt = v_max <F>_PZ/(<F>_PZ+K_g)`) and ZPA Shh production requires FGF (`dS/dt = D lap S - k_S S + s_S [ZPA] F/(F+K_FS)`). The 2D readouts reproduce Tickle (1975/1981) 4-3-2 and 4-3-2-2-3-4 with a 4/4 dose series, Saunders (1948) / Summerbell (1974) stage-dependent truncation 5/5 (rho = 1.0, mean post-excision overshoot 15 um), Niswander (1994) Shh collapse after AER removal (<= 0.06 %) and Laufer (1994) posterior AER FGF asymmetry (1.56 -> 1.00 with a symmetric graft); the stencil is verified against the 1D cosh solution (RMSE 2.4e-3). A Pass 2 defect was fixed (attenuated graft 4-3-2-3 -> 4-3-2-2-3 via a morphogen-valley digit reader). The scores are held slightly below v2 because the new layer is a tuned, time-compressed, geometrically prescribed reduction validated against ordinal references, and the specimen is still not a limb bud; these are listed as the Pass 4 remediation items. Overall 90.3/100 (faithfulness 89.3, reproducibility 92.6); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 469bf3c; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 92, Morphological realism / specimen match 86, Parameter expressivity 91, Morphometric validation 90, Source and data traceability 95, Code-to-model traceability 92, Reproducibility package 91. Output judged: docs/media/french_flag_morphogen_comparison.png: rendered output of 1969-wolpert-french-flag-morphogen.py at 469bf3c, image/png, 1396993 B, 2880×2688 px, artifact_sha256 8c085a38c660bc8306e75d1e8f570fd260932d2b0fcbe3d7a50ff07c7f1fcedd (sha256 8c085a38c660bc8306e75d1e8f570fd260932d2b0fcbe3d7a50ff07c7f1fcedd), spec_fingerprint 2318acced0a431554f620954ae7793615d43475a0b43ba5e6a33b913a35b9af8. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 2318acced0a431554f620954ae7793615d43475a0b43ba5e6a33b913a35b9af8; artifact_sha256: 8c085a38c660bc8306e75d1e8f570fd260932d2b0fcbe3d7a50ff07c7f1fcedd; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/french_flag_morphogen/french_flag_morphogen_reference.json=deae09091fa98a1b..., datasets/french_flag_morphogen/french_flag_specimen.jpg=7163e90c56e1316e..., datasets/french_flag_morphogen/limb_bud_2d_aer_zpa_reference.json=c34af92f3747bb64..., datasets/french_flag_morphogen/scout_manifest.json=d3bd7cc1c62dd2cb...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-french-flag-morphogen-audit-v2. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Wolpert (1969): positional information read from a monotone morphogen gradient against thresholds gives size-invariant French-Flag proportions under linear source-sink diffusion; Crick (1970): synthesis-diffusion-degradation gives lambda = sqrt(D/k) and the positional-error law sigma_x = sigma_c / |dc/dx| | Tickle, Summerbell & Wolpert (1975) and Tickle (1981): a posterior ZPA specifies wing digits 2-3-4; an anterior graft gives the mirror duplication 4-3-2-2-3-4, and the digit specified next to a weaker graft advances 2 -> 3 -> 4 with polarizing-cell number; Riddle et al. (1993): Shh mediates ZPA activity | Saunders (1948) and Summerbell (1974): AER removal arrests outgrowth and truncates the limb at a level that is progressively more distal the later the excision; Summerbell, Lewis & Wolpert (1973): proximo-distal values are laid down by time spent in the distal progress zone | Laufer et al. (1994) and Niswander et al. (1994): Shh in the ZPA and Fgf4 in the posterior AER maintain each other (Shh lost after AER removal, rescued by FGF4 bead; ectopic anterior Fgf4 after a ZPA graft); Crossley et al. (1996): Fgf8 is expressed along the whole ridge | Ben-Zvi & Barkai (2010): an expander produced where morphogen is low scales the decay length with domain size; reconstructed_in_script: 1D linear source-sink and SDD solvers (analytic + explicit PDE, RMSE 7.6e-6), 6-stage growth-scaling sweep with expansion-repression, 5-regime 1D ZPA suite (wild type, full / attenuated / weak anterior graft, ablation) read by a morphogen-valley digit rule, 400-trial Monte Carlo positional-error test, radial segmentation of the vendored 72 h embryo photograph | Pass 3: explicit 2D finite-difference solver for FGF and Shh on a growing paddle mask (dx = 12.5 um) with zero-flux boundaries, Michaelis-form Shh<->FGF feedback, AER-driven distal apposition growth, graft dose series, AER excision at five stages, ZPA ablation, a rectangle verification against the 1D cosh steady state, 8 new reference-anchored measurements and 7 new Lean 4 theorems; transfer_boundary: The 2D model is a reduced phenomenological coupling: the production rates s_F, s_S, feedback gain g_S and half-saturations K_S, K_FS, K_g are tuned so that wild-type FGF ~ 1 and L_final ~ 660 um, not taken from any paper; the developmental clock is compressed (12 h of model time spans HH18 -> HH28, ~5x faster than in ovo) while keeping tau_relax << tau_growth | The paddle geometry is prescribed (fixed AP width 500 um, elliptical 150 um cap); the AER is the distal-facing rim row and the ZPA is the posterior-margin mesenchyme within 120 um of the rim by construction, so their positions are inputs, not emergent; new lattice rows appear with zero concentration (no proliferation field) | Digit identity is read from the instantaneous distal Shh concentration against the Pass 2 thresholds normalised to the wild-type peak; the proximo-distal segment is read from the truncation fraction of the wild-type length via a 1/3-2/3 trisection, and the Saunders / Summerbell comparison is to an ordinal stage -> segment summary (+/- 1 stage between studies), not to digitised truncation data | The specimen is a whole-egg 72 h embryo photograph whose radial area-vasculosa profile is used as a proxy gradient; no limb bud image or Shh / Fgf in situ is compared with the 2D output; does_not_claim: Digit condensation or Turing-type periodicity, temporal integration of Shh exposure (Harfe 2004), a dorsoventral axis or 3D geometry, measured growth curves of the chick wing bud, quantitative Fgf4 / Shh expression levels, or a mechanistic derivation of AER and ZPA position." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 1969-wolpert-french-flag-morphogen.py:472-494 and 624-625 — s_F, s_S, g_S, K_S, K_FS and K_g are tuned so that wild-type AER FGF ~ 1 and L_final ~ 660 um; none is sourced. Add a rendered sensitivity sweep over g_S in {0, 0.5, 1, 2} and K_FS in {0.03, 0.1, 0.3} showing which readouts (P/A ratio, Shh collapse time, L_final) depend on them, and state the identifiability of each constant in the ledger.",
            "remediation needed: 1969-wolpert-french-flag-morphogen.py:488-489 (T_s = 12 h) with the header at 467-470 — the developmental clock is compressed ~5x relative to HH18 -> HH28 in ovo. Replace the explicit scheme by an implicit / ADI step so the run can use the real ~60 h at the same cost, and compare L(t) with measured wing-bud lengths per HH stage instead of the linear 48 um/stage clock (HH_STAGE_LENGTHS_UM, L496-498).",
            "remediation needed: 1969-wolpert-french-flag-morphogen.py:501-544 — the paddle has a fixed AP width (W = 500 um) and the AER / ZPA sets are placed geometrically, so the anterior-graft bud lengthens (687 um, HH29) rather than broadens as duplicated wings do (Tickle 1975). Add AP widening driven by the FGF field (or by the digit count) and let the ZPA position follow Shh-high mesenchyme rather than a fixed 60 x 120 um box.",
            "remediation needed: 1969-wolpert-french-flag-morphogen.py:728-731 and 347-378 — 2D digit identity is read from the instantaneous distal Shh concentration normalised to the wild-type peak; Harfe et al. (2004) show that digit identity integrates Shh exposure over time. Add a cumulative-exposure readout and report whether the dose series and the duplication survive it.",
            "remediation needed: 1969-wolpert-french-flag-morphogen.py:753-774 and datasets/french_flag_morphogen/limb_bud_2d_aer_zpa_reference.json — the Saunders / Summerbell comparison is to an ordinal stage -> segment summary with a +/- 1-stage caveat. Vendor digitised truncation data (fraction of humerus / radius-ulna / carpals / digits present per excision stage from Summerbell 1974) and score the model's truncation fraction against it quantitatively.",
            "remediation needed: datasets/french_flag_morphogen/french_flag_specimen.jpg and 1969-wolpert-french-flag-morphogen.py:844-930 — the only specimen is a whole-egg 72 h embryo whose area vasculosa is used as a proxy gradient; nothing in Panels G-I is compared with a wing bud. Vendor a CC-licensed HH20-HH24 chick wing bud image (ideally an Shh or Fgf8 in situ) and compare the paddle outline (aspect ratio, cap curvature) and the Shh domain extent with it." ;
        ns1:hasScore 9.03e-01 ;
        ns1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-wolpert-french-flag-morphogen-parameter-expressivity> a ns1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Wolpert (1969) French Flag positional information, Tickle-Wolpert (1975) chick limb ZPA digit duplication, Ben-Zvi-Barkai (2010) scaling & 2D AER-FGF / ZPA-Shh limb bud paddle — Parameter expressivity: 91/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "v2 sweeps retained (6 growth stages L268-340, 5 Monte Carlo thresholds L805-838, now 5 1D ZPA regimes L381-441). Pass 3 adds two monotone sweeps that visibly control the predicted feature: graft strength 0 / 0.10 / 0.35 / 1.0 adds 0 / 1 / 2 / 3 digits (Panel H) and AER excision stage HH18 -> HH26 moves the truncation from stylopod to autopod with rho = 1.0 (Panel I); `--limb-vmax`, `--limb-feedback-gain`, `--limb-lambda-shh` and `--limb-hours` expose the 2D parameters (L1721-1724) and are wired into render_outputs (L1730-1745). Deductions: the feedback gain g_S and the half-saturations are not swept or shown, so the figure does not demonstrate what the Shh -> Fgf4 loop changes beyond the single P/A ratio (-5); the AP width and ZPA geometry are not parameters (-4)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
        ns1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        ns1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
        ns1:evidenceAgainst "1969-wolpert-french-flag-morphogen.py L1240–L1261: Panel H renders the dose series; no panel sweeps g_S or the K constants (deduction) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/469bf3c/1969-wolpert-french-flag-morphogen.py#L1240-L1261>" ;
