        dct:source "Independent bounded 1-D least-squares minimisation by the referee of the same objective (not an external datum)" ;
        rdfs:comment "Closes Pass 3.1 R2's unimplemented-fit finding. The fit also shows the Hill form is mis-specified for this model: the BVP reach has log-log slope 0.48 in G over (0, 2] and no plateau (44.19 cells at G = 2), the fitted half-saturation 2.26 lies outside the sweep, max |Hill - BVP| = 5.6 cells; the Lean theorem (L30-L60) formalises this Hill numerator, not the BVP" ;
